could probably use modified rules for swarms (little 's'). Perhaps represent special powers as free Numina?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm maybe.<br /> <br /> I might need to tie in with a base building aspect, the whole Hive thing<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm wondering if I should make Titles a thing. Like a real important game mechanic, but I might be too complex","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T17:30:03-08:00","id":844818,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Marshal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blades - Melee</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bows - Ranged</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Plates - Armor Defense</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scribe</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Staves - Warp </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spheres - Scry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clocks - Time</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stewards</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hammers - Create</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Records - post/precognition</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Diplomat</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crowns - Command</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Quills - Telepathy</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shade</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Veils - Shadows/Fly</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloaks - illusions</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chalices - poisons and potions</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So here\u2019s the advances I got since I asked for advice what powers to give the lists in. If anyone wants to suggest things to fill in the empty slots for Stewards, Scribes, and Diplomats, you\u2019re free to do so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ideas for Stewards is going to shift a little more into a more \u201cselfcentered\u201d fashion, being primarily administrators and managers of their realm instead of social butterflies (not just literally). They are the sort of people who ensure things run smoothy, maybe are the best builders.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maybe something space manipulating for them?</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Diplomats, I think maybe should be telepathy focused, all forms of it. Not sure what their 3 is.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scribes are outright the \u201cwizards\u201d and mystics I think.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It may be self explanatory as to why I put Shades and Marshals with what I did.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also, though it isn\u2019t said here: every Caste will have their own unique \u201cperks\u201d. All will start out with Form bonuses and one unique thing, maybe a gear or structure, a unique Servant template to force elite warriors out of. As they get stronger and gain more Authority, they unlock more such bonuses, such as in the case of the Marshals, they can eventually build Ultralisk equivalents to act as Officers. Unsure of what to give the other Splats</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:38:49-08:00","id":844873,"title":"","content":"For unled servitors, what about treating them as if Down and Dirty combat is used against them? So they can still do some damage if you bury your foes in numbers, but it is obviously inefficient.<br /> <hr /><br /> Plus, if you are fighting <i>against</i> the Endless, using Down and Dirty combat against unled Servants can let you look/feel like a bug-stomping badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-09-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:05:17-08:00","id":844922,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Steward</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Colonies require proper administration first and foremost; only then can they be truly prosperous.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The busy worker ant that slowly delves deeper tunnels whilst her sisters gather more food, the swarm of insects that communicates through discrete to better solve complex problems, the businessman that looks at his employees and begins assigning them their duties\u2026</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stewards are meant to be ideal Colony administrators. Whilst all Monarchs are expected to manage their Colonies to be self sufficient and are able to complete their duties as demanded by those above them, it is only the administrators that dabble in the exotic\u2026 industries unique to the Endless. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Stewards possess an instinctive understanding of finance and urban planning, though that does not mean the results resemble anything orderly. To the Kingmakers, the Stewards serve the vital role of producing extra resources for other, more needy yet important Castes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Noble Forms for the Stewards are built to be strong yet capable of quick thinking. Industry and creation demand not only a strong back for the builder, but keen senses an a sharp wit. One very important and common feature of Stewards is expanded senses, such as extra eyes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Noble Form Benefits </b> Industry demands lots of things for its Monarchs. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence, Wit, Stamina +1. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size +1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Senses: Perception bonus +2</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Boons </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>1st</b> Recycling Glands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>2nd</b> Extractor Building</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>3rd</b> Neural Towers</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:44:18-08:00","id":844930,"title":"","content":"By the way, if you ever need any inspiration, may I suggest The Swarm of War by Vexmaster over on Fanfiction.net, especially the early chapters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:52:11-08:00","id":844933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=844930#post844930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, if you ever need any inspiration, may I suggest The Swarm of War by Vexmaster over on Fanfiction.net, especially the early chapters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know that one. Explain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also... I know too many Swarm related things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:01:29-08:00","id":844935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=844933#post844933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know that one. Explain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also... I know too many Swarm related things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a several-hundred word fan fiction centred on a starcraft nerd who is reincarnated as a Zerg larva. The parts I was talking about are mostly about how he and the remnants of his brood settle on a primitive world without access to easy resource gathering (I.e. Minerals and Vespene geysers). Here's a link.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m.fanfiction.net/s/7080862/1/\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.fanfiction.net/s/7080862/1/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:04:22-08:00","id":844936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=844935#post844935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a several-hundred word fan fiction centred on a starcraft nerd who is reincarnated as a Zerg larva. The parts I was talking about are mostly about how he and the remnants of his brood settle on a primitive world without access to easy resource gathering (I.e. Minerals and Vespene geysers). Here's a link.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m.fanfiction.net/s/7080862/1/\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.fanfiction.net/s/7080862/1/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's... serval hundred thousands words long. I... have too many things to read and write I am afraid.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I am familiar with Warhammer.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, a lore dump:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Endless Physiology </b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To the understand the Endless, one must first understand the distinction between the various types of creatures.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first and by far the most important is one that may not be truly apparent to casual observers. The Endless on Earth, not the Monarchs, not the Colonies under them, are not \u201ctrue\u201d Endless life forms. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Endless, the <i>True</i> Endless, hail from a part of the Universe where the laws of reality as we understand them do not exist and as a result actually have a hard time existing in our portion of the Universe. It is only through the use of massive physics bubbles that forcibly simulate the functions and rules of the Void that the True Endless are even able to be anywhere within hundreds of thousands of lightyears by Earth - They would otherwise die as the reality around them causes their insides to crystalize and their blood to combust simultaneously as the chemical bonds of their matter fall into fatal combinations.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This unfortunately is a very difficult and resource intensive procedure. Warping physics on the scale of an entire world is time consuming and does not leave room for expansion without constantly burning up resources and mental energy. The Kingmakers can afford to cover their fleets\u2026 but not much else.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is where the other type of Endless comes into play, the Conscripted. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs and even the entire Colonies under them are modified Terran life forms that have received alterations to significant parts of their genome, the inclusion of Endless biodata into the genetic code. This allows the Terran life to simulate, to a limited degree the abilities of the true Endless, most especially Void energies, and Psionics. The reason why many Terrestrial Endless resemble modified Terran life forms is that quite simply put, that is what they are: True Endless are much more varied in their forms and more powerful Endless shed more of the Terran heritage away to resemble the Trueborn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are two types of Conscripted: Monarchs and Servitors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs are modified humans that receive extensive genetic modifications that allow them to act as leaders on Earth perfect hybrids that are able to switch between two states of being and wield powerful telepathic abilities. Their cover is ideal for interacting with non-Endless, and should they need to can assume powerful forms. The process that creates them is peculiar though, the converted human is actually capable of disobedience and there is actually very little incentive to ensure loyalty to the Kingmakers: outside the promise of wealth and power that is.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Servitors is a catch all term, referring to the vast multitude of different types of creatures created to serve. Whether they be powerful Servants or lowly creatures. Often Servitors are made up of many different species, assembled and spliced to meet the needs of the desiring Monarch. The lowest of these is the Drone, a simple, yet adaptive unit around the size of a mastiff that serves as the main workhorse of any Colony regardless of what forms it possesses. Most Servitors are rather mindless and will only take actions to stay alive without being controlled by higher beings. Most servitors, especially drones take about a few hours to produce, but have a lifespan less than a week. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Servants are advanced Servitors, capable of limited problem solving and intelligence. They exist to act as intermediaries to their Monarch and act as extensions of her will. They emanate localized telepathic signals that command lesser Servitors from the same Colony to complete an assigned task. However, Servitors are expensive and take a portion of the Monarch\u2019s Psionic power to maintain, meaning that a Monarch is only able to produce and command a limited number of them at any given time. The most basic form of Servitor available to all Monarchs regardless of Caste is the \u201cForeman\u201d, a larger, smarter, and stronger Drone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies are the base camps, the castles, the keeps, the fortresses of a Monarch. They are often hidden deep underground, in a realm where that exists both in realspace\u2026 and not, though there is often the odd nomadic Colony that travels overland or by air, but the ideal Colony is at the very center of a Monarch\u2019s territory or lands. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It consists of \u201cbuildings\u201d, actually larger creatures that process resources or serve other vital functions, such birth more Endless, convert scavenged materials into useful things, or more. In fact, the Endless as a whole do not possess technology as we understand it; rather, they simply create life forms or subvert existing ones to suit their needs.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:12:40-08:00","id":844937,"title":"","content":"That's fine. I only meant the first couple of chapters but I understand if you don't have time (heaven knows I have too little time to do everything).<br /> <br /> I like the new lore, and that mention of a realm not-quite-here has intrigued me. Just out of curiosity, could I build a Colony that lives inside something like a massive whale and which travels the seas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:17:40-08:00","id":844939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=844937#post844937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine. I only meant the first couple of chapters but I understand if you don't have time (heaven knows I have too little time to do everything).<br /> <br /> I like the new lore, and that mention of a realm not-quite-here has intrigued me. Just out of curiosity, could I build a Colony that lives inside something like a massive whale and which travels the seas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Youd.... be better off making your own whale sized forms. And even then you'd need something like a whole pod, but totally doable and able to simulate a full colony. Because ad big as whales are, a single whale isn't bug enough to do everything needed<br /> <br /> Also this provides me an excuse to bring up a topic. Despite the insectoid theming, the Endless do not have to be buglike. They can be mammalian or reptilian in appearance or even birdie for some avian strains. The Zerg actually lean very much on reptilian for instance.<br /> <br /> So you can have lots of shaggy pelts and feathers if you desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T02:45:01-08:00","id":844987,"title":"","content":"BTW, would it be OK if I collated the stuff you're writing in thesis posts into a Gdoc? It's just for ease of writing. I can email you a copy or whatever if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T06:49:57-08:00","id":845046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=844987#post844987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, would it be OK if I collated the stuff you're writing in thesis posts into a Gdoc? It's just for ease of writing. I can email you a copy or whatever if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I write them all in Gdocs actually, but for my purposes I don't link to them directly and just copy paste.<br /> <br /> I got... 5 folders already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:05:44-08:00","id":845048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845046#post845046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I write them all in Gdocs actually, but for my purposes I don't link to them directly and just copy paste.<br /> <br /> I got... 5 folders already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, it was just for my sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:07:14-08:00","id":845049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=844818#post844818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marshal<br /> Blades - Melee<br /> Bows - Ranged<br /> Plates - Armor Defense<br /> <br /> Scribe<br /> Staves - Warp <br /> Spheres - Scry<br /> Clocks - Time<br /> <br /> Stewards<br /> Hammers - Create<br /> Records - post/precognition<br /> <br /> Diplomat<br /> Crowns - Command<br /> Quills - Telepathy<br /> <br /> Shade<br /> Veils - Shadows/Fly<br /> Cloaks - illusions<br /> Chalices - poisons and potions<br /> <br /> So here\u2019s the advances I got since I asked for advice what powers to give the lists in. If anyone wants to suggest things to fill in the empty slots for Stewards, Scribes, and Diplomats, you\u2019re free to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> The ideas for Stewards is going to shift a little more into a more \u201cselfcentered\u201d fashion, being primarily administrators and managers of their realm instead of social butterflies (not just literally). They are the sort of people who ensure things run smoothy, maybe are the best builders.<br /> Maybe something space manipulating for them?<br /> <br /> Diplomats, I think maybe should be telepathy focused, all forms of it. Not sure what their 3 is.<br /> <br /> Scribes are outright the \u201cwizards\u201d and mystics I think.<br /> <br /> It may be self explanatory as to why I put Shades and Marshals with what I did.<br /> <br /> Also, though it isn\u2019t said here: every Caste will have their own unique \u201cperks\u201d. All will start out with Form bonuses and one unique thing, maybe a gear or structure, a unique Servant template to force elite warriors out of. As they get stronger and gain more Authority, they unlock more such bonuses, such as in the case of the Marshals, they can eventually build Ultralisk equivalents to act as Officers. Unsure of what to give the other Splats</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm personally against having one and only one X-splat that gets all the fighting powers at in-house costs, while no one else does. I might jump Bows to Stewards (since currently the other Castes have powers I can imagine with combat applications) or to Diplomats (if they're telepathy-based, they can be causing damage to other's minds) and give Marshals healy powers, for both fixing themselves and their minions, maybe giving Physical bonuses. Proposed name of Leeches? Or Leeches could go under Stewards, for fixing up themselves, their people, and their castle. Drums (shock-and-awe tactics, intimidation) could work for Marshals or Diplomats, maybe.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, changing the spread to use only ten powers (because coming up with unique spreads for fifteen lines sounds daunting):<br /> <br /> <b>Marshal</b><br /> Blades - melee, intimidation, power<br /> Bows - ranged, lightning, finesse<br /> *Plates - armor, defense, resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe</b><br /> \u200bQuills - mind-reading, discovery, telepathy<br /> Records - postcognition, precognition, time<br /> *Spheres - scrying, warping, space<br /> <br /> <b>Steward</b><br /> Cloaks - illusions, disguise, shapeshifting<br /> *Hammers - creation, repair, healing<br /> Records - postcognition, precognition, time<br /> <br /> <b>Diplomat</b><br /> Bows - ranged, lightning, finesse<br /> *Crowns - commands, control, royalty<br /> Quills - mind-reading, discovery, telepathy<br /> <br /> <b>Shade</b><br /> Blades - melee, intimidation, power<br /> Cloaks - illusions, disguise, shapeshifting<br /> *Veils - speed, flight, shadows<br /> <br /> Powers with a * are Caste-unique powers (might mean other Castes can't learn it without being taught; might mean that they're just the only Caste who gets it at in-house cost). Spheres subsumes Staffs, since both are about space. Records subsumes Clocks, because both are about time (and having both Clocks and Cloaks could be confusing). Dropped Chalices because I don't know if poisons needs to be its own thing, it might fall under Blades or Cloaks depending on how you spin it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:37:09-08:00","id":845067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845049#post845049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I'm personally against having one and only one X-splat that gets all the fighting powers at in-house costs, while no one else does. I might jump Bows to Stewards (since currently the other Castes have powers I can imagine with combat applications) or to Diplomats (if they're telepathy-based, they can be causing damage to other's minds) and give Marshals healy powers, for both fixing themselves and their minions, maybe giving Physical bonuses. Proposed name of Leeches? Or Leeches could go under Stewards, for fixing up themselves, their people, and their castle. Drums (shock-and-awe tactics, intimidation) could work for Marshals or Diplomats, maybe.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, changing the spread to use only ten powers (because coming up with unique spreads for fifteen lines sounds daunting):<br /> <br /> <b>Marshal</b><br /> Blades - melee, intimidation, power<br /> Bows - ranged, lightning, finesse<br /> *Plates - armor, defense, resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe</b><br /> \u200bQuills - mind-reading, discovery, telepathy<br /> Records - postcognition, precognition, time<br /> *Spheres - scrying, warping, space<br /> <br /> <b>Steward</b><br /> Cloaks - illusions, disguise, shapeshifting<br /> *Hammers - creation, repair, healing<br /> Records - postcognition, precognition, time<br /> <br /> <b>Diplomat</b><br /> Bows - ranged, lightning, finesse<br /> *Crowns - commands, control, royalty<br /> Quills - mind-reading, discovery, telepathy<br /> <br /> <b>Shade</b><br /> Blades - melee, intimidation, power<br /> Cloaks - illusions, disguise, shapeshifting<br /> *Veils - speed, flight, shadows<br /> <br /> Powers with a * are Caste-unique powers (might mean other Castes can't learn it without being taught; might mean that they're just the only Caste who gets it at in-house cost). Spheres subsumes Staffs, since both are about space. Records subsumes Clocks, because both are about time (and having both Clocks and Cloaks could be confusing). Dropped Chalices because I don't know if poisons needs to be its own thing, it might fall under Blades or Cloaks depending on how you spin it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understood it was that in Almarck's scheme, all of the Castes could purchase all of the powers but get the their 3 caste powers at a reduced cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:44:28-08:00","id":845072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845067#post845067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I understood it was that in Almarck's scheme, all of the Castes could purchase all of the powers but get the their 3 caste powers at a reduced cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> And another thing to keep in mind, the way Castes are setup is well based off of how medieval societial roles are arranged. Marshals have all 3 combat powers in their list because... that's what they are made for. Everyone had tools suited to their professions and asside from dabblers such as people going on hunts, most noblemen had no reason to pickup a sword.<br /> <br /> Scribes or clergy were all about study, learning, experimentation and magic. So they recieve the Powers linked to these items.<br /> <br /> Stewards are the same way, focused on managing. This is why I gave them records, representing their taskmaster nature.<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's kinda... self evident that &quot;castebased&quot; societies would encourage high degrees of specialization.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind, we could realistically expand each caste to having 4-5 in house powers, Werewolf afterall gives you like up to 6-7 in house buys for its system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-10-2016, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:03:32-08:00","id":845081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845072#post845072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> And another thing to keep in mind, the way Castes are setup is well based off of how medieval societial roles are arranged. Marshals have all 3 combat powers in their list because... that's what they are made for. Everyone had tools suited to their professions and asside from dabblers such as people going on hunts, most noblemen had no reason to pickup a sword.<br /> <br /> Scribes or clergy were all about study, learning, experimentation and magic. So they recieve the Powers linked to these items.<br /> <br /> Stewards are the same way, focused on managing. This is why I gave them records, representing their taskmaster nature.<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's kinda... self evident that &quot;castebased&quot; societies would encourage high degrees of specialization.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind, we could realistically expand each caste to having 4-5 in house powers, Werewolf afterall gives you like up to 6-7 in house buys for its system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the societal roles idea, but from a gameplay perspective, I'd like to have more options, rather than fewer. Given that each dot is granting several powers at a time, I'd imagine they'd be costly, and more so out-of-Caste; if I want my Steward to be able to defend their castle, or my Shade to work as an assassin, or my Scribe to act like Indiana Jones, or my Diplomat to defend themself, I don't want to pay out the nose to pick up Bows or Blades. Further, my Marshal would get no powers not related to combat right now, which similarly limits their playability. (I know 1e Werewolf does this quite a bit, and I dislike it there, too; 2e seems to be doing better with giving each Auspice combat-powers and non-combat-powers, despite their similarly role-based X-splat.)<br /> <br /> Expanding in-Caste powers a la Werewolf is a valid option, as is doing something like 2e Changeling, where every power is the same cost, but different Seemings get different bonuses/special effects for free (and others have to purchase them), or like Beast, where your starting powers are determined by Family, but after that everything costs the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:09:44-08:00","id":845087,"title":"","content":"Actually how I envision character creation and advancement to play out is<br /> <br /> <br /> 4 dots free at start. 2 based on Caste list. 1 that has to be outside caste, and 1 that goes anywhere.<br /> <br /> 3 experience for in caste buys. And 5 experience for out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind, you get everything at a given dot level, but 80% of the time its only going to be 1 thing. A new gear item, a new power, or a noble form stats up.. or if I decide on including them, buildings and swarm increases. The other 20%, it's 2 items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:21:20-08:00","id":845093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845087#post845087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually how I envision character creation and advancement to play out is<br /> <br /> <br /> 4 dots free at start. 2 based on Caste list. 1 that has to be outside caste, and 1 that goes anywhere.<br /> <br /> 3 experience for in caste buys. And 5 experience for out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind, you get everything at a given dot level, but 80% of the time its only going to be 1 thing. A new gear item, a new power, or a noble form stats up.. or if I decide on including them, buildings and swarm increases. The other 20%, it's 2 items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so that's 2-4 extra sessions to purchase an in-caste power versus out-of-caste (depending on how generous the ST is and how often my Monarch elects to punch themself in the face for Beats). I'd still argue for all Castes to have at least one in-Caste combat-based power, and Marshals to have at least one in-Caste non-combat-based power. Even with the current envisioned CC requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:34:58-08:00","id":845098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845093#post845093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, so that's 2-4 extra sessions to purchase an in-caste power versus out-of-caste (depending on how generous the ST is and how often my Monarch elects to punch themself in the face for Beats). I'd still argue for all Castes to have at least one in-Caste combat-based power, and Marshals to have at least one in-Caste non-combat-based power. Even with the current envisioned CC requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think maybe Shades should have Bows or Blades.<br /> <br /> The others can make due with hax attacks that have combat benefits such as psi attacks against their opponents minds.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember , every Monarch in their noble form is probably also likely to go throw an army of Drones at their opponents since if you're willing to be an alien space bug, might as well add a few dozen more.<br /> May be slightly weaker without Blades or Bows for more damage or not depending on the rules I use for swarms building, but it's not like Nobles are without offensive options.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:01:35-08:00","id":845111,"title":"","content":"5 EXP seems a little high for a single power. I mean, that's the price for a power stat increase if I'm not mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:45:58-08:00","id":845136,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845111#post845111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 EXP seems a little high for a single power. I mean, that's the price for a power stat increase if I'm not mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it'd depend on what the final state of Monarch studies Los like distribution wise.<br /> Amy be 2 4. Maybe 3 5 we will have to see.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:48:16-08:00","id":845138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845136#post845136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well it'd depend on what the final state of Monarch studies Los like distribution wise.<br /> Amy be 2 4. Maybe 3 5 we will have to see.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why not 3 and 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:54:11-08:00","id":845143,"title":"","content":"I'd say 2 3. Makes the cost respectable but not enormous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:57:02-08:00","id":845144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845138#post845138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not 3 and 4?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shrug. Well week what the prices should be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, I'm wondering now if I should begin work on setting up Servitors.<br /> <br /> There's 2 types, the drone swarm which is a basic labour unit that can be expended on things. Not sure how to stat it out yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> The otheriis the Servant. Which is the elite henchman. Which has a full stats block based on what template or prefab bed form you select.<br /> <br /> Regardless I am thinking for both, they each would have inventory slots that you fill in. Obviouslyv there's probably going to be restrictions like say no artillery cannons for drones...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:20:39-08:00","id":845153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845144#post845144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Shrug. Well week what the prices should be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, I'm wondering now if I should begin work on setting up Servitors.<br /> <br /> There's 2 types, the drone swarm which is a basic labour unit that can be expended on things. Not sure how to stat it out yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> The otheriis the Servant. Which is the elite henchman. Which has a full stats block based on what template or prefab bed form you select.<br /> <br /> Regardless I am thinking for both, they each would have inventory slots that you fill in. Obviouslyv there's probably going to be restrictions like say no artillery cannons for drones...</div> </div> </div> </div>I might abstract things out more with drones. For example, start with one Drone Swarm at Size 3, that has three Skills with a pool of three, with one being an attack skill that does 0 Bashing. As you rank up in different powers, it affects things like pool size, added skills, more swarms, causing Conditions, doing more damage, doing Lethal/Aggrivated damage, immunities to types of attacks, greater health, greater Defense, larger swarm, etc. So a Monarch with a really high Bows might, in fact, have a Swarm with artillery canons, or giant lightning guns, or long-range acid vomiting, or whatever flavor they want their 3L Firearms attack to be.<br /> <br /> I'd have the limits be based on what powers you have, or maaaaybe on Authority, but I don't care for inventory-management systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:45:09-08:00","id":845159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845153#post845153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might abstract things out more with drones. For example, start with one Drone Swarm at Size 3, that has three Skills with a pool of three, with one being an attack skill that does 0 Bashing. As you rank up in different powers, it affects things like pool size, added skills, more swarms, causing Conditions, doing more damage, doing Lethal/Aggrivated damage, immunities to types of attacks, greater health, greater Defense, larger swarm, etc. So a Monarch with a really high Bows might, in fact, have a Swarm with artillery canons, or giant lightning guns, or long-range acid vomiting, or whatever flavor they want their 3L Firearms attack to be.<br /> <br /> I'd have the limits be based on what powers you have, or maaaaybe on Authority, but I don't care for inventory-management systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well inventory might not be a the right word, so much as a system for determining what extra things ontop of the base template you optionally add to your creatures.<br /> <br /> Such as if you want to make them have more melee or ranged firepower or give them wings versus more armor. And so on.<br /> <br /> One thing I really wanted to do was to actually have Monarchs pay for their units, as in well pay a cost of biomass or some resource around their colony. Obviously better troops would be a pricier investment but would be more powerful. But I am unsure about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:54:42-08:00","id":845168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845159#post845159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well inventory might not be a the right word, so much as a system for determining what extra things ontop of the base template you optionally add to your creatures.<br /> <br /> Such as if you want to make them have more melee or ranged firepower or give them wings versus more armor. And so on.<br /> <br /> One thing I really wanted to do was to actually have Monarchs pay for their units, as in well pay a cost of biomass or some resource around their colony. Obviously better troops would be a pricier investment but would be more powerful. But I am unsure about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that the system for determining what extra things your creatures get was the powers system. As in, your swarm can fly if you're high enough in Veils, they get more armor with Plates, greater ranged attack with Bows, etc. And the level of your powers is the direct limit on what they can have. <br /> <br /> If that is/could be the case, I can also see an alternate method of doing the powers: rather than buying the first dot, then second, then third, you could pick which set you get each time you put a dot in. So like with Veils, with the first dot, you could choose to have your self able to go fast, your minions able to go fast, or your base able to move fast. With the next dot, you could pick another thing to go fast, or you could upgrade &quot;go fast&quot; to &quot;fly&quot;. <br /> <br /> If that's not the case, I'd limit the number of powers/benefits a swarm can get by Authority. So at Authority 1, you have to pick if your swarm has extra armor, flight, or a killer ranged attack; at Authority 2 you can pick two; Authority 3 lets you have them all; Authority 4 means you can double up or add a new thing.<br /> <br /> For having swarms cost, they could need to invest N Psy Energy into it to keep it going. Maybe N is 1+powers-the-swarm-has-above-Authority or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T11:45:21-08:00","id":845195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845168#post845168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For having swarms cost, they could need to invest N Psy Energy into it to keep it going. Maybe N is 1+powers-the-swarm-has-above-Authority or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>For this you could probably take a cue from Genius in the way that Mania and Wonders work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:01:22-08:00","id":845200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845168#post845168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that the system for determining what extra things your creatures get was the powers system. As in, your swarm can fly if you're high enough in Veils, they get more armor with Plates, greater ranged attack with Bows, etc. And the level of your powers is the direct limit on what they can have.<br /> <br /> If that is/could be the case, I can also see an alternate method of doing the powers: rather than buying the first dot, then second, then third, you could pick which set you get each time you put a dot in. So like with Veils, with the first dot, you could choose to have your self able to go fast, your minions able to go fast, or your base able to move fast. With the next dot, you could pick another thing to go fast, or you could upgrade &quot;go fast&quot; to &quot;fly&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If that's not the case, I'd limit the number of powers/benefits a swarm can get by Authority. So at Authority 1, you have to pick if your swarm has extra armor, flight, or a killer ranged attack; at Authority 2 you can pick two; Authority 3 lets you have them all; Authority 4 means you can double up or add a new thing.<br /> <br /> For having swarms cost, they could need to invest N Psy Energy into it to keep it going. Maybe N is 1+powers-the-swarm-has-above-Authority or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The powers system contains to things pertaining to swarms.<br /> <br /> <br /> It contains automatic upgrades to your colony. Which is what produces all of your units <br /> <br /> It also contains... blueprints... for lack of a better term. Addons, upgrades, or specialist strains that you can build by expending resource","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:28:15-08:00","id":845208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845200#post845200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no. The powers system contains to things pertaining to swarms.<br /> <br /> <br /> It contains automatic upgrades to your colony. Which is what produces all of your units<br /> <br /> It also contains... blueprints... for lack of a better term. Addons, upgrades, or specialist strains that you can build by expending resource</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Is that mechanical way of doing powers set, or still in flux? I don't want to keep throwing out non-viable suggestions, or propose routes that you've determined you don't want the line to go down. For the record, these mechanics sound much closer to a minis game than to CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:35:41-08:00","id":845211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845208#post845208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. Is that mechanical way of doing powers set, or still in flux? I don't want to keep throwing out non-viable suggestions, or propose routes that you've determined you don't want the line to go down. For the record, these mechanics sound much closer to a minis game than to CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The layout is set for powers. I've gone through and shambles for months how I wanted it. So simplistifally, a layout similar to disciplines but add in other things mixed in instead of devotions<br /> <br /> And yes I am aware of the minigame aspect of Colony management. It's kinda like playing a game of Civ in my head.... which is why I am unsure about it.<br /> <br /> I may actually have to simply things somewhere. The most obvious being is making it more like a stockpile that you can expend with some options. Spend biomass into cheap warriors, invest into an elite. Use it to build something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-10-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:47:33-08:00","id":845215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845211#post845211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The layout is set for powers. I've gone through and shambles for months how I wanted it. So simplistifally, a layout similar to disciplines but add in other things mixed in instead of devotions<br /> <br /> And yes I am aware of the minigame aspect of Colony management. It's kinda like playing a game of Civ in my head.... which is why I am unsure about it.<br /> <br /> I may actually have to simply things somewhere. The most obvious being is making it more like a stockpile that you can expend with some options. Spend biomass into cheap warriors, invest into an elite. Use it to build something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha; I'll stop making suggestions about changing the powers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My suggestion for Swarm simplification, then, would be to Merit-ize it. Have Swarm and Servant be Merits. Each dot in Authority gives a free dot to invest in one of those merits. More dots in a single one means more power (greater size, health, dice pools, whatever); you can choose to throw all your points in one, or have a bunch of single-dot ones. So an Authority 3 Monarch could have one 3-dot Swarm, a 1-dot Swarm and a 2-dot Servant, three 1-dot Servants, etc. Maybe base Swarm off of Staff, with Servant off of Retainer or 1e Hedgebeast Companion or something.<br /> <br /> Additionally, they can be bought as regular Merits. For the powers, if they already have a dot level, say that the corresponding Swarm/Servant needs to have at least that many dots to use the ability. This way, you don't have to track any new sort of resources, and you can have different playstyles: on Monarch who uses their minimum dots to get a few Swarms to maintain their Colony, but invests the rest of their XP/powers in themself; another who buys a lot of Servants, but isn't too much more powerful than them; one who overwhelms their foes with lots of weak bugs; and so forth.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Making them Merits also makes the mechanics match the flavor of your biomass idea, due to Sanctity of Merits: you would be investing pieces of yourself into the Swarm/Servants, but then be able to get them back when they were destroyed. If you were tired of having them, or needed the XP for something else, you could destroy them yourself, get back the biomass/XP, and do other things with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 03-10-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:50:11-08:00","id":845216,"title":"","content":"It just struck me, we don't have a Discipline for telekinesis or manipulation of gravity. Is that intentional?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:04:29-08:00","id":845223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845216#post845216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just struck me, we don't have a Discipline for telekinesis or manipulation of gravity. Is that intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I don't think I thought of tk. Or if if did it was mostly to space and time warping.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> . Well I think the Colony itself should be covered as a merit since that simplifies that. Maybe powers to add passive to drones for free. You can order your colony to spit out temporary combat units that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am however still wanted to represent Servants with equipment since i dont feel a merit covers what i want but that might just be sunk cost fallacy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:14:15-08:00","id":845230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845223#post845223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. I don't think I thought of tk. Or if if did it was mostly to space and time warping.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> . Well I think the Colony itself should be covered as a merit since that simplifies that. Maybe powers to add passive to drones for free. You can order your colony to spit out temporary combat units that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am however still wanted to represent Servants with equipment since i dont feel a merit covers what i want but that might just be sunk cost fallacy</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to go down the tk route, might I suggest Icons (as in religious icons) for the name of the power.<br /> <br /> On colonies and Servants, I would say to make Colonies a merit and Servants something similar that works off of authority. Like, each tier of Authority gives you a certain number of points to distribute between individual Servants and their stats. I'm not sure what you would do with ordinary units like drones etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:15:49-08:00","id":845232,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Servants could work similarly to Offshoots from the Womb of Terrors Channel from Leviathan: the Tempest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:41:48-08:00","id":845243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845232#post845232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Servants could work similarly to Offshoots from the Womb of Terrors Channel from Leviathan: the Tempest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe... although I gotsome better ideas now<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Alright so how about this, your colony is actually represented as 5 seperate &quot;mana&quot; charges, similar to mummy pillars.<br /> <br /> This represents the current and maximum resources of your colony in a given field. Such as say you have 4 military power.<br /> Or 5 industrial power<br /> <br /> What you can spend these points on is determined by your powers or if you select to upgrade the Colony with specialist buildings. Some examples powers possess colony upgrades such as say flight for drones or Improved weapons for swarms.<br /> <br /> Some merits also upgrade the colony such as say an aquatic adaptation thing for underwater.<br /> <br /> <br /> I could perhaps integrate high powered Servants here, for when you have the required resources, you can spawn one. So you can spend on a lot of little guys.... or you can buy a living battletank if you have the presiquites<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think how I'll handle the Colony is that it's basically 5 merits rated 1 to 10 with a load of sub merits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:27:53-08:00","id":845270,"title":"","content":"Is there an overall name for the powers, like Disciplines, Contracts, Gifts and so on? If not, does Principalities work? Like, you would have the Principality of Blades, the Principality of Spheres etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:37:26-08:00","id":845276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845270#post845270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an overall name for the powers, like Disciplines, Contracts, Gifts and so on? If not, does Principalities work? Like, you would have the Principality of Blades, the Principality of Spheres etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was originally thinking Evolutions or Studies, but yeah Principality would be better for the theming...<br /> <br /> <br /> I kinda find it funny really how much of the termonology is more based on chivilric topics instead of alien things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:39:28-08:00","id":845280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845276#post845276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was originally thinking Evolutions or Studies, but yeah Principality would be better for the theming...<br /> <br /> <br /> I kinda find it funny really how much of the termonology is more based on chivilric topics instead of alien things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. It has a rather appealing irony to it. It might just be my rather dry and desolate sense of humour though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:39:48-08:00","id":845450,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>New Trait: Colony </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Monarchs are tended to by many lesser creatures, all various Strains of the Endless made to serve her. They act as everything from a labor force, a private army, personal servants, and everything in between, all at her beck and call. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traditionally, Colonies are located in Beneath, a sort of place underground that skirts between realworld location and alternate reality, usually accessed through wormholes or through spatially folded physical locations. As a general rule a Monarch may access or pull forces from her Colony from any Wormholes from her own Court or via physically entering the Beneath through the realspace anchors of her Colony. Generally speaking, Wormholes are safer and more expensive, but the anchor point of a Colony is a vulnerability that anyone with the knowledge can find.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But as many servants and warriors a Monarch is able to own, there are limits to how much this force can do, its capabilities, its ability to replenish losses, its own lacks from incomplete Geneweb, and other factors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies are represented by five attributes, each representing an estimation of the Colony\u2019s abilities at given tasks. These are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Military</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Knowledge</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Industry</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Espionage</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Diplomacy</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All are rated from 1 to 10, with a single dot in each at the start, plus an extra dot in the Monarch\u2019s primary area of focus. Similar to Willpower, these attributes have permanent dots and temporary scores, which occur due to the Monarch requiring that some of her Colony\u2019s resources be spent on task.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At any time, a Monarch or Servant may order the Colony to dispatch a unit of Drones to fulfill an assigned task, with the cost in Colony resources dependant on the task. The time it takes for the Colony to arrive onto the location of the assigned task is dependant on how far is the nearest Wormhole.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now I just need to decide what these features are\u2026</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m thinking Conscription could be a thing, where any dots or resources can be spent on getting combat units, but spending Military is just flatout better.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maybe some form of purchasing power?<br /> <br /> Also thinking we need &quot;buildings&quot; to be included as merits.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T01:38:15-08:00","id":845524,"title":"","content":"For the last 2 Principalities:<br /> <br /> Censers - smokescreens, gas clouds, airborne poisons<br /> Steeds - methods of travel, swimming, burrowing, flight, space travel (ala Byakhee)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T02:34:44-08:00","id":845535,"title":"","content":"Also, could a Servant or even a basic 'minion' be based on a plant? Like some kind of spy-ivy or brain-tree that stores information or acts as a relay for telepathic communications and so on? Or would that fall under the Colony?<br /> <br /> In fact, I could imagine the latter being a kind of spymaster that's in charge of the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-11-2016, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T05:45:34-08:00","id":845571,"title":"","content":"Is this at all how the Beneath is meant to look?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://ewkn.deviantart.com/art/Underworld-123444067\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/a75fef13-cad2-4e72-9370-6478e0eaec16/d21hu1v-160c4f2e-46a6-45e8-b90d-aafcfb0f908b.jpg/v1/fill/w_1497,h_534,q_70,strp/underworld_by_ewkn_d21hu1v-pre.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..nhoyJ4i0BansdQ9hndmIoo3JrKVjhj5AZYVzbqT__7c\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ewkn.deviantart.com/art/Underworld-123444067\" target=\"_blank\"> Underworld by eWKn on DeviantArt </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ewkn.deviantart.com/art/Underworld-123444067\" target=\"_blank\"> http://ewkn.deviantart.com/art/Underworld-123444067 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Underworld &mdash; artwork by eWKn on DeviantArt. Published: 2009-05-23 &middot; Likes: 580 &middot; Views: 26129 &middot; Comments: 25 </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T10:41:58-08:00","id":845719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845524#post845524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the last 2 Principalities:<br /> <br /> Censers - smokescreens, gas clouds, airborne poisons<br /> Steeds - methods of travel, swimming, burrowing, flight, space travel (ala Byakhee)</div> </div> </div> </div>Censers, maybe. Not sure yet.<br /> <br /> Steeds... maybe not. Has to be an item and well, an entire power for all of the movement things just... doesn't feel right. Would be better off to put the various movement options in other things since they're all... different from each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845535#post845535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, could a Servant or even a basic 'minion' be based on a plant? Like some kind of spy-ivy or brain-tree that stores information or acts as a relay for telepathic communications and so on? Or would that fall under the Colony?<br /> <br /> In fact, I could imagine the latter being a kind of spymaster that's in charge of the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see why not. Although such things tend to be rather obvious due to their unearthly appearance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=845571#post845571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this at all how the Beneath is meant to look?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://ewkn.deviantart.com/art/Underworld-123444067\" target=\"_blank\">http://ewkn.deviantart.com/art/Underworld-123444067</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, except that in some places you can see the sky, space, and are on the ocean","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:50:06-08:00","id":845791,"title":"","content":"So... Colony Actions. Basic things every Colony can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Conscript. Convert any number of Colony Attributes into points for building a Swarm. You melt down assets, rapidly spawn disposable units using available materials, doing everything neccesary to destroy your enemies with numbers, though dedicated military assets are always better for this task. Military Attributes produce 2, others produce 1. This Swarm may then be commanded for the rest of the Story, dying off by the time of the next Story should it otherwise survive. Conscription once undergone cannot be undone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Construct.Order your industrial base to immediately begin work on a structure of some sort, either growing a specialized life form or piling building materials in short order. Alternatively, this may be used to produce items on a large scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spy. Order a covert band of spies, small things to shadow a given person or area, informing you of goings on in the location discretely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> now.... for Diplomacy and Science.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T07:34:30-08:00","id":846063,"title":"","content":"Question: How do Monarchs age? Do they age normally or at, like, half normal pace or at normal pace until a certain age at which they stop aging or are they just immortal-unless-killed