um.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:48:15-07:00","id":846564,"title":"","content":"Do you think it would be possible to have a form between Noble and human in which you can use very minor powers? Perhaps it could be faster to change into and out of, a halfway point if you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-13-2016, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:53:08-07:00","id":846613,"title":"","content":"Here're another few of ideas for the Knowledge aspect of the Colony:<br /> <br /> <b>Assimilate:</b> Spend a point of Knowledge and 6 hours analysing a particular species of living thing in order to decipher the genetic sequences allowing for a particular ability of theirs. This could be a polar bear's aptitude for surviving in cold temperatures, a fish's gills or a chameleon's independent eyes. This trait is then stored in the genetic memory of your Colony (write it down!) and can be used with the ability Adaptation. Only one trait can be copied per use of this ability. In order to Assimilate a life form at least one living example of it must be obtained. This subject is killed in the process. Genetic information of this sort may be traded among Monarchs and many Scribes spend a great deal of their time assimilating useful creatures.<br /> In game terms, each trait grants a particular ability which is endemic to that species of animal. A trait from a polar bear could grant a resistance to the Extreme Cold Tilt while a fish's gills could allow the creature to breathe underwater. In the case of traits which could mimic the abilities of a Principality, they cannot produce the effect but they can modify it. For example, the venom of a poison dart frog might make venoms provided by the Principality of Chalices act as neurotoxins or muscle relaxants or make them cause seizures.<br /> In some cases, the trait could merely affect cosmetic details such as coloration. In these cases the Storyteller might forgo the Knowledge cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Adaptation: </b>You dip into your reservoir of genetic information, extract a useful trait and 'install' it into one of your minion types. This costs a point of Knowledge. Each trait may only be used on creatures of a roughly similar anatomy and size to the creature from which the trait was assimilated. Each usage of this ability can install <u>one</u> such trait into <u>one </u>type of creature. 'Creature' also includes base buildings and, at the Storyteller's discretion, Monarchs. The trait need not be beneficial. These adaptations lasts the remainder of the story unless a <u>permanent dot</u> of Knowledge is spent to make it permanent. This permanency cannot be applied to Monarchs.<br /> <br /> <b>Evolution: </b>The Monarch adapts a trait in his genetic library, making it suitable for a different kind of creature. This entails the expenditure of 3 points of Knowledge and the destruction of the original genetic information, although the information may be reclaimed by Assimilating it again. For example, a chameleon's eyes could be made to work with a creature with a mammalian anatomy, a fish's gills on an avian or a polar bear's immunity to cold on a whale-sized creature. This ability cannot change the nature of the trait, only what it is compatible with. These modified traits may be traded just as readily as the unmodified ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-13-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:30:13-07:00","id":846649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=846499#post846499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">K. Thanks. I'll see that tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I saw the like on the post with the Covenants. I assume that's you Almarck.<br /> <br /> Or not. Who else is doing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-13-2016, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:40:49-07:00","id":846652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=846613#post846613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here're another few of ideas for the Knowledge aspect of the Colony:<br /> <br /> <b>Assimilate:</b> Spend a point of Knowledge and 6 hours analysing a particular species of living thing in order to decipher the genetic sequences allowing for a particular ability of theirs. This could be a polar bear's aptitude for surviving in cold temperatures, a fish's gills or a chameleon's independent eyes. This trait is then stored in the genetic memory of your Colony (write it down!) and can be used with the ability Adaptation. Only one trait can be copied per use of this ability. In order to Assimilate a life form at least one living example of it must be obtained. This subject is killed in the process. Genetic information of this sort may be traded among Monarchs and many Scribes spend a great deal of their time assimilating useful creatures.<br /> In game terms, each trait grants a particular ability which is endemic to that species of animal. A trait from a polar bear could grant a resistance to the Extreme Cold Tilt while a fish's gills could allow the creature to breathe underwater. In the case of traits which could mimic the abilities of a Principality, they cannot produce the effect but they can modify it. For example, the venom of a poison dart frog might make venoms provided by the Principality of Chalices act as neurotoxins or muscle relaxants or make them cause seizures.<br /> In some cases, the trait could merely affect cosmetic details such as coloration. In these cases the Storyteller might forgo the Knowledge cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Adaptation: </b>You dip into your reservoir of genetic information, extract a useful trait and 'install' it into one of your minion types. This costs a point of Knowledge. Each trait may only be used on creatures of a roughly similar anatomy and size to the creature from which the trait was assimilated. Each usage of this ability can install <u>one</u> such trait into <u>one </u>type of creature. 'Creature' also includes base buildings and, at the Storyteller's discretion, Monarchs. The trait need not be beneficial. These adaptations lasts the remainder of the story unless a <u>permanent dot</u> of Knowledge is spent to make it permanent. This permanency cannot be applied to Monarchs.<br /> <br /> <b>Evolution: </b>The Monarch adapts a trait in his genetic library, making it suitable for a different kind of creature. This entails the expenditure of 3 points of Knowledge and the destruction of the original genetic information, although the information may be reclaimed by Assimilating it again. For example, a chameleon's eyes could be made to work with a creature with a mammalian anatomy, a fish's gills on an avian or a polar bear's immunity to cold on a whale-sized creature. This ability cannot change the nature of the trait, only what it is compatible with. These modified traits may be traded just as readily as the unmodified ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assimilate looks pretty good. Makes it easy to have Monarchs in the local environments. Are these all &quot;default&quot; uses of Knowledge without gaining Principalities?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=846649#post846649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I saw the like on the post with the Covenants. I assume that's you Almarck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not me<br /> just started reading","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fo