 it; some responses:<br /> <br /> 1) Swarm ideas: Diplomacy or Espionage could get an info-gather task; the former finding public/mortal information, the latter finding secret/supernatural information. Military could have some kind of defending-an-area thing. Economic...act as temporary dots in Resources? Honestly, I'm having some trouble with these; Colony-management sounds less interesting to me than dealing with the fact that you've been infected with an alien microbe and now have weird powers and mutations and you're not sure how human you still are and you keep having these megalomaniac urges to take over the world.<br /> <br /> 2) Powers: I agree that Records and Clocks should be merged. Based on the structure so far, it looks like each has one power that they and only they get; the other two are secondary for another group. For Marshal secondary, I'd like to give them Crowns, but that means that Diplomat's new power needs to be unique to them. Maybe splitting Crowns into single-target and multi-target (along the lines of Dominate and Majesty; former is more powerful/stronger control, while latter affects more targets but is weaker)? With Marshals sharing the multi-target one. Scepters for multi-target, Crowns for single-target. Which leaves Stewards, who have to share with Marshals. Hmm. Well, armies need supplies; stewards grow supplies. What if there was a growth-power, something for generating a lot of small things, like food/bullets/etc? Call it Seeds. Distinct from Hammers, since Hammers is more about single big things? So then the list looks like this (italic marks unique powers)<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Marshal</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blades - melee</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Bows </i>- ranged</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Plates - armor, defense</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scepters - subversion, conversion</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seeds - resources, supplies</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scribe </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chalices - poisons and potions</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Quills - telepathy, peaceful action</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spheres </i>- scry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Staves - warp, space</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stewards </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Hammers </i>- create</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Plates - armor, defense</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Records - post/precognition, time</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seeds - resources, supplies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Staves - warp, space</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Diplomat </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Crowns</i> - command, control</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Quills - telepathy, peaceful action</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Records - post/precognition, time</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scepters - subversion, conversion</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Veils - shadows, flight</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shade</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blades - melee</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chalices - poisons, potions</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Cloaks </i>- illusions</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Veils - shadows, flight</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, the Colony aspect is to tie into the theme as a noble; the raw resources and power of your nation are yours to command. In the game play, it's mostly a manapool for large scale powers beyond just yourself. The &quot;Management&quot; will largely be the issue of wondering if using all of your colony's resources for one thing leaves you vulnerable to another Colony, a roleplay risk, if you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> But we've spent quite a deal on Colony haven't we?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways... I actually never decided on what hammers is for other than being a tool for creation. But I suppose for now, Seeds will work as something to do with playing with resources someway. Maybe early on it's about stealing resources.<br /> <br /> I also actually never really noticed that there was a theme of every Caste having exactly one unique power. This was mostly just a side effect of the way I split things up, but I think I'll keep it this way just for theming. Admitedly, maybe I need to switch Blades for Bows for the Shades to make Blades the unique, but eh... buh my assassins!<br /> <br /> I'll go make a quick write up for Plates, ugh Shields, soon. I keep forgetting which name to use!<br /> <br /> <br /> But while I do so.... I actually need to decide how I want to &quot;theme&quot; powers. Specifically, the dice mechanics they will use, the limitations, clauses for them happening. How to describe how they work? Do I go for more aggressive or passive abilities? <br /> <br /> There's obviously the nobility theme in the naming... but what about the secondary theme? Do I paint for more &quot;evil&quot;? Body horror? Eldritch subversion and corruption?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:24:07-07:00","id":847092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847084#post847084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Colony aspect is to tie into the theme as a noble; the raw resources and power of your nation are yours to command. In the game play, it's mostly a manapool for large scale powers beyond just yourself. The &quot;Management&quot; will largely be the issue of wondering if using all of your colony's resources for one thing leaves you vulnerable to another Colony, a roleplay risk, if you will.<br /> <br /> But we've spent quite a deal on Colony haven't we?<br /> <br /> Anyways... I actually never decided on what hammers is for other than being a tool for creation. But I suppose for now, Seeds will work as something to do with playing with resources someway. Maybe early on it's about stealing resources.<br /> <br /> I also actually never really noticed that there was a theme of every Caste having exactly one unique power. This was mostly just a side effect of the way I split things up, but I think I'll keep it this way just for theming. Admitedly, maybe I need to switch Blades for Bows for the Shades to make Blades the unique, but eh... buh my assassins!<br /> <br /> I'll go make a quick write up for Plates, ugh Shields, soon. I keep forgetting which name to use!<br /> <br /> But while I do so.... I actually need to decide how I want to &quot;theme&quot; powers. Specifically, the dice mechanics they will use, the limitations, clauses for them happening. How to describe how they work? Do I go for more aggressive or passive abilities?<br /> <br /> There's obviously the nobility theme in the naming... but what about the secondary theme? Do I paint for more &quot;evil&quot;? Body horror? Eldritch subversion and corruption?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think Bows are better for assassins (easier to be stealthy at long-range). And if Plates is easier to remember than Shields, go with that. Although, if this were to be <i>really</i> balanced, each Caste could have one unique power, then share one with each of the other Castes (where their roles overlap); they currently don't but now I want to try to make them fit.<br /> <br /> In terms of description, my vote is for a combo of body horror and subversion of self. There hasn't been a lot of flavor shared yet about how one feels when one becomes a Monarch, but there's an ongoing theme in both the CoD and in alien media of unnatural transformation: it can be embraced, but it's horrifying, and most fight against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:48:16-07:00","id":847100,"title":"","content":"So it looks like Diplomat currently has one power shared with each other Caste, and one of its own. The other four get paired: Marshal and Steward share two, Scribe and Shade share two. Marshal and Scribe lack any; Steward and Shade lack any.<br /> <br /> So lets see. Seeds was built for a Steward/Marshal share, that should stay how it is. Shields/Plates is the other one shared. Shields/Plates doesn't really lend itself to Scribes, but it's not terrible. I could also see Scribes getting Blades (because the pen is mighter than the sword, right?) and having Shields/Plates being unique (and giving Shades Bows). I like that a little better, but it could go either way.<br /> <br /> So now Stewards needs something to share with Shade, and Scribes needs to drop something. Scribes and Shades share Censers and Chalices. I could see either as a Steward power, EDIT: but since Censers has a historical basis with Scribes, Stewards can get Chalices (they were the ones who dealt with the food, after all). So, swaparoo, Stewards and Shades share Chalices, Scribes have Blades instead.<br /> <br /> New line-up:<br /> <br /> <b>Marshal</b><br /> Blades - melee<br /> Bows - ranged<br /> <i>Shields </i>- armor, defense<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> Seeds - resources, supplies<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe </b><br /> Blades - melee<br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> <i>Spheres </i>- scry<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Stewards </b><br /> Chalices - poisons and potions<br /> <i>Hammers </i>- create<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Seeds - resources, supplies<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Diplomat</b><br /> <i>Crowns </i>- command, control<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> Veils - shadows, flight<br /> <br /> <b>Shade</b><br /> Bows - ranged<br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Chalices - poisons, potions<br /> <i>Cloaks</i> - illusions<br /> Veils - shadows, flight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 03-14-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:04:52-07:00","id":847111,"title":"","content":"Will be doing stuff still.<br /> But can spare a moment<br /> <br /> the reason censers was on Scribes was because of the tie in with religion. Scribes were often also part of the priesthood in some cultures and the censers reflected the burning of intense as part of it. Of course it's fine to change that.<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason for shields on stewards was the it's the idea of fortresses, fortification and castle walls. Large bastions. Defending the settlement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:10:51-07:00","id":847116,"title":"","content":"Stewards were also those who controlled the food; they could get Chalices instead of Censers, and it would still make sense. Gonna update that one.<br /> <br /> I really don't want to give up Seeds, though I see the point about Shields. I'll noodle on something appropriate for Marshals/Scribes. Something about getting and sending information? Armies need to know what the enemy formation looks like, and need to inform other battalions, while Scribes are all about info. That sounds like Spheres, though. Could Scribes get some other unique info-gathering power? Rather than about the appearance of things, about the truth of things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:14:40-07:00","id":847119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847116#post847116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stewards were also those who controlled the food; they could get Chalices instead of Censers, and it would still make sense. Gonna update that one.<br /> <br /> I really don't want to give up Seeds, though I see the point about Shields. I'll noodle on something appropriate for Marshals/Scribes. Something about getting and sending information? Armies need to know what the enemy formation looks like, and need to inform other battalions, while Scribes are all about info. That sounds like Spheres, though. Could Scribes get some other unique info-gathering power? Rather than about the appearance of things, about the truth of things?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be a good thing to consider, but I don't think certain concepts would be picked up by the endless &quot;truth&quot; is nebulous after all.<br /> <br /> How about...<br /> There's also &quot;alchemy&quot; to consider, a theme learned men were known for in the old days. We're talking about a race that has mastery of chemistry and physics to sure a degree that they can warp physical constants and rules to do things. Break down and analysis of items, even magical components could be likely. Chalices covers the water aspect of that though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:24:29-07:00","id":847126,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Shields</b></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A Noble\u2019s body should be strong and made to endure any form of attack, her defenses able to withstand assault. Through hardened flesh, large ammounts of psychic shielding, and overall a willingness to live up to the name \u201cEndless\u201d, the Monarch persists.</i></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Monarch Active Powers Granted:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Impenetrable Bastion 0</b></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>All of the Monarch\u2019s natural weaponry is wreathed in Void energies, allowing them to ignore any number of protections granted to the object.</i></span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>No Action</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice pool: None</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch reduces any damage inflicted upon her body by her Shields rating.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Noble Form Upgrades:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>0</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stamina +1, Health +1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>00</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +1, Speed +1, Health +1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +1, Size +1, Speed +1, Health +2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>0000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +2, Size +1, Speed +2, Health +3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>00000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +2, Size +2, Speed +2, Health +4</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Admittedly pretty underwhelming compared to Resilience, but that's fine right now. I'll be going through and upgrading the earlier Principalities later on, giving them more toys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:54:54-07:00","id":847150,"title":"","content":"Are the Noble Form upgrades cumulative, or stacking? I.E. does the 2nd level's +1 Strength include the 1st levels, or is the Monarch at effective +2 Strength? Also, are the modifications to the derived traits in addition to the stats? I.E. if level 2 has +1 Stamina and +1 Health, is the Monarch's Health increasing by 1 or 2 total?<br /> <br /> I like alchemy as a power. Chalices can cover poisons/potions/things you drink, but for super-materials/transforming objects, alchemy works. Names, though, names are hard...Bezoars? Stones? Metals? Unguents? Also, having this means dropping either Seeds or Shields; since you've just finished Shields, it probably shouldn't be them :P<br /> <br /> Although...Scribes and Shades both want information about other people, Scribes because info, Shades because manipulations. If Diplomats didn't already have Quills, I'd say roll Chalices into new-alchemy (probably still called Chalices), have Quills be shared between Scribes and Shades, and...find something new for Diplomats/Scribes.<br /> <br /> Updated list:<br /> <br /> <b>Marshal</b><br /> <i>Blades </i>- melee<br /> Bows - ranged<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> Shields- armor, defense<br /> Spheres- scry<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe </b><br /> <i>Bezoars </i>- alchemy<br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> Spheres- scry<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Stewards </b><br /> Chalices - poisons and potions<br /> <i>Hammers </i>- create<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Seeds - resources, supplies<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Diplomat</b><br /> <i>Crowns </i>- command, control<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> Veils - shadows, flight<br /> <br /> <b>Shade</b><br /> Bows - ranged<br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Chalices - poisons, potions<br /> <i>Cloaks</i> - illusions<br /> Veils - shadows, flight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":".  Scribes, not Shades 03-14-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:09:27-07:00","id":847159,"title":"","content":"You just get what's at that level list and the increases all factor in their benefits automatically. I just put all the buffs in a single lines each level for quick reference so you don't need to math out what you get.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's go with Reagents?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Quills. I think it's more of a peaceful action telepathy, but I am not sure.<br /> <br /> Actually... I think Veils should drop the flight and be more about lying and shadows and illusions. They all work together so they should be the same. This could be the Shade unique power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cloaks can take up the flying aspect because what are wings but a type of cloak? but it might need other uses to be... more. I don't want to make a general movement power though... so what other things can it take that fit for Diplomats and Shades since it's trading places with veils","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-14-2016, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:20:00-07:00","id":847170,"title":"","content":"Just an idea here, for Diplomats one of the Caste boons should be the ability to make a Servant that can parasitically control its host, like the Goa'uld from Stargate.<br /> <br /> For the Geodics, would the big ones be at all similar to Ramiel, the 5th angel from Evangelion? (look up '5th angel battle evangelion' on youtube if you don't know that one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:21:04-07:00","id":847171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847119#post847119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be a good thing to consider, but I don't think certain concepts would be picked up by the endless &amp;quot;truth&amp;quot; is nebulous after all.<br /> <br /> How about...<br /> There's also &amp;quot;alchemy&amp;quot; to consider, a theme learned men were known for in the old days. We're talking about a race that has mastery of chemistry and physics to sure a degree that they can warp physical constants and rules to do things. Break down and analysis of items, even magical components could be likely. Chalices covers the water aspect of that though.</div> </div> </div> </div>For an 'alchemy' principality, how does Crucibles sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:24:27-07:00","id":847174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847126#post847126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Shields</b></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A Noble\u2019s body should be strong and made to endure any form of attack, her defenses able to withstand assault. Through hardened flesh, large ammounts of psychic shielding, and overall a willingness to live up to the name \u201cEndless\u201d, the Monarch persists.</i></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Monarch Active Powers Granted:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Impenetrable Bastion 0</b></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>All of the Monarch\u2019s natural weaponry is wreathed in Void energies, allowing them to ignore any number of protections granted to the object.</i></span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>No Action</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice pool: None</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch reduces any damage inflicted upon her body by her Shields rating.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Noble Form Upgrades:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>0</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stamina +1, Health +1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>00</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +1, Speed +1, Health +1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +1, Size +1, Speed +1, Health +2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>0000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +2, Size +1, Speed +2, Health +3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>00000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Stamina +2, Size +2, Speed +2, Health +4</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Admittedly pretty underwhelming compared to Resilience, but that's fine right now. I'll be going through and upgrading the earlier Principalities later on, giving them more toys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised that Shields doesn't add any armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:38:00-07:00","id":847185,"title":"","content":"Gotcha, makes sense. Although, for Shields, I might argue for increased Dexterity rather than Strength, since Dex is used in Defense.<br /> <br /> I'm all for Reagents. Is Chalices being dropped? Shades having poisons make sense, but Chalices may tread on Reagents' toes. If Chalices is dropped, either something new needs to be in Shades/Scribes, or, if Quills is moved to Shades, something new needs to be in Scribes/Diplomats. (The Power of Paperwork!)<br /> <br /> What do you mean by &quot;peaceful action telepathy&quot;? Message-sending, probably, and not mind-control, but what about mind-reading?<br /> <br /> Diplomats/Shades, lesse, there's looking like you belong, but that doesn't really gel with flight. Being speedy, maybe, but you said you didn't want general move-y. Being sneaky? Not making footfalls means people won't notice you as much, treading so lightly you're walking on air, muffling sounds with gravity reversers, that might work.<br /> <br /> Updated list (with Chalices):<br /> <br /> <b>Marshal</b><br /> <i>Blades </i>- melee<br /> Bows - ranged<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> Shields- armor, defense<br /> Spheres- scry<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe </b><br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> <i>Reagents </i>- alchemy<br /> Spheres- scry<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Stewards </b><br /> Chalices - poisons and potions<br /> <i>Hammers </i>- create<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Seeds - resources, supplies<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Diplomat</b><br /> Cloaks - flight, sneaking, gravity<br /> <i>Crowns </i>- command, control<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> <br /> <b>Shade</b><br /> Bows - ranged<br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Chalices - poisons, potions<br /> Cloaks - flight, sneaking, gravity<br /> <i>Veils </i>- shadows, illusions, lying<br /> <br /> Edit: didn't see ajf, I like Crucibles too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 03-14-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:44:35-07:00","id":847189,"title":"","content":"Here's a link to the ramiel video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=mdU8dyjgXU0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=mdU8dyjgXU0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=mdU8dyjgXU0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=mdU8dyjgXU0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:01:13-07:00","id":847198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847174#post847174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm surprised that Shields doesn't add any armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's active power automatically reduces damage taken by rating. It's better than armor since it stacks with additional armor and Armor piercing won't work against it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .... I also don't think Chalices will be dropped. <br /> <br /> I think the list is pretty much set now. Thanks to you. I will note that seeds might be dropped to give Shields to Stewards but that's the only change I can see being made.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for quills. It's about sending messages. Not control or mind reading. The whole point is to be either helping or others by delivering messages to others. They can choose to reply back in some case, but that's consenual.<br /> <br /> Maybe mind reading won't or shouldn't be within a Monarchs power set. Most hive minds don't do that. They just eat the brains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-14-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:03:08-07:00","id":847200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847198#post847198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. It's active power automatically reduces damage taken by rating. It's better than armor since it stacks with additional armor and Armor piercing won't work against it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .... I also don't think Chalices will be dropped. <br /> <br /> I think the list is pretty much set now. Thanks to you. I will note that seeds might be dropped to give Shields to Stewards but that's the only change I can see being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I was just surprised that you didn't use the armour rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:15:38-07:00","id":847206,"title":"","content":"I thought I dropped Seeds in my list, turns out I didn't. Meant to replace it with Shields. Seeds could be rolled into Hammers, really. Glad I could help!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the Quills explanation. I think that emotion/&quot;aura&quot;/surface thought reading should be an available power for Monarchs, though. Could be Quills, could be Crowns, could be Scepters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:21:27-07:00","id":847210,"title":"","content":"Or probably just part of Spheres for aura or surface thought reading. It'd be part of Lifesense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:24:52-07:00","id":847214,"title":"","content":"I'd put it under Spheres and make Spheres about general 'awareness' and perception. That way you could put sonar an vibration sensing under Spheres as well.<br /> <br /> What would burrowing be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:33:38-07:00","id":847219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847214#post847214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd put it under Spheres and make Spheres about general 'awareness' and perception. That way you could put sonar an vibration sensing under Spheres as well.<br /> <br /> What would burrowing be?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Universal rule I think. All zerg can burrow after all!<br /> Probably best to assume faster if you have better claws, but even if not....<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so while I tidy up the other Castes and get them some intros, I'm wondering about how to design the base Noble Form traits.<br /> <br /> Marshalls I had a good idea of because well... I had a good model that I was very familiar with that I wanted to use as a sample character.<br /> <img src=\"http://media.heroesnexus.com/attachments/0/964/anubarak_flat1920x.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> He's actually pretty much half the reason we've got the weird blend of Nobility since he was a Prince in his home setting...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But the others I don't have as much of a basis of so I don't know how to assign bonus stats or abilities for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Currently Mashal's get: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength, Dexterity, Stamina +1. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Natural Melee +1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Natural Armor 1/1</span></span><br /> <br /> But that may not be enough I wonder... Hm<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:58:39-07:00","id":847226,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Shade</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Mysteries are webs: A perfect snare and hiding spot, easy to get tangled, but can be unraveled</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A spider lying in wait above their invisible webs, a venomous scorpion that hides under stones and sands, a praying mantis that blends against trees hidden in plain sight, the assassin who holds his knife against his victims neck, threatening murder to gain a valuable piece of information\u2026.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Shade is meant to be a sneak, a master of subterfuge, stealth, and conspiracy. His task is simple, to learn of the hidden plots, the threats to the realm brewing underneath the notice of others, dispatching them himself if he needs to. A Shade\u2019s Colony resembles something like a network of spies and thieves, individual Drones spying upon one another as if paranoid about the threat of covert operatives...</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Though it should be no surprise that many Shades are loyal to their Courts, many Kings feel threatened about letting an individual who could secretly end their lives and not face repercussions so close to their highest Circles. Still, they serve a vital function, even if their actions escape the bounds of honor or border on breaking Law.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Above all else, Shades value pragmatism</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Noble Form Benefits </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Favored Principalities </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bows - ranged</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chalices - poisons, potions</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloaks - flight, sneaking, gravity</span>