:Arial\">Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chalices - poisons, potions</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloaks - flight, sneaking, gravity</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Veils </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- shadows, illusions, lying</span><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Any ideas for caste boons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:15:19-07:00","id":847235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847231#post847231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool. Any ideas for caste boons?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not yet. I'm going to need to figure out the state of Servants and Colonies more thuroughly before I do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T05:57:25-07:00","id":847638,"title":"","content":"What is the Beneath? As far as I can tell, it's essentially a kind of sub-universe, an infinite pocket dimension containing every environment that could exist.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're going to make it into something which contains space, sky, sea and so on, might it not make sense to give it a name less connected to underground. Perhaps the Hollow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:21:32-07:00","id":847668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847638#post847638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Beneath? As far as I can tell, it's essentially a kind of sub-universe, an infinite pocket dimension containing every environment that could exist.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're going to make it into something which contains space, sky, sea and so on, might it not make sense to give it a name less connected to underground. Perhaps the Hollow?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about simply Elsewhere? Hyperspace? Subspace? I'm sure there is also a medieval term that could apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T08:33:51-07:00","id":847704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847668#post847668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about simply Elsewhere? Hyperspace? Subspace? I'm sure there is also a medieval term that could apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say underworld if it wasn't already taken. I can imagine Scribes looking into the physics of the place and calling it everything from Hollow Earth to The Other Place to Paraspace and still not understanding it. It's just that it's going to be by necessity a large part a large part of the game due to the fact that a lot of the action is going to happen there given that it's difficult to have armies of bioengineered horrors and crystalline constructs clashing unnoticed in the normal world.<br /> <br /> Nice to see you again Vent0!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-15-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T09:03:54-07:00","id":847714,"title":"","content":"Um. Ace? Where'd you get bezoars? I thought we were going with Crucibles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T09:17:24-07:00","id":847722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847704#post847704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say underworld if it wasn't already taken. I can imagine Scribes looking into the physics of the place and calling it everything from Hollow Earth to The Other Place to Paraspace and still not understanding it. It's just that it's going to be by necessity a large part a large part of the game due to the fact that a lot of the action is going to happen there given that it's difficult to have armies of bioengineered horrors and crystalline constructs clashing unnoticed in the normal world.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about The Arena, then?<br /> <br /> And good point about it being the place where a lot of the Army-on-Army action can happen, to keep it out of the public view. The only risk then is taking the focus too much out of the &quot;normal&quot; world, to where Monarchs become insular little extra-dimensional fiefdoms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847704#post847704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice to see you again Vent0!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Yeah, I've been following this the whole time. Just haven't been able to contribute much because my own model deviated from the current trend near the beginning. So most of my inspiration/ideas are incompatible with what is being discussed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T09:26:35-07:00","id":847730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847722#post847722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about The Arena, then?<br /> <br /> And good point about it being the place where a lot of the Army-on-Army action can happen, to keep it out of the public view. The only risk then is taking the focus too much out of the &quot;normal&quot; world, to where Monarchs become insular little extra-dimensional fiefdoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the fear I had for the splat. It feels like it's becoming too disconnected with the normal world. What drives Monarchs to be with normal people? What benefits do Colonies provide in the 'real' world and what can one do in the 'real' world to benefit the Colony? What connects Monarchs to humanity or even to the other splats? I think that we'll have to really play up the fact that this metamorphosis is not consensual for most people and while it gives them great power, it's power that they are <u>forced</u> to exercise by the schemes and plots of the Kingmakers and the more powerful Monarchs. The more powerful Monarchs could get away with this disconnection but it should still be a problem. Touchstones will definitely be quite important, I think, if we want to maintain the human element.<br /> <br /> The less powerful Monarchs (i.e. the newbie players) would probably have to deal with heavy taxes and required service to the higher-ups to drive the war machine against the Geodics and even other Courts. I would imagine that a lot of the inter-monarch conflict is going to be political though, mostly about gaining influence so that you have more leeway to do the things that you want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847722#post847722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Yeah, I've been following this the whole time. Just haven't been able to contribute much because my own model deviated from the current trend near the beginning. So most of my inspiration/ideas are incompatible with what is being discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you think it was going to be like originally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-15-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T09:30:05-07:00","id":847733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847714#post847714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um. Ace? Where'd you get bezoars? I thought we were going with Crucibles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Placeholder name I came up with; I don't know if Almarck wants to go with Crucibles or Reagents. I thought the latest list had Reagents...no, it does, it was just the earlier one that had Bezoars. IDK, I'll repost the list with what I think are the current names and placements (Reagents as alchemy, no Seeds).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847722#post847722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Yeah, I've been following this the whole time. Just haven't been able to contribute much because my own model deviated from the current trend near the beginning. So most of my inspiration/ideas are incompatible with what is being discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>*fistbump* I hear that. I'm curious as to where your ideas diverged.<br /> <br /> EDIT: why do I keep double-posting with ajf, this is ridiculous<br /> <br /> <b>Marshal</b><br /> <i>Blades </i>- melee<br /> Bows - ranged<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> Shields- armor, defense<br /> Spheres- scry<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe </b><br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> <i>Reagents </i>- alchemy<br /> Spheres- scry<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Stewards </b><br /> Chalices - poisons and potions<br /> <i>Hammers </i>- create<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Shields- armor, defense<br /> Staves - warp, space<br /> <br /> <b>Diplomat</b><br /> Cloaks - flight, sneaking, gravity<br /> <i>Crowns </i>- command, control<br /> Quills - telepathy, peaceful action<br /> Records - post/precognition, time<br /> Scepters - subversion, conversion<br /> <br /> <b>Shade</b><br /> Bows - ranged<br /> Censers - smokescreen, gasses, incense<br /> Chalices - poisons, potions<br /> Cloaks - flight, sneaking, gravity<br /> <i>Veils </i>- shadows, illusions, lying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T09:31:45-07:00","id":847736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847722#post847722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about The Arena, then?<br /> <br /> And good point about it being the place where a lot of the Army-on-Army action can happen, to keep it out of the public view. The only risk then is taking the focus too much out of the &quot;normal&quot; world, to where Monarchs become insular little extra-dimensional fiefdoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I got a few ideas to solve this. Most notably, most monarchs being rather... hesitant with working with their Colonies at the begining. The only reason many Monarchs manage them at all is simply a case of being required to by both by those above them.... and because if they don't the Colony keeps pestering them or does things on its own.<br /> Later on, this hesitation goes away, but again, most supernats with other worlds get less interested in the mundane world without duties going there as they get beefier.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that many Monarchs will use the Colony to solve earthly ends, such as ensuring a safe family.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The other thing is that the Beneath may not have several important resources the Colony needs. Mostly, food, oxygen, and sunlight. Biodiversity. Also perhaps the battles are about taking things in the Above world, such as surface bound genevaults.<br /> <br /> There's perhaps landmarks or important objects hidden in plain veiw...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks. Yeah, I've been following this the whole time. Just haven't been able to contribute much because my own model deviated from the current trend near the beginning. So most of my inspiration/ideas are incompatible with what is being discussed. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to hear that. Dreaming and I were discussing things in private and I suppose left you in the dust<br /> <br /> I will note that I've had to discard a few things from the older thread. He and I haven't spoken much as of late, so I've had to more or less just spew ideas out from my head as they come to me. This has been my outlet to compare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-15-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T10:05:19-07:00","id":847749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847730#post847730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you think it was going to be like originally?</div> </div> </div> </div>Back when it was still being discussed as inspired by Tyranids, Zerg, et al, I was thinking of &quot;assimilating&quot; mechanics from most of the other lines, and the overall Hive-mind being an emergent intelligence that was mostly background, except when it (unfortunately) wasn't. Integrity-equivalent was a little different and Power Stat was based around the Hive/Colony similar to Beast's Lair. I was still debating whether a Fuel stat was needed or to just make expanded Willpower the thing (representing the expanded psychic abilities). Willpower, though &quot;common&quot; is prone to fairly extreme results when you uncouple it from the 1-a-turn limit.<br /> <br /> I'll see how much I can reverse engineer my notes into this model. I was largely stuck at the build-a-creature part. Too many ideas on how to handle things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847736#post847736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to hear that. Dreaming and I were discussing things in private and I suppose left you in the dust<br /> <br /> I will note that I've had to discard a few things from the older thread. He and I haven't spoken much as of late, so I've had to more or less just spew ideas out from my head as they come to me. This has been my outlet to compare.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. You've done leaps and bounds on the background and setting material. Way more developed than my placeholders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T10:20:09-07:00","id":847756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847749#post847749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll see how much I can reverse engineer my notes into this model. I was largely stuck at the build-a-creature part. Too many ideas on how to handle things.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm likely to discard &quot;Build-a-creature&quot; as much as I don't want to. Now I think that if you have the Blueprints unlocked from your Principalities, you can build a Servant at your Colony by paying the appropriate cost. Each one will probably have upgrades on their template that require other or higher Principalities than the base by simply paying for it. It won't be an interconnected web of gear and items and servants who can take them<br /> <br /> Such as say &quot;Foreman&quot; having options to unlock wings with the right Cloaks or better guns with Bows","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T11:22:14-07:00","id":847772,"title":"","content":"... so on thinking about Hunter conspiracies to challenge a monarch, how about one that is based entirely on using steam punk robotics ?<br /> <br /> Various units of different types. Mostly all small deployables. But they can use Mechs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T11:36:40-07:00","id":847776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847756#post847756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm likely to discard &quot;Build-a-creature&quot; as much as I don't want to. Now I think that if you have the Blueprints unlocked from your Principalities, you can build a Servant at your Colony by paying the appropriate cost. Each one will probably have upgrades on their template that require other or higher Principalities than the base by simply paying for it. It won't be an interconnected web of gear and items and servants who can take them<br /> <br /> Such as say &quot;Foreman&quot; having options to unlock wings with the right Cloaks or better guns with Bows</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about how we could maybe uncouple the blueprints from the Principalities and make them an independent thing that you would buy with EXP. If we made the templates very general and generic (e.g. heavy transport, scout, footsoldier etc) and then made it so that you could 'upgrade' them with abilities from Principalities (want a swarm of flying footsoldiers? Footsoldier + Cloaks, want your scouts to be able to blink, Scout + Staves). This is excluding the caste-specific templates like the Marshal's Titan Beast. They could still be upgraded though. What do you think? Or has this already been considered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T12:45:53-07:00","id":847800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847772#post847772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... so on thinking about Hunter conspiracies to challenge a monarch, how about one that is based entirely on using steam punk robotics ?<br /> <br /> Various units of different types. Mostly all small deployables. But they can use Mechs</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about Steam-punk robotics. How does steam-punk fit into things?<br /> <br /> What about an international task force. Like Valkyrie, but not USA based. Basically X-COM. We can debate how historically rooted they are, and what sinister influence they may or may not have over the arms trade and military escalation, if you want.<br /> <br /> For another, what about something leveraging some <i>really</i> old group that happened upon Endless abilities, and use them to stop the Endless? Co-opted mutations, psychic awakening techniques, etc. Or they just want to learn about the Endless. Cheiron-Group style.<br /> <br /> Or one that has help from one of the other ephemeral powers (spirits or angels, most likely, but ghost might be possible too), who help out the Conspiracy because they don't want the Endless on &quot;their&quot; turf. Maybe even use the Wardens from Immortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-15-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T12:51:39-07:00","id":847802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847776#post847776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about how we could maybe uncouple the blueprints from the Principalities and make them an independent thing that you would buy with EXP. If we made the templates very general and generic (e.g. heavy transport, scout, footsoldier etc) and then made it so that you could 'upgrade' them with abilities from Principalities (want a swarm of flying footsoldiers? Footsoldier + Cloaks, want your scouts to be able to blink, Scout + Staves). This is excluding the caste-specific templates like the Marshal's Titan Beast. They could still be upgraded though. What do you think? Or has this already been considered?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, right now it's just a matter of if you have the Preresiquites met or not. Simpler that way I feel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847800#post847800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure about Steam-punk robotics. How does steam-punk fit into things?<br /> <br /> What about an international task force. Like Valkyrie, but not USA based. Basically X-COM. We can debate how historically rooted they are, and what sinister influence they may or may not have over the arms trade and military escalation, if you want.<br /> <br /> For another, what about something leveraging some <i>really</i> old group that happened upon Endless abilities, and use them to stop the Endless? Co-opted mutations, psychic awakening techniques, etc. Or they just want to learn about the Endless. Cheiron-Group style.<br /> <br /> Or one that has help from one of the other ephemeral powers (spirits or angels, most likely, but ghost might be possible too), who help out the Conspiracy because they don't want the Endless on &quot;their&quot; turf. Maybe even use the Wardens from Immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an astetic thing from a seperate idea thread that works onto this. And mostly the thought is that this is a group that existed independant of the Endless before they came.<br /> <br /> The thing that Dreaming and I worked out is that the Endless are actually fairly recent as far as Supernaturals go, a contrast to the other races that have been on Earth since the dawn of time. So recent in fact that the earliest &quot;prototype&quot; Monarchs were involved in the World Wars.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking that whatever group we needed was to use either armies of its own... or really big units to crush Endless forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T12:52:09-07:00","id":847803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847800#post847800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure about Steam-punk robotics. How does steam-punk fit into things?<br /> <br /> What about an international task force. Like Valkyrie, but not USA based. Basically X-COM. We can debate how historically rooted they are, and what sinister influence they may or may not have over the arms trade and military escalation, if you want.<br /> <br /> For another, what about something leveraging some <i>really</i> old group that happened upon Endless abilities, and use them to stop the Endless? Co-opted mutations, psychic awakening techniques, etc. Or they just want to learn about the Endless. Cheiron-Group style.<br /> <br /> Or one that has help from one of the other ephemeral powers (spirits or angels, most likely, but ghost might be possible too), who help out the Conspiracy because they don't want the Endless on &amp;quot;their&amp;quot; turf. Maybe even use the Wardens from Immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of an XCOM conspiracy, especially if it had two 'branches', one more military and one more cheiron group. I could imagine them employing (or creating) lots of Hybrids to act as counters to the Monarchs and their stuff. I could imagine something like the Engels from CthulhuTech to act as a counter to the ultralisk-equivalents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T12:55:45-07:00","id":847806,"title":"","content":"Made some edits to the above.<br /> <br /> ... Also, I already did that, sort of...<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/673903-conspiracy-ronin-enterprizes\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...in-enterprizes</a><br /> <br /> Using biotech powered armor.<br /> <br /> But the thing is... I came to realize it's not enough to face the extreme numerical disadvantages of single actor infantry units.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And honestly, Chiron does biotech already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-15-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:08:08-07:00","id":847811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847806#post847806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Made some edits to the above.<br /> <br /> ... Also, I already did that, sort of...<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/673903-conspiracy-ronin-enterprizes\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...in-enterprizes</a><br /> <br /> Using biotech powered armor.<br /> <br /> But the thing is... I came to realize it's not enough to face the extreme numerical disadvantages of single actor infantry units.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And honestly, Chiron does biotech already.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what about ditching the Bio-Tech and going straight Tech? Or Cyber-Tech? Because MEC-Troopers were awesome. A certain level of firepower can help even the numbers against the Endless hordes. And weird physics-warping bug/lizard/man-bear-pigs makes for great R&amp;D inspiration. Such a group might have existed already, but didn't really have it's &quot;cause&quot; (or big enough threat to secure funding) until the Endless came along.<br /> <br /> Less, For (medical) Science! and more Militant Imperialism?<br /> <hr /><br /> Also on the topic of the arrival of the Endless giving a Conspiracy purpose, anyone have any ideas on an ancient Conspiracy that actually destroyed their foes, then slowly faded into irrelevancy, before these new invaders gave them reason to take up the Vigil again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-15-2016, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:15:54-07:00","id":847819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847811#post847811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what about ditching the Bio-Tech and going straight Tech? Or Cyber-Tech? Because MEC-Troopers were awesome. A certain level of firepower can help even the numbers against the Endless hordes. And weird physics-warping bug/lizard/man-bear-pigs makes for great R&amp;D inspiration. Such a group might have existed already, but didn't really have it's &quot;cause&quot; (or big enough threat to secure funding) until the Endless came along.<br /> <br /> Less, For (medical) Science! and more Militant Imperialism?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps. It'd be a 