> Perhaps. It'd be a better flavor than Biotech and weird science at least. MEC troopers entirely then? Cyborgs that use robots. I will note that the Mech rules that I made also allow for MEC Trooper like units.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a combination of the MECs for shock troops and ultralisk counters and stuff like the nanosuit troopers for the 'rank and file' as it were?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:21:44-07:00","id":847826,"title":"","content":"Why not just use the Cheiron Group as-is? Or a faction of them that focuses on Monarchs, maybe. Network Zero fits well with Monarchs, as does VALKYRIE; one of the Lucifuge's multiple-choice pasts could be as children of Monarchs. Not every splat gets/needs a dedicated Hunter-group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:30:25-07:00","id":847829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847826#post847826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just use the Cheiron Group as-is? Or a faction of them that focuses on Monarchs, maybe. Network Zero fits well with Monarchs, as does VALKYRIE; one of the Lucifuge's multiple-choice pasts could be as children of Monarchs. Not every splat gets/needs a dedicated Hunter-group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But we could have MECs!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:50:02-07:00","id":847840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847819#post847819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps. It'd be a better flavor than Biotech and weird science at least. MEC troopers entirely then? Cyborgs that use robots. I will note that the Mech rules that I made also allow for MEC Trooper like units.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Supreme Commander MCU-like Cyborg MEC Troopers? And you have rules already? All the better.<br /> <br /> &quot;The war took my legs, but [Hunter Conspiracy Placeholder] gave me new ones that never tire.&quot;<br /> &quot;Time stole my squad, but [HCP] has given me new soldiers that never age.&quot;<br /> &quot;Peace removed my purpose, but [HCP] has given me a new one that is Endless.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-15-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:57:14-07:00","id":847848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847826#post847826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just use the Cheiron Group as-is? Or a faction of them that focuses on Monarchs, maybe. Network Zero fits well with Monarchs, as does VALKYRIE; one of the Lucifuge's multiple-choice pasts could be as children of Monarchs. Not every splat gets/needs a dedicated Hunter-group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine fighting Monarchs when they get the ball rolling to be... very different from fighting other Splats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847840#post847840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Supreme Commander MCU-like Cyborg MEC Troopers? And you have rules already? All the better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not only that, but rules up to date with current edition. Well, in the sense you can pilot a Mech no problem. Not sure about commanding robot legions with mass fabricators.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...hs-walkers-ect</a><br /> <br /> Well, the Steam punk Astetic was mostly to justify that these people come from an older era and are really much of a remnant of something else. Assuming we kept the theme of them being an old group that just slinked and nearly died in the shadows, I'm thinking maybe they did war against the Geodics before, and for a while things went dormant. Then the Monarchs arrived, their old enemy woke up and well... you get the idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> But other astetics might include rival alien tech from a race that no longer remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T14:15:11-07:00","id":847856,"title":"","content":"Proposal: Additional justifications for only fielding the &quot;Big Guns&quot; in the Endless's Other-Space might be that some of the parts exploit quirks in the weird physics there. It's junk in &quot;Real-Space&quot;, though that hasn't stopped them from using some of the principles to be a contributor to Furbys and modern robotics development. <hr /><br /> If the &quot;almost disappeared&quot; history is used for the Tech group, I'd vote for a rich, detailed history of oppression, quiet resistance, and then co-opting the tools of their enemy to bring about their destruction... only for none of that to matter, practically, to the modern game. Old Glory, in other words.","signature":