urces. So, there might indeed by some older Steam-punk-esque designs, from when core components burnt out around the Industrial Revolution, and then were replaced with the best equivalents from the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:08:08-07:00","id":847976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847971#post847971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As far as aesthetic? Anything could work. If they did fight the Geodics, how about a mix of that and modern to slightly out-dated tech? I'm thinking the core &quot;super&quot; components use legacy Geodic-based tech or replicas, with anything that can be replaced by the technology of the day, phased into it to reduce the reliance upon such (previously) irreplaceable resources. So, there might indeed by some older Steam-punk-esque designs, from when core components burnt out around the Industrial Revolution, and then were replaced with the best equivalents from the day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Geodic tech might well be geodic bodies.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this starts sounding cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Modern Mechs probably resemble ipods or maybe incorperate some designs ... or parts stolen from the Monarchs as part off experiments.<br /> <br /> Early, early mechs probably are almost crystaline themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-15-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T03:35:35-07:00","id":848064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847976#post847976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geodic tech might well be geodic bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you know what they say about omelets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847976#post847976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early, early mechs probably are almost crystaline themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Though, if the &quot;burns out&quot; story is used, it might be better to say most <i>were</i>. There might be some truly ancient, unused crystalline mech dating from back then, but most, I think, would have seen use and needed parts replaced. Heh, this even gives the justification for the weird &quot;older is better&quot; trope that seems to be common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:00:53-07:00","id":848104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848064#post848064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you know what they say about omelettes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps geodic 'corpses' could be the fuel for the energy cores of the mechs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:39:26-07:00","id":848121,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Another idea if &quot;Geodic Technology&quot; doesn't make sense: there was <i>another</i> alien group that conscripted/enslaved HCP's ancestors to fight against the Geodics, giving them the advanced technological weapons and tools to do so. HCP defeated the Geodics (but obviously didn't eliminate them), then turned upon the aliens who used them as shock troops and destroyed <i>them</i>. Geodic parts still might be key ingredients (which would certainly help explain why the Geodics and Other-Aliens were in conflict).<br /> <br /> &lt;shrug&gt; Depends on if you want to add yet another alien group to the mix, just to plug a small logic hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:50:56-07:00","id":848276,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Well, we can always assume that there might have been Geodic technologies that were discovered long before the Geodics themselves made a scene.<br /> Also, there's the assumption that early geodics were &quot;raised&quot; in proportion of their power, with early, weak Phase 1's being too few in number to beat back the Guardians effectively. The Current Generation is Phase 2's<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lore Time:<br /> <br /> The Endless are not the first race to land upon our Earth. There are a multitude of creatures that traveled the stars and set foot upon our lands. The Endless and their Monarchs are but the latest in a long line of travelers, but there is without a doubt a first.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long ago, in a distant time lost to memory, when the land was still being formed when even the ancient Celestines we all know were just newborns, the earth was struck visited by a meteor, more a seed\u2026 a ship that lodged itself all the way down to the Earth\u2019s core. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Its inhabitants were unharmed by the collusion, the heat failing to melt the perfect exterior of their craft, but remained dormant for a timeless aeon. It was only when humankind\u2019s first forays into electronics, into radiowave that this race woke from their slumber, the electromagnetic waves stirring them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ship broke itself free from the core, rising until it was just underneath the crush. There it released its payload: a race totally unlike anything in either Terran understanding, the Xan-Qui, the Geodics.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Geodics are named such for their appearance, crystalline and rigid forms that look like ordinary earth, but despite their appearances they are not inert, floating by some electromagnetic means. They employ technology of a sort, far more advanced than anything we own, controlling these devices through electromagnetic manipulation. This same electronic field generates natural forcefields and beam weaponry comparable to firearms or in some cases artillary cannons. A \u201csingle\u201d geodic is more akin to a swarm of crystals gathered around a primary node, a central intelligence that governs the rest. The size of a Geodic varies, but increased size means increased power in every measurable aspect.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately for us, they are not a race that seems at all willing to make friends. Communication is impossible without any form of specialized machinery and the only translated messages that have been sent to humankind have all been requests of unconditional surrender. We are at a loss as to understand why.<br /> <br /> It was only due to the combine ingenuity of a small army, the Eternal Guardians, that humanity still lives today, destroying the Geodics with their own stolen technology.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:02:21-07:00","id":848314,"title":"","content":"If they only awoke due to Radio-waves, that puts the Guardians origin as quite recent. Also, how would the HCP acquire Geodic tech, being that far behind the curve? I doubt even phase 1s just left human usable weapons lying around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:15:27-07:00","id":848324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848314#post848314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they only awoke due to Radio-waves, that puts the Guardians origin as quite recent. Also, how would the HCP acquire Geodic tech, being that far behind the curve? I doubt even phase 1s just left human usable weapons lying around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They probably found samples elsewhere. The seedship tackled the planet, likely atleast fragmenting off some chunks. Maybe there's been pieces that were fragmented off and found elsewhere. Meaning that they had access to alien tech before meeting the aliens themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:20:00-07:00","id":848327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848314#post848314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they only awoke due to Radio-waves, that puts the Guardians origin as quite recent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, and this is just a science grump on my part, the universe is awash with electromagnetic radiation, including radio waves. Why would the Geodics only awaken once humans specifically began to mess around with radios? If you wanted the Geodics and Eternal Guardins to be more recent, perhaps the Tunguska Event in 1908 was their arrival on Earth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:40:59-07:00","id":848346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848327#post848327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, and this is just a science grump on my part, the universe is awash with electromagnetic radiation, including radio waves. Why would the Geodics only awaken once humans specifically began to mess around with radios? If you wanted the Geodics and Eternal Guardins to be more recent, perhaps the Tunguska Event in 1908 was their arrival on Earth?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe. I'm actually spit balling ideas currently.<br /> <br /> Granted, radio was the earliest time I could think of that I could justify &quot;mech&quot; technology with a growing tech base due to global industrialization. Probably better time peroids to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:01:27-07:00","id":848365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848346#post848346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe. I'm actually spit balling ideas currently.<br /> <br /> Granted, radio was the earliest time I could think of that I could justify &quot;mech&quot; technology with a growing tech base due to global industrialization. Probably better time peroids to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, depending upon the Geodic's goals and methods, they could have awoken the first wave at any time in history. If you want to get crazy old, you could tie them into the controversial population bottleneck 70K years ago.<br /> <br /> Do we know more about Geodic methods and/or goals? Expansion, imperialism, experimentation, etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:15:35-07:00","id":848378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848365#post848365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know more about Geodic methods and/or goals? Expansion, imperialism, experimentation, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Omnicidal hostility and aggressive xenoforming are what I imagine are their shticks.<br /> <br /> I imagine Tiberium like corruption is one of their gimmicks, but no where near as fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-16-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:45:51-07:00","id":848389,"title":"","content":"If they are omnicidal and xeno-formers, why didn't they start already? Planetary impact wasn't in the plan? Why'd it take so long to wake up? Considering the tech gap, I doubt humans could have ever made it useful without help.<br /> <br /> Given a force that explicitly made <i>use</i> of humans, the tech part is easy to explain - the aliens deliberately made the devices and trained the humans in their use (to accomplish the alien's purposes). That the same tools got turned on them would be an oversight.<br /> <br /> Spinning ideas... what if Earth possessed something the Geodics didn't anticipate (their Bane, in other words). <i>That</i> set the Xenoforming schedule back. A small task force would occasionally awaken and see what could be done about it, but their resources were limited. It was only upon one of their periodic awakenings and maintenance checks that they discovered semi-intelligent tool using hominds. Hatching the plan of conscripting them as slave labor, they developed tools for them to complete the necessary works to restore the main ship (and exterminate the humans once their usefulness has expired). After some time, with repairs nearing completion, their human tools turned on them and wiped out the repair crew before they could activate the ship (thus, betraying them <i>first</i>). Cue the nascent Guardians resting on their laurels and ushing in their brief golden age... before their tools started to break down. Times passes and they slowly fade into irrelevance. Then the event (arrival of the Endless, constant local source radio-waves, automated repairs finally completing, etc.) awakens the rest of the Geodic ship. Who promptly detect the Endless as the greater threat and move to wage war with them. The strange hominds using their tools can wait to be exterminated in due time.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? It kinda paints the Geodics as the Bigger Bad, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-16-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:44:27-07:00","id":848423,"title":"","content":"Geodics kind of are the Bigger Bad though. The Endless are beings of godlike psionic power but for the most part they can't come here. The Geodics can. It's like the difference between the Idigam still stuck on the Moon and the ones that are here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:51:21-07:00","id":848426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848389#post848389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are omnicidal and xeno-formers, why didn't they start already? Planetary impact wasn't in the plan? Why'd it take so long to wake up? Considering the tech gap, I doubt humans could have ever made it useful without help.<br /> <br /> Given a force that explicitly made <i>use</i> of humans, the tech part is easy to explain - the aliens deliberately made the devices and trained the humans in their use (to accomplish the alien's purposes). That the same tools got turned on them would be an oversight.<br /> <br /> Spinning ideas... what if Earth possessed something the Geodics didn't anticipate (their Bane, in other words). <i>That</i> set the Xenoforming schedule back. A small task force would occasionally awaken and see what could be done about it, but their resources were limited. It was only upon one of their periodic awakenings and maintenance checks that they discovered semi-intelligent tool using hominds. Hatching the plan of conscripting them as slave labor, they developed tools for them to complete the necessary works to restore the main ship (and exterminate the humans once their usefulness has expired). After some time, with repairs nearing completion, their human tools turned on them and wiped out the repair crew before they could activate the ship (thus, betraying them <i>first</i>). Cue the nascent Guardians resting on their laurels and ushing in their brief golden age... before their tools started to break down. Times passes and they slowly fade into irrelevance. Then the event (arrival of the Endless, constant local source radio-waves, automated repairs finally completing, etc.) awakens the rest of the Geodic ship. Who promptly detect the Endless as the greater threat and move to wage war with them. The strange hominds using their tools can wait to be exterminated in due time.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? It kinda paints the Geodics as the Bigger Bad, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Local big bad of course. Well, relative to the planet.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, let's take what you said, add some tidbits. The seed ship was fragmented, several fragments destroyed or unable to wake up, due to damaged stasis chambers. Oppurtunistic homids dug into these damaged fragments, found and stole technology. This security breach triggered several Geodics to awaken, causing the first war. Beneath formed as a result of this expansion and warfare. Initial forces defeated by humans using stolen reverse engineered technology. Mech Tech is actually based off of Geodic battlesuits. Decline of Guardians.<br /> <br /> Second Wave Geodics awaken later on, after Endless arrival and subsequent coopting of Beneath and further expansions of that realm alerted the previously dormant Geodics of what had transpired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T18:29:53-07:00","id":848525,"title":"","content":"Are the Geodics humanoid, then? &lt;shrug&gt; Still not seeing how humans would be able to use-figure out the tech if they found it. What about a mix? Geodics trained some, but other humans found/looted other ship/shards, and that was how they were able to break free?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T18:33:12-07:00","id":848526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848525#post848525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Geodics humanoid, then? &lt;shrug&gt; Still not seeing how humans would be able to use-figure out the tech if they found it. What about a mix? Geodics trained some, but other humans found/looted other ship/shards, and that was how they were able to break free?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. I don't think they were conventional in their biology.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking however that the technology that had was psionic in nature, maybe even empathic This is how humans were able to figure it out despite being leagues below the needed levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T00:02:32-07:00","id":848656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848526#post848526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No. I don't think they were conventional in their biology.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking however that the technology that had was psionic in nature, maybe even empathic This is how humans were able to figure it out despite being leagues below the needed levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had kind of imagined them as effectively tiberium with a kind of collective consciousness. When they are threatened, parts of the consciousness take control of individual groups of crystals, separate themselves from the main consciousness and uses the little crystalline bodies as 'weapons platforms'. Perhaps the crystals themselves could be a form of 'solidified energy', so the more laser beams that they shoot, the smaller they get. It would also make it possible for them to be used as a fuel source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:25:54-07:00","id":848749,"title":"","content":"Geodisc idea is cool, but how did this history happen with most of humans unaware of it? Because this is the world of darkness, people are willfully ignorant, but there's not blatant battles against the supernatural, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:41:47-07:00","id":848755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848749#post848749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geodisc idea is cool, but how did this history happen with most of humans unaware of it? Because this is the world of darkness, people are willfully ignorant, but there's not blatant battles against the supernatural, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the battles happened in the Beneath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:11:49-07:00","id":848764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848755#post848755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the battles happened in the Beneath?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but humans won (presumably). So they go back to the real world and...forget? Hide? Don't abuse all these wonderful toys they have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:19:12-07:00","id":848767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848526#post848526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No. I don't think they were conventional in their biology.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking however that the technology that had was psionic in nature, maybe even empathic This is how humans were able to figure it out despite being leagues below the needed levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. If it is psychic/empathic, that might work.<br /> <br /> Idea Spinning: What if the Geodic tech they found had tutorial and integration programs (even minor AIs) for assisting &quot;new&quot; or &quot;young&quot; Geodics use them? The devices the HCP forebears found merely assumed that they where kids and showed them the ropes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848764#post848764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but humans won (presumably). So they go back to the real world and...forget? Hide? Don't abuse all these wonderful toys they have?</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably did, but they didn't have the ability to maintain their toys. So, brief time as god-kings in their immediate area, then realizing that the good times are limited.<br /> <br /> It's only been lately, with both advanced industry and a new compatible supernatural power source, that they can approach their old heights.<br /> <br /> If you gave a functional modern computer to the Romans, for instance, they'd have awesome capabilities... until hard-drives started to die and they can't replace them. A broken fan or cooling system might be replaced with something equivalent, but what would they be able to do about stuff they barely (if at all) understand, let alone have the infrastructure for? For another example, knowing how to build nuclear plants does you no good if you can't actually get and refine the fuel rods.<br /> <hr /><br /> While this is fun, we've had a few pages of discussion on what is essentially a Hunter Antagonist group, and thus a minor part of the setting. Should we move this into a separate thread to maintain focus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-17-2016, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:39:17-07:00","id":848842,"title":"","content":"Here's a question: What is the social structure of the Monarchs? I assume that it's fairly feudal, with the more powerful towards the top of the pyramid and with the Kingmakers at the top.<br /> <br /> Another important question is this: What does it feel like to be a Monarch?<br /> <br /> Can you feel all the animalistic minds of your colony boiling away somewhere below your brainstem, reaching out into your mind with tendrils of instinct just as you bind them with the lash of your command? Do you hear them cry out when they die? Do you die with each of them as they do, over and over again? Do you feel the crunch of your foes' bones beneath their teeth? The blood running down their throat? What does it feel like to be a king of monsters and beasts, and to be only a step away from becoming a monster and a beast yourself?<br /> <br /> I think that something that would be interesting to play with would be the way that Monarchs are never alone. They've always got their Colony demanding their attention, at any time another Monarch could drop in telepathically. There's no privacy in a collective, no room for the I. There is only the us. The Endless are a race of us while humanity is a race of I. That difference could be played with I think. Not quite duality like Geist but rather collectivism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-17-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:14:10-07:00","id":848854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848764#post848764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but humans won (presumably). So they go back to the real world and...forget? Hide? Don't abuse all these wonderful toys they have?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was only a small but innovative faction of humans, like a Conspiracy. I have yet to even establish the location of these events though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848767#post848767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. If it is psychic/empathic, that might work.<br /> <br /> Idea Spinning: What if the Geodic tech they found had tutorial and integration programs (even minor AIs) for assisting &quot;new&quot; or &quot;young&quot; Geodics use them? The devices the HCP forebears found merely assumed that they where kids and showed them the ropes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That could work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They probably did, but they didn't have the ability to maintain their toys. So, brief time as god-kings in their immediate area, then realizing that the good times are limited.<br /> <br /> It's only been lately, with both advanced industry and a new compatible supernatural power source, that they can approach their old heights.<br /> <br /> If you gave a functional modern computer to the Romans, for instance, they'd have awesome capabilities... until hard-drives started to die and they can't replace them. A broken fan or cooling system might be replaced with something equivalent, but what would they be able to do about stuff they barely (if at all) understand, let alone have the infrastructure for? For another example, knowing how to build nuclear plants does you no good if you can't actually get and refine the fuel rods. <hr /><br /> While this is fun, we've had a few pages of discussion on what is essentially a Hunter Antagonist group, and thus a minor part of the setting. Should we move this into a separate thread to maintain focus? </div> </div> </div>The Geodics will be a major part of the setting, well, in the sense that they're the major nonMonarch antagonist from the Beneath. HCP/Guardians have their history woven so tightly with the Geodics and as a result, it's kinda nigh impossible to talk about the Geodics without touching on the human element.<br /> <br /> I suppose we can make a Hunter splat thread though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848842#post848842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: What is the social structure of the Monarchs? I assume that it's fairly feudal, with the more powerful towards the top of the pyramid and with the Kingmakers at the top.<br /> <br /> Another important question is this: What does it feel like to be a Monarch?<br /> <br /> Can you feel all the animalistic minds of your colony boiling away somewhere below your brainstem, reaching out into your mind with tendrils of instinct just as you bind them with the lash of your command? Do you hear them cry out when they die? Do you die with each of them as they do, over and over again? Do you feel the crunch of your foes' bones beneath their teeth? The blood running down their throat? What does it feel like to be a king of monsters and beasts, and to be only a step away from becoming a monster and a beast yourself?<br /> <br /> I think that something that would be interesting to play with would be the way that Monarchs are never alone. They've always got their Colony demanding their attention, at any time another Monarch could drop in telepathically. There's no <i>privacy </i>in a collective, no room for the <i>I. </i>There is only the <i>us. </i>The Endless are a race of <i>us</i>eswhile humanity is a race of <i>I</i>s. That difference could be played with I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are right about the Feudal social structure. with the exception of Puppet Kings, the top Monarchs are the ones who are more likely to kick your ass or demolish your town.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the other part:<br /> It probably all depends on Autonomy, the morality trait that represents not only how much control the Monarch exerts over the Colony, but also represents how attached you are to it. But dreaming I think is the situation where the Monarch is most aware of the goings on of the Colony, without the distractions of her own existance shrouding everything going on around her. She was a human first and foremost, and that line of thinking is hard to break away from in the waking world.<br /> <br /> Hm, I suppose the more OCD or &quot;low&quot; autonomy Monarchs also perhaps put forth more subconscious telepathic commands when they sleep...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming we move on: How about Caste based starting attribute trait distributions? Any thoughts on them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:53:59-07:00","id":848876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848854#post848854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming we move on: How about Caste based starting attribute trait distributions? Any thoughts on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, the bonuses each Caste's Noble Form gets upon character creation? Lesse, so far there's just the Marshals, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=847219#post847219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently Mashal's get: <br /> Strength, Dexterity, Stamina +1.<br /> Natural Melee +1<br /> Natural Armor 1/1</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think this is an awful lot of stuff to get innately; I'd have them choose one Attribute, one Skill, and one &quot;other thing&quot;. Of course, I'd grant this to both Noble and normal form...<br /> <br /> Anyway. Ideas! <br /> <br /> <b>Marshal</b><br /> Attribute bonus: Strength, Dexterity, Stamina<br /> Skill bonus: Athletics, Brawl, Weaponry<br /> Other bonus: Armor 1/1 (does not stack with mundane armor)<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe </b><br /> Attribute bonus: Intelligence, Wits, Resolve<br /> Skill bonus: Academics, Investigation, Occult<br /> Other bonus: understand all human and Monarch languages and ciphers<br /> <br /> <b>Stewards </b><br /> Attribute bonus: Resolve, Composure, Stamina<br /> Skill bonus: Crafts, Computers Science<br /> Other bonus: know the location of anything you've created<br /> <br /> <b>Diplomat</b><br /> Attribute bonus: Presence, Manipulation, Composure<br /> Skill bonus: Empathy, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> Other bonus: start at one higher impression level for Social Maneuvering<br /> <br /> <b>Shade</b><br /> Attribute bonus: Wits, Manipulation, Dexterity<br /> Skill bonus: Larceny, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> Other bonus: +2 Defense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T17:44:08-07:00","id":849049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848876#post848876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in, the bonuses each Caste's Noble Form gets upon character creation? Lesse, so far there's just the Marshals, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I think this is an awful lot of stuff to get innately; I'd have them choose one Attribute, one Skill, and one &quot;other thing&quot;. Of course, I'd grant this to both Noble and normal form...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the idea of Noble form, atleast the Marshall one was more or less to be somewhat able to Rival a Werewolf's Urshul, atleast after factoring in Pricipalities, so of course it gets a bunch of attribute gains, natural armor, and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other Castes would be better in other fields. having similar attributes.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do like the idea of other Bonuses, though, but Shade maybe needs something better for hiding.<br /> <br /> Anyone have other thoughts or would like to put support for Ace of Almonds's model?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T18:36:37-07:00","id":849064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=848854#post848854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was only a small but innovative faction of humans, like a Conspiracy. I have yet to even establish the location of these events though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Likely regions include India (for the crazy Ancient Aliens and Mahabharata link), or Africa (for the &quot;natural&quot; nuclear fission reactors under the ground). Tunguska's a bit recent. No source, but maybe tie in the extreme weather even of 535?<br /> <br /> Do you think HCP is a contributor to the Lost Boys group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T18:55:31-07:00","id":849073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=849064#post849064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Likely regions include India (for the crazy Ancient Aliens and Mahabharata link), or Africa (for the &quot;natural&quot; nuclear fission reactors under the ground). Tunguska's a bit recent. No source, but maybe tie in the extreme weather even of 535?<br /> <br /> Do you think HCP is a contributor to the Lost Boys group?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> India reminds me of League of extraordinary Gentlemen where Captain Nemos famous sub was a creation of Indian industrial engineering.<br /> <br /> I... I think I might go place them there. Add in more alien visitiomations maybe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-17-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T21:48:52-07:00","id":849138,"title":"","content":"I'll be openning up a thread on some other sites I go to really soon now that I have Caste's more or less functional. Still need Form traits and boons, but before then, I am adding this to the front page.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Court </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch is unlike typical supernaturals in that they lack a \u201cSocial Splat\u201d equivalent. Instead, they possess membership in a Court, a ruling body of other Monarchs in order of relative power leading up all the way to the King or Queen. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The King or Queen is an absolute ruler of all Monarchs in this group, though there may be other Monarchs that hold sway or limit her powers in a sort of Council. The deliberations and laws passed by this group affect an nation, small by the standards of global politics, but large enough that one might realistically hide under all of France.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Below the Council and the King or Queen are the Vassals that serve under them, who contribute taxes of material or provide warriors for their levees. And below those Vassals are serve under them who do the same thing, and there\u2019s the Vassals under that group. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Many new Monarchs are not given a choice when selecting a Court. They are either with the local one or they aren\u2019t. And if they aren\u2019t, well, there was a reason small nations sometimes were short lived.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While many Monarchs have to put up with taxes or get dragged onto wars against their own Court members or even other Courts, Monarchs in a Court do have the advantage that their telepathy range covers the entire region that their Court controls and some miles outside of it, largely due to neural networking infrastructure.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Principalities </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every Monarch must be versed in the arts of rulership. Within her very genetic code are the instinctive and preprogrammed mannerisms and gene sequences necessary to rule and command over her Colony like a Queen. But Monarchs are imperfect, knowing and using only a fraction of what lies within them. With time and practice, she may awaken these dormant and hidden genomes and genesplices to tap into her true potential, growing stronger with her increased mastery.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Blades </i>of engaging foes up close, rending and crushing them with your own physical might. Favored most of all by Marshals</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Bows </i> of striking enemies from afar, leveraging deadly range for lethal strikes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Shields </i> of warding, growing thick carapices and enduring sieges through fortification and fortitude.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Staves</i> of wizardry, warping space and physics to suit your ends. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spheres</i> of divination, seeing information through visions and prophesy. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Crucibles</i> of alchemy, of changing substance to suit your ends. Favored most of all by Scribes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Hammers</i> of creation, shaping the world by tools, hand, and claw. Stewards prize this above all.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Challices</i> of elixirs, potions and poisons to mend and maim.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Records</i> of time, of seeing into the past\u2026 and recalling future events.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Scepters</i> of dominion, converting and subverting lesser beings by your will.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Crowns</i> of command, forcing and hammering at the will of another. Diplomat\u2019s signature Principality.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Quills</i> of messages, conversing with others through unspoken and unwritten word.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Veils</i> of deception, of tricks, illusions, and lies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Censers</i> of clouds, vapors that fill the lungs with pleasure or pain</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Cloaks </i> of wings, to fly and to move against gravity and physics.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:09:59-07:00","id":849240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=849138#post849138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Principalities </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every Monarch must be versed in the arts of rulership. Within her very genetic code are the instinctive and preprogrammed mannerisms and gene sequences necessary to rule and command over her Colony like a Queen. But Monarchs are imperfect, knowing and using only a fraction of what lies within them. With time and practice, she may awaken these dormant and hidden genomes and genesplices to tap into her true potential, growing stronger with her increased mastery.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Blades </i>of engaging foes up close, rending and crushing them with your own physical might. Favored most of all by Marshals</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Bows </i> of striking enemies from afar, leveraging deadly range for lethal strikes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Shields </i> of warding, growing thick carapices and enduring sieges through fortification and fortitude.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Staves</i> of wizardry, warping space and physics to suit your ends. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spheres</i> of divination, seeing information through visions and prophesy. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Crucibles</i> of alchemy, of changing substance to suit your ends. Favored most of all by Scribes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Hammers</i> of creation, shaping the world by tools, hand, and claw. Stewards prize this above all.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Challices</i> of elixirs, potions and poisons to mend and maim.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Records</i> of time, of seeing into the past\u2026 and recalling future events.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Scepters</i> of dominion, converting and subverting lesser beings by your will.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Crowns</i> of command, forcing and hammering at the will of another. Diplomat\u2019s signature Principality.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Quills</i> of messages, conversing with others through unspoken and unwritten word.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Veils</i> of deception, of tricks, illusions, and lies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Censers</i> of clouds, vapors that fill the lungs with pleasure or pain</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Cloaks </i> of wings, to fly and to move against gravity and physics.</span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seeing a bit of conceptual overlap. Maybe I missed something earlier, but what really separates Spheres and Records? Is Records Past <i>or</i> Future, while Spheres is Now, unbound by range? Crucibles and Hammers close, though I can still see the small dividing line. Scepters and Crowns are nearly identical in concept, from what I can tell. What can Cloaks manage that Staves cannot? I have no idea about what Censers do, and how the effects cannot simply be replicated via Crucibles (substance based) or Scepters/Crowns (psychic based)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:48:20-07:00","id":849292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=849240#post849240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm seeing a bit of conceptual overlap. Maybe I missed something earlier, but what really separates Spheres and Records? Is Records Past <i>or</i> Future, while Spheres is Now, unbound by range? Crucibles and Hammers close, though I can still see the small dividing line. Scepters and Crowns are nearly identical in concept, from what I can tell. What can Cloaks manage that Staves cannot? I have no idea about what Censers do, and how the effects cannot simply be replicated via Crucibles (substance based) or Scepters/Crowns (psychic based)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mad a mistake in the above yeah.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spheres is Now as well as more detailed scanning analysis<br /> <br /> Records is past and future but bound by physical space. And has actual time manipulation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Crucible is about small scale objects and mostly about breaking things down to create substances<br /> Hammers is... big things, larger scale shaping. Earthquakes would be a reasonable hammers use for instance.<br /> <br /> Scepters and Crowns. One is more aggressive and more forceful against fewer targets. The other is more subliminal coercion and works in an area.<br /> <br /> Cloaks is about your own shaping and warping. It's mostly gravity and mobility and surviving in more biomes.<br /> Staves is mostly about short lived space warping.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Censers is where we get into Pheremones and smoke screens. That's what's unique to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:31:37-07:00","id":849312,"title":"","content":"And Principalities are handled like Disciplines, right (in that they are ranked 1-5 dots, with each dot unlocking one ability)? As opposed to Arcana or Transmutions, which have multiple options at each rank?<br /> <br /> Other than dots potentially unlocking Servant abilities, Noble Form upgrades, etc. But those are tied to <i>that</i> dot, not separate options purchased at the level, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:53:22-07:00","id":849322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=849312#post849312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Principalities are handled like Disciplines, right (in that they are ranked 1-5 dots, with each dot unlocking one ability)? As opposed to Arcana or Transmutions, which have multiple options at each rank?<br /> <br /> Other than dots potentially unlocking Servant abilities, Noble Form upgrades, etc. But those are tied to <i>that</i> dot, not separate options purchased at the level, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes on all counts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:57:18-07:00","id":849380,"title":"","content":"What &quot;forms&quot; can Servants take? I'm assuming a small selection of stock creatures (Foreman, Soldier, etc.) at least. What about creatures as equipment/symbionts? Servants as swarms/mobile Tilts? Servants as parasites/Conditions? Servants as structures?<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> Solider (creature), can pick up and use a Plasma Bug (equipment), while moving under the vision blocking influence of a Dark Swarm (Tilt).<br /> Mike Victim gets implanted with a Sensory Parasite(Condition) allowing the Monarch to tap his senses.<br /> The Monarch instructs a Nexus Worm (structure) to root itself on a spot so they have easy access to their Colony, and a quick escape.<br /> A Scout (creature) sneaks through the apartment complex, infecting the tenants with Dream Leeches (Condition), which will funnel the Willpower they would acquire from restful sleep to the Monarch/Colony.<br /> <br /> Or even the ability to shift between states?<br /> An Evisceroid (creature) kills a guard, then crawls into and reanimates their body (Condition, tied to the creature the guard was before).<br /> Carapace Beetle (creature) can wrap itself around its Monarch, giving them its defensive benefits (equipment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-18-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:33:12-07:00","id":849392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=849380#post849380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What &quot;forms&quot; can Servants take? I'm assuming a small selection of stock creatures (Foreman, Soldier, etc.) at least. What about creatures as equipment/symbionts? Servants as swarms/mobile Tilts? Servants as parasites/Conditions? Servants as structures?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Servants can either be Swarms or Creatures. Not equipment. Those are classified as funnily enough &quot;items&quot;. I think certain powerful servants might blend the line between structure and creature too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sensory Parasite is probably either going to go in a power, or be a Colony action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or even the ability to shift between states?<br /> An Evisceroid (creature) kills a guard, then crawls into and reanimates their body (Condition, tied to the creature the guard was before).<br /> Carapace Beetle (creature) can wrap itself around its Monarch, giving them its defensive benefits (equipment). </div> </div> </div>Had not thought of that though. Maybe. I'd need to set up the Servant rules sometime over the weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Mem