 from the world or, in the case of Vitae, from other people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T14:41:25-07:00","id":850808,"title":"","content":"Here's my go at the principality of Cloaks, minus any Colony benefits. If you could gve me some advice or feedback that would be great.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b><u>Principality of Cloaks</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Gravity is a force which the science of men has little comprehension of. They know its results \u2013 barely - and that is a pervasive force but almost nothing about its nature or manipulation. The Endless, however, know it intimately and bestow a portion of this knowledge upon those Monarchs proven worthy.</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Monarch Active Powers</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>O</b><br /> <br /> <u>Leap</u><br /> The Monarch manipulates the gravity acting upon him for a moment, using it to boost a jump to inhuman levels.<br /> Cost: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Dice Pool: Authority + Cloaks + Strength<br /> Effect:<br /> The distance that the Monarch jumps is multiplied by (Activation Successes + Cloaks).<br /> <br /> <b>OO</b><br /> <br /> <u>On The Walls</u><br /> The Monarch becomes able to manipulate the direction that gravity acts upon him, allowing him to walk upon a surface of any orientation, from perpendicular to the ground all the way to walking completely upside-down.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Authority + Cloaks + Resolve<br /> Duration: Minutes equal to successes rolled<br /> Effect:<br /> The Monarch becomes able to walk upon any surface, no matter its orientation to the ground. He could walk up the side of a skyscraper or along the wall of a building. This also means that for the duration of the power he falls in the direction which is now \u2018down\u2019 to him. The Monarch may spend another Instant action in order to change his gravitational orientation while the power is active at no cost.<br /> <br /> <b>OOO</b><br /> <br /> <u>Gravity Hammer</u><br /> Massively increasing the gravitational pull upon an object that he is using to make an attack, the Monarch unleashes a titanic blow upon his foe, enough to break bones, shatter walls and inflict massive damage.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Dice Pool: Authority + Cloaks + Strength<br /> Duration: 1 attack<br /> Effect:<br /> This power can be activated reflexively while the Monarch is making a physical melee attack. If the attack is upon an enemy, it does extra damage of the same kind it would do otherwise equal to (Cloaks + Activation Successes) and inflicts the Leg Wrack, Arm Wrack or Knocked Down Tilts in addition to the Stunned Tilt. If used upon an inanimate object, the attack deals damage to Structure, bypassing Durability equal to the Monarch\u2019s Authority.<br /> <br /> <b>OOOO</b><br /> <br /> <u>Immovable Object</u><br /> By manipulating the gravity acting upon him, the Monarch becomes immovable and inviolable.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Dice Pool: Authority + Cloaks + Resolve<br /> Duration: Turns equal to (Activation Successes*2)<br /> Effect:<br /> The Monarch becomes completely immovable no matter his location in space. He could be on the ground, in the air or underwater. Regardless of the force applied to him, he will not move, nor will he be harmed by any force acting upon him. He could stand in the way of a speeding truck, activate this power and punch a perfect hole through the thing. However, this protection only applies to kinetic energy, gravity or powers which produce or manipulate either. It will not shield the Monarch from heat, electricity or bolts of magical power, although it will protect against bullets, clubs or swords.<br /> <br /> <b>OOOOO</b><br /> <br /> <u>Living Singularity</u><br /> The Monarch gains the ability to transform momentarily into a singularity, buffeting everything and everyone around him with vicious gravitational flux and dealing massive damage to living creatures and inanimate structures alike.<br /> Cost: 3 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Authority + Cloaks + Presence<br /> Duration: Turns equal to (Cloaks + Activation Successes)<br /> Effect:<br /> The Monarch becomes a miniature living singularity, dealing 1 Aggravated Damage per turn to everything in a radius of Authority meters. This damage cannot be soaked, nor stopped by armour. Anything save powerful magical or hypertechnological shields will fail before this power. Structures are dealt damage equal to rating every turn, ignoring durability. Additionally, everything within twice the radius with a Size less than 3 times that of the Monarch\u2019s Noble Form must devote the entirety of its turn to a Strength + Stamina roll to avoid being pulled a number of yards equal to the Monarch\u2019s Authority towards the singularity. Any object not fastened down or not of Size greater than 3 times that of the Monarch\u2019s Noble Form will be sucked towards the singularity. Anything in physical contact with the singularity is dealt Aggravated damage equal to the Monarch\u2019s Authority each turn. When the object suffers Damage equal to or greater than its Size, it is sucked into the singularity and destroyed. Nothing save the greatest of magics can retrieve it now.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Noble Form Upgrades</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>O</b><br /> The Monarch gains the ability to change his own apparent weight, allowing him to stand on a blade of grass. He does not actually change his mass but rather how gravity interacts with his mass, meaning that his body does not become softer as he becomes \u2018lighter\u2019. He may not increase his \u2018weight\u2019 beyond his normal.<br /> The Monarch gains +2 Speed in Noble Form as he manipulates gravity upon his body to his advantage.<br /> <br /> <b>OO</b><br /> The Monarch becomes able to walk upon any surface, no matter its orientation to the ground. He could walk up the side of a skyscraper or along the wall of a building. This also means that for the duration of the power he falls in the direction which is now \u2018down\u2019 to him. The Monarch may spend another Instant action in order to change his gravitational orientation while the power is active at no cost.<br /> The Monarch gains + 3 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increase.<br /> <br /> <b>OOO</b><br /> The Monarch becomes able to make his mass \u2018go into the negative\u2019, and can subtly manipulate the direction in which gravity acts upon him, allowing him to move in three dimensions (i.e. fly) at half his Speed.<br /> The Monarch gains + 5 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increases.<br /> <br /> <b>OOOO</b><br /> The Monarch achieves greater control over his mass and gravitation, allowing him to fly at his full Speed<br /> The Monarch gains + 7 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increases.<br /> <br /> <b>OOOOO</b><br /> With even greater control over his mass and gravitation, the Monarch becomes able to fly at double his Speed.<br /> The Monarch gains + 10 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increases.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-22-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"lin