the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=851364#post851364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How's Staves going Almarck?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Taking a back seat due to math. Calculus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:57:39-07:00","id":853210,"title":"","content":"Alright. So here's a slightly revised look into Cloaks<br /> <br /> I will note that I don't know what to do about Singularity since... well, it felt odd to me for some reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cloaks</b></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gravity is a force which the science of men has little comprehension of. They know its results \u2013 barely - and that is a pervasive force but almost nothing about its nature or manipulation. The Endless are so familiar with it, that an expert Monarch might regard it like less nobles would think of as clothes, acting as a convenient and flexible tool, almost like wings.</span><br /> </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">b]Monarch Active Powers Granted:[/b]</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Leap 0</b></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch manipulates the gravity acting upon him for a moment, using it to boost a jump to inhuman levels. </span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Psi or None (if Noble Form) </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action: Reflexive </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Scene </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She can leap great distances, multiplying the distance of any jump she makes by1 + Cloaks</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>On The Walls 00 </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch becomes able to manipulate the direction that gravity acts upon him, allowing him to walk upon a surface of any orientation, from perpendicular to the ground all the way to walking completely upside-down.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 Psi or None (if Noble Form) </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action</b>Instant </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch becomes able to walk upon any surface, no matter its orientation to the ground. He could walk up the side of a skyscraper or along the wall of a building. This also means that for the duration of the power he falls in the direction which is now \u2018down\u2019 to him. The Monarch may spend another Instant action in order to change his gravitational orientation while the power is active at no cost.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Gravity Crush 000</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Massively increasing the gravitational pull upon an object that he is using to make an attack, the Monarch unleashes a titanic blow upon his foe, enough to break bones, shatter walls and inflict massive damage. </i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 Psi</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b> Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> 1 attack</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power can be activated reflexively while the Monarch is making a physical melee attack. If the attack is upon an enemy, she may inflict the Leg Wrack, Arm Wrack, Knocked Down, or Stunned Tilts in addition the attack\u2019s normal effects. If used upon an inanimate object, the attack deals damage to Structure, bypassing Durability equal to the Monarch\u2019s Cloaks.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Immovable Object 0000</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By manipulating the gravity acting upon him, the Monarch becomes immovable and inviolable.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2 Psi</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Authority + Cloaks + Resolve</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Turns equal to (Activation Successes*2)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch becomes completely immovable no matter his location in space. He could be on the ground, in the air or underwater. Regardless of the force applied to him, he will not move, nor will he be harmed by any force acting upon him. He could stand in the way of a speeding truck, activate this power and punch a perfect hole through the thing. However, this protection only applies to kinetic energy, gravity or powers which produce or manipulate either. It will not shield the Monarch from heat, electricity or bolts of magical power, although it will protect against bullets, clubs or swords that are nonmagical in nature.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She also becomes unable to attack at range as anything she could do would be attracted back to her own body before it could escape her gravity field. And because she is unable to move, she is considered having a Defense of 0.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Noble Form Upgrades:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>0</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch gains the ability to change his own apparent weight, allowing him to stand on a blade of grass. He does not actually change his mass but rather how gravity interacts with his mass, meaning that his body does not become softer as he becomes \u2018lighter\u2019. He may not increase his \u2018weight\u2019 beyond his normal.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch gains +2 Speed in Noble Form as he manipulates gravity upon his body to his advantage.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>00</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch becomes able to walk upon any surface, no matter its orientation to the ground. He could walk up the side of a skyscraper or along the wall of a building. This also means that for the duration of the power he falls in the direction which is now \u2018down\u2019 to him. The Monarch may order to change his gravitational orientation while the power is active at no cost, so long as he is able to grab hold of a surface to cling onto and orient towards.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch gains + 3 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increase.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch becomes able to make his mass \u2018go into the negative\u2019, and can subtly manipulate the direction in which gravity acts upon him, allowing him to move in three dimensions (i.e. fly) at half his Speed.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch gains + 5 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increases.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>0000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch achieves greater control over his mass and gravitation, allowing him to fly at his full Speed</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch gains + 7 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increases.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>00000</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With even greater control over his mass and gravitation, the Monarch becomes able to fly at double his Speed.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch gains + 10 Speed while in Noble Form, not cumulative with the previous increases.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:24:29-07:00","id":854144,"title":"","content":"So, as it turns out, I am actually fairly bad at writing powers even though I developed the subsystem and set the themes.<br /> <br /> I think my problem stems from a relatively limited grasp of creative dice mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I got this so far..<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Spheres</b></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A Monarch must know what she does, acting upon wisdom and not ignorance. Through the power of peering through the manifolds and calculating the advanced quantum reality behind the seams, a Lord of Spheres knows much. </i></span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See the Unseen. See into Twilight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloud the Visions, Disrupt scrying attempts +1 Int</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know the Answers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unquestioned Truth, incapable of seeing illussions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-27-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T03:34:34-07:00","id":854403,"title":"","content":"Do Monarchs have complete sensory input from their Colony/Servants inherently? At all times, or must they focus? Because if not, the first dot could do that. Noble Form upgrades might be increases to &quot;Perception&quot; rolls.<br /> <br /> Additional abilities might do the &quot;ask questions&quot; effect of Auspex and other 2E powers. Higher abilities could be Astral Projection, or outright Clairvoyance. Or even upping the limit on who/what you can ask about (either options, or range, potentially capping out at &quot;unlimited range&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T06:54:41-07:00","id":854453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854144#post854144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as it turns out, I am actually fairly bad at writing powers even though I developed the subsystem and set the themes.<br /> <br /> I think my problem stems from a relatively limited grasp of creative dice mechanics.<br /> <br /> I got this so far..<br /> <b>Spheres</b><br /> <i>A Monarch must know what she does, acting upon wisdom and not ignorance. Through the power of peering through the manifolds and calculating the advanced quantum reality behind the seams, a Lord of Spheres knows much.</i><br /> See the Unseen. See into Twilight.<br /> Cloud the Visions, Disrupt scrying attempts +1 Int<br /> Know the Answers.<br /> Unquestioned Truth, incapable of seeing illusions.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are these the powers in order? I can take a stab at mechanizing them. (Are &quot;See the Unseen&quot; and &quot;See into Twilight&quot; two different powers, or part of the same one? Is a fifth power needed?)<br /> <br /> Also, is it possible to update the first post with what has been decided so far? i.e. the lists of powers, Blades, Shields, Cloaks, Castes, Courts, Colony. That way, the entire thread doesn't have to be combed through to double check things. Either that or share the gDocs for viewing.<br /> <br /> Also also, took a stab at the last Cloaks power; created a lower power version of Singularity (because that much Agg a turn? Yikes!) and an alternate fifth dot.<br /> <br /> <b>Living Singularity</b><br /> The Monarch summons a singularity, buffeting everything and everyone around her with vicious gravitational force.<br /> Cost: 3 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: Rather than a singularity, a wave of force is created, pushing everything away from the activation point. This causes no damage, but may move obects slightly. The Monarch cannot use this power again in the scene.<br /> Failure: No singularity is created. The Monarch can try again next turn at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: The Monarch creates a small singularity within visual range. Everything within Authority * 10 feet of the singularity (including the Monarch), is pulled towards it at a rate of Authority feet per turn. Motile beings can attempt to move away, but require successes greater than the activation roll on a Strength + Athletics check to do so. They can also choose to hold on to something, and hope it doesn't get pulled in, too. Objects attached to the ground take 1 Structure damage a turn, bypassing Durability, and detach when destroyed. Ranged attacks veer towards the singularity instead of their intended target.<br /> When within Authority * 3 feet of the singularity, living beings take 1 Bashing a turn from the gravitational forces. When within Authority feet, that damage is Lethal. Touching the Singularity makes the damage Aggravated.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and the Monarch can choose to be affected or not by the singularity.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth Becomes Sky</b><br /> At the height of her power, the Monarch can turn gravity off, if only briefly.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Authority + Empathy<br /> Duration: Successes minutes<br /> Dramatic Failure: Gravity increases instead. Everything within Authority feet of the Monarch comes crashing to the ground, and the Monarch takes 3 Lethal damage.<br /> Failure: Gravity does not fall. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: Within a sphere of Authority * 10 feet around the Monarch, gravity ceases to function. Objects slowly begin to float, and can be sent flying with a touch. Beings unfamiliar with zero gravity take -2 to all physical actions. The sphere moves with the Monarch; anything that exits the sphere's influence has gravity apply normally the following round.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and the Monarch gains her Noble form benefits from Cloaks if she's in human form while the power is active. The power lasts for the scene, or until the Monarch drops it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T07:29:13-07:00","id":854465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854403#post854403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Monarchs have complete sensory input from their Colony/Servants inherently? At all times, or must they focus? Because if not, the first dot could do that. Noble Form upgrades might be increases to &quot;Perception&quot; rolls.<br /> <br /> Additional abilities might do the &quot;ask questions&quot; effect of Auspex and other 2E powers. Higher abilities could be Astral Projection, or outright Clairvoyance. Or even upping the limit on who/what you can ask about (either options, or range, potentially capping out at &quot;unlimited range&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Hadn't thought of that. I guess a &quot;Scry on Drones&quot; effect should be in place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Clairvoyance would be good too but I never was a divination expert when ever I roll that kind of magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854453#post854453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are these the powers in order? I can take a stab at mechanizing them. (Are &quot;See the Unseen&quot; and &quot;See into Twilight&quot; two different powers, or part of the same one? Is a fifth power needed?)<br /> <br /> Also, is it possible to update the first post with what has been decided so far? i.e. the lists of powers, Blades, Shields, Cloaks, Castes, Courts, Colony. That way, the entire thread doesn't have to be combed through to double check things. Either that or share the gDocs for viewing.<br /> <br /> Also also, took a stab at the last Cloaks power; created a lower power version of Singularity (because that much Agg a turn? Yikes!) and an alternate fifth dot.<br /> <br /> <b>Living Singularity</b><br /> The Monarch summons a singularity, buffeting everything and everyone around her with vicious gravitational force.<br /> Cost: 3 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: Rather than a singularity, a wave of force is created, pushing everything away from the activation point. This causes no damage, but may move obects slightly. The Monarch cannot use this power again in the scene.<br /> Failure: No singularity is created. The Monarch can try again next turn at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: The Monarch creates a small singularity within visual range. Everything within Authority * 10 feet of the singularity (including the Monarch), is pulled towards it at a rate of Authority feet per turn. Motile beings can attempt to move away, but require successes greater than the activation roll on a Strength + Athletics check to do so. They can also choose to hold on to something, and hope it doesn't get pulled in, too. Objects attached to the ground take 1 Structure damage a turn, bypassing Durability, and detach when destroyed. Ranged attacks veer towards the singularity instead of their intended target.<br /> When within Authority * 3 feet of the singularity, living beings take 1 Bashing a turn from the gravitational forces. When within Authority feet, that damage is Lethal. Touching the Singularity makes the damage Aggravated.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and the Monarch can choose to be affected or not by the singularity.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth Becomes Sky</b><br /> At the height of her power, the Monarch can turn gravity off, if only briefly.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Authority + Empathy<br /> Duration: Successes minutes<br /> Dramatic Failure: Gravity increases instead. Everything within Authority feet of the Monarch comes crashing to the ground, and the Monarch takes 3 Lethal damage.<br /> Failure: Gravity does not fall. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: Within a sphere of Authority * 10 feet around the Monarch, gravity ceases to function. Objects slowly begin to float, and can be sent flying with a touch. Beings unfamiliar with zero gravity take -2 to all physical actions. The sphere moves with the Monarch; anything that exits the sphere's influence has gravity apply normally the following round.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and the Monarch gains her Noble form benefits from Cloaks if she's in human form while the power is active. The power lasts for the scene, or until the Monarch drops it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Earth Becomes Sky is really cool. I like anti gravity.<br /> <br /> Also, the powers aren't in order.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also... why do you guys use Authority for things in the power breakdown? Wouldn't it make more sense to use the Principality's level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-28-2016, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T07:56:19-07:00","id":854477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854465#post854465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. Hadn't thought of that. I guess a &quot;Scry on Drones&quot; effect should be in place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Clairvoyance would be good too but I never was a divination expert when ever I roll that kind of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Earth Becomes Sky is really cool. I like anti gravity.<br /> <br /> Also, the powers aren't in order.<br /> <br /> Also... why do you guys use Authority for things in the power breakdown? Wouldn't it make more sense to use the Principality's level?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like most CoD systems use Power Trait as a determination of how powerful/big things get (Wyrd, Blood Potency, Azoth, etc.) Admittedly, I'm not super familiar with every line, but I think only Mage uses the &quot;dots you have in power&quot; in the roll, and they don't have you buy specific powers, you buy an area and then play with stuff in that area. If Monarchs are meant to be more like that, then I'd say using Principalities in the roll would make sense, but as single one-off powers, it doesn't. Additionally, sometimes it's pointless; if Earth Becomes Sky used Cloaks as a measure of effect-size instead of Authority, then the effect size would always be the same (because you need 5 dots of Cloaks to use it, and you can't get more than 5), and it might as well be a static size. If you want a power to have a difference in effect between a just-infected Monarch and the King, using Authority makes more sense than the respective Principality. If you don't, using a static number or number based on successes makes sense. (I kinda hate using Principalities in the activation roll, though; it means high-dot powers are hardly ever gonna fail, because you get an automatic bonus of 3-5 dice.)<br /> <br /> That's why I do it, anyway. Gonna go hammer on Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T08:06:15-07:00","id":854481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854465#post854465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. Hadn't thought of that. I guess a &quot;Scry on Drones&quot; effect should be in place.<br /> <br /> Clairvoyance would be good too but I never was a divination expert when ever I roll that kind of magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, general awareness of your minions seems implicit, but there is a wide gulf from &quot;nothing to report/under attack/etc.&quot; to seeing through your creature's senses.<br /> <br /> Maybe a conceptual track could look like:<br /> See through your colony's senses -&gt; use their distributed senses/thought-power for uncovering clue (Investigation system) -&gt; using your psychic awareness to pick up details about a target you can sense -&gt; unbind your psychic presence to remote spy (Astral Projection) -&gt; cast your psychic net beyond sensory range (IE, ask questions about anything, even if you can see a direct target).<br /> <br /> 2 and 3 work well with 1 and 4. 4 kinda but doesn't quite obsolete 1. 5 might be kept to general, vague answers (that could be followed up with detailed investigation) so as not to obsolete 1-4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854465#post854465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also... why do you guys use Authority for things in the power breakdown? Wouldn't it make more sense to use the Principality's level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how much you want to value the dot ratings, and how you want the Dice Roll to look. Authority has slower growth, but a higher cap. Principalities dots unlocks abilities and confers increasing potency. Basing it off Authority means it starts small, and increases slowly, but caps out at 20 dice, before modifiers. Basing off Principality, means a starting character could have a large pool to start with, or buy it up easier than Authority, though it caps out at 15 dice, before modifiers.<br /> <br /> I suppose, flavor-wise, it depends on what Authority means. Is it general power and standing (and thus should increase general powers) or is it merely related to the Colony's power and role? Are Principalities core to the Monarch condition, or specialized tricks that many have taught themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T08:35:17-07:00","id":854491,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> \u200bI'll have to think about it some more. But I'm thinking that the Principalities are more like specific precepts of ruler ship that are genetically implanted but often dormant where mastery of them is key to success.<br /> What do you think about that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a><br /> Actually...<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Vampire use Skill + Attribute + Renown/Discipline rating in their roll often having big dice pools.<br /> <br /> Demon uses Primum instead but in its case, Demon powers do not have dot level categories associated with them like Renown or Disciplines do. They roll Primum + Attribute + Skill.<br /> <br /> Mage is unique in that since it learns a very large multitude of freeform powers, it's balancing mechanic was that it has lower dicepools than otherwise without using rotes or other casting boosts. In 1e It was Gnosis (power trait) + Arcana (discipline). In 2e, I think it's the same but rotes let you add skill dots to the roll.<br /> <br /> The splats that have things resembling Discipline/Principality dots use them to determine their areas of effect if it matters. Cataclysm for Werewolf for instances goes on Renown X Miles. Although, maybe for<br /> <br /> <br /> It also seems to be a thing that high level supernaturals... hardly fail activation rolls anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, one thing you can consider doing Ace, is making power that upgrade preestablished ones.<br /> An example of this is in Vampire where Obscufate 3 isn't so much a new power so much as a modification to the previous levels of Obscufate adding Invisibility as an option for the lower leveled Obscufate 3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T09:05:38-07:00","id":854505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854491#post854491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> \u200bI'll have to think about it some more. But I'm thinking that the Principalities are more like specific precepts of ruler ship that are genetically implanted but often dormant where mastery of them is key to success.<br /> What do you think about that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a><br /> Actually...<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Vampire use Skill + Attribute + Renown/Discipline rating in their roll often having big dice pools.<br /> <br /> Demon uses Primum instead but in its case, Demon powers do not have dot level categories associated with them like Renown or Disciplines do. They roll Primum + Attribute + Skill.<br /> <br /> Mage is unique in that since it learns a very large multitude of freeform powers, it's balancing mechanic was that it has lower dicepools than otherwise without using rotes or other casting boosts. In 1e It was Gnosis (power trait) + Arcana (discipline). In 2e, I think it's the same but rotes let you add skill dots to the roll.<br /> <br /> The splats that have things resembling Discipline/Principality dots use them to determine their areas of effect if it matters. Cataclysm for Werewolf for instances goes on Renown X Miles. Although, maybe for<br /> <br /> <br /> It also seems to be a thing that high level supernaturals... hardly fail activation rolls anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, one thing you can consider doing Ace, is making power that upgrade preestablished ones.<br /> An example of this is in Vampire where Obscufate 3 isn't so much a new power so much as a modification to the previous levels of Obscufate adding Invisibility as an option for the lower leveled Obscufate 3</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna disagree about Renown; Renown is not Gifts. Some Gifts have a prereq of a level of renown, but you don't add your dots in Technology to your roll for Iron Trechery, for example. It's a separate, outside stat. Also, it doesn't apply to all gifts.<br /> <br /> Vampire does do it; guess I was less familiar with it than I thought. I don't like it, but that's personal opinion. I like the Monarch powers better as styled after Changeling or Promethean, where the activation pools are Attribute + Power Trait, Power Trait + Skill, or Attribute + Skill. If you like them better like Vampire, it's always reviseable; just replace any instance of Authority in the roll with [Principality].<br /> <br /> I'll keep the upgradable-power thing in mind; having an early simple-scry and a later better-scry could make the numbers work better.<br /> <br /> Tangent: for Cloaks, part of their thing was being sneaky. Maybe instead of their Noble Form just getting Speed out the wazoo, they could also pick up Stealth bonuses? Or maybe Dex ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T09:25:56-07:00","id":854514,"title":"","content":"The sneaky part of cloaks was moved over to Veils, last I checked. Though you are right and we'd need something to do other than have Cloaks give you so much speed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T09:51:52-07:00","id":854521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854514#post854514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sneaky part of cloaks was moved over to Veils, last I checked. Though you are right and we'd need something to do other than have Cloaks give you so much speed</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Veils got disguise, but Cloaks got moving silently. I'm not really sure of any other Skill/Attribute for Cloaks to give a bonus on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:56:21-07:00","id":854557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=854521#post854521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Veils got disguise, but Cloaks got moving silently. I'm not really sure of any other Skill/Attribute for Cloaks to give a bonus on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe size or health?<br /> <br /> <br /> Having gravity control let's you vest against the square cube law","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T11:09:43-07:00","id":854561,"title":"","content":"I don't see how gravity control would impact size or health at all. Maaaaaybe Defense, since you can pull/push attacks away from you.<br /> <br /> Here's a pass at Spheres. Wasn't real sure about Colony powers (there doesn't seem to be another Principality with those written up yet). Didn't give an anti-scry power, thought that might fit better with Veils. Also, maybe instead of Empathy the Noble Form could get a special sense or two, like with the Colony.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Spheres</b></u><br /> <i>A Monarch must know what she does, acting upon wisdom and not ignorance. Through the power of peering through the manifolds and calculating the advanced quantum reality behind the seams, a Lord of Spheres knows much. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Active Powers</b><br /> [1] Unquestioned Truth<br /> A Monarch can see through disguises of any kind, be they mundane or something more. This doesn't help her find something hidden, though.<br /> Cost: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dice Pool: None or Wits + Composure + Authority<br /> Effect: The Monarch can tell when someone or something is not showing its true form. For mundane disguises, she picks out inconsistancies: the hint of stocking under a wig, the way the light glints off some make-up, the newness of a coat of paint. For supernatural disguises, she sees through passive effects (like a Monarch's true form or a Changeling's Mask). For active effects (such as Veils or a Demon's true form), roll as a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> [2] See the Unseen<br /> There are layers to the world, and beings lurking beyond the next shadow. The Endless have ways of peeling back the layers to see what's underneith.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble form)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Effect: The Monarch can see and hear into Twilight. He cannot affect beings there, but can communicate with them.<br /> <br /> [3] Looking Glass<br /> With practice, a Monarch can pick a target and let her senses travel with it, be it a living being or a lone object.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free when target is her Colony)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Composure + Authority<br /> Duration: One week<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch's senses are garbled, giving her a -1 to all rolls due to distraction for the scene.<br /> Failure: The Monarch's senses fail to follow. She can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: The Monarch focuses on a person or thing within range of her senses. For the next week, she is able to see, hear, smell, and otherwise sense the area around that target by concentrating. She loses all senses but touch in her own form when doing so, but she can swap back at any time. She can mark a number of people and objects equal to her Autonomy.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, but the Monarch does not lose her own senses when spying on the target.<br /> <br /> [4] Know the Answer<br /> For facts with an objective truth, a Monarch can suss out exactly what that truth is.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Authority<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch recieves an false or dangerous answer and believes it to be true.<br /> Failure: The Monarch recives no insight. He can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: For each success, the Monarch can ask the ST one yes-or-no question (i.e. &quot;Is this woman lying because she's under threat? Was the goblet stolen by my rival? Has this man been dead for more than a day?&quot;). This provides no proof or evidence of the truth; merely an innate knowledge. Facts that have been hidden using supernatural powers get a Clash of Wills; failure means the Monarch knows there should be a truth, but something has obscured it.<br /> Exceptional Success: No further effect beyond multiple successes.<br /> <br /> [5] Clairvoyance<br /> The Masters of Spheres can sense anything, anywhere.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi (free when target is her Colony)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Authority<br /> Duration: Concentration<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch loses her own senses completely. She gains the Insensate Tilt for the scene.<br /> Failure: The Monarch fails to scry. She can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: The Monarch focuses on a person, place, or thing she has encountered before. She is able to see, hear, smell, and otherwise sense the area around that target by concentrating. She loses all senses but touch in her own form when doing so, but she can swap back at any time.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, but the Monarch does not lose her own senses when scrying.<br /> <br /> <b>Noble Form</b><br /> [1] +2 to Perception rolls.<br /> [2] +2 to Perception rolls. +2 to Empathy rolls.<br /> [3] +4 to Perception rolls. +2 to Empathy rolls.<br /> [4] +4 to Perception rolls. +4 to Empathy rolls.<br /> [5] +6 to Perception rolls. +4 to Empathy rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Colony Powers</b><br /> [1] Colonies get +1 Perception.<br /> [2] Colonies get single special sense: heat-vision, vibration sense, echolocation, EM sense, etc.<br /> [3] Use a colony-member's senses at any distance.<br /> [4] Colonies get +2 Perception.<br /> [5] Colonies get another special sense: heat-vision, vibration sense, echolocation, EM sense, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:06:56-07:00","id":854805,"title":"","content":"Alright. So. I've gone ahead and posted the prototypes of Principalities we have on the first page.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I realize right now that maybe before we go work on balancing and specific mechanics, we just... focus on creating as many powers and as much content as possible. <br /> <br /> I thank both you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> for your contributions for Principalities. <br /> <br /> I'll be working on the Colony mechanics. We got enough data I think to make something really basic to refine at a latter point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:42:44-07:00","id":854829,"title":"","content":"Muchos gracias for putting all the stuff on the front page. Not sure if creating all the content, then making them fit the rules is better or worse than trying to do the rules and hoping there's still enough interest to get mechanics done. Either way, I'm up for creating Principalities. Would it be better to fill out the sparse ones (Blades, Bows, Shields) or work on the untouched?<br /> <br /> Also, something I just noticed on the first page: it says Monarchs get access to &quot;all Monarch powers&quot;. What does that mean? Just Noble Form benefits? Does that have some effect on Principalities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T20:08:03-07:00","id":854841,"title":"","content":"Work on the untouched, the idea being that if everything is setup, going back and adjusting them to fit in later would be easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll have to adjust what I posted there, but not today, I am afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:13:21-07:00","id":855019,"title":"","content":"In that case, I'll start work on Quills. Themes of telepathy, conversation, and peaceful action. For ideas, I've got messaging an individual, messaging a group, calming people down, creating hidden messages, bonuses to Socialize and Empathy. Lemme know other ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:18:07-07:00","id":855026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855019#post855019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, I'll start work on Quills. Themes of telepathy, conversation, and peaceful action. For ideas, I've got messaging an individual, messaging a group, calming people down, creating hidden messages, bonuses to Socialize and Empathy. Lemme know other ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Re-writing memories. that's where the name came from in the first place anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:26:01-07:00","id":855033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855026#post855026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Re-writing memories. that's where the name came from in the first place anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That seems like it would fit better under Scepters, now (&quot;converting and subverting lesser beings by your will through corruption and hammering against the will of others&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:38:22-07:00","id":855039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855033#post855033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? That seems like it would fit better under Scepters, now (&quot;converting and subverting lesser beings by your will through corruption and hammering against the will of others&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scepters is more about implanting subtle commands. Quills is about becoming both reader and author of the minds of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:46:09-07:00","id":855046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855039#post855039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scepters is more about implanting subtle commands. Quills is about becoming both reader and author of the minds of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hammering against the will of others&quot; doesn't sound subtle. Besides, I thought Crowns got swapped with Scepters for subtly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless#post760136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Scepters </i>of dominion, converting and subverting lesser beings by your will through corruption and hammering against the will of others<br /> <i>Crowns </i>of command, of allowing others to see your authority and swaying the masses with honeyed words. Diplomat\u2019s signature Principality.<br /> <i>Quills</i> of messages, conversing with others through unspoken and unwritten word.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's different from what got talked about in this thread, but this sounds more like:<br /> Scepters: Dominate-esque, corrupt/suborn someone to your will, not subtle<br /> Crowns: Majesty-esque, convince a bunch of people of stuff, somewhat subtle<br /> Quills: telepathy and secret messages, most subtle<br /> <br /> If that's not the case, then these need new words, because the current ones are misleading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:51:46-07:00","id":855048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855046#post855046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Hammering against the will of others&quot; doesn't sound subtle. Besides, I thought Crowns got swapped with Scepters for subtly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know it's different from what got talked about in this thread, but this sounds more like:<br /> Scepters: Dominate-esque, corrupt/suborn someone to your will, not subtle<br /> Crowns: Majesty-esque, convince a bunch of people of stuff, somewhat subtle<br /> Quills: telepathy and secret messages, most subtle<br /> <br /> If that's not the case, then these need new words, because the current ones are misleading.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, I guess I was mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:57:58-07:00","id":855051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855048#post855048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, I guess I was mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one of us is. Possibly both of us. Gonna wait for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> to weigh in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:59:45-07:00","id":855053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855051#post855051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, one of us is. Possibly both of us. Gonna wait for <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> to weigh in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T07:36:21-07:00","id":855064,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Are there going to be cross-Principality abilities (like Devotions)? Because I can see a Quills and Scepters/Crowns mixed one where you write a message that readers take as <i>true</i>. Even if it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:14:38-07:00","id":855080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855064#post855064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Are there going to be cross-Principality abilities (like Devotions)? Because I can see a Quills and Scepters/Crowns mixed one where you write a message that readers take as <i>true</i>. Even if it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe in the future we will. Certainly going to be a thing for Servant or Colony unlocks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways. Scepters is not made to be subtle. It's psi attacks and hostile aggressive telepathy. The idea being &quot;rule with an iron rod&quot;. But it should largely be focused effort I think, few targets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Crowns is subliminal messaging and passive conversion and such. The subtle version. It's more AoE centric than Scepters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And Quills is &quot;peaceful&quot; telepathy, be idea being that of sending messages. Although it may need more themes to make it more appealing if it's too sparse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:31:58-07:00","id":855088,"title":"","content":"Principality-synergy sounds fun, but let's build the walls before worrying about the windows.<br /> <br /> I agree that Quills needs more than just telepathy/message-sending. Editing memories as a higher-level power might work, as long as that is specifically outside the range of Scepters. Having a &quot;calm down&quot; power would also work, but that may tread too close to Crowns. (Given that telepathy is innate to Monarchs, it might make more sense to put advanced telepathy into Crowns, mind-editing into Scepters, and find some other thing for Scribes/Diplomats to share, but I'm at a lack of ideas.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:03:13-07:00","id":855103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855088#post855088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Principality-synergy sounds fun, but let's build the walls before worrying about the windows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they are possible, it makes sense to save such powers for those. If not, then such powers might fit under existing Principalities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855088#post855088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Quills needs more than just telepathy/message-sending. Editing memories as a higher-level power might work, as long as that is specifically outside the range of Scepters. Having a &quot;calm down&quot; power would also work, but that may tread too close to Crowns. (Given that telepathy is innate to Monarchs, it might make more sense to put advanced telepathy into Crowns, mind-editing into Scepters, and find some other thing for Scribes/Diplomats to share, but I'm at a lack of ideas.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe direct knowledge/skill sharing (because a direct experience dump is better than a message or picture, and giving all your minions/allies your 5 dots in Firearms, for instance, can be quite potent)? Or establishing a mental network beyond the confines of a Monarch's Colony (allowing your entire group to act as one has advantages)? Or grouping other &quot;magic writing&quot; ideas in there and let it have things like Wards or Alarms?<br /> <br /> Is Mind-<i>Reading</i> under the purview of any other Principality? Maybe you could argue it like &quot;reading their mind like an open book&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-29-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T10:43:27-07:00","id":855128,"title":"","content":"Quills could do mind reading I think. Sceptre is more about control anyways","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:37:09-07:00","id":855710,"title":"","content":"So... on revising colonies, how does everyone feel about revising Colonies to be more like Mummy cults?<br /> <br /> <br /> Instead of resource pools, the Attributes of a Colony are used in rolls and have things they automatically can do. It might be simpler to keep track of.<br /> <br /> Unlike Mummy cults Colony actions don't tie up the entire colony too..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:38:54-07:00","id":855712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855710#post855710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... on revising colonies, how does everyone feel about revising Colonies to be more like Mummy cults?<br /> <br /> <br /> Instead of resource pools, the Attributes of a Colony are used in rolls and have things they automatically can do. It might be simpler to keep track of.<br /> <br /> Unlike Mummy cults Colony actions don't tie up the entire colony too..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can get behind that. Simpler I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:41:34-07:00","id":855713,"title":"","content":"Also, I hate to self-shoutout but I don't suppose you could be persuaded to have a quick look at a new project of mine could you? It's the Demigod: the Empyrean fansplat. I you could i would be eternally thankful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:47:47-07:00","id":855717,"title":"","content":"Right. I noticed it a few times. I take it Dragons is on the shelf for some reason?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:50:47-07:00","id":855719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855717#post855717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. I noticed it a few times. I take it Dragons is on the shelf for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran out of steam for it. I knew what themes I wanted to get across but the framework as it was didn't fit. So I put it on the shelf and started over. I'm much more happy with Demigod so far, although it hasn't got the same attention as Dragon. Plus I get to put in a couple of interesting extra themes like the relationship between humanity and the divine and the way that we perceive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:40:34-07:00","id":855780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855710#post855710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... on revising colonies, how does everyone feel about revising Colonies to be more like Mummy cults?<br /> <br /> <br /> Instead of resource pools, the Attributes of a Colony are used in rolls and have things they automatically can do. It might be simpler to keep track of.<br /> <br /> Unlike Mummy cults Colony actions don't tie up the entire colony too..</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I kinda like the expanded options and little bit more complexity of individual resources and categories offers. Maybe offer a simplified version, and a more elaborate version? Those who don't care much about the Colony's details (or just want a quicker, more streamlined game) use the simplified rules, while other that focus on Colony use the full rule-set?<br /> <br /> What did you have in mind for more detailed rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:51:18-07:00","id":855791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855710#post855710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... on revising colonies, how does everyone feel about revising Colonies to be more like Mummy cults?<br /> <br /> <br /> Instead of resource pools, the Attributes of a Colony are used in rolls and have things they automatically can do. It might be simpler to keep track of.<br /> <br /> Unlike Mummy cults Colony actions don't tie up the entire colony too..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with Mummy at all, but I am a fan of simplified rules. Would the Principality unlocks add different things a Colony could automatically do or adjust their Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:52:14-07:00","id":855792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855780#post855780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I kinda like the expanded options and little bit more complexity of individual resources and categories offers. Maybe offer a simplified version, and a more elaborate version? Those who don't care much about the Colony's details (or just want a quicker, more streamlined game) use the simplified rules, while other that focus on Colony use the full rule-set?<br /> <br /> What did you have in mind for more detailed rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mostly the reason for changing is that currently Diplomacy and knowledge don't make sense to have expendable assets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right now I am thinking instead of 5 seperate pools there's one big generic resource pools that can be used for a bunch of things. While the other stats are attributes used in dice rolls. Resources could be used to augmented these rolls like willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> What principalities do in this scenario is unlock more options or improve existing ones.<br /> <br /> For instance you get swarm ranged weapons you can by when you conscript.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or you can open up wormholes using staves3+","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:43:37-07:00","id":855959,"title":"","content":"Quills here!<br /> <br /> I may have gone too far down the &quot;brain is a book&quot; metaphor with these. Also, I'm not sold on the names of Active Power 3, 4, and 5. Or on the Noble Form bonuses. Eh. Drafts.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Quills</b></u><br /> <i>The mind is a mutable thing, and can be transformed and manipulated even by sloppy human science. To a Monarch, a brain is as parchment, able to be read and edited at will.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Active Powers</b><br /> [1] Cryptogram<br /> With little effort, a Monarch can leave secret messages for only a select few to read.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Variable<br /> Duration: Variable<br /> Effect: When creating a message, the Monarch can choose to have it understandable by a finite class of people (such as Monarchs, Diplomats, those who have read a particular book, or the writer). Anyone else reading sees it as gibberish; an extended Intelligence + Academics - the Monarch's Authority + Quills can be made to decipher it if the reader suspects it's something more.<br /> <br /> [2] Treat as Equals<br /> A Monarch can pick another being to mentally communicate with, as though they were both of Endless stock.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant, Contested (optional)<br /> Dice Pool: Presense + Authority vs Composure + Power Trait (can choose not to resist)<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch cannot communicate mentally with the target, and cannot try again with that target for a week.<br /> Failure: The Monarch cannot communicate mentally with the target. She can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: If target is willing, or if the Monarch gains more successes, the Monarch can mentally communicate with the target as though they were both Monarchs. The target's effective authority is equal to their Power Trait or Resolve, whichever is higher. The target cannot communicate telepathically with any other Monarch, only ones that use this power.<br /> Exceptional Success: The effects last for a full day.<br /> <br /> [3] Read Mind<br /> Thoughts are more complex than books, but a Monarch can still leaf through and find what he seeks.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi (1 Psi in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Extended (one roll per minute), Contested (optional)<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Authority vs Resolve + Power Trait (can choose not to resist)<br /> Duration: Variable<br /> Dramatic Failure: The reader becomes the read; the target learns one thing from the Monarch's mind that he'd rather keep hidden.<br /> Failure: The Monarch gains no successes, or fewer than the target, and learns nothing more.<br /> Success: The Monarch gains successes. Based on the information he is trying to find, he needs a certain total. The target experiences the memories as the Noble does, and is not incapacitated by this power.<br /> 1 success: current thoughts, significant events of the last week<br /> 3 successes: common thoughts, significant events of the last year, insignificant events of the last week<br /> 6 successes: hidden or private thoughts, significant older life events, insignificant events of the last year<br /> 10 successes: supressed thoughts, trauma, insignificant older life events<br /> +2 successes: each scene's worth of memories beyond the first<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch makes a great deal of progress, and the target is breifly stunned, losing her next action.<br /> <br /> [4] Supression<br /> At their core, skills are no more than neural connections created through training. A Monarch can strike these connections out, potentially crippling her foes.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant, Resisted<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Authority - Resolve<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: Rather than removing connections, the Monarch reinforces them. The target is immune to any Quills power for the scene.<br /> Failure: The Monarch changes no one's mind. She can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: For each success, the Monarch causes a target to temorarily lose a dot in any Skill. If the target has no dots in the Skill (or no dots remaining), the target loses the ability to use that skill at all, and may suffer other effects at Storyteller disgression (Academics loss makes the target illiterate; Athletics loss causes dangerous clumsiness; Empathy loss supresses facial recognition).<br /> Exceptional Success: No effect beyond further successes.<br /> <br /> [5] Editor<br /> At the height of his power, a Monarch can not only read minds, but change their contents.<br /> Effect: When using Read Mind, the Monarch can choose to edit memories that he reads. After finding a particular memory, the Monarch can change it, requiring further successes based on the degree of change. After editing, the target is convinced her memories are real; only overwhelming evidence can change her mind, causing a Breaking Point in the process.<br /> 1 success: minor detail (one digit in a phone number, someone's hair color, ambient smell)<br /> 3 successes: moderate detail (presense/absense of someone, time of day, prevalent emotion)<br /> 6 succcesses: major detail (changing location, added or removed conversation, motives/rational for actions)<br /> 10 successes: extreme detail (completely erasing a memory, creating a new memory from scratch)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Noble Form Bonuses</b><br /> [1] +2 Empathy<br /> [2] +2 Empathy, +2 Academics<br /> [3] +4 Empathy, +2 Academics<br /> [4] +4 Empathy, +4 Academics<br /> [5] +6 Empathy, +4 Academics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:57:02-07:00","id":855977,"title":"","content":"Suppression's very creative. I don't think I've ever seen a power that can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:06:43-07:00","id":855984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855977#post855977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppression's very creative. I don't think I've ever seen a power that can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It came from Vent0's idea about granting skills, but flipped to make it a weapon. Plus, there are syndromes caused by neural trauma that do things like destroy abilities to read, or recognize faces, or recognize half of the world, or have a sense of self. Which fits super well with brain-mucking powers. I guess if the power line is supposed to be more positive/nicer, it could be changed to boost/teach, or to do both, but that might get too powerful. Plus Scribes/Diplomats aren't getting any of the damage-focused powers, they need some way to be nasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 03-30-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:07:19-07:00","id":855986,"title":"","content":"Really leery about 5 - it kinda tramples over Crowns'/Scepters' conceptual space.<br /> <br /> Other Quill related ideas (of unknown dot levels):<ul><li>The ability to write a message that is immediately understood by a certain class of beings. Not a secret message, like 1. More of a transmission or Proclamation, conveying the message to all concerned (secret messages passed instantly to allies, instantly notifying your &quot;tenants&quot; as to your decrees/laws, whispering campaigns spreading an foe's secrets to their enemies, alerting all Monarchs in the area of a threat, trash-talking to opposing organizations, etc.).</li> <li>Disrupting communications between foes - words, body langauge, etc. Though this kind of steps on the Tower of Babel Embed. Might even work against another Monarch's over control over their Colony (something few suspect Quills, seen as a benign power, is capable of). Like Suppression, but interpersonal.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-30-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:14:28-07:00","id":855992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855986#post855986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really leery about 5 - it kinda tramples over Crowns'/Scepters' conceptual space.<br /> <br /> Other Quill related ideas (of unknown dot levels):<ul><li>The ability to write a message that is immediately understood by a certain class of beings. Not a secret message, like 1. More of a transmission or Proclamation, conveying the message to all concerned (secret messages passed instantly to allies, instantly notifying your &quot;tenants&quot; as to your decrees/laws, whispering campaigns spreading an foe's secrets to their enemies, alerting all Monarchs in the area of a threat, etc.).</li> <li>Disrupting communications between foes - words, body langauge, etc. Though this kind of steps on the Tower of Babel Embed. Might even work against another Monarch's over control over their Colony (something few suspect Quills, seen as a benign power, is capable of). Like Suppression, but interpersonal.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think memory edits infringe on Scepters (except in the sense that Scepters is Dominate, and Dominate gives memory editing IIRC). Crowns, maybe, but I didn't envision Crowns as being that direct.<br /> <br /> I had intended that Cryptogram also meant whoever it was meant for also automatically understood it. Can edit to make that explicit.<br /> <br /> I do like the disruption idea. Although that sort of thing could also fall under Crowns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:24:28-07:00","id":856002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=855992#post855992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think memory edits infringe on Scepters (except in the sense that Scepters is Dominate, and Dominate gives memory editing IIRC). Crowns, maybe, but I didn't envision Crowns as being that direct.<br /> <br /> I had intended that Cryptogram also meant whoever it was meant for also automatically understood it. Can edit to make that explicit.<br /> <br /> I do like the disruption idea. Although that sort of thing could also fall under Crowns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I read Cryptogram as basically Special Message (only designated targets understand the message once they see it). What I was proposing was open transmission - if some Kindred is giving you problem, you active [Proclamation] and let every &quot;Hunter&quot; or &quot;Cainite Heresy member&quot; in the area know where their Haven is - whether you know who or where those people are.<br /> <br /> Regrading eveything else... this is where I see cross-Principality powers coming in handy. Mind Editing? Scepters + Quills. Disrupt Communications? Crowns + Quills. Words Can Break My Bones? Bows + Quills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:43:33-07:00","id":856185,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if memory editing is needed to primarily be in quills but it certainly could be a cross principality thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing to note, not every power needs 5 or even 4 powers even the high magical ones. They could have other passive bonuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Second. I have decided I don't like skill bonuses since they feel like they replace skills or even surpass when in noble form. Instead what about dice tricks like 8 or 9 again. Or preventing opponents from using dice tricks. Or use rote action or something when using willpower instead of +3. Or rerolls when total failures happen<br /> This way the principalities work with existing skills and have more synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:59:34-07:00","id":856476,"title":"","content":"Really rough draft of modified Colony rules. Looking at converting zombie swarm rules made by Claire into something usable for us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>New Trait: Colony </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Monarchs are tended to by many lesser creatures, all various strains of the Endless made to serve her. They act as everything from a labor force, a private army, personal servants, and everything in between, all at her beck and call. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traditionally, Colonies are located in Beneath, a place underground that skirts between realworld location and alternate reality, usually accessed through wormholes or through spatially folded physical locations. As a general rule a Monarch may access or pull forces from her Colony from any Wormholes from her own Court or via physically entering the Beneath through the realspace anchors of her Colony. Generally speaking, Wormholes are safer and more expensive, but the anchor point of a Colony is a vulnerability that anyone with the knowledge can find.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But as many servants and warriors a Monarch is able to own, there are limits to how much this force can do, its capabilities, its ability to replenish losses, its own lacks from incomplete Geneweb, and other factors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies are represented by five attributes, each representing an estimation of the Colony\u2019s abilities at given tasks. These are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Military</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Knowledge</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Industry</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Espionage</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Diplomacy</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All are rated from 1 to 10, with a single dot in each at the start, plus an extra dot in the Monarch\u2019s primary area of focus. Raising Colony Attributes is a single merit dot.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At any time, a Monarch or Servant may order the Colony to dispatch a unit of Drones to fulfill an assigned task, rolling one of the attributes above for the dice pool for an appropriate task. Alternatively, there are few tasks that can be done without a dice roll. Colonies have some basic default Tasks, with more being unlocked as the Monarch grows in Principalities.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aside from attributes, Colonies possess a resource pool called Wealth, representing the total output of the Monarch\u2019s controlled Territory and resource harvesting abilities.. Wealth has no real cap, but it does not replenish in the middle of the Chronicle. Territories will be detailed later in their own section.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Starting Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Conscription </i> Create an army. Swarm rules with \u201csuccesses\u201d as points to spend on improving. Spending Wealth allows you to add extra points ontop of it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spy </i> Spy on a target.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Create: Raw Resources </i> </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch commands his industrial centres to synthesize materials or commodities, either to trade with another colony, for an individual construction project or simply to supply Swarms or Servants working in the field. This can only create raw materials or form them into simple shapes. For example, this could be used to produce blocks of stone but not a statue.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Although the process used to enact this ability are a combination of biological factories and psi-chemistry that can produce most anything from most anything else the Storyteller may limit exceedingly rare materials such as precious metals or gems. Bear in mind that things produced through Create: Raw Resources will not necessarily be a perfect copy of their earthly counterparts. Wood will behave similarly but might not have a grain or rings.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The amount of points that must be spent to create a given resource is dependent upon the rarity, complexity and desired bulk of the final product. (Edit to accomidate new mechanics.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Note: \u201cCreate\u201d</b> has multiple uses, with Principalities unlocking more things to create. For now, only basic harvesting is available.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Research</i> Study a topic via experimentation or knowledge. \u201cPassively\u201d roll dice for extended research actions? Spend Wealth for bonuses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence</i> Something involving propaganda or political maneuvers.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-31-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:19:00-07:00","id":856571,"title":"","content":"But I <i>like</i> every dot getting a power :P<br /> <br /> Created an alternate dot-5 for Quills; re-worded the first dot; modified Noble Form powers to give -agains instead of flat bonuses; everything else is a re-post. Personally, I think there should be some kind of pattern to Noble Form benefits, something like: each dot gets a new bonus. Bonuses can be Attributes, Skills, or Traits. Each Principality gets two, and aren't shared by any other. One bonus starts at the first dot; the other at the second dot. Attributes increase by 1 every other level. Skills gain a greater -again every other level (9-again --&gt; 8-again --&gt; rote). Traits increase by 2 every other level. Stuff that doesn't fall into those categories should go into Active Powers, given a dot rating, and be made free (or cheaper) when in Noble Form.<br /> <br /> As for colony mechanics, I like them. I'm at a loss as to what conscription does, though (the rest I can see how to mechanize, but &quot;conscription&quot; is vague: is the Colony gearing up its own parts for war, or picking up fodder from the local populace, or building weapons/armor, or what?).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Quills</b></u><br /> <i>The mind is a mutable thing, and can be transformed and manipulated even by sloppy human science. To a Monarch, a brain is as parchment, able to be read at will.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Active Powers</b><br /> [1]<i> Cryptogram</i><br /> With little effort, a Monarch can leave secret messages for only a select few to read.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Effect: When creating a message, the Monarch can choose to have it understandable by a finite class of people (such as Monarchs, Diplomats, a single Court, those who have read a particular book, those who hunt vampires, those who can talk to spirits, only the writer, etc.). Anyone else reading sees it as gibberish; an extended Intelligence + Academics - the Monarch's Authority + Quills can be made to decipher it if the reader suspects the nonsense is something more. This power lasts as long as the message exists.<br /> <br /> [2] <i>Treat as Equals</i><br /> A Monarch can pick another being to mentally communicate with, as though they were both of Endless stock.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant, Contested (optional)<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Authority vs Composure + Power Trait (can choose not to resist)<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch cannot communicate mentally with the target, and cannot try again with that target for a week.<br /> Failure: The Monarch cannot communicate mentally with the target. She can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: If target is willing, or if the Monarch gains more successes, the Monarch can mentally communicate with the target as though they were both Monarchs. The target's effective authority is equal to their Power Trait or Resolve, whichever is higher. The target cannot communicate telepathically with any other Monarch, only ones that use this power.<br /> Exceptional Success: The effects last for a full day.<br /> <br /> [3] <i>Read Mind</i><br /> Thoughts are more complex than books, but a Monarch can still leaf through and find what he seeks.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi (1 Psi in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Extended (one roll per minute), Contested (optional)<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Authority vs Resolve + Power Trait (can choose not to resist)<br /> Duration: Variable<br /> Dramatic Failure: The reader becomes the read; the target learns one thing from the Monarch's mind that he'd rather keep hidden.<br /> Failure: The Monarch gains no successes, or fewer than the target, and learns nothing more.<br /> Success: The Monarch gains successes. Based on the information he is trying to find, he needs a certain total. The target experiences the memories as the Noble does, and is not incapacitated by this power.<br /> 1 success: current thoughts, significant events of the last week<br /> 3 successes: common thoughts, significant events of the last year, insignificant events of the last week<br /> 6 successes: hidden or private thoughts, significant older life events, insignificant events of the last year<br /> 10 successes: suppressed thoughts, trauma, insignificant older life events<br /> +2 successes: each scene's worth of memories beyond the first<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch makes a great deal of progress, and the target is briefly stunned, losing her next action.<br /> <br /> [4] <i>Suppression</i><br /> At their core, skills are no more than neural connections created through training. A Monarch can strike these connections out, potentially crippling her foes.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant, Resisted<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Authority - Resolve<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: Rather than removing connections, the Monarch reinforces them. The target is immune to any Quills power for the scene.<br /> Failure: The Monarch changes no one's mind. She can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: For each success, the Monarch causes a target to temporarily lose a dot in any Skill. If the target has no dots in the Skill (or no dots remaining), the target loses the ability to use that skill at all, and may suffer other effects at Storyteller discretion (Academics loss makes the target illiterate; Athletics loss causes dangerous clumsiness; Empathy loss removes facial recognition).<br /> Exceptional Success: No effect beyond further successes.<br /> <br /> [5] <i>Hive Mind</i><br /> At the height of his power, a Monarch can not only read minds, but connect them to each other. This provides a staggering benefit for those connected, allowing them to share knowledge, skills, and even Principalities.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi (1 in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant, Contested (optional)<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Authority vs. Resolve + Power Trait (can choose not to resist)<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: Mental feedback severs the connection before it's formed. The Monarch takes three resistant lethal damage, and suffers from the Insensate Tilt for Authority rounds.<br /> Failure: The minds remain unlinked. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: The Monarch connects his mind to another, on a deeper level than mere telepathy. This provides all the benefits of normal telepathy, as well as the ability to borrow dots in Skills and Principalities. Only one Skill or Principality can be borrowed in a turn, and the total dots borrowed per turn cannot exceed the Successes on this roll. The Skill or Principality can be changed on the user's turn as a Reflexive action, and borrowing a Skill or Principality does not cause it to be removed from the borrowed-from. Additionally, both the Monarch and the target can read each other's minds as though they used Read Mind with 2*successes.<br /> The Monarch can choose to link multiple minds. Each mind beyond the first gives a cumulative -2 penalty to the roll. Targets can borrow from any mind linked, not just the Monarch's.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and two different Skills or Principalities can be borrowed at a time. The total dots borrowed cannot exceed successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Noble Form Bonuses</b><br /> [1] 9-again Empathy<br /> [2] 9-again Empathy, 9-again Academics<br /> [3] 8-again Empathy, 9-again Academics<br /> [4] 8-again Empathy, 8-again Academics<br /> [5] Rote Empathy, 8-again Academics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:17:11-07:00","id":856608,"title":"","content":"I made some typos. I'll be clarifying later today. Nice work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the noble form benefits I suppose I agree. I'll look to making a standardized set today. Semi standardized....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:30:39-07:00","id":856719,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also, revised previous post on Colony Prototype<br /> <br /> Swarm mechanics meant you rolled Military to define build points, for some reason it went to Spy...<br /> <br /> <br /> -------<br /> Almost all Principalities awaken something within the Monarch, increased mental or physical faculties or awareness into topics while in Noble form. The growth of these topics or understandings however can be quite confusing for players.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Principality may have one or two things that they improve upon, the speed of this growth determined within the Principality itself. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The three speeds are:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Greater, the fastest growth rate which uses the leftmost column of the tables below</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lesser, the average growth rate which uses the middle column of the tables below</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Least, the slowest growth rate which uses the rightmost column of the tables below</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Below are tables referencing the specific bonuses that a specific dot rating for a Principality would offer.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bonuses are noncumilative within the same Principality, though other Principalities might be cumalitive depending on the bonus. I.E. Bows 2 does not mean mean you have +2 Dexterity because you possess both Bows 1 and Bows 2, but Blades 5 can contribute Dexterity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attribute, the Principality increases raw Attributes which can affect base statistics. This stacks with other Principalities that raise the attributes.</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 624px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dots</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Greater</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lesser</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Least</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">0</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+0</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">+0</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">00</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+0</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">+0</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">000</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+0</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">0000</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+0</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">00000</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skill, the Principality confers advantages when using specific skills. This does not stack with other Principalities that raise the same skills, nor does it affect base attributes.</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 