> </div> </div> </div>Cruel isn't he. And just as I was having a nice cup of orange juice too. I'll have to clean off my keyboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:16:13-07:00","id":857137,"title":"","content":"Worth it.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the keyboard, but it is kinda the point of the holiday to troll everyone you know and love in hilarious manners.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, back to work I gues.<br /> anyone see the concept posted above?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-01-2016, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:30:31-07:00","id":857142,"title":"","content":"Well you know it's a real shame this is being shut down because I came up with a new Principality. The Principality of Pantaloons.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Pantaloons</b></u><br /> <i>For all a Noble's noble nobility, there is no task more respected than that of clowning. Monarchs with this rare gift weaponize the absurd, the comedic, the hilarious, to strike down their ignoble Noble rivals.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Active Powers</b><br /> [1] The Phantom Fart<br /> Bad smells and loud noises are funny, particularly when someone else is making them. The Monarch can compell farts, belches, and other embarassing bodily effects.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Authority<br /> Duration: Variable<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch lets one rip. A real one. Ewwww.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens. More beans needed. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: The Monarch chooses one embarassing bodily sound or oder to come from the target per success. This can be burps, farts, BO, or other funny things.<br /> Exceptional Success: No benefit beyond multiple successes.<br /> <br /> [2] Master of the Pants<br /> Underwear is funny, okay? And butts are funnier. So being able to manipulate that which covers the deriere is critical for the budding Pantaloons Monarch.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Authority<br /> Duration: Concentration<br /> Dramatic Failure: The pants turn on their master. All undergarments in the scene attempt to smother the Monarch, doing two bashing.<br /> Failure: The pants remain unbroken. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: With a thought, the Monarch can control any and all pants, shorts, underwear, skirts, slacks, kilts, boxers, or other form of clothing designed to cover the butt in the scene. The Monarch can cause the article to force the wearer to walk, bend, or dance, as well as cause the clothing to fall down or disappear.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch's control extends to any pies, soda water, or scarves in the area.<br /> <br /> [3] Giggle Loop<br /> Laughter, like yawning, is contagious. Laughter, like hiccups, is hard to stop. A Monarch can cause everone, including herself, to become caught in a cycle of laughter, incapacitating them.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: (5 - Composure) + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The giggle loop breaks down. Everyone is shocked and appalled by the fact that the Monarch tried to make this funny. -3 to all social rolls for the scene.<br /> Failure: Nobody's laughing. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: The Monarch giggles. Someone else gwafaws. Still another chortles. Then everyone breaks out into laughter. No one can take any aggressive action while the giggle loop is in effect. That wouldn't be funny. Instead, any aggression is channeled into trying to one-up whatever made everyone laugh. <br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch can control who falls prey to the dreaded giggle loop.<br /> <br /> [4] Interrupting MOO<br /> A large part of humor is surprise and the unexpected. A Monarch can literally summon the unlikely, as long as it's funny. Meta is betta.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Effect: If a player mishears a word, and it makes the scene hilarious, a Psi can be spent to make that word be what actually was said, impacting the scene accordingly. Alternatively, the player can come up with a hilarious pun, reference, or absurdity, and similarly impact the scene.<br /> <br /> [5] Joke Warfare<br /> Wenn ist das Nunst\u00fcck git und Slotermeyer? Ja! Beiherhund das Oder die Flipperwaldt gersput!<br /> Cost: 0 Psi<br /> Action: Three rounds<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Effect: Speak the words aloud. Any who hear it die. Due to the psychic nature of Monarchs, anyone who hears the joke can understand it.<br /> <br /> <b>Noble Form Bonuses</b><br /> [1] 9-again on all joke-telling<br /> [2] 9-again on all joke-telling, +1 to pretending you meant to do that<br /> [3] 8-again on all joke-telling, +1 to pretending you meant to do that<br /> [4] 8-again on all joke-telling, +2 to pretending you meant to do that<br /> [5] Rote on all joke-telling, +2 to pretending you meant to do that, 9-again on running away from the ST because your puns were so bad<br /> <br /> <b>Colony Powers</b><br /> [1] All colony members become colored like clown triggerfish<br /> [2] Prank task: have your Colony set up an elaborate practical joke (saran wrapping everything in a building, painting a town red, moving everything three inches to the right)<br /> [3] Colony members can use Giggle Loop<br /> [4] Colony members may instead be colored in the manner of other clown traditions<br /> [5] Colony members can use Joke Warfare","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:38:51-07:00","id":857147,"title":"","content":"Monty Python? Really? How dare you pull out such revolving and stale humor.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:58:47-07:00","id":858173,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The following rules are adapted from the zombie swarm rules in Claire Redfields\u2019s Zombie Creation Project upgraded into GMC, which were originated and modified, FWC, which in turn are adapted from the 1st edition rules and David Hill's excellent swarm form rules for <b>Vampire</b>. Basically, this is similar to what Valve does with the Source Engine with many authors copying and modifying a base system in succession.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Swarms</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every Monarch has the power of a nation at her beck and call, able to conjure up actual </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>armies </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">to slaughter her enemies. Whereas many other forces in the supernatural world rely on small, more hardened and better trained forces, even really powerful guardians, the Endless live up to their name and send uncountable numbers against their foes. To truly understand the Wrath of the Endless, is to face a tidal wave of chitin and scale: the Swarm.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swarms possess traits similar to those of ephemeral beings, including a Rank, three broad Attributes and Advantages. While some ephemeral entities like spirits can form into swarms, such things are best handled by their own specific rules. A swarm\u2019s Rank is not a measure of its supernatural power (and doesn\u2019t act as Supernatural Tolerance), but rather its size and durability. Like ephemeral beings, a swarm\u2019s traits technically range from 1-10, but rarely ever surpass Rank 5. A swarm possesses <b>Power</b>, <b>Finesse</b>, and <b>Resistance </b>Attributes, like ephemeral beings.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Power </b>governs the swarm\u2019s raw strength when it exerts itself and ability to overcome victims, but most swarms have relatively low <b>Power</b>.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Finesse </b>describes how mobile the swarm is, and how well it can get around things like barriers.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Resistance </b>represents the swarm\u2019s overall durability to harm and environmental conditions.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike other Swarms, Endless Swarms are capable of Mental and Social interaction, largely as a result of having a number of \u201celite\u201d Foremen or even more elite and powerful Servants acting as figureheads and controllers. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to create a Swarm, a Monarch orders a Conscription, ordering her Colony to mass produce new fighters, allocate resources to producing more fighters, or even temporarily suspending other preexisting Drones and ordering them to fight...</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She rolls her Colony\u2019s Military + Authority, successes translating to a size from the chart below, where the Monarch is able to assemble a Swarm of the appropriate size and allocate attribute dots as she desires.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower may not be spent on this roll, but each point of Wealth spent on Conscription adds 1 dice to the roll.</span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\"><b>Rank</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\"><b>Trait Limits</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\"><b>Attribute Dots</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\"><b>Free Aspects</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\"><b>Swarm Size</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">1 dot</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">1-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">2 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">2-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">3 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">4-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">4 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">8-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">5 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">13</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">16-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">6 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">16</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">32-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">7 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">19</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">64-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">8 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">22</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">128-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">9 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">25</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">256-yard radius</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">10 dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">28</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 2px\">512-yard radius</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Advantages</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swarms don\u2019t have Integrity traits, Virtues and Vices, or Willpower. They are mindless agglomerations of frenzied creatures. Neither do they have a Size trait, since they are treated as a single entity rather than individual creatures. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of Numina, they have Aspects, special abilities bestowed to them from their Monarch representing unique powers, special equipment, or other factors.. Unlike for a regular Swarm, there\u2019s no limit to the number of Aspects a Swarm may take. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, gaining Swarm Aspects requires that the Monarch has Principalities that allow for them. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second, each Aspect makes the Swarm more expensive to field, thus in order to save costs and be efficient, the number of fighters has to drop, in essence, shrinking the Swarm to give it more capabilities.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thankfully, larger more powerful Swarms have some leeway into how many Aspects they may have largely due to the advantages of mass production and redundancy. In the Swarm table, it lists the number of Aspects a Swarm of a given size may field without it impacting the Swarm\u2019s size. Each Aspect above that limit requires that the Swarm shrinks by 1 rank or size category. It does not gain the Free Aspects of its new size category, but does gain the Trait limits and attribute dots of the new category.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Health: </b>A swarm\u2019s Health is equal to its Rank + Resistance.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiative: </b>Initiative is equal to Finesse.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Defense: </b>Defense is equal to Power or Finesse, whichever is higher.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Speed: </b>Speed is equal to Power + Finesse + a species factor. Take an average species factor if the swarm is composed of multiple creatures, like insects and spiders. Swarms possess any special movement abilities of the base creature, like flight or wall-crawling.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fighting the Swarm</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swarms attack by surrounding their prey and suffocating, biting and stinging them to death. Everyone caught in the swarm suffers from panic and limited visibility and hearing. Victims suffer the persistent Distracted Condition until they escape. A swarm rolls its Power to attack. The swarm can condense its size by one or more Ranks to increase the damage done by an additional die per step. For example, a Rank 4 swarm (8-yard radius) with Power 2 could condense into a 1-yard swarm and attack a single target with 5 dice. Condensing like this leaves the swarm more vulnerable, and swarms cannot swell to larger size Ranks. For each step by which it condenses, add one die to any attacker\u2019s dice pool. Only full-body armor protects against the swarm, and then only at half its rating. Defense does not apply, though supernatural powers like Celerity work normally. Damage caused by Endless Swarms is lethal.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swarms are difficult to harm. After rolling attacks against the swarm as normal, factoring in armor and other modifiers, the swarm takes one point of damage of the appropriate type, or two points with an exceptional success. Damage suffered reduces its Health. Fire, explosions, chemical sprays and other area effects cause normal damage or even no damage depending on the circumstances and the opponent. The swarm\u2019s maximum Rank is limited by its Health, so as it takes damage, the swarm shrinks in size. Past rank 6, only especially potent or wide reaching fire, explosions, or chemical attacks would do normal, the swarm having grown to enormous size and having become nigh impregnable to even area of affect weapons. At rank 6, even area of effect weapons may only do 1 point of damage or even no damage, while other types of weapons do no damage without special caveats. Also, at really extreme numerical differences, the GM may decide to resolve combat with only a single roll such as with Down and Dirty Combat. In such cases, the Swarm adds its Rank to the roll.<br /> Against other swarms, both do full damage to each other.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Endless Swarms Summary</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Able to Mentally and Socially interact.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Are telepathic and subservient to Monarchs, are able to rebel if necessary.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Formed by Conscription (Colony Military + Monarch Authority), each success dictating size. Wealth may be spent for a +1 bonus to this roll.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-03-2016, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T01:17:00-07:00","id":858215,"title":"","content":"Now that's what i'm talking about for an alien swarm. Looks like fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:07:17-07:00","id":859052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/859045-conspiracy-guardians-haans-chowdhury-productions-power-armored-and-mech-using-hunters#post859045\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/859045-conspiracy-guardians-haans-chowdhury-productions-power-armored-and-mech-using-hunters#post859045\"> [Conspiracy] Guardians/Haans-Chowdhury Productions, Power Armored and Mech using Hunters - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/859045-conspiracy-guardians-haans-chowdhury-productions-power-armored-and-mech-using-hunters#post859045\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/859045-conspiracy-guardians-haans-chowdhury-productions-power-armored-and-mech-using-hunters#post859045 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Guardians/ Haans-Chowdhury Productions The alien and eldritch Endless and their Monarchs were not the first to come to this world; the Geodics laid that claim long </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> And this is finally up. Maybe I'll do Geodics next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone want to tackle Censers next? I think that'll be somewhat of a problem maybe .... I'm thinking pheremones among other things would be what it'll operate by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:09:49-07:00","id":859054,"title":"","content":"Y'know, I really like the Swarm rules. It's got the right balance of simplicity and realism. I might be more forgiving when it came to AoE attacks, simply because CofD in general doesn't really have them (it tends to be either individual attacks or Environmental Tilts, not a lot in between).<br /> <br /> Jumping back a topic, I'm not as sold on the Principality bonuses. If there's a tertiary thing, I think it should start at the 3rd dot, regardless of which thing it's for, and increase every two. (Also, I kinda like having Greater/Medial/Lesser or something similar as names, rather than Greater/Lesser/Least). Of course, this makes 3 and 5 more valuable dots, as they get two increases rather than one, so maybe tertiary things shouldn't be a thing, or the increase should be every three.<br /> <br /> Counter-proposal with tertiary traits: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Attributes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Skills</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Derived Traits</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1/0/0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9-again/-/-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1/0/0</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1/1/0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9-again/9-again/-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2/1/0</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2/1/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8-again/9-again/9-again</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3/2/1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2/2/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8-again/8-again/9-again</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4/3/2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3/2/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">rote/8-again/8-again</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5/4/3</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I could try Censors; I had quite a few ideas for Crowns and Scepters, too. Pheromones, smokescreens, asphyxiation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:19:17-07:00","id":859057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859054#post859054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, I really like the Swarm rules. It's got the right balance of simplicity and realism. I might be more forgiving when it came to AoE attacks, simply because CofD in general doesn't really have them (it tends to be either individual attacks or Environmental Tilts, not a lot in between).<br /> <br /> Jumping back a topic, I'm not as sold on the Principality bonuses. If there's a tertiary thing, I think it should start at the 3rd dot, regardless of which thing it's for, and increase every two. (Also, I kinda like having Greater/Medial/Lesser or something similar as names, rather than Greater/Lesser/Least). Of course, this makes 3 and 5 more valuable dots, as they get two increases rather than one, so maybe tertiary things shouldn't be a thing, or the increase should be every three.<br /> <br /> Counter-proposal with tertiary traits: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Attributes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Skills</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Derived Traits</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1/0/0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9-again/-/-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1/0/0</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1/1/0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9-again/9-again/-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2/1/0</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2/1/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8-again/9-again/9-again</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3/2/1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2/2/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8-again/8-again/9-again</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4/3/2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3/2/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">rote/8-again/8-again</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5/4/3</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I could try Censors; I had quite a few ideas for Crowns and Scepters, too. Pheromones, smokescreens, asphyxiation...</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme of breath should definately be explored there.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sold on my &quot;chart&quot; either. It's mostly something to prototype. My thought was to basically have an &quot;as level X- 2&quot; or &quot;-4&quot; for Lesser or Least to simplify the math. I realized it made things too... loaded at the last dot, but I wanted feedback on it before I decided to scrap or redo it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what do you mean by &quot;Tetrary&quot;? Just in case there's not a communication failure.<br /> <br /> Most Princeps, in my veiw would have 2 things they boosted and what they were was mostly attributes, skills, or other traits... with them having different &quot;growth speeds&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:52:36-07:00","id":859079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859057#post859057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The theme of breath should definately be explored there.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sold on my &quot;chart&quot; either. It's mostly something to prototype. My thought was to basically have an &quot;as level X- 2&quot; or &quot;-4&quot; for Lesser or Least to simplify the math. I realized it made things too... loaded at the last dot, but I wanted feedback on it before I decided to scrap or redo it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what do you mean by &quot;Tetrary&quot;? Just in case there's not a communication failure.<br /> <br /> Most Princeps, in my veiw would have 2 things they boosted and what they were was mostly attributes, skills, or other traits... with them having different &quot;growth speeds&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;tertiary&quot; I meant the third benefit in the set, the &quot;Least&quot; one. I feel like having it only show up at the fifth dot is both loaded, and a little messy in the sense that it's an added on mechanic that only comes up at high levels that a player may not reach more than once (depending on how they buy things). Also, if only some Principalities are getting third/Least benefits, how is that determined? I personally can't think of a fair and consistent way to arbitrate which would get a third and which wouldn't.<br /> <br /> If there's three, I like the &quot;as level-1&quot; and &quot;as level-2&quot; for the second and third benefit rates better. If more Principalities would not have a Least benefit, I'm more in favor of saying none of them do, so it's consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:57:38-07:00","id":859083,"title":"","content":"The least thing is just a matter of progression speed rather than principalities having 3 progressions in each.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's possible for Principalities to have Greater-Median, Greater-least, Median-Least, or just one of Least, Median, or Greater.<br /> <br /> The reason why Least exists is to make for a slight bonus in cases where giving Median might be too much or to make slight bonuses distributed in multiple places rather than having certain Principalities give bigger boosts<br /> For instance say Spheres, Reagents, and hammers all possess a least Intelligence component and there no Principality that offers Greater or median Intelligence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:09:42-07:00","id":859089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859083#post859083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The least thing is just a matter of progression speed rather than principalities having 3 progressions in each.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's possible for Principalities to have Greater-Median, Greater-least, Median-Least, or just one of Least, Median, or Greater.<br /> <br /> The reason why Least exists is to make for a slight bonus in cases where giving Median might be too much or to make slight bonuses distributed in multiple places rather than having certain Principalities give bigger boosts<br /> For instance say Spheres, Reagents, and hammers all possess a least Intelligence component and there no Principality that offers Greater or median Intelligence</div> </div> </div> </div>How would that determination be made? How does one decide which Principality gets a Median and Least, as opposed to a Greater and Median? Why would Intelligence be out of the consideration for Greater?<br /> <br /> I had assumed that each Principality would get one of each progression (one Greater, Medial, and Lesser). I assumed this because I wanted each Principality to be balanced with the others in the sense that no Principality got more/less than any other (in terms of raw numbers, and leaving aside the variable value-judgements one could make about what Attribute/Skill/Derived Trait is better or worse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:18:41-07:00","id":859095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859089#post859089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would that determination be made? How does one decide which Principality gets a Median and Least, as opposed to a Greater and Median? Why would Intelligence be out of the consideration for Greater?<br /> <br /> I had assumed that each Principality would get one of each progression (one Greater, Medial, and Lesser). I assumed this because I wanted each Principality to be balanced with the others in the sense that no Principality got more/less than any other (in terms of raw numbers, and leaving aside the variable value-judgements one could make about what Attribute/Skill/Derived Trait is better or worse).</div> </div> </div> </div>The balancing factor would be based on how many powers or other bonuses you got. <br /> <br /> When I first envisioned principalities it was mostly going to influence attribute bonuses or increase statistics like say size. With the exception of physical principalities of bows blades and shield, attribute or trait gains were a consolation prize to avoid empty levels or for when most of the gains were in colony based actions rather than something inherent to you.<br /> <br /> After ajf pushed for the speed boosts on cloaks and you added skill bonuses to the stuff you made things were different. And it's my fault for failing to communicate the intention of Monarch progression since the original principalities were all inherently physical<br /> <br /> I suppose before we continue, we need to make a decision on what route we go...<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on that matter?<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't mind scaling back the noble form benefits to make them more special and less all encompassing. More closer to the original intents<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't mind going with the route proposed so far if that's what you feel needs to happen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:57:15-07:00","id":859117,"title":"","content":"Perhaps for the meanwhile, we do not put in Noble form benefits until later on in development, when all of the principalities are done, just to see if there's any obvious differences in power level that we could adjust, see if we really need them....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:01:15-07:00","id":859123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859095#post859095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The balancing factor would be based on how many powers or other bonuses you got.<br /> <br /> When I first envisioned principalities it was mostly going to influence attribute bonuses or increase statistics like say size. With the exception of physical principalities of bows blades and shield, attribute or trait gains were a consolation prize to avoid empty levels or for when most of the gains were in colony based actions rather than something inherent to you.<br /> <br /> After ajf pushed for the speed boosts on cloaks and you added skill bonuses to the stuff you made things were different. And it's my fault for failing to communicate the intention of Monarch progression since the original principalities were all inherently physical<br /> <br /> I suppose before we continue, we need to make a decision on what route we go...<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on that matter?<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't mind scaling back the noble form benefits to make them more special and less all encompassing. More closer to the original intents<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't mind going with the route proposed so far if that's what you feel needs to happen</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Blades et al did throw me off, since it had boosts at every level.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm fine with having Noble Form benefits alternate or fill in where Colony benefits don't show up. I'm also fine with getting a Noble Form, Colony, and Power at each dot. And I'm also fine with dropping the Noble Form benefits entirely and leaving that sort of thing to Castes.<br /> <br /> But it should be consistent. Assuming it goes the &quot;fill in&quot; route, if Blades, Bows, and Shields are getting Noble Form benefits at every dot, they shouldn't be getting any Colony benefits. If they get Noble Form benefits at every level, as well as Colony powers, so should the other Principalities. <br /> <br /> In terms of working on things, the &quot;fill in&quot; option is easiest from a &quot;thinking of ideas to fill the levels&quot; perspective. If an Attribute is added instead of a Colony benefit, the first time, it increases by 1 each time (cumulative). If it's a Skill, go from 9-again to 8-again to rote; for a Trait, increase by 2 each time (cumulative).<br /> <br /> Example 1: Blades<br /> [1] +1 Strength<br /> [2] 9-again Weaponry<br /> [3] Colongy: Double successes from Conscription <br /> [4] +1 Strength<br /> [5] 8-again Weaponry<br /> <br /> Example 2: Quills<br /> [1] 9-again Empathy<br /> [2] Colony: Espionage tasks are rote<br /> [3] 8-again Empathy<br /> [4] Colony: can use Read Minds on Espionage targets<br /> [5] rote Empathy<br /> <br /> Example 3: Cloaks<br /> [1] Colony: double Speed<br /> [2] +2 Speed<br /> [3] Colony: can fly<br /> [4] +2 Speed<br /> [5] +1 Dexterity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:08:02-07:00","id":859127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859123#post859123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see. Blades et al did throw me off, since it had boosts at every level.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm fine with having Noble Form benefits alternate or fill in where Colony benefits don't show up. I'm also fine with getting a Noble Form, Colony, and Power at each dot. And I'm also fine with dropping the Noble Form benefits entirely and leaving that sort of thing to Castes.<br /> <br /> But it should be consistent. Assuming it goes the &quot;fill in&quot; route, if Blades, Bows, and Shields are getting Noble Form benefits at every dot, they shouldn't be getting any Colony benefits. If they get Noble Form benefits at every level, as well as Colony powers, so should the other Principalities. <br /> <br /> In terms of working on things, the &quot;fill in&quot; option is easiest from a &quot;thinking of ideas to fill the levels&quot; perspective. If an Attribute is added instead of a Colony benefit, the first time, it increases by 1 each time (cumulative). If it's a Skill, go from 9-again to 8-again to rote; for a Trait, increase by 2 each time (cumulative).<br /> <br /> Example 1: Blades<br /> [1] +1 Strength<br /> [2] 9-again Weaponry<br /> [3] Colongy: Double successes from Conscription <br /> [4] +1 Strength<br /> [5] 8-again Weaponry<br /> <br /> Example 2: Quills<br /> [1] 9-again Empathy<br /> [2] Colony: Espionage tasks are rote<br /> [3] 8-again Empathy<br /> [4] Colony: can use Read Minds on Espionage targets<br /> [5] rote Empathy<br /> <br /> Example 3: Cloaks<br /> [1] Colony: double Speed<br /> [2] +2 Speed<br /> [3] Colony: can fly<br /> [4] +2 Speed<br /> [5] +1 Dexterity</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something worth noting. After writing up the Swarm rules, one thing that I'm Definately going to put is that every Principality also provides atleast one Aspect, the first is also going to be 1st dot and always written so that it scales to get better with higher dots.<br /> <br /> Second colony benefits is mostly about unlocking new actions colonies can take.... rather than making rote or improving existing ones. But this may change most likely.... eh for now assume there are no colony benefits that factor into principalities for now<br /> <br /> Also going to make the dice pool colony attribute and authority for all colony actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:13:15-07:00","id":859130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859127#post859127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Something worth noting. After writing up the Swarm rules, one thing that I'm Definately going to put is that every Principality also provides atleast one Aspect, the first is also going to be 1st dot and always written so that it scales to get better with higher dots.<br /> <br /> Second colony benefits is mostly about unlocking new actions colonies can take.... rather than making rote or improving existing ones.<br /> <br /> Also going to make the dice pool colony attribute and authority for all colony actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure what you mean by Aspect, but it sounds like something that starts at the first dot, then increases each dot. Which could be counted as a separate benefit for Principalities.<br /> <br /> The Colony stuff I put was meant as a placeholder, more to show how the benefits could vary between Principalities (lots of Noble Form vs lots of Colony vs a balance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:19:31-07:00","id":859134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859130#post859130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite sure what you mean by Aspect, but it sounds like something that starts at the first dot, then increases each dot. Which could be counted as a separate benefit for Principalities.<br /> <br /> The Colony stuff I put was meant as a placeholder, more to show how the benefits could vary between Principalities (lots of Noble Form vs lots of Colony vs a balance).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aspects are Swarm specific ability things. I covered and touched them in the Swarm rules, but basically you can take a number of free aspects and any aspects above this reduce swarm size. This covers things like melee weaposn, ranged weapons, flying, ect.<br /> And they get better with higher dots in principalities.<br /> <br /> Anyways.... for now, can we assume that aside from blades, bows, and Shields that we assume that there's no other on noble benefits, focus on making powers and fill in the gaps or balance things out afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:50:36-07:00","id":859148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859134#post859134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aspects are Swarm specific ability things. I covered and touched them in the Swarm rules, but basically you can take a number of free aspects and any aspects above this reduce swarm size. This covers things like melee weaposn, ranged weapons, flying, ect.<br /> And they get better with higher dots in principalities.<br /> <br /> Anyways.... for now, can we assume that aside from blades, bows, and Shields that we assume that there's no other on noble benefits, focus on making powers and fill in the gaps or balance things out afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>The write-up said that Aspects existed, but I didn't get a good sense for what they were.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to focus on the power-aspect of Principalities. I'll give Aspect ideas if I think of them.<br /> <br /> I think creating a baseline of how balance works is important, though. For Blades, Bows, and Shields, if they're getting Noble benefits and nothing else is, they should either forgo Colony benefits, or forgo powers. Based on your example of melee/ranged weapons as Aspects, I assume you intend them to get Colony benefits. Based on previous posts, it also sounds like they're getting powers (shooting lightning was mentioned). Having those three Principalities get all that make them (and by extension, Marshals) overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:55:11-07:00","id":859152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859148#post859148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The write-up said that Aspects existed, but I didn't get a good sense for what they were.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to focus on the power-aspect of Principalities. I'll give Aspect ideas if I think of them.<br /> <br /> I think creating a baseline of how balance works is important, though. For Blades, Bows, and Shields, if they're getting Noble benefits and nothing else is, they should either forgo Colony benefits, or forgo powers. Based on your example of melee/ranged weapons as Aspects, I assume you intend them to get Colony benefits. Based on previous posts, it also sounds like they're getting powers (shooting lightning was mentioned). Having those three Principalities get all that make them (and by extension, Marshals) overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they forgo powers save a very few combat related things.<br /> <br /> <br /> The lightning and acid attacks all use basic weapon rules despite being thematically different. Basically attacks of a different flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:48:09-07:00","id":859179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859152#post859152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually they forgo powers save a very few combat related things.<br /> <br /> <br /> The lightning and acid attacks all use basic weapon rules despite being thematically different. Basically attacks of a different flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Basic weapons&quot; that are always at hand, cannot be confiscated, and do lethal damage, at the very least. That's a power. Not a big power, sure, and maybe the theme's not wide enough to give other powers. But a 1L ranged attack is a power. Either every Principality needs their own cool-attack-power-at-dot-one, or said power needs to replace the first dot of the Noble Form or Colony benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:09:58-07:00","id":859204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859179#post859179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Basic weapons&quot; that are always at hand, cannot be confiscated, and do lethal damage, at the very least. That's a power. Not a big power, sure, and maybe the theme's not wide enough to give other powers. But a 1L ranged attack is a power. Either every Principality needs their own cool-attack-power-at-dot-one, or said power needs to replace the first dot of the Noble Form or Colony benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except that the whole point of bows is literally just doing that kind of offense ability without any deviation. It's also one of the princess that cannot be used at all in human form. If every other Principality did get offense abilitiesthat what then becomes bow's role? Or if melee blades?<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind I will admit it does need nerfing or that blades needs buffing....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:32:26-07:00","id":859224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859204#post859204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except that the whole point of bows is literally just doing that kind of offense ability without any deviation. It's also one of the princess that cannot be used at all in human form. If every other Principality did get offense abilitiesthat what then becomes bow's role? Or if melee blades?<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind I will admit it does need nerfing or that blades needs buffing....</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Blades and Bows are too limited to be Principalities. If getting a cool ranged attack is important to the Monarch concept, maybe they should get it inherently, as a benefit of Noble Form. If it's something that should be an option, but not inherent, maybe it would work better as a Merit. Same deal with melee attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:39:23-07:00","id":859230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859224#post859224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe Blades and Bows are too limited to be Principalities. If getting a cool ranged attack is important to the Monarch concept, maybe they should get it inherently, as a benefit of Noble Form. If it's something that should be an option, but not inherent, maybe it would work better as a Merit. Same deal with melee attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe, maybe not. Vigor was good enough to design a discipline out of. Granted, its bonuses were more varied and &quot;chunky&quot;. More specifically, it gave Jump, dots as damage up for melee and &quot;bow attacks&quot; and dots in extra strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blades does dots in damage, slightly less strength, but comes with an infinite AP effect as its &quot;capstone&quot;, affects your Swarm with an Aspect, and comes with potentially other advantages. Bows is in essence a ranged version of blades, but with slight differences.<br /> <br /> <br /> I could merge them together... but that'd make an entirely offense Discipline, and then we'd need to come up with a replacement for something Marshal Specific, since the merged discipline might have to go with Shades.<br /> <br /> <br /> And even if I made &quot;ranged attacks&quot; inherent to being a Monarch, that still requires that a means exists to improve upon it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:40:59-07:00","id":859232,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> <br /> <br /> You may want to speak your opinions on this matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:44:38-07:00","id":859235,"title":"","content":"I think that Bows might be wanting something... More. Perhaps something to aid in targeting? Like, 'telescopic' vision or similar. Other than that, I don't know. I think that Bows should definitely stay as a Principality.<br /> <br /> Blades could probably do with something else as well but I'm not quite sure what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:49:44-07:00","id":859236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859235#post859235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Bows might be wanting something... More. Perhaps something to aid in targeting? Like, 'telescopic' vision or similar. Other than that, I don't know. I think that Bows should definitely stay as a Principality.<br /> <br /> Blades could probably do with something else as well but I'm not quite sure what.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Burrowing was one option to add for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Bows has the option of &quot;full auto&quot; at later levels, but that needs to be balanced. I think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:08:23-07:00","id":859245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859230#post859230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe, maybe not. Vigor was good enough to design a discipline out of. Granted, its bonuses were more varied and &quot;chunky&quot;. More specifically, it gave Jump, dots as damage up for melee and &quot;bow attacks&quot; and dots in extra strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blades does dots in damage, slightly less strength, but comes with an infinite AP effect as its &quot;capstone&quot;, affects your Swarm with an Aspect, and comes with potentially other advantages. Bows is in essence a ranged version of blades, but with slight differences.<br /> <br /> <br /> I could merge them together... but that'd make an entirely offense Discipline, and then we'd need to come up with a replacement for something Marshal Specific, since the merged discipline might have to go with Shades.<br /> <br /> <br /> And even if I made &quot;ranged attacks&quot; inherent to being a Monarch, that still requires that a means exists to improve upon it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Vigor covers more than just &quot;melee attacks&quot; or &quot;ranged attacks&quot;. It covers physical strength and ability, with various benefits. Vampire does have its three special Disciplines that are physically-based and don't work like any other Discipline, but I don't think that design pattern should be used. To my knowledge, there's not any other line that has a few outlier powers like that.<br /> <br /> When I read Blades and Bows, I assumed they were incomplete, as they only had one power each, at different levels. Both are already entirely offensive Principalities, with nothing more to them than &quot;do damage to the thing in front of me&quot; and &quot;do damage to the thing over there&quot;. Further, from the write-up, there's nothing restricting Bows 1 to Noble Form. They could be combined as a Principality, and get a power line like:<br /> 1) get a 1L brawl attack, free in Noble<br /> 2) get a 0L ranged attack, free in Noble<br /> 3) add a Tilt/Condition to Principality attacks based on flavor<br /> 4) increase damage of Principality attacks by one<br /> 5) ignore durability and armor with Principality attacks<br /> <br /> Or, they could have a mirrored structure, with the benefits only applying to their own Principality's attack:<br /> 1) get a 1L brawl/0L ranged attack, free in Noble<br /> 2) add a Tilt/Condition to that attack based on theme<br /> 3) spend a Psi to get the rote action on your attack<br /> 4) increase damage by one<br /> 5) ignore durability and armor<br /> <br /> And if someone thinks of a cooler power, replace the &quot;increase damage by one&quot; with that. EDIT: Like ignoring called shot penalties or increasing effective Range per afj's suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 04-04-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:37:06-07:00","id":859258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859245#post859245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vigor covers more than just &quot;melee attacks&quot; or &quot;ranged attacks&quot;. It covers physical strength and ability, with various benefits. Vampire does have its three special Disciplines that are physically-based and don't work like any other Discipline, but I don't think that design pattern should be used. To my knowledge, there's not any other line that has a few outlier powers like that.<br /> <br /> When I read Blades and Bows, I assumed they were incomplete, as they only had one power each, at different levels. Both are already entirely offensive Principalities, with nothing more to them than &quot;do damage to the thing in front of me&quot; and &quot;do damage to the thing over there&quot;. Further, from the write-up, there's nothing restricting Bows 1 to Noble Form. They could be combined as a Principality, and get a power line like:<br /> 1) get a 1L brawl attack, free in Noble<br /> 2) get a 0L ranged attack, free in Noble<br /> 3) add a Tilt/Condition to Principality attacks based on flavor<br /> 4) increase damage of Principality attacks by one<br /> 5) ignore durability and armor with Principality attacks<br /> <br /> Or, they could have a mirrored structure, with the benefits only applying to their own Principality's attack:<br /> 1) get a 1L brawl/0L ranged attack, free in Noble<br /> 2) add a Tilt/Condition to that attack based on theme<br /> 3) spend a Psi to get the rote action on your attack<br /> 4) increase damage by one<br /> 5) ignore durability and armor<br /> <br /> And if someone thinks of a cooler power, replace the &quot;increase damage by one&quot; with that. EDIT: Like ignoring called shot penalties or increasing effective Range per afj's suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, they do, or atleast they are supposed to be limited to Noble form.. There's a reason why the effective powers and boosts are tied to Noble form, but that oversight is probably because back then, it was the exception rather than the rule for Principality use in the human guise. I.E. Most stuff didn't work while human. That was slowly being phased out when I made my edits to Ajf's version of cloaks.<br /> <br /> Also, Bows already does increase in range with more dots. Specifically, it's the stuff that says &quot;Close Range&quot;, &quot;Medium Range&quot;, &quot;Long Range&quot;, because absolute range figures only work if you have a strict battlemap and I quite like what Hurt Locker uses to replace old range values. Bows also does improve to be more &quot;gunlike&quot; with more &quot;shooting&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> ... I honestly am at a loss though and do not understand your proposed changes or the intent behind them. They're supposed to be &quot;do damage&quot;/ &quot;buff me up&quot;/&quot;increase my agility&quot; because... that's kinda the main point of them. Anything else they do is a side benefit. I mean, there's a reason they're named for weapons of war and the biggest users of them are made to be combat monsters.... I'm even more bewildered by your insistence of them <i>not </i>directly scaling in damage with increased dots.<br /> <br /> I guess Tilts are okay to add, but I think it might be better for Cross Principality things to help restrict flavors. I.E. Reagents + Bows for corroding acid tilts. Or Staves + Bows for electrical/space warp stuffs...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:41:23-07:00","id":859260,"title":"","content":"I'll try and read up and give more detailed feedback later, but I could see Blades and Bows both having enough to justify them. Even if Monarchs get a default attack (though why should they, that's what servants are for), those Principalities could do a lot to improve upon a base. Persionally, I'm in favor or more options rather than straight damages increases. I think the idea of applying Tilts/Conditions, or adding the Armory/Hurt Locker weapon descriptors to your attacks is a good idea. As for Noble Form Only, I could see a higher dot version allowing a quick surreptitious strike (maybe costing 1 Psi per attack) usable in human form (be it spines shooting right through the skin before closing, acid spit, or a psionic attack).<br /> <br /> Non-combat applicability could be using them (or Bows, at least) to project/convey effects at a distance. That might be more cross-Principality, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-04-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T16:02:18-07:00","id":859306,"title":"","content":"And... I deleted my post just as I was about to publish it. Bleh, redo.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, summary for changes I would like to make.<br /> Some of you are potentially disappointed, but I don't want to &quot;nerf&quot; the Principalities especially since my thoughts are that as they were, they were too weak and needed more in general in addition to what they already had.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aspects: Both Bows and Blades will have selectable Aspects to Swarms. The first ones will be damage or new attacks. Bows will be slower than Blades here by 1 point. All Principalities will have Aspects similar to these.<br /> Potential for a &quot;Burrowing&quot; aspect?<br /> <br /> <br /> For Monarchs:<br /> Damage scales directly with dots. This isn't changing.<br /> At every odd level, you get bonus Attribute dots corresponding to what you're taking. At 2nd level, this may be given to your human form by spending 1 Psi.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also at 2nd, Blades gets a burrow move that also scales with level. Meanwhile, Bows gets the ability to do more range via categories like &quot;Short&quot;, &quot;Medium&quot;, or &quot;Long&quot;. Bows cannot be used in close/melee range at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> At 3rd, both get the ability to inflict a basic tilt by spending 1 Psi before an attack.<br /> <br /> 4th level. Blades ignores Armor or Durability with attacks. Bows does not allow targets their defense unless they can dodge firearms.<br /> <br /> <br /> At 5th level, Bows can go up to Extreme range?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Other things like specific tilts or conditions. will be covered by Cross Principalities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My reasoning for keeping the damage scaling with dots is because it's consistent with a bunch of other powers that do the same thing, which are often even better than the Principalities because they can be applied to preexisting weapons for overall higher net damage: Vigor applies its dots to all melee and bow attacks, Werewolf Slaughterer adds Purity to anything melee, which includes Werewolf claws for a single a attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-04-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T07:08:57-07:00","id":859616,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I think part of my intent got lost. My main gripe, even with the changes, is that Bows and Blades are more powerful than any other Principality. They get powers at every level, they get Aspects for your Colony, and they get increases to Attributes. Based on what you were saying before, every other Principality gets powers and Aspects, full stop. If you don't want to nerf Blades and Bows, everything else needs buffing. Even if you're not a combat monkey, getting a free, always-there ranged attack plus an increase to Dex is a no-brainer to take, even out-of-Caste.<br /> <br /> Now this might get mitigated somewhat by the weapon being Noble-only. That wasn't said in the initial write-up, I thought it was any form. Then it depends on how much of the game is anticipated to be spent in Noble Form. Discussion indicates that Monarchs go Noble more often then Demons go true form, based on the presence of their otherworld. So maybe this is better than buying an Attribute, maybe not. It's still better than any other Principality.<br /> <br /> However, your perspective is that, without the Attribute bonuses, the power became too weak. That's why I was suggesting other upgrades/abilities that could be given, or merging the two so that they could get enough powers on their own. Removing the &quot;Noble only&quot; restriction would also make them more powerful (and if you want them to be cooler in Noble form, make it be free or cheaper or more powerful there). I'm not sure <i>why</i> Blades and Bows were only supposed to be usable in Noble form (as in, the reason behind that design choice). I think it fits with both the source media and other Principalities to be able to use it in any form (human suddenly has bladed hands, or a sharpened proboscis, or spits acid, that's totally a thing that happens in alien movies). <br /> <br /> As for damage scaling, I'm against it for two reasons. First, it's boring. Getting more abilities and options is cooler than just +1 to damage rating. Second, nothing else works like this. Vigor in Vampire adds to Strength, not Damage, for the scene at a cost of 1 Vitae. This increases your chance to hit, but the way the math works, you only get 1 more success (and thus 1 more damage) per three dice added. In Werewolf, there is no Gift of Slaughterer, or Slaughter, or anything that adds Purity to damage rating. There's no gifts or abilities that add anything to damage rating. I've checked. If it did, by your description, that damage is only added for one attack, presumably at some cost. The way Blades and Bows are written, that damage is added to all attacks, for free. My guess is the reason that nothing has powers that add to damage rating like that is it makes them way too fatal. If you have a 5L weapon, you only need two successes to outright kill the average person, or take out a PC that isn't pushing Stamina. And with a +3 to your pool from your Attribute bonuses, that's a pretty easy thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T08:08:59-07:00","id":859653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859616#post859616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I think part of my intent got lost. My main gripe, even with the changes, is that Bows and Blades are more powerful than any other Principality. They get powers at every level, they get Aspects for your Colony, and they get increases to Attributes. Based on what you were saying before, every other Principality gets powers and Aspects, full stop. If you don't want to nerf Blades and Bows, everything else needs buffing. Even if you're not a combat monkey, getting a free, always-there ranged attack plus an increase to Dex is a no-brainer to take, even out-of-Caste.<br /> <br /> Now this might get mitigated somewhat by the weapon being Noble-only. That wasn't said in the initial write-up, I thought it was any form. Then it depends on how much of the game is anticipated to be spent in Noble Form. Discussion indicates that Monarchs go Noble more often then Demons go true form, based on the presence of their otherworld. So maybe this is better than buying an Attribute, maybe not. It's still better than any other Principality.<br /> <br /> However, your perspective is that, without the Attribute bonuses, the power became too weak. That's why I was suggesting other upgrades/abilities that could be given, or merging the two so that they could get enough powers on their own. Removing the &quot;Noble only&quot; restriction would also make them more powerful (and if you want them to be cooler in Noble form, make it be free or cheaper or more powerful there). I'm not sure <i>why</i> Blades and Bows were only supposed to be usable in Noble form (as in, the reason behind that design choice). I think it fits with both the source media and other Principalities to be able to use it in any form (human suddenly has bladed hands, or a sharpened proboscis, or spits acid, that's totally a thing that happens in alien movies).<br /> <br /> As for damage scaling, I'm against it for two reasons. First, it's boring. Getting more abilities and options is cooler than just +1 to damage rating. Second, nothing else works like this. Vigor in Vampire adds to Strength, not Damage, for the scene at a cost of 1 Vitae. This increases your chance to hit, but the way the math works, you only get 1 more success (and thus 1 more damage) per three dice added. In Werewolf, there is no Gift of Slaughterer, or Slaughter, or anything that adds Purity to damage rating. There's no gifts or abilities that add anything to damage rating. I've checked. If it did, by your description, that damage is only added for one attack, presumably at some cost. The way Blades and Bows are written, that damage is added to all attacks, for free. My guess is the reason that nothing has powers that add to damage rating like that is it makes them way too fatal. If you have a 5L weapon, you only need two successes to outright kill the average person, or take out a PC that isn't pushing Stamina. And with a +3 to your pool from your Attribute bonuses, that's a pretty easy thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm more used actually to sources that limit such weapons it to monstrous forms. And we can discuss this design intent if we need to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways.... They add to damage, more specifically, to successful attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Vigor:<br /> Active: By spending Vitae a vampire can energize her dead muscles,<br /> giving her a brief but substantial burst of strength. For each point of<br /> Vitae spent choose one effect from the following list. A vampire may<br /> spend additional Vitae to invoke multiple effects simultaneously, but<br /> no effect of Vigor may be used more than once per turn.<br /> \u2022 Add her dots in Vigor as a weapon bonus to all Athletics,<br /> Brawl, and Weaponry attacks made this turn. This puts<br /> enormous strain on weapons, especially those not intended for<br /> heavy hitting. Improvised weapons take one point of damage<br /> for every dot of Vigor over that tool\u2019s durability whenever they<br /> are used in this manner.<br /> \u2022 Lift and hurl objects normally far too unwieldy to use as<br /> weapons, such as boulders, cars, and other people. Any object she<br /> can lift, with Size no greater than her Strength, can be used as an<br /> improvised melee or throwing weapon. Improvised weapons have<br /> a weapon bonus equal to the lower of their Size or Durability.<br /> Objects with Size greater than 5 deal lethal damage to mortals,<br /> while those with Size 10 or more deal lethal even to vampires<br /> <br /> <br /> SLAUGHTERER (PURITY)<br /> Rage is just another source of strength. Drink deep of its<br /> power and let the blood flow free.<br /> Cost: 1 Essence<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> This Facet can only be used when the Uratha is in Gau-<br /> ru form and hits with a Brawl attack. The Uratha adds his<br /> Purity Renown to the damage he inflicts. If the Uratha is in<br /> Basu-Im, Slaughterer costs no Essence to use and he will use<br /> it instinctively.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. They are temporary for one attack, but I don't think that getting &quot;free&quot; attack damage is a gamebreaker in of itself. Especially since combat rounds may or may not end sooner than it can be a problem. And well, having them be really weak damage attacks just did not sit well with me. Your abilities should be and large encourage you to get to use your natural weapons.... which cannot happen if they're weaker than normal weapons.<br /> <br /> I'm also of the opinion that past level 4, combat powers should almost always garentee fatality on a hit on normal humans. If you're supposed to be a powerful &quot;endgame&quot; alien overlord, the only humans that are a threat should be those wearing really good powered armor... and even then you should tear them appart.<br /> <br /> Another limitation of Bows and Blades is that they do not stack with other weaponry, as Vigor and Slaughterer do. Neither apply to guns, but Vigor allows bows.<br /> Both can apply to claw and bite attacks, which I might add in Werewolf, bite attacks can become aggravated damage easily, <i>give</i> you 1 Essence, and start out at 2 damage already so stacking Purity route Slaughterer/Primal Strength (really easy) can get you really ridiculous strength and damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, Monarchs don't need to expend resources to trigger theirs while other Splats do except for certain powers, but keep in mind. Vampire has one of the easiest ways to replenish resources, Werewolf has rituals for it as well. I don't even know how much resources a Monarch is supposed to replenish, but they have a smaller fuel tank than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Also if you're worried about them being too powerful.... Bows and Blades, both current and my soon to be published revised versions aren't gamebreakingly powerful, I doubt that an &quot;equal exp&quot; Monarch can handle an equal exp Werewolf in most circumstances in Urshul or Dalu, even with them unable to use Slaughterer and giving them a decent melee weapon. Infact, just letting him use Berserker's Might hard counters's said Monarch's attacks... In Gauru, the same werewolf needs 3 Monarchs with maxed out Bows and Blades to pose a threat to him and depending on if they're human or not for the purposes of his Aggravated damage, he can probably instantly kill them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, this may not alleivate your worries as you're more interested in the internal balance on Monarch. Now, I cannot do away with the the temptation for Monarchs picking up the ranged or melee weapons just to be decent in combat without guns; I actually think it's fine to want to have some competency there. It's kinda like Werewolf's heavy emphasis on Purity combat boosts. I think what'll encourage choosing other Principalities is that... blades and bows are very limited to military actions and don't give as much stuff. Seriously, Blades and Bows even with the revisions are very clearly limited.<br /> <br /> The other Principalities are more flexible in their applications and have &quot;more&quot; in general. &quot;Practicality&quot; vs &quot;Flexibility&quot; in a sense.<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think about swapping the skill bonuses in in Principalities for more Attribute gains all around? Now, this might require use to do away with standardization....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways. Revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Bows </u></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Not all rulers must charge into battle and wage war in the up and close. A Monarch must be able to strike her enemies from afar, using sharpened projectiles, acid, or bolts of pure Void energies</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Active Powers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[1]</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> Marksman\u2019s Strike</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch\u2019s own body can act as a defense at range.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: None</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dicepool: Athletics + Dexterity - Target\u2019s Defense.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect While in Noble form, a Monarch\u2019s body may let out a projectile of any sorts, whether it is acid, lightning, or something more esoteric. On a successful hit, the target takes damage equal to her level in Bows plus successes, subtracting Armor as normal for a ballistics weapon, regardless of what form of projectile delivered. This attack may not be used when the Monarch is engaged in a melee with the target and may only be used on opponents within Close range.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[2] </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Emerging Marksman</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the Monarch\u2019s skills at ranged combat increases, the depth and range of her attacks increases.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her Marksman\u2019s Strike becomes a Medium range attack, able to reach foes in this distance.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Upon reaching her 4 dot in Bows, her ranged attack extends to Long range. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[3] </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Snipe</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regardless of her form, the Monarch\u2019s skill at ranged combat is deadly.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Psi </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch may choose to activate this Power when she makes a ranged attack, regardless of her form, or if she uses her own or a manmade or Endless made ranged weapon. If the attack successfully causes damage, the opponent suffers a Tilt either Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, or Knocked Down</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[5] </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Quickened Volley</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the peak of her mastery, the Monarch\u2019s attacks are deadly.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch no longer requires to subtract her target\u2019s defense from her Marksman\u2019s Strike dice pool. If the opponent is still able to evade or apply Defense against firearms attacks, he is entitled to keep her \u201cagainst firearms\u201d defense as per normal against the Monarch\u2019s attack. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition, the Monarch\u2019s weapons are now Extreme ranged weapons.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Noble Form Bonuses</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[1] Dexterity +1, Speed +1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[2] Dexterity +1, Speed +1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[3] Dexterity +2, Speed +2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[4] Dexterity +2, Speed +2, Size +1, Health +1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[5] Dexterity +3, Speed +3, Size +1, Health +1</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Blades </u></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The ideal Monarch must be ready and able to fight against foes using physical might and powerful weaponry with her own foreclaws and thrashing limbs. Though, this often means cutting limbs and rending talons, \u201cBlades\u201d refers also to all manner of close combat natural weaponry whether they be blunt club feet, sharpened teeth, or spiny tails.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Active Powers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[1]</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> Natural Weaponry</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch\u2019s own limbs become tools of death. Slaying foes with impunity.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: In Noble form, your brawl attacks using your limbs treat them as though they possessed Damage equal to your Blades.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[2] </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Unearthing Scythes</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch\u2019s limbs are able to rend not only flesh, but stone and earth, tunneling through the earth.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By activating this Power, a Monarch gains the ability to burrow through solid materials such as stone or even metals. Her speed while doing so is equal to her Strength + double her Blades rating.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[3] </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Overwhelming Attack</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch\u2019s attacks are powerful, able to stun and wound opponents no matter her form or choice of weapons. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Psi </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch may choose to activate this Power when she makes a melee attack, regardless of her form, or if she uses her own hands or a manmade or Endless made melee weapon. If the attack successfully causes damage, the opponent suffers a Tilt either Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, or Knocked Down</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[4] </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Transencdant Strikes.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>All of the Monarch\u2019s natural weaponry is wreathed in Void energies, allowing them to ignore any number of protections granted to the object.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Psi</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: 1 Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power may only be activated in Noble form. While the Monarch is in this form, her melee attacks bypass Armor and Durability entirely regardless of their source and magnitude. Other forms of protection that are not Armor or Durability or referred to as such do get bypassed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Noble Form Bonuses (non-Cumilative)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[1] </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Speed +1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[2] </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +1, Speed +1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[3] </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +3, Speed +2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[4] </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +3, Speed +2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[5] </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength +3, Speed +3, Size +1, Health +1</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-05-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:31:38-07:00","id":859696,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Not sure. Might just need to think about them a bit more.<br /> <br /> Because I can come up with ideas better than details currently, some more Bows and Blades power ideas:<br /> <br /> Counter-attack powers. For Blades, maybe a 1-per-Turn (or capped at Dex) Reflexive counter-strike. Imagine the rapid movement of a mantis's strike, as a reflex action. For Bows, I'd think something like an Accuracy (reduces Defense and/or Cover) bonus against targets that have hit you on the previous round. Yeah, you still have to return fire, but it still makes enemies hesitant to target you.<br /> <br /> I like the bonus to called shots and applying Tilts. I think the Extreme range mod combined with the other abilities is a bit much. Isn't Extreme range reserved for things like sniper rifles or artillery? I'd think there is sufficient delay for defense to be retained, considering the Monarch's attack forms. I think the complete ignoring of Armor or Durability is also a bit overpowered. I can see reducing effective Armor or Durability by Blades and/or Authority, maybe. Only the toughest defenses will mean anything, but they still mean <i>something</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:38:06-07:00","id":859699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859696#post859696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Not sure. Might just need to think about them a bit more.<br /> <br /> Because I can come up with ideas better than details currently, some more Bows and Blades power ideas:<br /> <br /> Counter-attack powers. For Blades, maybe a 1-per-Turn (or capped at Dex) Reflexive counter-strike. Imagine the rapid movement of a mantis's strike, as a reflex action. For Bows, I'd think something like an Accuracy (reduces Defense and/or Cover) bonus against targets that have hit you on the previous round. Yeah, you still have to return fire, but it still makes enemies hesitant to target you.<br /> <br /> I like the bonus to called shots and applying Tilts. I think the Extreme range mod combined with the other abilities is a bit much. Isn't Extreme range reserved for things like sniper rifles or artillery? I'd think there is sufficient delay for defense to be retained, considering the Monarch's attack forms. I think the complete ignoring of Armor or Durability is also a bit overpowered. I can see reducing effective Armor or Durability by Blades and/or Authority, maybe. Only the toughest defenses will mean anything, but they still mean <i>something</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright. If you think so. I wouldn't mind alterations.<br /> <br /> Come up with alternatives. I do admittedly think Extreme range is mostly a placeholder.<br /> <br /> As for the Armor thing. Well, what splats does the Armor negation work against? And how effective or useful would it be?<br /> The alternative I guess would be giving a really high Armor Piercing rating....<br /> <br /> Counter attack sounds nice, but wouldn't that be better combining it with Shields?<br /> <br /> Accuracy for retaliation fire is probably better than Extreme range.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the defense ignoring thing for Bows, well, the attack travels at speeds comparable to a bullet at that point. It's just a matter of getting velocity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You know, we might as well discuss Shields since we're dealing with Blades and Bows.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-05-2016, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:15:01-07:00","id":859723,"title":"","content":