 game balance it would be best to finish everything else first?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking for now, excluding passive bonuses to skills or attributes or traits might be best ignored from now....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:13:12-07:00","id":859762,"title":"","content":"Part of me wants to keep arguing about balance, but it may have stopped being productive, so I won't. I still disagree with the decisions made about Blades and Bows, but understand that Almarck makes the final call and that I may be in the minority in my opinions.<br /> <br /> So. New Principalities, can do. Unless someone else wants them, I'll start work on Censers. I'd also like to work on Crowns and Scepters, again unless someone else particularly does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:19:17-07:00","id":859770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859762#post859762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of me wants to keep arguing about balance, but it may have stopped being productive, so I won't. I still disagree with the decisions made about Blades and Bows, but understand that Almarck makes the final call and that I may be in the minority in my opinions.<br /> <br /> So. New Principalities, can do. Unless someone else wants them, I'll start work on Censers. I'd also like to work on Crowns and Scepters, again unless someone else particularly does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually it seems half and half on the changing last I checked. It's just more that right now it's not the time to argue about changing them....<br /> <br /> We can talk about it again once we have a big picture or scale of abilities. You're also welcome to escalate the power of the Principalities you're in charge of.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to look at doing Territories next. And then clean up Colonies to naked then neater and more fleshed out","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:34:00-07:00","id":859840,"title":"","content":"As much as I like the burrowing thing in Blades, I think that there should probably be a difference in how it works in different materials. I mean, the way it is now, a Monarch can burrow through solid steel (like a bank vault for example) at the same speed as through soft dirt. Just thought I'd bring it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:34:41-07:00","id":859841,"title":"","content":"Also, Territories? Sounds interesting. I look forward to seeing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:41:25-07:00","id":859847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859840#post859840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like the burrowing thing in Blades, I think that there should probably be a difference in how it works in different materials. I mean, the way it is now, a Monarch can burrow through solid steel (like a bank vault for example) at the same speed as through soft dirt. Just thought I'd bring it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd roll it into a general &quot;reduce effective Durability&quot; effect. Because that's basically what you are doing - attacking the ground/wall beneath/in front of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:46:09-07:00","id":859848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859840#post859840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like the burrowing thing in Blades, I think that there should probably be a difference in how it works in different materials. I mean, the way it is now, a Monarch can burrow through solid steel (like a bank vault for example) at the same speed as through soft dirt. Just thought I'd bring it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I copied and modded it from the werewolf version which didn't say that different materials had different resistance to burrowing.<br /> <br /> Anyways for Territories well Provinces..... I imagine I'd be treated similarly to hallows, loci or the sort with the amount for focus imagine give it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:54:02-07:00","id":859850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859848#post859848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I copied and modded it from the werewolf version which didn't say that different materials had different resistance to burrowing.<br /> <br /> Anyways for Territories well Provinces..... I imagine I'd be treated similarly to hallows, loci or the sort with the amount for focus imagine give it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loci and Hallows are just small patches of land in a larger region. Is that the intent? Because &quot;Territories&quot; sounds like it covers more area.<br /> <hr /><br /> Idea regarding that: Depending in how &quot;feng shui&quot; you want to make Monarches, maybe they could each &quot;manage&quot; a portion of the domain/play-area to cultivate different effects? Like how a Werewolf Pack will adjust the Resonance of their territory to suit them, Monarch groups could manage their Colonies and larger lands to achieve the proper flow/balance/psychic resonance to advance their own goals?<br /> <br /> ...Nevermind. Sounds too derivative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-05-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:58:07-07:00","id":859903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=859850#post859850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loci and Hallows are just small patches of land in a larger region. Is that the intent? Because &quot;Territories&quot; sounds like it covers more area. <hr /><br /> Idea regarding that: Depending in how &quot;feng shui&quot; you want to make Monarches, maybe they could each &quot;manage&quot; a portion of the domain/play-area to cultivate different effects? Like how a Werewolf Pack will adjust the Resonance of their territory to suit them, Monarch groups could manage their Colonies and larger lands to achieve the proper flow/balance/psychic resonance to advance their own goals?<br /> <br /> ...Nevermind. Sounds too derivative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah... Mummy does Fung Shei too...<br /> <br /> Anyways. Provinces I think are probably going to be the word I use...<br /> <br /> The scope of which is obviously... way above what most splats deal with, since it defines pretty much a county's resources...<br /> I definately need more thinking on this. Mostly, I think the advantages will be tied to a sort of &quot;subliminal authority&quot; where people passively notice you're the &quot;boss&quot; of the area and treat you as such without being aware of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> How they generate resources and what type of wealth though... I don't know. Just normal harvesting. It'd be clearer to establish it in the Beneath though without the human question","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T02:26:19-07:00","id":860194,"title":"","content":"For organising resources in Provinces, I'd take a leaf out of the book of RTS video games and give each Province a rating in different, fairly broad, categories. For example:<br /> <br /> Organics: Covers food material for supplying troops and Colonies<br /> <br /> Metallics: Used for constructing permanent structures, as well as for augmenting creatures with armour (Shields bonuses)<br /> <br /> Void Resonance: The closeness of a particular Province in the Beneath to the Void, allowing Monarchs to harvest Psi.<br /> <br /> Energy: Natural sources of energy, from rivers that can be dammed and directed to warmth that can be gathered to sunlight for growing organics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:17:24-07:00","id":860321,"title":"","content":"&quot;We require more Metallics&quot;, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:51:01-07:00","id":860343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=860321#post860321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;We require more Metallics&amp;quot;, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that yes.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that creating a particular kind of swarm, Colony improvement or Servant requires a certain amount of a given resource. Neural networking towers can only be constructed in areas with sufficient Void Resonance while a Monarch can only produce a Titan Beast if he has enough Metallics for the armoured carapace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:52:41-07:00","id":860345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=860194#post860194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For organising resources in Provinces, I'd take a leaf out of the book of RTS video games and give each Province a rating in different, fairly broad, categories. For example:<br /> <br /> Organics: Covers food material for supplying troops and Colonies<br /> <br /> Metallics: Used for constructing permanent structures, as well as for augmenting creatures with armour (Shields bonuses)<br /> <br /> Void Resonance: The closeness of a particular Province in the Beneath to the Void, allowing Monarchs to harvest Psi.<br /> <br /> Energy: Natural sources of energy, from rivers that can be dammed and directed to warmth that can be gathered to sunlight for growing organics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except I went through the effort of removing specific resources... While different types of resources can work for a computer game, they don't feel particularly impressive in a Tabletop one without increasing complexity by alot.<br /> <br /> .... Instead, what I thought up was that every Province would do 2 things:<br /> The first is provide Wealth, representing resources of all sorts, biomass, minerals, Void materials, ect.<br /> <br /> The alternative to using a Province for resources though... is using them for their features. Think of them not just as Loci, but also as magic items, giving benefits based on their &quot;level&quot; or how they're spent and this is often related to the type of territory it is, what's in it.<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance.<br /> <br /> We have this province that's classified as an<br /> <br /> &quot;Edenic Zone&quot;. This means it's got plenty of biodiversity relative to many other places. This can mean anything from a wildlife preserve, a zoo... or a farmland ect.<br /> At &quot;dots 3&quot; it can be used to Generate 3 wealth. But it also has an effect tied to its genestocks like say....<br /> &quot;Spend Wealth from this Territory on Conscription to gain an extra Free Aspect instead of the usual benefits&quot;<br /> <br /> Or we can have....<br /> <br /> &quot;Mineral Field&quot; representing places to get high concentrations of metal quite cheaply. This can be of course a mine, a crystal growth... or a scrap yard.<br /> And it might have the option to say.<br /> &quot;Access to Juggernaught template.&quot;<br /> <br /> While I originally thought of Principalities unlocking Servants, a part of me wonders about tying Servant unlocking with Provinces with Principalities being the system used to improve Servants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You don't neccesarily need to do the work yourself either as your Colony can do the harvesting on your behalf. ... Now we just need to come up with types of Provinces....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:57:21-07:00","id":860349,"title":"","content":"I can understand that. Plus it would kick start some interesting stories if you needed that particular kind of mineral from that particular territory controlled by a rival Court so you can complete that project.<br /> <br /> I would say to put a link to a map maker in the Storyteller's section though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:06:45-07:00","id":860356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=860349#post860349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand that. Plus it would kick start some interesting stories if you needed that particular kind of mineral from that particular territory controlled by a rival Court so you can complete that project.<br /> <br /> I would say to put a link to a map maker in the Storyteller's section though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, you need atleast a... gridmap to do this right. Sadly, I don't know any.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> What do you think of the above? Got ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:13:45-07:00","id":860521,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> Well, Province traits being a booster or requirement for certain Servants or Projects is pretty different. And it would give Monarchs are reason to leave their own Hives/Territories, which seems lacking right now. I like it. Not sure on the exact details, though.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts: You don't <i>need</i> a grid-map for this, any more than you need it for a city. Maybe as a ST aid, you could recommend cards, to help keep track of what Province has what. You might even elaborate them out into a kind of pseudo-characters, in that they have Traits, and might have Conditions or Tilts applied to them (such as Exhausted if you tap the resources too hard, or applied Surveilled to the Province instead of a character, to represent it is under heavy observation). And with the Beneath, you don't necessary care where a Province is located in relation to you on the map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:28:48-07:00","id":860532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=860521#post860521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> Well, Province traits being a booster or requirement for certain Servants or Projects is pretty different. And it would give Monarchs are reason to leave their own Hives/Territories, which seems lacking right now. I like it. Not sure on the exact details, though.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts: You don't <i>need</i> a grid-map for this, any more than you need it for a city. Maybe as a ST aid, you could recommend cards, to help keep track of what Province has what. You might even elaborate them out into a kind of pseudo-characters, in that they have Traits, and might have Conditions or Tilts applied to them (such as Exhausted if you tap the resources too hard, or applied Surveilled to the Province instead of a character, to represent it is under heavy observation). And with the Beneath, you don't necessary care where a Province is located in relation to you on the map.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funny that you mention cards. The entire colony and province system was actually rooted in MtG lands.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways... .condition cards and data for Colonies is going require some thought, maybe going to need the &quot;tags&quot; idea that Claire wrote up a while ago.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah... making Provinces contain specific advantages is a great way to encourage being proactive... <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:56:33-07:00","id":860546,"title":"","content":"Nothing quite like Settlers of Catan with screaming hoards of chitinous aliens. &quot;I'm annexing your lands. I need the wool, sorry.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:39:47-07:00","id":861103,"title":"","content":"Actually, what I was thinking Servants would aside from the most basic (which I think will be a one type per caste thing) would require Province control to be able to operate. Perhaps the justification being that said areas possess unique materials in the Beneath and has good access to the neccesary Sequences in the form of biodiversity.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also attaching immobile &quot;Artifacts&quot; to Provinces, big things in the Beneath that represent things like say alien tech from other races or even occult remnants of large magnitude. <br /> <br /> <br /> So does anyone got ideas for Province &quot;types&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:54:53-07:00","id":861113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861103#post861103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So does anyone got ideas for Province &quot;types&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps if you have a 'type' (plain, Ocean, mountainous etc) and then a modifier (verdant, barren, arid, flooded etc)?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:58:32-07:00","id":861160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861113#post861113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps if you have a 'type' (plain, Ocean, mountainous etc) and then a modifier (verdant, barren, arid, flooded etc)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well I guess geography is a thing but I was hoping for more.... flexible definitions. Rigid adherence to geography is not as suited to some locales. <br /> <br /> For instance, the Carribiean Court would be full of tropical islands with minimal diversification.<br /> <br /> I meant I wanted to know more about specific types, their qualifications, their bonuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eden ice zones for instance had good biodiversity and when you used Wealth from these areas for soldiers yiu had free Aspects for swarm representing good malleable dna.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stuff like that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T12:28:16-07:00","id":861205,"title":"","content":"I'd almost being in favor of Provinces being nothing more than a collection of tags. Some may have more, some less. You might assign values to specific traits such that you can say &quot;X is a 4-dot Province&quot; because it possesses Bio-Diversity \u2022\u2022\u2022 and Metal Deposits \u2022. Also allows for industrious Monarchs to work on &quot;improving the Province&quot; adding traits/dots to it (increasing value, at the risk of another taking that value).<br /> <br /> Bio-Diversity might give: +X Aspects or Servant Health for the next Month/Chapter due to plentiful genetic material. Keeping control of the Province extends/resets the &quot;timer&quot;, but even if your lands have been taken from you, you can still benefit for awhile. Some Aspects or other traits might require you to possess a Province with Bio-Diversity \u2022\u2022\u2022+ for added effect.<br /> <br /> Metal Deposits might give: Servants can be created with metal armor (2/2 armor) and claws (+2 Lethal), unlocking such Aspects for the next Month/Chapter.<br /> <br /> This way it doesn't matter whether it is a mountain or a lake-bed - what does it <b>have</b>? That's what's important.<br /> <hr /><br /> Side note: Now I'm almost more interested in Provinces and the competition for, than anything else in M:tE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-07-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T12:45:50-07:00","id":861219,"title":"","content":"To be incredibly fair, Provinces and Domains and Estates were the things Real World Monarchs wanted more than anything else since more land meant more wealth. In here the same rule has to be true to help replicate the feel of what it means to be a Monarch<br /> <br /> <br /> On that note, your proposal reminds me of a variation of Eu4s development except more detailed. I wonder if I should formalize wars too around similar systems.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I will borrow some of it, though probably make some variation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:14:05-07:00","id":861240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861219#post861219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be incredibly fair, Provinces and Domains and Estates were the things Real World Monarchs wanted more than anything else since more land meant more wealth. In here the same rule has to be true to help replicate the feel of what it means to be a Monarch<br /> <br /> <br /> On that note, your proposal reminds me of a variation of Eu4s development except more detailed. I wonder if I should formalize wars too around similar systems.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I will borrow some of it, though probably make some variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> I abstracted out the Province derived benefits to lasting a Month/Chapter because tracking which Servants you made when (and thus, what your Province options were at the time) would be a book-keeping nightmare. I'd just generalize it as your swarms die out after the set interval if deprived and get replaced by &quot;valid&quot; swarms. The Month/Chapter duration was picked so you don't have to worry about your resource options changing mid-story, and so that you can have Chronicles in which you can re-take your thron- I mean, Province.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:22:46-07:00","id":861248,"title":"","content":"Ideas for tags that could be used for areas: Water-laden, Diseased, Radioactive, Abandoned Structures, Cleared (as in open land), Bugged (the spying kind), Salted (previous owner removed anything useful and inverted it), Extreme Cold, Extreme Heat, Fault-line (risk of seismic shenanigans), Flammable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, here's the new censer-ation! (that pun works better when spoken)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Censers</b></u><br /> <i>Air is most notable in its absence. A Monarch who has studied Censers can manipulate fog, smoke, and other vapors, creating a tool out of what others take for granted.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Active Powers</b><br /> [1] Smokescreen<br /> <i>With a hiss of breath, the Monarch can fill an area with fog, hiding anyone in the area.</i><br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Extended (1 round/roll)<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch chokes and coughs, drawing attention to herself. She takes a -2 penalty to all Stealth attempts for the rest of the scene.<br /> Failure: The Monarch makes no progress.<br /> Success: The Monarch makes progress. She fills an area the size of Successes cubic feet with fog. Any inside the area are treated as fully concealed, and suffer from the Blinded Tilt.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch can choose to blow away the fog instead.<br /> <br /> [2] Air From My Lungs<br /> <i>A Monarch can alter his need for air, replacing it with another.</i><br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Effect: A Monarch can change what gasses he needs to survive. He can replace a need for oxygen with any other gas, such as nitrogen, hydrogen, carbon dioxide, or dihydrogen oxide. He does not count as an aerobic being unless he chooses to require oxygen. He can ignore lack of air for minutes equal to his Stamina + Censers.<br /> <br /> [3] Blowhard<br /> <i>With the strength of the her lungs, a Monarch can send an opponent flying with a gale-like wind.</i><br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant, Resisted<br /> Dice Pool: Strength + Authority - Defense<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch blows herself over. She falls Prone, and cannot rise until her next action.<br /> Failure: The Monarch creates no wind, or not enough to affect her target, and nothing happens.<br /> Success: The Monarch picks a target, and can do one of the following per successes:<br /> -Knock the target Prone<br /> -Push the target back 10 feet (can stack). If the target hits a solid, unmoving object, he takes 1 bashing, ignoring armor.<br /> -Distract the target, giving him -2 to Defense for the rest of the round<br /> -Attempt to remove something from target (can stack). Roll successes spent vs. Wits + Strength. If Monarch succeeds, the item is removed from the target.<br /> Exceptional Success: No further benefit beyond multiple successes.<br /> <br /> [4] Climate Control<br /> <i>Whether the weather is cold, whether the weather is hot, Monarchs can alter weather altogether, whether we like it or not.</i><br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Extended (1 roll/minute)<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Authority<br /> Duration: Day<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch badly manipulates the ambient air, causing a bolt from the blue to hit him. He takes 3 lethal from electrocution.<br /> Failure: No successes are generated.<br /> Success: The Monarch makes progress. He can alter the weather in the next scene. The Monarch requires five successes per difference between current and goal weather, based on the chart below. For example, to go from Clear to Heavy Precipitation takes 15 successes, while to go from Breezy to Calm takes 5 successes. Other changes may be achieved at the disgretion of the GM. Only natural weather may be generated.<br /> Clear == Cloudy == Precipitation == Heavy Precipitation == Lightning storm<br /> Calm == Breezy == Windy == Heavy Winds == Gale == Tornado == Hurricane<br /> Change temperature by 5C -&gt; +3 Successes<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch can choose when the effects begin, as soon as the next round or as late as next week.<br /> <br /> [5] Area Aeration<br /> <i>By manipulating the composition of the air, a Monarch can create ambient conditions with varying effects.</i><br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The gaseous mixture of the area is altered, but not in a way that benefits the Monarch. An area she wants deoxygenated becomes oxygen-enriched; a place she wants depressurized suffers sudden pressurization. Invert her intended effects based on the Success chart.<br /> Failure: The air is unmoved. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: The Monarch can pick a number of discrete areas equal to her successes to suffer an air-related environmental Condition. Example Conditions are below.<br /> Deoxygenated: Oxygen has been removed from the area. Aerobic beings are treated as holding their breath, and follow the rules for suffocation. Resolution: Oxygen-Enriched<br /> Oxygen-Enriched: Oxygen has been added to the area. Aerobic sentient beings feel fantastic, if a bit loopy, gaining +2 to Social checks between similarly-affected organisms, and a -2 to Composure checks. Checks to stay concious from bashing damage gain a +3. Any sparks or open flames cause this Condition to be replaced with the Inferno Condition. Resolution: Deoxygenated<br /> Pressurized: Air has been added to the area. Effective weights are doubled. Strength and Stamina checks take a -2. Resolution: Depressurized<br /> Depressurized: Air has been removed from the area. Effective weights are halved. Dexterity and Stamina checks take a -2. Resolution: Pressurized<br /> Humid: Dihydrogen oxide has been added to the area. Clouds and fog begin to form, and it may start to rain or sleet. Any checks requiring sight are at a -2, as are Stamina checks to resist diseases or infections. Extreme temperatures are counted as one value higher. Resolution: Dry<br /> Dry: Dihydrogen oxide has been removed from the area. Water is sucked from skin; every minute, roll Stamina + Composure. Dramatic: Take 1 lethal. Failure: Take 1 bashing. Success: no effect. Exceptional: Consider next roll a success. Extreme temperatures are counted as one value lower. Resolution: Humid<br /> Toxic Gasses: A poisonous gas has been added to the area, such as chorine or carbon monoxide. Treat the area as inflicting a Toxicity 3 inhaled poison. Resolution: Atmospheric<br /> Atmospheric: The air returns to the standard Earth composition. Any Environmental Tilts related to the air cease. Resolution: Any Tilt above<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and the Monarch can extend the effects for a full day, if she wishes.<br /> <br /> <b>Colony/Aspect Ideas</b><br /> Fog of War<br /> Smoke Bomb<br /> Weather generation<br /> <br /> <b>Cross Principality Ideas</b><br /> Bows + Censers: Toxic gas attack<br /> Censers + Quills: Group benediction/blessing<br /> Censers + Scepters: Pheromone seduction<br /> Censers + Spheres: Block scry<br /> Censers + Veils: Ninja vanish","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:55:00-07:00","id":861269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861248#post861248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Censers</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. Other ideas (for replacers, Aspects, or Cross-Principality [can we get a term for these?]):<ul><li>Noxious Gas: Inflict the Sick Tilt on nearby targets.</li> <li>Scent Marks: Tags a creature/surface with indentifiable scents, for tracking (or information, with Quills?).</li> <li>Air Walking: Air becomes as hard as ground. Not-quite-flight.</li> <li>Gaseous Form: Less conceptual support with the Monarch/Endless power set, but I thought I'd throw that out here.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:04:36-07:00","id":861280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861269#post861269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it. Other ideas (for replacers, Aspects, or Cross-Principality [can we get a term for these?]):<ul><li>Noxious Gas: Inflict the Sick Tilt on nearby targets.</li> <li>Scent Marks: Tags a creature/surface with indentifiable scents, for tracking (or information, with Quills?).</li> <li>Air Walking: Air becomes as hard as ground. Not-quite-flight.</li> <li>Gaseous Form: Less conceptual support with the Monarch/Endless power set, but I thought I'd throw that out here.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Noxious Gas is kinda covered by the Toxic Gasses option in Area Aeration? Although Toxic Gasses is harsher than just the Sick Condition. Could add it as an option, I suppose. Not sure if that's covered by Air From My Lung's immunity or not.<br /> <br /> I'm now mad at myself that I didn't think of Gaseous Form, I totally would have included that. Might be more fun than Climate Control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:25:39-07:00","id":861300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861280#post861280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Noxious Gas is kinda covered by the Toxic Gasses option in Area Aeration? Although Toxic Gasses is harsher than just the Sick Condition. Could add it as an option, I suppose. Not sure if that's covered by Air From My Lung's immunity or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, perhaps as an Aspect for Servants - they stink <i>so bad</i> that their foes are gagging too badly to defend themselves. Less extreme than poisonous gases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861280#post861280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now mad at myself that I didn't think of Gaseous Form, I totally would have included that. Might be more fun than Climate Control.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the fun of open development.<br /> <hr /><br /> Another idea:<ul><li>Projectile Deflection: Maybe X'd with Shields, but basically air/fog so dense it deflects Bows attacks and Firearms (+Defense to all in area?).</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:28:49-07:00","id":861308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861280#post861280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Noxious Gas is kinda covered by the Toxic Gasses option in Area Aeration? Although Toxic Gasses is harsher than just the Sick Condition. Could add it as an option, I suppose. Not sure if that's covered by Air From My Lung's immunity or not.<br /> <br /> I'm now mad at myself that I didn't think of Gaseous Form, I totally would have included that. Might be more fun than Climate Control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Climate Control is probably somethin that requires Hammers in a Crossover to do anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of. We're going to want to come up with official terms for the following:<br /> <br /> Powers, because powers seems... generic.<br /> Cross Principalities, because we need something simpler to say.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways I have some current thoughts:<br /> <br /> <br /> Provinces are probably significanly smaller than real world provinces, probably like every city being something like 10 to 40 of the things depending on size or importance.. France having 40 Provinces in an official probably might have close to 300 to 400 Monarch Provinces all together. <br /> <br /> However, these Provinces probably are much &quot;bigger&quot; in the Beneath, because real world space concerns aren't as much of an issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking what Provinces have is a list of the following traits.<br /> <br /> <b>Name </b> Because they might as well be memorable.<br /> <b>Resources </b> Merits representing the total Wealth of an area as described my Vent0. Types of Resources are: Biomass, Minerals, Energy, and ect. All of these are a type of wealth. Resources type doesn't neccesarily matter so much, except for when tags or traits involve them.<br /> <br /> <b>Tags </b> define what the conditions of the territory are. They are usually for when characters are there and need mechanical representation. Alternatively, they may have an impact on resource acquisition if the tag is bad or something. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits </b> This is where things get interesting. Every Province has one... or more Traits, representing unique bonuses. When a Province is created, the Storyteller assigns it traits based on its resources. Some traits require a specific level of a Resource type, while other traits are not as strict.<br /> <br /> Some example traits based on Vent0's suggestion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Eden's Blessing </i>. Biomass in this Province is highly diverse and very suited to build armies out of. When spent on Conscription, instead of the usual benefits, Biomass Wealth automatically raises the Swarm's rank by 1.<br /> <i>Ancestral Arms </i> An ancient Endless bioform's corpse lies here. Massive and powerful and impossible to. However... you might be able to clone a smaller... easier to control version.<br /> <i>Oracle</i> An alien ship was found here. It contains a single AI that is unable to be transfered. It might prove to be a valuable Advisor.<br /> <i>Evolution Pit</i> Here is a pit, a spawning pool full of pure Endless DNA left as a result of the Kingmaker's experiments. The waters here could bring you more in line to one of the True Endless... until your genetics reassert themselves and reject it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You may even consider offering the services of your Provinces to other Monarchs... for a price of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:33:21-07:00","id":861314,"title":"","content":"One question Vent0, how is the Monarch achieving this? When I suggested Censers, I was thinking something similar to the Tyranid Venomthrope or that poisonous version of the Ultralisk in HotS. While I like the ideas and stuff, I'm not sure that they all work in the context of the way that Monarchs work. From what I've seen, Monarchs tend to have fairly small-scale powers on their own while large-scale stuff is accomplished via the Colony. This just strikes me as not fitting all that well (mostly the 3 and 4 dot powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:38:46-07:00","id":861318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861314#post861314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question Vent0, how is the Monarch achieving this? When I suggested Censers, I was thinking something similar to the Tyranid Venomthrope or that poisonous version of the Ultralisk in HotS. While I like the ideas and stuff, I'm not sure that they all work in the context of the way that Monarchs work. From what I've seen, Monarchs tend to have fairly small-scale powers on their own while large-scale stuff is accomplished via the Colony. This just strikes me as not fitting all that well (mostly the 3 and 4 dot powers).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually it's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> who built it.<br /> <br /> Still... I think that might be something I leave you both to decide on.<br /> <br /> I do think weather manipulation might be too much, but creating ambient area conditions may or may not be in theme. I do like the Smoke screen and.... [2] doesn't work. In Noble form they should already be able to exist in a hard vaccuum as it's part of general Endless traits. <br /> <br /> Blowhard I think has lots of applications aside from the obvious knock things down. Such as dispersing poison gas. I will note that technically, it can be done using wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:45:16-07:00","id":861326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861314#post861314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question Vent0, how is the Monarch achieving this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots, and <b>Lots</b>, of Psi, I'd guess. Very little can't be done when you are breaking physics with your mind.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a><br /> As for terms, what about<b></b>:<ul><li>Provinces: Keep as is. Maybe Estates?</li> <li>Powers (of Principalities): Mandates or Prerogatives? As in the reality-bending powers that are your due.</li> <li>Powers (for Servant): Aspects? Evolutions? Adaptations?</li> <li>Cross-Principalities: Embassies? Consulates?</li> </ul><br /> I'm trying to leverage Royal sounding terms that match conceptually (even though it is for alien bio-horrors - that's part of the fun/joke/charm). I <i>want</i> to use direct terms, but that's counter theme, at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-07-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:18:37-07:00","id":861404,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> <br /> <br /> Any comments?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861308#post861308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Climate Control is probably somethin that requires Hammers in a Crossover to do anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of. We're going to want to come up with official terms for the following:<br /> <br /> Powers, because powers seems... generic.<br /> Cross Principalities, because we need something simpler to say.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways I have some current thoughts:<br /> <br /> <br /> Provinces are probably significanly smaller than real world provinces, probably like every city being something like 10 to 40 of the things depending on size or importance.. France having 40 Provinces in an official probably might have close to 300 to 400 Monarch Provinces all together.<br /> <br /> However, these Provinces probably are much &quot;bigger&quot; in the Beneath, because real world space concerns aren't as much of an issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking what Provinces have is a list of the following traits.<br /> <br /> <b>Name </b> Because they might as well be memorable.<br /> <b>Resources </b> Merits representing the total Wealth of an area as described my Vent0. Types of Resources are: Biomass, Minerals, Energy, and ect. All of these are a type of wealth. Resources type doesn't neccesarily matter so much, except for when tags or traits involve them.<br /> <br /> <b>Tags </b> define what the conditions of the territory are. They are usually for when characters are there and need mechanical representation. Alternatively, they may have an impact on resource acquisition if the tag is bad or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits </b> This is where things get interesting. Every Province has one... or more Traits, representing unique bonuses. When a Province is created, the Storyteller assigns it traits based on its resources. Some traits require a specific level of a Resource type, while other traits are not as strict.<br /> <br /> Some example traits based on Vent0's suggestion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Eden's Blessing </i>. Biomass in this Province is highly diverse and very suited to build armies out of. When spent on Conscription, instead of the usual benefits, Biomass Wealth automatically raises the Swarm's rank by 1.<br /> <i>Ancestral Arms </i> An ancient Endless bioform's corpse lies here. Massive and powerful and impossible to. However... you might be able to clone a smaller... easier to control version.<br /> <i>Oracle</i> An alien ship was found here. It contains a single AI that is unable to be transfered. It might prove to be a valuable Advisor.<br /> <i>Evolution Pit</i> Here is a pit, a spawning pool full of pure Endless DNA left as a result of the Kingmaker's experiments. The waters here could bring you more in line to one of the True Endless... until your genetics reassert themselves and reject it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You may even consider offering the services of your Provinces to other Monarchs... for a price of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861326#post861326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots, and <b>Lots</b>, of Psi, I'd guess. Very little can't be done when you are breaking physics with your mind.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a><br /> As for terms, what about<b></b>:<ul><li>Provinces: Keep as is. Maybe Estates?</li> <li>Powers (of Principalities): Mandates or Prerogatives? As in the reality-bending powers that are your due.</li> <li>Powers (for Servant): Aspects? Evolutions? Adaptations?</li> <li>Cross-Principalities: Embassies? Consulates?</li> </ul><br /> I'm trying to leverage Royal sounding terms that match conceptually (even though it is for alien bio-horrors - that's part of the fun/joke/charm). I <i>want</i> to use direct terms, but that's counter theme, at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Estates/Provinces. Maybe there's a devision where Estates represents buildings.<br /> I guess Mandates are the powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aspects are for Swarms. I guess maybe Servants get that too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hm... Cross Principalities is weird...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:38:42-07:00","id":861498,"title":"","content":"Alliances?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:41:17-07:00","id":861502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861498#post861498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alliances?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Term for your Pack, Coterie, Cabal/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpat