nk\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:30:44-07:00","id":861536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861508#post861508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Union... might be better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As long as we have something. Cross-Principalities was a pain to type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:02:46-07:00","id":861802,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I forgot about Monarchs being immune to vacuum in Noble Form. 2 might still work for human form? Or finding something else works.<br /> <br /> Weather Control is kinda big, it could become a Colony Aspect instead. Conveniently, the rules still work for it, it's just a different pool. (Also I like big powers and I cannot lie.)<br /> <br /> Blowhard can be used for more than the examples I gave, yeah. Those were more &quot;mechanical benefits to having a big gust of wind&quot; rather than an exhaustive list. I can work on it. I do think it's perfectly in-theme for an alien to be able to knock people down with the power of air, tho.<br /> <br /> Proposed: keep 1 the same. Remove 2, replace with 3 (with altered mechanics to reflect the fact that it's a big gust of wind). New 3 is &quot;walking on air&quot; power. New 4 power is &quot;gaseous form&quot;. Keep 5, because while it's big, I don't think it's Colony-big. Back to mechanics-land, weeee.....<br /> <br /> I don't have a strong opinion on names. I do like Mandate for Principality powers and Union for cross-Principality powers, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 04-08-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:56:42-07:00","id":861832,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> What are some of the top-level (no need for specifics, really) interactions you see with the various Province attributes?<br /> <br /> <b>Name </b>- This is just what it is called; self-explanatory.<br /> <b>Resources - &quot;</b>Types of Resources are: Biomass, Minerals, Energy, and ect. All of these are a type of wealth. Resources type doesn't necessarily matter so much, except for when tags or traits involve them&quot; How do these work? What uses the general &quot;Wealth&quot; score, and what types of things might use specific values? (I'm assuming, at the moment, the general Wealth is like Colorless Mana costs in M:tG, while specific types are the Colored Mana costs)<br /> <b>Tags </b>- &quot;define what the conditions of the territory are. They are usually for when characters are there and need mechanical representation. Alternatively, they may have an impact on resource acquisition if the tag is bad or something.&quot; Can you list some examples of what you have in mind?<br /> <br /> Regarding the <u>Oracle</u> Trait, how many aliens have been around, if leaving hyper-advanced ships/computers is a general trait?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:01:21-07:00","id":861836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861802#post861802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I forgot about Monarchs being immune to vacuum in Noble Form. 2 might still work for human form? Or finding something else works.<br /> <br /> Weather Control is kinda big, it could become a Colony Aspect instead. Conveniently, the rules still work for it, it's just a different pool. (Also I like big powers and I cannot lie.)<br /> <br /> Blowhard can be used for more than the examples I gave, yeah. Those were more &quot;mechanical benefits to having a big gust of wind&quot; rather than an exhaustive list. I can work on it. I do think it's perfectly in-theme for an alien to be able to knock people down with the power of air, tho.<br /> <br /> Proposed: keep 1 the same. Remove 2, replace with 3 (with altered mechanics to reflect the fact that it's a big gust of wind). New 3 is &quot;walking on air&quot; power. New 4 power is &quot;gaseous form&quot;. Keep 5, because while it's big, I don't think it's Colony-big. Back to mechanics-land, weeee.....<br /> <br /> I don't have a strong opinion on names. I do like Mandate for Principality powers and Union for cross-Principality powers, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, tell me when you've got that sorted out and I'll save it to my logbook.<br /> <br /> Mandates it is for powers I suppose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:08:56-07:00","id":861843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861832#post861832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> What are some of the top-level (no need for specifics, really) interactions you see with the various Province attributes?<br /> <br /> <b>Name </b>- This is just what it is called; self-explanatory.<br /> <b>Resources - &quot;</b>Types of Resources are: Biomass, Minerals, Energy, and ect. All of these are a type of wealth. Resources type doesn't necessarily matter so much, except for when tags or traits involve them&quot; How do these work? What uses the general &quot;Wealth&quot; score, and what types of things might use specific values? (I'm assuming, at the moment, the general Wealth is like Colorless Mana costs in M:tG, while specific types are the Colored Mana costs)<br /> <b>Tags </b>- &quot;define what the conditions of the territory are. They are usually for when characters are there and need mechanical representation. Alternatively, they may have an impact on resource acquisition if the tag is bad or something.&quot; Can you list some examples of what you have in mind?<br /> <br /> Regarding the <u>Oracle</u> Trait, how many aliens have been around, if leaving hyper-advanced ships/computers is a general trait?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The tags and traits I've listed are examples and are by no means final. The alien AIs can be plot hooks or not. Or just random curiousities. Also, for negative tags, imagine a Radioactive/Hazards tag. Basically, it possesses the unique resource Radioactives but is hazardous to go to for some reason. This requires that in order to access the resources of province, you need to expend resources from another Province to pay for the higher than average replacement costs of Drones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways. The way I have it right now, Resources represent things that are Raw. It gets converted to Wealth when it's been harvested and moved to the Colony proper. There's no harvesting roll, but so long as the Resources remain unharvested someone can probably steal it. I imagine there's logistical factors that prevent you from having everything harvested.<br /> Mind, I could just go back and edit Wealth away to just Resources. Maybe that'd be simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:36:53-07:00","id":861856,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that Resources are the potential bounty of a Province while Wealth is what you get when you harvest it. Perhaps a merit similar to Haunts, Hallows, Loci etc could be used to represent a Province where the players (or a single player) have set up proper harvesting operations while an undeveloped Province would have to be harvested 'manually' by sending Drones in and would not be as efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:39:18-07:00","id":861861,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like Wealth being more general. Different areas could have different flavors (if you've got metal!Wealth, your Colony builds clockwork stuff; bio!Wealth means you create critters; crystal!Wealth causes celestial sphere stuff), but I'm in favor of less micro-managing resource management.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Censers 0.2. Included suggestions from Vent0; 3 and 4 are new; 2 is old but with new success/exceptional mechanics; 1 and 5 are unchanged.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Censers</b></u><br /> <i>Air is most notable in its absence. A Monarch who has studied Censers can manipulate fog, smoke, and other vapors, creating a tool out of what others take for granted.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> [1] Smokescreen<br /> <i>With a hiss of breath, the Monarch can fill an area with fog, hiding anyone in the area.</i><br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Extended (1 round/roll)<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch chokes and coughs, drawing attention to herself. She takes a -2 penalty to all Stealth attempts for the rest of the scene.<br /> Failure: The Monarch makes no progress.<br /> Success: The Monarch makes progress. She fills an area the size of Successes cubic feet with fog. Any inside the area are treated as fully concealed, and suffer from the Blinded Tilt.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch can choose to blow away the fog instead.<br /> <br /> [2] Blowhard<br /> <i>With the strength of the his lungs, a Monarch can send an opponent flying with a gale-like wind.</i><br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Strength + Authority<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Dramatic Failure: The Monarch blows himself over. He falls Prone, and cannot rise until his next action.<br /> Failure: The Monarch creates no wind, or not enough to affect his target, and nothing happens.<br /> Success: The Monarch picks a direction, and sends a gust of wind from him to there. Distance depends on successes: 1 success is Close, 2 is Short, 3 is Medium, 4 and above is Long. The gust is powerful enough to extinguish flames, rattle buildings, and send objects lighter than 30 lbs flying. Bipeds in the way must make a Dexterity + Athletics check. Dramatic failure: the target is bowled over and lands hard, falling Prone and taking 2 bashing. Failure: the target is pushed over, falling Prone. Success: the target is pushed back 10 feet, but doesn't fall. Exceptional: the target is unmoved. Quadrupeds, beings with more legs, and vehicals make the same check at +3.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch may immediately send a second gust at the same location for free. Affected targets must roll again at a -2.<br /> <br /> [3] Walking on Air<br /> <i>Air has its own density, with certain gasses rising or falling. A Monarch can use this property to make herself lighter than air, able to walk on it as though it were earth.</i><br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Effect: The Monarch can walk on air as though it were solid ground, or contiue treating it as air. She can move her Speed in the air, but cannot run. She treats liquids as solid ground, and cannot choose to move through them. She can end this effect as a Reflexive action.<br /> <br /> [4] Gaseous Form<br /> <i>A Monarch can manipulate his own form to become a gas.</i><br /> Cost: 2 Psi (1 Psi in Noble Form)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: Something about the air here isn't right.<br /> Failure: The Monarch retains his too-solid flesh. He can try again at a -1 cumulative penalty.<br /> Success: The Monarch's form becomes gaseous. He can flow through and around anything solid, including his clothing. He remains visible as a shimmering haze, though he can stretch and shrink his volume up from 1/10th to 10 times his normal size. He can affect objects as though he generated 1 success on Blowhard for free. He can enter any area that is not air-tight. The Monarch is muchly immune to damage in this form, although strong gusts of wind that separate his molecules may cause aggravated damage. He re-solidifies at the end of the scene.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and the Monarch can become solid as a Reflexive action.<br /> <br /> [5] Area Aeration<br /> <i>By manipulating the composition of the air, a Monarch can create ambient conditions with varying effects.</i><br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The gaseous mixture of the area is altered, but not in a way that benefits the Monarch. An area she wants deoxygenated becomes oxygen-enriched; a place she wants depressurized suffers sudden pressurization. Invert her intended effects based on the Success chart.<br /> Failure: The air is unmoved. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: The Monarch can pick a number of discrete areas equal to her successes to suffer an air-related environmental Condition. Example Conditions are below.<br /> Deoxygenated: Oxygen has been removed from the area. Aerobic beings are treated as holding their breath, and follow the rules for suffocation. Resolution: Oxygen-Enriched<br /> Oxygen-Enriched: Oxygen has been added to the area. Aerobic sentient beings feel fantastic, if a bit loopy, gaining +2 to Social checks between similarly-affected organisms, and a -2 to Composure checks. Checks to stay concious from bashing damage gain a +3. Any sparks or open flames cause this Condition to be replaced with the Inferno Condition. Resolution: Deoxygenated<br /> Pressurized: Air has been added to the area. Effective weights are doubled. Strength and Stamina checks take a -2. Resolution: Depressurized<br /> Depressurized: Air has been removed from the area. Effective weights are halved. Dexterity and Stamina checks take a -2. Resolution: Pressurized<br /> Humid: Dihydrogen oxide has been added to the area. Clouds and fog begin to form, and it may start to rain or sleet. Any checks requiring sight are at a -2, as are Stamina checks to resist diseases or infections. Extreme temperatures are counted as one value higher. Resolution: Dry<br /> Dry: Dihydrogen oxide has been removed from the area. Water is sucked from skin; every minute, roll Stamina + Composure. Dramatic: Take 1 lethal. Failure: Take 1 bashing. Success: no effect. Exceptional: Consider next roll a success. Extreme temperatures are counted as one value lower. Resolution: Humid<br /> Toxic Gasses: A poisonous gas has been added to the area, such as chorine or carbon monoxide. Treat the area as inflicting a Toxicity 3 inhaled poison. Resolution: Atmospheric<br /> Atmospheric: The air returns to the standard Earth composition. Any Environmental Tilts related to the air cease. Resolution: Any Tilt above<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and the Monarch can extend the effects for a full day, if she wishes.<br /> <br /> <b>Colony Aspect Ideas</b><br /> Fog of War: hide an area from notice<br /> Raise a Stink: inflict the Sick Tilt to any who come within an area of Colony.<br /> Smoke Bomb: As Smokescreen<br /> Weather generation: Alter the weather in the next scene. Requires five successes per difference between current and goal weather, based on the chart below. For example, to go from Clear to Heavy Precipitation takes 15 successes, while to go from Breezy to Calm takes 5 successes. Other changes may be achieved at the disgretion of the ST. Only natural weather may be generated.<br /> Clear == Cloudy == Precipitation == Heavy Precipitation == Lightning storm<br /> Calm == Breezy == Windy == Heavy Winds == Gale == Tornado == Hurricane<br /> Change temperature by 5C -&gt; +3 Successes<br /> <br /> <b>Union Ideas</b><br /> Bows + Censers: Toxic gas attack<br /> Censers + Quills: Group benediction/blessing, scent marking<br /> Censers + Scepters: Pheromone seduction<br /> Censers + Sheilds: Block projectiles<br /> Censers + Spheres: Block scry<br /> Censers + Veils: Ninja vanish, holograms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":".  formatting 04-08-2016, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:40:10-07:00","id":861862,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>I've got Colony stuff improved once again. Just bear in mind Wealth represents &quot;Harvested&quot; resources.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Starting Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unless otherwise stated, a Monarch does not need to be involved in her Colony\u2019s actions. Willpower is not allowed to be spent on Colony actions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Conscription </i> Create an army, a Swarm to do your bidding. Roll Military + Authority. Successes translate to the finished Swarm\u2019s Rank. The Monarch then is able to assign the Swarm\u2019s attributes and allocate Aspects as need be. This process can take an hour for every success rolled, though the Monarch need not be present through all of it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wealth may be spent for additional dice on a 1:1 basis.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spy </i> Order your colony to Spy on a target location or creature via dispatching smaller Endless. Roll Espionage + Authority to determine their effectiveness at stealth and camouflage. You receive only basic details such as \u201ctarget is flying away\u201d \u201ctarget notices us.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most opponents also recieve a -5 penalty to detect the spying as most foes do not anticipate bugs turning against them. This penalty may be reduced or eliminated for some more knowledgeably or supernatural foes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wealth may be spent for additional dice on a 1:1 basis.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Harvest </i> Order your Colony to harvest the Resources in a Province. Roll Industry + Authority, with each roll taking an hour or more depending on distance from the Colony. Successes translates to a number of Resource being removed from the Province and moved to the Colony, up to the limit the Province has remaining.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harvested Resources perish or are consumed at the start of a new Story, unless Stockpiled, another action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resources cannot be spent on this action unless the Province requires other resources.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Research</i> Order your your Colony to perform research and experimentation on your behalf using Knowledge + Authority as a dice pool. Each roll is one hour.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wealth may be spent for additional dice on a 1:1 basis.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence</i> Influence another party by dispatching a diplomat of your own. ? Roll Diplomacy + Authority, where Successes translates to X? Only able to be done once to a given party or persons per Story.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wealth may be spent for additional dice on a 1:1 basis.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:20:31-07:00","id":861892,"title":"","content":"Nice. Have you looked at the Cult rules being developed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/858523-cults-for-everyone\">here</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:43:17-07:00","id":861913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=861892#post861892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. Have you looked at the Cult rules being developed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/858523-cults-for-everyone\">here</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A little yeah. <br /> <br /> I'm mostly just unsure of what's relevant to take because Cults... are not Endless Colonies. <br /> They're not cultists... well, most of them aren't. And mechanically, at this point there's a big gulf of mechanics that might make it difficult to bridge certain mechanics. The Cult Merits for instance. I can probably borrow things from Reach or Grasp and put them into Colony ratings though.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you could point out things worth borrowing from, I'd appreciate the suggestions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:07:18-07:00","id":861931,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And Provinces are refined further into this shape. Merged Traits and Tags to the same thing for each of communication.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Provinces </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Provinces are the measurement by which territory is handled in Monarch, with each Monarch possessing at least one Province within the Realm which holds their Colony, this is traditionally given to a new Monarch by petitioning to serve and swear fealty to a Monarch with a number of Provinces. A Monarch is awarded more Provinces through being granted them by higher powers\u2026 or taking them by force rather than spending Merits, though Merits can be used to improve Provinces.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a Monarch\u2019s final Province is lost to another Monarch, instead of losing the Province, traditionally, the Monarch must swear fealty to the other and become his Vassal, though this doesn\u2019t always happen.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The size of a Province is varies, though due to spatial warping it is often most common for the area Provinces contain to be much larger or wider in the Beneath than it is in Realspace. Some could be the size of a zoo, a park\u2026 or a single office building in the real world, but turn into massive structures in the Beneath.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Provinces provide a variety of resources, which all directly translate into Wealth that may be spent on Colony actions or be exchanged to other Monarchs. Resources replenish every Story, provided at least a week has passed between points in a Chronicle. Courtless Monarchs in particular also rely on being close to their own or Allied Provinces to be able to communicate to their Colonies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition all Provinces have special traits and properties that influence how the work, either by providing unique access to certain things, providing special benefits for specific resources in their region, or by </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Province consists of the following Traits.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Name</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A name by which it is addressed or called. Depending on the tastes of the controlling Monarch, the dictates of the local King, names are malleable. With the name of the Province, comes a Title which refers to the Province in formal turns. I.E. Duchy of Bradersik, County of Parador, Island of Mareten, Field of Xyig.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Resources</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Provinces possess at least one raw Resource with a rating of atleast one which once harvested is converted into Wealth (usually) of equal quantity for the Colony and is then able to be spent on various things. Resources replenish once per \u201cStory\u201d.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The most common types of resources are.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Biomass, representing both food and genetic material.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minerals, representing inorganic, usually mundane materials.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Radioactives, representing volatile and powerful substances.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other resource types are available, and might or might not be specific or unique resources produced by the Province when worked.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Resource ratings of a Province can be increased by spending merit dots representing time spent developing its infrastructure either in or out of the Beneath. However, the risk of that is if you lose the Province, that means unless significant damage and property damage has been caused, the the new owner benefits from the previous owners expenditures.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Traits</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is where things get interesting.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every Province has one or more Traits, representing unique effects or mechanics specific to the Province.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a Province is created, the Storyteller assigns it a relevant trait based on what he or she feels is most appropriate. A Monarch does not get to decide what Traits a Colony possesses.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traits can be good or bad, depending on what they are and a Province can have any number of them.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Storyteller is able to also remove or add new traits, usually by basing them on plot events or having changes reflect an alteration of the Status Quo.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sample Traits </b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Template Foundry</i> All Monarchs are able to create Servants, but without the proper infastructure, genetic sequences, or the like, they are limited to creating only the most basic Servants. With a Template Foundry, she is able to create a more powerful, more advanced creation.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Hazard X </i> The Province is dangerous for some reason, killing Drones fast enough to be a problem. Maybe radiation, forgotten beasts, or more. Harvesting actions done in the Province require that Wealth equivalent to the Hazard rating be spent, representing aggressive replacement costs.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Evolution Pit </i> A Monarch is powerful but not perfect. She is only a shadow of the True Endless\u2019s perfection. However, some places possess a small fraction of Endless experimentation, largely the result of unfinished but surviving experimentation. By hunting and consuming Biomass from this area, maybe she can approach a True Endless\u2019s power\u2026 until her own flawed sequences reassert themselves.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Biomass of this Province may instead of being spent in Colony actions, may be consumed by a Monarch. By eating 1 unit of Biomass, the Monarch grows stronger in one fashion. Usually, this is an attribute increase of some magnitude or an increase in her Natural Weaponry, or Shields.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Servile Mechanoid</i> The Province has a control center, one compromised by Endless growths and corruption. This control center is known to be the primary control apparatus for a powerful construct within the Beneath.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is a trivial matter to permanently dispatch some Drones and Foremen to maintain and control this growth and in turn control the construct. Doing this requires Knowledge 4.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Though not a \u201creal\u201d Endless by any means, this entity can act as a Servant, especially since controlling its command node is taking a good chunk of your psionic powers to do so.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, once destroyed, chances are it cannot be reactivated unless its control center can rebuild a replacement.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Dwellers</i> Not all of those in the Beneath are Endless or Geodics. Sometimes humans find themselves trapped here and stuck for generations, forming settlements. Sometimes, they aren\u2019t human. Those don\u2019t matter to you though, so long as they pay the taxes for your protection.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Within this Province is a settlement of non-Endless, treated as a seperate Colony with Attributes at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. They are minor and are subservient to those strong enough to subdue them. Controlling them may have side benefits, but the most obvious one is that the harvest and deliver Resources from the Province to their controller.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Storyteller's discretion, they may interact with Traits from other Provinces such as being able to endure the Hazards of another Province at no risk to themselves, being able to control control the Servile Mechanoid, or even be needed to operate Infrastructure of a given Province.. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regardless of what the Monarch has them do, they can only do one thing.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Infrastructure, Resource</i> The Province is heavily developed, possessing facilities to aid in Harvesting in a specific resource such as bio furnaces, bore mines, or other extractors. Harvesting actions do not require a roll for a particular resource, though it still requires time to harvest it. This does not affect harvesting other resources, though that does not rule out the existence of other Infrastructure.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Defensible Terrain </i> The terrain here is favorable for defense. The defending Swarm (usually the owner\u2019s) takes less 2 damage from other Swarms engaging it here.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sidebar: \u201cIt\u2019s all mine!\u201d</b> A Province is only ever really owned by a single Monarch. Though she may allow Alliance members to benefit from the Province as a show of friendship, this does mean that often times she has to sacrifice some functionality or limit her own use of her own property. This is especially true for Provinces with strong or useful traits that have limited uses in a given Story. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another option exists however, in that she may allow others even those outside of her Alliance access to a Province\u2019s resources or ability\u2026 for a price.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:14:28-07:00","id":862725,"title":"","content":"Alright.<br /> <br /> Saved Censers to the list. Later on I'll get to work on posting them into the first page.<br /> <br /> So, here's a question: Hammers and Reagents are I think may or may not be hard to settle with. Do we keep them as is?<br /> <br /> Thinking of making a potentially major change, in that there's a separation of Beneath and topside Provinces. Surface Provinces covering a whole city or region, with Beneath Provinces being more numerous, but due to spacial warping and well... 3D movement, they can afford to be quite spacious. Not as much as a Surface province, but quite large.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> You mean something of an automatic harvesting operation so it just gets delivered manually without the need for transfers. I'm thinking... hm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Harvester Detachment, Special (1-5)</b><br /> Requires a Province without an Extractor. May be upgraded to higher level extractors.<br /> <br /> This Province has a permanent settlement of Drones from your Colony. Every Story, they automatically extract and process Resources up to this merit's dot rating and deliver them to your Colony without needing to roll or tie up your Colony doing the extraction. If there are multiple types of resources, you may choose what their priorities are. Should the Province be lost, you lose this merit, but the conqueror does not take it as part of the Spoils of War.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So.... with the base systems out of the way, I am left wondering what else I should do.<br /> I can't do Principaities since asside from determining dicepools, I am not creative enough, but I can set up more fluff or mechanics.<br /> <br /> My topics avialable for now are:<br /> <br /> The Beneath, the realm under the Earth. Though the Geodics and Terran Endless spend most of their time here, they are not the only dwellers. Thinking of minor races.<br /> Geodics, well, at last.<br /> Kingmakers, stories and information about the Mysterious creators of the Monarchs and their modes of operation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-09-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T03:37:33-07:00","id":863096,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I think Provinces should be tied to Topside, even if in only a &quot;tip of the iceberg&quot; way. It reinforces some remaining need to interact with the &quot;normal&quot; world, and offers another approach: come at a Province from the Beneath, where you can cut loose, or try to sneak into it from the mortal world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T04:01:03-07:00","id":863100,"title":"","content":"I'm still a little confused about how Provinces (and the Beneath in general) tie to the physical world. Is it a kind of 'mostly relative' thing, like the Shadow, or is it 'completely unrelated except that <i>this </i>door opens <i>here</i>'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T07:03:56-07:00","id":863139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863100#post863100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still a little confused about how Provinces (and the Beneath in general) tie to the physical world. Is it a kind of 'mostly relative' thing, like the Shadow, or is it 'completely unrelated except that <i>this </i>door opens <i>here</i>'?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's currently both but I want opinions on what to settle on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T07:23:22-07:00","id":863141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863139#post863139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's currently both but I want opinions on what to settle on</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I'd prefer the latter, making the Beneath unbound from the normal world except for entrances. That's just my opinion though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T08:43:29-07:00","id":863164,"title":"","content":"Okay so we have a division on the nature of the Beneath....<br /> <br /> <br /> Vent0 wants them to be bound to Topside, Ajf115 wants them to be unbound.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps I can make this an example of Court law, in which case how it's bound is a result of the rules surrounding the divisions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T08:53:07-07:00","id":863172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863164#post863164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so we have a division on the nature of the Beneath....<br /> <br /> <br /> Vent0 wants them to be bound to Topside, Ajf115 wants them to be unbound.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps I can make this an example of Court law, in which case how it's bound is a result of the rules surrounding the divisions.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If I may, I shall propose a compromise. In the grand scale, the Beneath is an independent realm. However, those areas through which one enters it are not simple gateways, they are places where the 'normal' world and the beneath physically overlap. Such areas can be anything from the size of a broom cupboard to kilometres and as a consequence of the 'blending', the topography and geography of those areas roughly corresponds on both 'sides'.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure whether this would work but it's just an idea.<br /> <br /> Also, how would the way the world works be a matter of court law?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:02:38-07:00","id":863176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863172#post863172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I may, I shall propose a compromise. In the grand scale, the Beneath is an independent realm. However, those areas through which one enters it are not simple gateways, they are places where the 'normal' world and the beneath physically overlap. Such areas can be anything from the size of a broom cupboard to kilometres and as a consequence of the 'blending', the topography and geography of those areas roughly corresponds on both 'sides'.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure whether this would work but it's just an idea.<br /> <br /> Also, how would the way the world works be a matter of court law?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking more about that the local court would establish the official divisions of territory in some manner. Whether or not beneath control counts for the surface or vice versa","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:25:34-07:00","id":863184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863176#post863176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking more about that the local court would establish the official divisions of territory in some manner. Whether or not beneath control counts for the surface or vice versa</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooooh. I was thinking that you were saying that the Laws of the Court decide the way the local Beneath works which, I would imagine, would probably require the help of a Kingmaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:32:56-07:00","id":863193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863184#post863184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ooooh. I was thinking that you were saying that the Laws of the Court decide the way the local Beneath works which, I would imagine, would probably require the help of a Kingmaker.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it's similar to how dividing states in the real world happened. Places got cordoned off because it looked neater.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I guess I can go for the compromise. Maybe a question of &quot;depth&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:00:24-07:00","id":863343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863164#post863164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so we have a division on the nature of the Beneath....<br /> <br /> <br /> Vent0 wants them to be bound to Topside, Ajf115 wants them to be unbound.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps I can make this an example of Court law, in which case how it's bound is a result of the rules surrounding the divisions.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no conflict. I don't like/want the realms completely separate, but a neighboring Province in the Beneath could be tied to a Topside location miles away for all I care.<br /> <br /> Example: Province A and B. In realspace, they are neighboring city blocks. In the Beneath, they are separated by other miles long Provinces. So in this example, it's shorter to walk them in the city, while in another case, it might be the opposite. Of course, bringing Swarms along for a city walk is riskier, so maybe the long way through the Beneath is still warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-10-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:16:36-07:00","id":863345,"title":"","content":"New concept:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Depth</b> A Measurement of the Province\u2019s overall separation of not just space, but from the reality, from the Surface world. As Depth increases, so does the chance of physics breaking\u2026.<br /> <br /> It goes all the way up to 10. Provinces that can have surface access directly go to 3. Most Monarchs don't venture below 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea of Depth is to emphasize &quot;You dug too deep&quot; as a concept found in games like Dwarf Fortress or Mine Craft. The more valuable things are found as you get deeper in to the Earth. Coincidentally, so are the dangerous things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, more traits.<br /> </span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Vitality Spring:</i> This Province possesses special waters that improve healing and longevity with regular treatment. Those who drink from these waters heal at an accelerated rate and resist illness better for a week. Aggravated damage recovers in a single day, lethal in 10 minutes, and bashing every round.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Watery:</i> This Province in the Beneath is either flooded with water, is actually a subterranean sea, or even a normal sea unto itself. Aquatic movement for the Colony must be enabled to do actions here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Airy:</i> This Province defies physics, being mostly an empty space or even possessing floating landmasses. There might even be a \u201csky\u201d that stretches for miles. Regardless, airborne movement must be enabled for the Colony to act here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>High Yield, Resource:</i> Though this Province doesn\u2019t produce more of a particular resource than other Provinces its size and industrial output, those that it does produce are of a higher quality. This particular Resource, when converted to Wealth and spent on Colony actions are worth 3 dice or triple the usual value.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Surface Access:</i> This Province has a route to the Surface or the Beneath. Normally, due to the esotic nature of the Beneath, it is near impossible to access it through purely physical means as those attempting to enter may not approach the right frequencies. This special shaft is one of the ways in, a tunnel of both real and fluxed space.The Kingmakers create these access points \u201cabove\u201d new Colonies so that they might have freedom to explore a realspace environment while being safely entrenched in the Beneath.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stranger still is that a Surface Access does not require that a Province conform to or be close to the surface in a \u201cobjective sense. A Surface Access can seemingly tunnel through another Province and the ones using it would never know about the Province above\u2026 There is a requirement however that the Province be somewhat \u201cclose\u201d to Realspace; any Province below Depth 3 cannot have a Surface Access.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Gateway: </i>This Province possesses a Gateway to somewhere else, a point of warped Space usually a tunnel or portal that leads to somewhere else. Usually this is another, but distant Province that also has a Gateway that links to the previous. This can lead to interesting or modified travel or expansion arrangements.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm looking at the Geodics again since I figure I might as well work on them. I realized something as I come to understand what I wanted the Beneath to be. <br /> Maybe the reason that the Geodics did not take over everything in the interm over millions is a simple fact that... they can't. <br /> <br /> Like the Kingmakers, the Geodics cannot exist on the surface or else reality would reject their existence and destroy them. The Beneath is a place designed to help create stable reality bubbles that allow them to exist, but it's not perfect and it's not stable. It's the result of eons of failed reality warping experiments and the life forms that moved in... and evolved to these conditions. It's only been up until now that they've actually been able to make solid progress in that field...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Geodics are also likely going to ironically be more &quot;Hivemind&quot; than even Monarchs. With a central intelligence core that manipulates and commands &quot;fragments&quot; or &quot;splinters&quot; of its overall self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:28:24-07:00","id":863351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863345#post863345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geodics are also likely going to ironically be more &amp;quot;Hivemind&amp;quot; than even Monarchs. With a central intelligence core that manipulates and commands &amp;quot;fragments&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;splinters&amp;quot; of its overall self.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... A race of alien sentient crystals with the power to make laser beams and shields with their bodies and which suffer from what is effectively a kind of extremely aggressive multiple personality disorder. Sounds cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T16:15:14-07:00","id":863372,"title":"","content":"Okay, so the rough relative timeline for Geodics looks like:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Decide to colonize Earth.</li> <li>Find out there are compatibility issues.</li> <li>Start crafting stable realms (the Beneath, likely of the &quot;deeper&quot; depth).</li> <li>[Fight with other aliens?]</li> <li>Reach the point where they can abduct people (see Guardians/HCP backstory).</li> <li>Abduct people (why?).</li> <li>Abductees fight back and blow their operations to hell.</li> <li>Endless arrive.</li> <li>Advances made in colonization efforts.</li> </ol>Thoughts/Suggestions: What if Geodics operate at the &quot;lower&quot; depths. They can have weaker versions or scouts that can operate in higher depths. They need to establish &quot;Anchors/Stabilizers&quot; to bring &quot;full&quot; Geodics up to higher Depths. The &quot;Human Abduction Experiment&quot; was an attempt to speed up the process, using human slaves to construct the Anchor/Stabilizer in &quot;Realspace&quot;, so that the full Geodic force could operate there. The experiment... failed (probably should have never designed those suits for them, no matter how quickly it would have spread things up). When the Endless arrive, and the Kingmakers make their first Monarchs and establish Access points of their own, the Geodics see that they can exploit the paths already paved to speed up their invasion as well.<br /> <br /> Some Game-y ideas: Keep the Anchor/Stabilizer scheme. This means that one constructed in or near one of your Provinces means you have big mean Geodics to deal with, but if you knock out the Stabilizer, you can reduce the attacks to mere scout skirmishes (until they get another one up somewhere). On the other hand, a Stabilizer likely makes it easier for you to use your own physics breaking powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T16:29:37-07:00","id":863380,"title":"","content":"\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863372#post863372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so the rough relative timeline for Geodics looks like:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Decide to colonize Earth.</li> <li>Find out there are compatibility issues.</li> <li>Start crafting stable realms (the Beneath, likely of the &quot;deeper&quot; depth).</li> <li>[Fight with other aliens?]</li> <li>Reach the point where they can abduct people (see Guardians/HCP backstory).</li> <li>Abduct people (why?).</li> <li>Abductees fight back and blow their operations to hell.</li> <li>Endless arrive.</li> <li>Advances made in colonization efforts.</li> </ol>Thoughts/Suggestions: What if Geodics operate at the &quot;lower&quot; depths. They can have weaker versions or scouts that can operate in higher depths. They need to establish &quot;Anchors/Stabilizers&quot; to bring &quot;full&quot; Geodics up to higher Depths. The &quot;Human Abduction Experiment&quot; was an attempt to speed up the process, using human slaves to construct the Anchor/Stabilizer in &quot;Realspace&quot;, so that the full Geodic force could operate there. The experiment... failed (probably should have never designed those suits for them, no matter how quickly it would have spread things up). When the Endless arrive, and the Kingmakers make their first Monarchs and establish Access points of their own, the Geodics see that they can exploit the paths already paved to speed up their invasion as well.<br /> <br /> Some Game-y ideas: Keep the Anchor/Stabilizer scheme. This means that one constructed in or near one of your Provinces means you have big mean Geodics to deal with, but if you knock out the Stabilizer, you can reduce the attacks to mere scout skirmishes (until they get another one up somewhere). On the other hand, a Stabilizer likely makes it easier for you to use your own physics breaking powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, that's my mostly. thoughts as well.<br /> <br /> Battlesuits exist to allow lesser geodics some measure of firepower while away from the Coremind. Unfortunately, a human could fit in them as well.<br /> .<br /> One other concept I had thought up were &quot;Figments&quot; specially projected hardlight... duplication of humans, meant to be infiltrators. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let's see terms.<br /> Splinters. Smallest division of a Geodic, a shard that is barely self aware, mostly used as an appendage of others.<br /> Fragments. A Geodic unit name.<br /> Fracturing. Dividing or spitting out chunks of a Geodic.<br /> Coremind. The Root intelligence of a geodic.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think a Stabilizer would be a help to a Monarch though. The reality that Geodics prefer is probably not the same as what Endless long for. If anything, they'd be opposed and provide a Penalty. Atleast, unless you reprogram it....<br /> <br /> <br /> But yes, the Beneath is malleable enough that lots of entities that shouldn't exist could thrive there, but for really high end reality deviants like True Endless or Coreminds, further means are required to thrive. We'd need a better name though. Pillar? Maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T17:03:10-07:00","id":863387,"title":"","content":"Pylon? As in they must construct additional ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:51:59-07:00","id":863685,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of there being an Upper Depth that connects to the real world, and a Lower Depth that only connects to the Upper Depth and where stuff is weirder. Other than that, my only opinion is to <i>not</i> call them Pylons. Pillars seems fine.<br /> <br /> Jumping back to Principalities:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=862725#post862725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a question: Hammers and Reagents are I think may or may not be hard to settle with. Do we keep them as is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what's being asked. Is it that there's not enough difference between them? Or that they're hard to create Mandates for? Or that something about them overlaps with general Colony stuff?<br /> <br /> I don't think they're any harder to differentiate than Crowns and Scepters (which is to say, they kinda are, but they do have enough of their own thing to work with). I could certainly work on their Mandates next. If creating things and changing things is something that Colonies should be doing, then maybe they should be dropped as Principalities, but there'd need to be new unique Principalities for Stewards and Scribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:58:00-07:00","id":863690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863685#post863685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of there being an Upper Depth that connects to the real world, and a Lower Depth that only connects to the Upper Depth and where stuff is weirder. Other than that, my only opinion is to <i>not</i> call them Pylons. Pillars seems fine.<br /> <br /> Jumping back to Principalities:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't understand what's being asked. Is it that there's not enough difference between them? Or that they're hard to create Mandates for? Or that something about them overlaps with general Colony stuff?<br /> <br /> I don't think they're any harder to differentiate than Crowns and Scepters (which is to say, they kinda are, but they do have enough of their own thing to work with). I could certainly work on their Mandates next. If creating things and changing things is something that Colonies should be doing, then maybe they should be dropped as Principalities, but there'd need to be new unique Principalities for Stewards and Scribes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it's largely just trying to figure out what makes them different or seperate from general Colony things. But I guess scale will be the main deciding factor.<br /> If you got a good idea for Mandates for them, then maybe I am worried too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also: One thing I considered doing was allowing each Province to have a &quot;building&quot; on it, that you make based on your Principalities. But that's probably too soon for me to write out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:08:00-07:00","id":863695,"title":"","content":"I would personally say that Reagents would be the transformation of substance while Hammers would be transformation of shape and form.<br /> <br /> Also, I thought it was Crucibles, not Reagents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:11:49-07:00","id":863697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863695#post863695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally say that Reagents would be the transformation of substance while Hammers would be transformation of shape and form.<br /> <br /> Also, I thought it was Crucibles, not Reagents?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's Crucibles, since it's a single item that can be held or used. I keep forgetting....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:14:29-07:00","id":863698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863690#post863690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, it's largely just trying to figure out what makes them different or seperate from general Colony things. But I guess scale will be the main deciding factor.<br /> If you got a good idea for Mandates for them, then maybe I am worried too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also: One thing I considered doing was allowing each Province to have a &quot;building&quot; on it, that you make based on your Principalities. But that's probably too soon for me to write out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Well, Hammers is &quot;creation, shaping the world by tools, hand, and claw&quot;. This could be physical manipulation of matter, creating/destroying objects, enhancing tools, moving things, burrowing (because I don't really get why burrowing is with Blades right now). Could be the &quot;solid&quot; to go with Censer's &quot;gas&quot; and Chalices' &quot;liquid&quot;.<br /> <br /> Crucibles is &quot;alchemy, of changing substance to suit your ends through chemistry&quot;. This could be changing objects, changing self, transmutation, reactions/energy creation. Could be &quot;plasma&quot; to go with the other three if you want to get all the types of matter out there, but that might be a stretch.<br /> <br /> If both focus on objects the Monarch uses or encounters, and on enhancing the ability of the Monarch herself, that may separate them out enough. Obviously the Aspects would optimize building for Hammers, and maybe change-of-material-type for Crucibles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:18:09-07:00","id":863700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863698#post863698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Well, Hammers is &quot;creation, shaping the world by tools, hand, and claw&quot;. This could be physical manipulation of matter, creating/destroying objects, enhancing tools, moving things, burrowing (because I don't really get why burrowing is with Blades right now). Could be the &quot;solid&quot; to go with Censer's &quot;gas&quot; and Chalices' &quot;liquid&quot;.<br /> <br /> Crucibles is &quot;alchemy, of changing substance to suit your ends through chemistry&quot;. This could be changing objects, changing self, transmutation, reactions/energy creation. Could be &quot;plasma&quot; to go with the other three if you want to get all the types of matter out there, but that might be a stretch.<br /> <br /> If both focus on objects the Monarch uses or encounters, and on enhancing the ability of the Monarch herself, that may separate them out enough. Obviously the Aspects would optimize building for Hammers, and maybe change-of-material-type for Crucibles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you feel it's appropriate, we can change Hammers to get burrowing later on. I put it with Blades mostly to give it more out of combat actions, but yeah, it probably doesn't need to be there.<br /> Alternatively... both can do burrowing and you burrow much faster with both...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:07:06-07:00","id":863853,"title":"","content":"Wait, important question that I just thought of. Is Monarch using 1e nWoD rules, or 2e CofD rules? I realize I've been putting in Conditions and similar from 2e, and assumed that was what was being used because that's the current system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:10:10-07:00","id":863855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=863853#post863853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, important question that I just thought of. Is Monarch using 1e nWoD rules, or 2e CofD rules? I realize I've been putting in Conditions and similar from 2e, and assumed that was what was being used because that's the current system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2e. <br /> <br /> Which is what I was comparing Blades and Bows against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T17:38:37-07:00","id":864629,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Beneath the World </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Beneath is the hidden world co-opted by the Endless to hide their Colonies in, so that they might grow and become numerous without interfering\u2026 or being intruded upon. However, this realm is not a creation of the Endless, it having existed for long before their arrival. The Kingmakers and many other beings are powerful enough to create points in and out of it, but they are not the true rulers. In fact, one might argue that in its current state, the Beneath does not have any \u201creal ruler\u201d.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Geodics created it as an attempt to Crysiform an environment that could support themselves, a slow process that took billions of years, however they failed to do so in the initial setup phase, creating of a world that was beholden to no singular life form. Even worse, before they could rectify this, others moved in, carbon life and spirits, primitive beings that bent their world in different directions. And the more of them that are or the closer a region in the Beneath to the Surface, the more it confirmed to Terran standards of life.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Beneath\u2019s unique make-up is such that the dimension cannot truly decide what it is or what kind of physical model it is meant to emulate. As long as a life form can conform to the barest essentials of Euclidean physics are upheld, such as existing in a 3 Dimensional space and operating on Linear time as opposed to acasual, the lifeform in question can exist in the Beneath, treating it for the most part as their home dimension. This allows Terran Endless and humans to exist within it and Spirits when in its Realm are forced to manifest as in their home dimension.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, many beings such as True Endless like the Kingmakers do not conform to Linear time or 3D space and thus cannot exist within the Beneath without special means. Unfortunately for the Geodics, the physics they exist in is still too different than that of most carbon life; because of its carbon centric domination close to the surface, more powerful Geodics cannot access the Surface without rapidly dying to the slightly altered physics or means to protect themselves.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One other trait of the Beneath\u2019s geography is that\u2026 occasionally, the place warps and twists, tunnels leading to different sections that previously were located elsewhere\u2026 or never existed before. Surface Access points never lose their connections to the above ground, but the areas around those Provinces are often very different once you stop and notice it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Denizens of the Beneath</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Though the Beneath is primarily held under the control of either the Monarch Colonies or Geodic Coreminds, they are not the sole denizens of the Beneath. The life forms here have adjusted to life without the Sun\u2019s light, changed by generations of gradual mutations due to altered physics; the Beneath allows many life forms to exist similar to their native environments, but it isn\u2019t perfect, especially with multiple generations slowly adapting to Beneath life over their native environments.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Beneath is home to a flourishing ecosystem of subterranean life. Mosses and lichens form the bases, with massive spires of fungi taking the role trees normally take. The Beneath though separated from the Sun\u2019s light still possesses a sort of\u2026 ambient energy that stimulates photosynthesis or equivalent systems in plant life; again due to its altered physics.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fauna varies, but most of it is recognizably descended from the surface world, though obviously\u2026 warped and more vicious than normal. Bioluminescence is a common adaptation with many species possessing some form of illumination; as a result, it\u2019s rare to find patches of complete darkness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Humans </i> The most common indigenous sentients. Most humans live in primarily in a primitive hunter-gatherer state with some occasional pockets of rudimentary civilization in some areas. Most settlements are likely descended from ancient migrations that somehow ended up in the Beneath.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Generally, humans who have lived entire generations in the Beneath are pale skinned and require serious acclimatization to function in the Surface world, in both physicality and socially, especially those with unique languages or lacking any formal education. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Monarchs, Beneath humans are ill-suited for warfare outside of command positions due to low replenishment rates, but as aides and companions, they have some uses, especially for Monarchs who want a touch of \u201chome\u201d in their \u201cnew\u201d home\u2026 or even potential recruiting grounds for new Monarchs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Mechanoids </i> Not a race per say, but rather a collective designation referring to any multitude of constructs or machine entities ranging from \u201cdumb\u201d drones, self aware consciousnesses, and posthuman data constructs. Most Mechanoids are the remnants of mad experiments, leftovers from long dead alien races, or tools from surprisingly advanced civilizations that faded away from collapse. Many of these machines still function, either carrying out their final orders until disrupted or replicating biological cycles in metal frames, harvesting materials to bring back to their factory-nests. Others lie dormant, sleeping and waiting for someone to program directives.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the most part, Monarchs do not receive as much benefits from machines as they would be to other factions. They already possess a self managing army and workforce full of disposable and replenishable assets that were theirs to control? What need would they have for hordes of metal? Still, if a force can be turned toward\u2019s a Monarch\u2019s uses, why not co-opt them? </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A part of me really wants to write about potential alien/alternate evolved sentient races found in the Beneath, mostly other aliens that settled her away from human eyes or... evolutionary wonders that were first &quot;born&quot; there and never knew the touch of sunlight, like alternative sentients. Also could be used to justify things better with HCP's tech access. Not all of it was Geodic. But eh... maybe not. Thoughts?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T18:34:23-07:00","id":864654,"title":"","content":"Yes. I'll elaborate more when not phone-bound. Multiple aliens in the beneath really only need a single paragraph or so per. Purpose is ideas and variety, yes? What about making Geodic Beneath timescale vague or variable - especially time becomes malleable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T18:48:55-07:00","id":864662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=864654#post864654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I'll elaborate more when not phone-bound. Multiple aliens in the beneath really only need a single paragraph or so per. Purpose is ideas and variety, yes? What about making Geodic Beneath timescale vague or variable - especially time becomes malleable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Likely yeah. Alot of these creatures have been subjected to... hundreds of thousands or millions of extra years of evolution relative to the surface world, especially past Depth 5 when time is more fluid. Not to say that they are better, of course.<br /> <br /> Granted, there should be a way to explain why players are not having Rip Van Winkle adventures where they've been gone for too long. Perhaps the Beneath has stablized relative to what it was before, due to the Geodics returning to control it, so at most an adventure should only make you missing for 3 times longer than normal at worst... Probably makes resource extraction a nightmare.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for each race, likely 2 paragraphs each, one about their history and role... and another on how useful they are to Endless eyes. Because it's kinda the point.... Hm, should vassalizing them be a thing? I need to work on the Servants thing more...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T19:26:40-07:00","id":864669,"title":"","content":"Well, depending on the level of detail required, you could have a short section on the most numerous (and useful) beings, then a few paragraphs and some notes on other creatures. Make note of modelling them as Servants (with various Adaptations being their inherent &quot;racial&quot; abilities), with maybe a pseudo-Principality or two (noting that these aren't &quot;true&quot; Principalities as Monarchs know them, but they do manipulate Void energies and are best understood/modeled this way). History, ecology, role/utility, and Province effect are variable, as needed. I say throw a bunch of flavorful ones out there and see what people like the most - expand on those.<br /> <br /> Regarding Geodics and the timescales, with the Geodic's alternate physics, you can be vague with whether their presence &quot;on Earth&quot; is only a few thousand years old (which is still plenty by human civilization), to millions or even billions of years old. Different sources or even different <i>data</i> might give conflicting results, but hey, that's what you get with variable and potentially non-linear time.<br /> <br /> I'd have the &quot;human natives&quot; less desirable to the Endless for new Monarchs - they want to colonize Earth, and what are these Beneath cast offs doing to advance that. Plus it cements a common ground for PCs - they all had prior lives on the surface in modern society before the... incident.<br /> <br /> As for more variable time, you could have it as a Province Trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-12-2016, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T19:48:29-07:00","id":864678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=864669#post864669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, depending on the level of detail required, you could have a short section on the most numerous (and useful) beings, then a few paragraphs and some notes on other creatures. Make note of modelling them as Servants (with various Adaptations being their inherent &quot;racial&quot; abilities), with maybe a pseudo-Principality or two (noting that these aren't &quot;true&quot; Principalities as Monarchs know them, but they do manipulate Void energies and are best understood/modeled this way). History, ecology, role/utility, and Province effect are variable, as needed. I say throw a bunch of flavorful ones out there and see what people like the most - expand on those.<br /> <br /> Regarding Geodics and the timescales, with the Geodic's alternate physics, you can be vague with whether their presence &quot;on Earth&quot; is only a few thousand years old (which is still plenty by human civilization), to millions or even billions of years old. Different sources or even different <i>data</i> might give conflicting results, but hey, that's what you get with variable and potentially non-linear time.<br /> <br /> I'd have the &quot;human natives&quot; less desirable to the Endless for new Monarchs - they want to colonize Earth, and what are these Beneath cast offs doing to advance that. Plus it cements a common ground for PCs - they all had prior lives on the surface in modern society before the... incident.<br /> <br /> As for more variable time, you could have it as a Province Trait.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright. I'll get to work.<br /> <br /> I'll make modifications for human desirability and add things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Any particular race ideas you would want to pitch?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:28:53-07:00","id":864880,"title":"","content":"Dinosaurs. There should be dinosaurs. Please put in dinosaurs. <br /> <br /> Note on variable time: It might be the deeper you go, the more time gets wonky (due to distance from realspace). That way, an ST doesn't have to do time shenanigans unless they and the players want to, and generally only at a higher power level. (Admittedly, I'm cribbing this idea from how the Hedge/Arcadia works in Changeling, but what's good storytelling without some blatant theft?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T07:44:39-07:00","id":864931,"title":"","content":"Mole Men - Because the Beneath, and you can spin it either comical or frightening (or both!) easily.<br /> <br /> Grey Goo - Because I played the game recently, and a high tech, non-Geodic alien intelligence that has Endless parallels in its behavior might be nice. Maybe simply call it the &quot;Sand&quot; for a nice unassuming name (because most of the time, the nanites sit around as inert sand).<br /> <br /> ??? - Something powerful, vicious, and scary, like the Hidden Fun Stuff in Dwarf Fortress.<br /> <br /> More depend on how Servants and Principalities are done. Sometimes you can look at a group of powers and think &quot;what would a collection of beings be like if they had these universally&quot;.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Terminology</b><br /> What about &quot;Dwellers&quot; for Beneath residents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-13-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:15:26-07:00","id":864950,"title":"","content":"I thought Geodiscs were the Hidden Fun Stuff equivalent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:21:36-07:00","id":864956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=864950#post864950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Geodiscs were the Hidden Fun Stuff equivalent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're the Big-Scary-Thing-We-Know-About. The Hidden Fun Stuff would be the Big-Scary-Thing-We-Only-Have-Rumours-About.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T15:25:17-07:00","id":865144,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These races have been subjected to unspoken eons of evolution, changed into creatures and beings so utterly different from their roots, even attaining sentience.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Gitserai</i> The first signs of these savage creatures are the burning luminescent \u201cclouds\u201d over head, blending in with other glowing lights. The second sign is usually a sharpened blade against your sternum.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The evolutionary descendants of raptors from the Mesolithic, this Dwellers race lurks in some of the darkest reaches of the Beneath. Biologically, they resemble winged raptors with their claws having evolved into hands. When unfoldered, these wings tend to glow in a dizzying array of colors, males typically more vibrant. In terms of technology, they are typically limited to hunter-gatherers. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They possess psionic abilities, communicating through telepathic-empathy links and empower their claws and teeth to shred many things they ought not be able to otherwise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fiercely territorial, most gitserai attack or ward away intruders and do not maintain long term connections with Monarchs. Still, they make a worthwhile investment for an armed escort.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Modkan</i> This short stock race is covered in hair from head to toe, but often those that see the Modkan do not see them in their natural forms. Gifted with a propensity for crude, yet functional machinery and metalworking, yet a vulnerability to their own industries\u2019s exhausts underground, the Modkan hide their short snouts behind hardened gas masks. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Barely standing up to a human\u2019s knee, these industrialists arm themselves with energy weapons to make up for their physical frailty. And should a limb be lost, it can be replaced with the right metallurgy. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They do not trust Monarchs for their warping flesh and greater size and will over, but fresh resources and material are highly prized, enough that they might be willing to exchange goods. Light in particular, electrical lights holds a special place in their hearts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kessen</i> This race is not flesh in blood or even could recognizably be called a \u201cself\u201d. In its dormant state, this nanite machine based\u2026 sludge gathers in pools where it busies itself devouring and converting nearby rock and any creatures that spend far too long within its grasp, breaking them down for raw resources. This is called a Spawning Pool</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But in times of plenty or danger, it forms scouts, converting some of its mass into separate, mobile forms. These creatures replicate organic shapes and structure, forming limbs, exoskeletons, even artificial organs or even brains. Then then go out and find more things to dissolve into the Spawning Pool that made them\u2026 or form new ones.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An odd blend of biological and mechanical state of beings, these entities are all still machines and are relatively eager to serve.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It has been hypothesized that the original Kessen were nanomachines that were lost in the Beneath not too long ago, but evolved rapidly into a new, independent life form over subjective millenia. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WARNING</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The following information is restricted information, reserved to the highest authorities. You require clearance to read it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">...</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2026</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2026 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ACCESS GRANTED</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Boundless</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evolution is not pretty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A horrible implication of the Monarch condition is that ones flesh is not a constant, static form. It writhes, twistes, evolves as the Monarch slowly adapts and unlocks the Principalities she has been given. One might have started with a somewhat humanoid or even a mostly human like appearance, but as the cycles of genetics and adaptation play out, such frailties are shifted for a more beastial, hardened appearance. She does however always retain the ability to human form, to choose not to change, if only for a time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But Monarchs that have spent far too long in the Beneath have a different set of priorities. Trapped in the dark Depths for too long, where time is malleable, survival is the only goal. And evolution, adaptation is the key to survival. In here, maintaining the human identity is nothing but a tax, a limitation, a burden on the more fit, more apt genetics the Kingmakers gifted her with.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When pushed too far in these places, the Monarch sheds aside the last vestiges of who they were originally, becoming one and all the embodiment of the every changing, Endless Swarm</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She removes from herself any pretenses of nobility, of restraint, of social order, replacing them with the need to constantly warp and change, to guide her legions up to ascension. She excises the final gene sequences that represented her original, weakened, stable state and devotes herself entirely to evolve, to grow, heedless of the cost.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By the time her former friends notice she has been missing and finally mounted a rescue party to save her, they find a bloated abberation that has shed aside weakness and affection a century ago.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:05:22-07:00","id":865287,"title":"","content":"<i>Nukukari</i>: One of the players in the Beneath, if only barely so due to their ability to form Surface Access points. Generally despised by the other factions, who see them as conceptual, technological, and literal thieves. There is some merit to the view - though the Nukukari are tremendously clever, industrious, and curious, they are very unimaginative. Never first, they simply copy or take what they see works for other races. The greatest extent of their originality is &quot;lets combine this thing with that other thing&quot;, which has led to unfortunate incidents such as the creation of the Tranquil.<br /> <br /> If you need something analyzed and replicated, however, they are a Monarch's most reliable bet. As long as they don't mind seeing knock-offs flooding the nearby Provinces before too long.<br /> <br /> <i>Tranquil</i>: A &quot;recent&quot; (considering the somewhat subjective time portions of the Beneath experience) development, thought to be the result of the Nukukari merging a hive mind with abducted specimens exhibiting &quot;the Plain&quot; phenomenon (see Hurt Locker). These generally uniform beings often flood into an conflict zone without warning and bring all combat to a grinding halt. Often even resource harvesting is inhibited, forcing one side or the other to come up with creative methods for removing the nuisances non-violently.<br /> <br /> They can be lured into certain Provinces by resourceful Monarchs, creating an enforced &quot;safe&quot; zone on their borders where hostility cannot happen, or to &quot;protect&quot; a more benign asset for a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-13-2016, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T08:46:43-07:00","id":866396,"title":"","content":"Well, after a short break from the project I am back. Now that the Beneath is covered I'm thinking about Geodics, the Masters of the alien realm. Or... maybe Servants are better for next.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I had this idea.... Servants doesn't just refer to advanced Endless biomorphs, but also to enslaved, coerced, or even infested races, including people from the races we just wrote about. You bring them in because they have got good skills, useful knowledge, or neat abilities, but they and &quot;forged&quot; servants are taxing on the Authority.<br /> <br /> Oh and if you so choose, you can augment these entities above their basic templates using Principalities. I'll call this Colony action &quot;Evolve&quot; and it doesn't require a dice roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Not... sure if the Plain make sense here. A good chunk of their abilities stem from... social norms and human society from what I understand. That might not work there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:25:48-07:00","id":866434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=866396#post866396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Not... sure if the Plain make sense here. A good chunk of their abilities stem from... social norms and human society from what I understand. That might not work there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence, the Hive-Mind and alien experimentation. I just thought an army of aggressive pacifists would be amusing to bring to the conflicts of the Beneath - its a problem that you can't actually solve by applied violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:42:21-07:00","id":866443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=866434#post866434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence, the Hive-Mind and alien experimentation. I just thought an army of aggressive pacifists would be amusing to bring to the conflicts of the Beneath - its a problem that you can't actually solve by applied violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>... It still bothers me for a reason I cannot explain. Gut feeling reaction.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... I'm going to move on.<br /> <br /> Dug through my notes and found an old, old draft of what Servants were like, back when DreamingGod was actively involved and the things were called Vassals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:46:37-07:00","id":866451,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First one is an &quot;intro&quot; to Vassals.<br /> <br /> Second one is an example template</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Both are very rough and are going to require some serious rework to accomodate alien Servants in the revised version.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vassals are more advanced creatures created by the Monarch to act as her lieutenants. Each is more free willed and intelligent than a basic drone and is able to act as a driver, manager, coordinator, or often, commander in the Monarch\u2019s stead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the most part, Vassals are created via a premade genetic template from the list of templates the Monarch possesses and paying a relevant resource cost based on the template. Once the relevant prices are paid, the new Vassal would be incubated, hatched and trained during a time span of about a week. Once the week has elapsed, the new Vassal is fit for active duty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pre-existing and soon to be hatched Vassals may be modified from the norm. Most templates possesses a number of \u201cMutation\u201d representing packages of genetic modifications. Each, for the cost for further resources, provides new abilities, augments existing ones, or changes the Vassal\u2019s equipment from the norm.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to apply a Mutation, the must have an open Mutation slot able to accept the Mutation. Vassals possess a predetermined number of slots inherent to their Template. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the description of each Mutation, it lists which Vassals it may be applied to. In the case of some mutations, such as weaponry or armor morphs, they may remove existing features or come with statistics penalties, also specified in the Mutation\u2019s description. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each specific Mutations may only be applied once to a Vassal once and obviously, if a Mutation replaces an existing feature from the template, such as a weapon, other Mutations that replace that feature may not be applied.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mutations take 1 hour to apply, during which the Vassal is disabled and inside a Cocoon. Additionally, some templates may receive multiple slots within the same category.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Removing or changing mutations from an existing Vassal or outright disposing of a Vassal does not refund the costs made to produce either.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As Vassals are part of the Monarch\u2019s Colony, any metanormal effects that involve Authority use the Monarch\u2019s Authority when determining the Vassal\u2019s.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Foreman, standard upgraded Drone</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hunter, basic ranged specailist unit. Stealthy and burrowing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ravager, armored ranger. Super bear with acid dripping out.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Consul, basic psitrooper. Support psionics and TK</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Knight, Infested \u201cSpecial unit\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Raptor, Light Airborne</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother, large utility beast/factory</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seeker, Psi utility airborne.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tyrant, Multi Armed melee infantry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warlord, tank beast</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terror, Fighter/Bomber Aircraft</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fiend, Psionic monster. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Template Name</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Source</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dexterity:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stamina:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wits:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Presence:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulation:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Composure:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skills:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perception:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Default Gear</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weapons:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armor:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abilities:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mutation Slots: #</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:22:49-07:00","id":867103,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Updated Geodics.<br /> <br /> Sooner or later, I realize I'm going to have to work on Principalities again, but I think I can have a workable draft for Servants real soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Endless are not the first race to land upon our Earth. There are a multitude of creatures that traveled the stars and set foot upon our lands. The Endless and their Monarchs are but the latest in a long line of travelers, but there is without a doubt a first.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long ago, in a distant time before memory, when the land was still being formed when even the ancient Celestines we all know were just newborns, the earth was struck visited by a meteor, more a seed\u2026 a ship that lodged itself all the way down to the Earth\u2019s core. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Its inhabitants were shattered, broken divided everywhere along the newborn world, sinking beneath the molten seas. They survived, becoming a broken, fracture people: a race totally unlike anything in either Terran understanding or even Physics, the Xan-Qui, the Geodics.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately for us, they are not a race that seems at all willing to make friends. They are a race that is scientifically impossible by our understanding, the very nature of our physics is just not compatable. Though the Geodics survived the fall to Earth, they are trapped within it, reduced to a mere fragment of its former self, one that should not exist as we understand it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to survive, over the eons, they created a vast labyrinth of underground tunnels and passage ways to facilitate their existence, a process made difficult due to the lack of coordination, massive technology regression, and long stretches of hibernation; the surviving machines the Geodics held were put to the task, burrowing tunnels, harvesting resources, while the ancients slept. They ultimately failed this task as carbon life\u2019s existence stole control corrupted the machines, forcing them to allow the new reality to also account of them. When they finally awoke, the Geodics could bring their Coreminds to the surface, their underground paradise becoming their prison. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They had no choice but to ensure that whatever intruders in their realm were removed, by any means necessary.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Physiology </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Geodics are named such for their appearance, crystalline yet shifting forms that look like ordinary earth, but despite their appearances they are not inert, floating by some electromagnetic means and bending in forming unusual shapes. They employ technology of a sort, far more advanced than anything we own, controlling these devices through electromagnetic manipulation and seeming telepathy. These same electronic field generates natural force fields and beam weaponry comparable to firearms or in some cases artillery cannons. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Though there may be thousands upon thousands of floating crystals in a Nexus, there is in truth only very few Geodics in a given Nexus, as in actually, a Geodic is a single, fragmented mind in a thousand bodies. In every Nexus, there is atleast one immobile monolith the size of a skyscrapper, seemingly made of stained glass. This is a Coremind, a vast and powerful entity of great and immeasurable will. Yet this power is ultimately difficult to move\u2026 and is much more susceptible to changes in physics than other lifeforms; it cannot leave the Nexus without dying or some sort of stabilizing Pillar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To make up for this, Coreminds have the ability to Fragment, forming lesser intelligences that are copies of one of the dozens of personalities and inclinations of the Coremind\u2019s congealed into a coherent, stable form. Once the Fragment has completed its duty, it disassembles itself, reforming back into itself.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Coreminds can Fragment a variety of ways and generally built their Fragments to suit a variety of tasks, either by creating one powerful and complicated agent to observe things in the surface world or a hundred smaller, dumber, more disposable units that matters little.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Technology </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Geodics possess a great deal of technology up to and including advanced funraces, electronic equivalents, communications technology, and most prevalent of all, suits.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Geodics often equip smarter fragments with suits to allow them better physical abilities when it would be cheaper to do so than say make a more advanced fragment. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The most common type of suit unit that a geodic will possess is a Battlesuit, often very similar to the Devics used by HCP.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rules</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Geodic Fragments are treated as always Manifested Ephemeral Beings, using many of the same rules as Angels and Spirits do, except Banes and Bans.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They always possess an Influence (Crystals) equal to their Rank, representing their innate powers of manipulating other crystaline structures, the Blast Numina, and Telekinesis, plus other relevant Numina.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Coreminds are above stats.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:33:46-07:00","id":867114,"title":"","content":"I have to say that the idea of 'zerg vs Ramiel' has got me salivating. This will be FUN when it's all put together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:38:14-07:00","id":867553,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, have two [EDIT]now-complete Principalities, brought to you by <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h3tvB8XFG3g\" target=\"_blank\">the girl from WLSD</a>. (I love the feathery psychic velociraptors, btw.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Crowns</b></u><br /> <i>A Diplomat knows that more flies are caught with rotten meat then with waved sticks. Crowns gives the people what they want, and in exchange, the Monarch profits.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> [1] Inclination<br /> Sometimes, a good impression is all it takes to get things done. A Monarch can improve someone's perspective, though it may still fall later if she abuses it.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Effect: Improve the target's impression rating by one. This power can only be used once on a given target per story. This power does not prevent impression levels from being lost.<br /> <br /> [2] Declaration<br /> By his presence alone, a Monarch can shape a room's mood to match his own.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: Based on the Monarch's current mood, anyone in the scene is inclined to match that mood, though strong emotion may snap them out of it. Any who roughly match the mood of the Monarch gain a +1 to skills or actions in favor of the mood (intimidation and attacks for anger, persuasion and social maneuvering for calm or happiness, empathy and resistance for sadness, etc), and a -1 to all other actions.<br /> <br /> [3] Motivation<br /> Mental reassurances and adjustment of pheromones can be all it takes to get someone to want to do something.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Extended (5 minutes of conversation per roll), Resisted<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Authority - Resolve<br /> Duration: Success weeks or until fulfilled<br /> Dramatic Failure: The target becomes contrary. The target gains an aspiration opposite the intended one that lasts for a week or until resolved.<br /> Failure: The target's motives are unchanged. The Monarch cannot try again in the scene.<br /> Success: When the Monarch reaches successes equal to the target's Willpower + Supernatural Tolerance, she picks a short-term aspiration for her target that would not cause a breaking point and is not mutually exclusive with any other aspiration he has. The target gains that aspiration in addition to any others he has. Fulfilling this aspiration grants the target a full Willpower refresh, in addition to any other benefits. The aspiration fades after weeks equal to successes, at which point it fades if not fulfilled.<br /> Exceptional Success: When reaching five more successes, the Monarch may pick an aspiration that may cause a breaking point for the target.<br /> <br /> [4] Cessation<br /> When negotiations have become heated, when an assassin makes a move, when violence will only make things worse, a Monarch can calm those around him.<br /> Cost: 2 Psi<br /> Action: Instant, Resisted<br /> Dice Pool: Composure + Authority - highest Composure<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: Tempers flare, and everyone becomes more emotional. Violence becomes more likely, and any attackers will prioritize the Monarch as a target.<br /> Failure: No one is calmed. The Monarch may try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: Everyone in the scene calms down. No one may attempt to attack or directly physically harm anyone else in the scene. All are inclined to behave calmly and rationally. Entering the scene causes the effect; leaving the scene ends the effect.<br /> Exceptional Success: As success, and all in the scene become more inclined towards the Monarch, giving him +1 to Empathy, Persuasion, and Socialize rolls for the scene.<br /> <br /> [5] Inspiration<br /> What's better than convincing one person to see your way? Convincing all of them!<br /> Cost: +2 Psi (Free in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: A Monarch can use Motivation on every person in the room. Individuals are convinced as she accrues more successes then their Willpower + Supernatural Tolerance. It is possible for some, but not all, in a room to be convinced. However, she can only work a room this way once per scene, regardless of how successful she is.<br /> <br /> <b>Colony Aspect Ideas</b><br /> Suborning other colonies<br /> Creating ambient emotional effects<br /> Increased colony size/control<br /> <br /> <b>Union Ideas</b><br /> Chalices: Happy juice (or sad juice, or angry juice, generally emotional juice)<br /> Cloaks: The Peter Pan effect (if you're happy, you can fly!)<br /> Quills: Subliminal message<br /> Scepters: Command target; target justifies actions<br /> Shields: Emotional protection<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Scepters</b></u><br /> <i>A Monarch is authority incarnate. Scepters allows an Endless to weild her nobility as a weapon, using force of personality to get her way.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> [1] Vex<br /> Pain is a powerful teacher. A Monarch can cause someone to suffer by simply thinking about it.<br /> Cost: None<br /> Action: Instant, Resisted<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Authority - target Resolve<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The target feels fine. The Monarch suffers from the headache. He takes one bashing, and suffers from a -2 penalty on all mental rolls and on all extended actions.<br /> Failure:<br /> Success: The target suffers from a headache. She takes one bashing damages, and suffers from a penalty equal to successes on all mental rolls and on all extended actions. The Monarch cannot effect more than one person with Vex at a time, but he may choose to end the effect to try to Vex another.<br /> Exceptional Success: The penalty caps at -5, but the Monarch may choose to Vex another without lifting the affects of the person he's currently Vexing.<br /> <br /> [2] Kneel<br /> With the power of her will, a Monarch can command someone to commit a simple act.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant, Contested<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Authority vs. Resolve + Authority<br /> Duration: Successes turns<br /> Dramatic Failure: The target remains unbowed, and will resist all uses of this power for the next week.<br /> Failure: The target remains unbowed. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> Success: The target obeys a single command for a number of rounds equal to successes. This command cannot take longer than a round to say, and must be straightforward (&quot;Kneel,&quot; &quot;Drop the gun,&quot; &quot;Walk away&quot;). If this action would cause a breaking point, the target gets a +2 to his resistance roll. The target can spend one willpower to choose to do nothing for a turn.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Monarch can issue a new command, so long as there are still turns remaining.<br /> <br /> [3] Cower<br /> Sometimes, it's easier for a Monarch to cause his enemies to fall into a trembling heap, and use them as stepping stones.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi<br /> Action: Instant, Contested<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Authority vs Composure + Authority<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Dramatic Failure: The target does not turn to jelly, which is honestly kind of scary. The Monarch is intimidated by the target, and takes a -2 to all actions taken against her.<br /> Failure: The target does not turn to jelly. The Monarch can try again at a cumulative -1.<br /> Success: The target suffers from the Insensate Tilt for the scene, or until they suffer any damage.<br /> Exceptional Success: Additionally, the target remembers nothing that happened while under the effect of this power.<br /> <br /> [4] Obey<br /> With greater practice, a Monarch can command more complicated acts from one she commands.<br /> Cost: +1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: Commands given by Kneel can be more complicated and involved. For commands that do not cause a breaking point, the effects of Kneel last for a scene per success, with exceptional lasting for up to a week or until completed. A Monarch cannot change the command of Kneel when using Obey<br /> <br /> [5] Delay<br /> At his mastery of Scepters, a Monarch can create a sleeper agent, ready to act at the opportune moment.<br /> Cost: +1 Psi <br /> Effect: Commands given by Kneel can be delayed in their execution. The Monarch can choose a time or set of circumstances when the command will take effect. One target cannot have more delayed commands than the lower of her Resolve or Composure. The command fades after successes months if the parameters are not met.<br /> <br /> <b>Colony Aspect Ideas</b><br /> Mind control brain slugs (a la Yeerks, Goa'uld, etc)<br /> Mind blast<br /> Memetic attacks<br /> <br /> <b>Union Ideas</b><br /> Cloaks: Telekinesis<br /> Crowns: Command target; target justifies actions<br /> Hammers: Mind-control device<br /> Quills: Memory edits<br /> Records: Delay commands<br /> Shields: Mental protections<br /> Staves: Command from afar<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if someone writes the flavor of powers for a given Principality, I'm happy to mechanize it (although I may argue that something is too powerful/not powerful enough). Spheres was one of the easiest things to work on, because of the ideas that were already present and the flexibility of putting them with powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":".  added missing Mandates 04-18-2016, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:05:09-07:00","id":867564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867553#post867553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of, have two mostly-complete Principalities, brought to you by <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h3tvB8XFG3g\" target=\"_blank\">the girl from WLSD</a>. (I love the feathery psychic velociraptors, btw.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Easily one of the more interesting races too.<br /> Maybe one day I should give them &quot;sheets&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Still...<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see what took you quite alot of time. That's alot of Mandates for mental hacking and intrusion.<br /> <br /> So, hm... Maybe the top of Sceptres is literally making someone into a Manchurian agent, a secret command that activates when a keyword, passphrase... or when conditions independant of the monarch happen. (At 4 O'Clock Tommorrow...) It'd be basically an upgrade to Obey.<br /> <br /> An Upgrade to the Crowns things might be useful for modifying your inclination or motivation power too. <br /> Maybe a passive aura of creating one emotional response on instinctive level....<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-18-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:11:25-07:00","id":867639,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> <br /> I think next on your list should be reagents and hammers.<br /> <br /> I think the big difference between the two should be in scale or method. Hammers works on what objects are right now, using their properties as they exist. And though applications of problem solving allow you to build big. It should also passively increase size.<br /> Crucibles is about changing them to suit your needs, melting them down, transmitting items... or creatures for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> An idea that I had lately we could have a social splat.<br /> More specifically I was thinking of making caste more of a choice or social function. Changing your caste required evolving or reworking your very identity but was doable.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what I think... is we need something to represent a.... core, animalistic or even alien root, something that is core to every Monarch and shapes them, to show that for all of the presenses the Monarchs arr more than simply ewrthly rulers. In a sense their caste replacement since caste issue becoming a social function...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-18-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:31:10-07:00","id":867651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867639#post867639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea that I had lately we could have a social splat.<br /> More specifically I was thinking of making caste more of a choice or social function. Changing your caste required evolving or reworking your very identity but was doable.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what I think... is we need something to represent a.... core, animalistic or even alien root, something that is core to every Monarch and shapes them, to show that for all of the presenses the Monarchs arr more than simply ewrthly rulers. In a sense their caste replacement since caste issue becoming a social function...</div> </div> </div> </div>Clade, maybe? Say, the Kingmakers aren't all unique nor all one unified whole, but each belong to certain preferential groupings, which affects the Monarchs they make (Clan from Vampire, kinda). Maybe a unique trait, maybe some modifications or favored Principalities, mechanically. But fluff-wise, talk about how Clade X are often chosen for possessing Y traits, or have intincts that drive them toward Z. Caste, the role they fill in the Hive/Colony/society, can change by needs or desires, but Clade is the undeniable pull of one's heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:45:34-07:00","id":867658,"title":"","content":"I might have a go at Reagents tonight if you don't mind. I've got a bunch of alchemy and transmutation stuff left over from Dragon: The Hunted that I could use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:49:51-07:00","id":867663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867658#post867658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have a go at Reagents tonight if you don't mind. I've got a bunch of alchemy and transmutation stuff left over from Dragon: The Hunted that I could use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet.<br /> <br /> While you get that I guess maybe Ace can do hammers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think my next priority then would be fashioning something out of servant rules then. Something simple....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:00:39-07:00","id":867668,"title":"","content":"I can work on Hammers, sure. I like the idea of making Castes a social splat rather than a born-as splat. They can still dictate cheaper Principalities. The born-as (Cade works for me) could be Attribute bonuses, since it determines how you were made, and maybe a &quot;weird thing you can do&quot; or &quot;weird thing you're better at&quot;. Maybe one that's better at larger Colony control (zergs!), one that's individually stronger but not as good at colonies, one that can shift its form (the Thing), stuff like that?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the ideas for Crowns and Scepters; have filled in the missing parts (and edited above). Trying to create different powers that didn't stomp on each other and weren't a straight pull from Vampire was tricky, yeah, but I think it turned out ok.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Crowns</b></u><br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> [2] Declaration<br /> By his presence alone, a Monarch can shape a room's mood to match his own.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: Based on the Monarch's current mood, anyone in the scene is inclined to match that mood, though strong emotion may snap them out of it. Any who roughly match the mood of the Monarch gain a +1 to skills or actions in favor of the mood (intimidation and attacks for anger, persuasion and social maneuvering for calm or happiness, empathy and resistance for sadness, etc), and a -1 to all other actions.<br /> <br /> [5] Inspiration<br /> What's better than convincing one person to see your way? Convincing all of them!<br /> Cost: +2 Psi (free in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: A Monarch can use Motivation on every person in the room. Individuals are convinced as she accrues more successes then their Willpower + Supernatural Tolerance. It is possible for some, but not all, in a room to be convinced. However, she can only work a room this way once per scene, regardless of how successful she is.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Scepters</b></u><br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> [5] Delay<br /> At his mastery of Scepters, a Monarch can create a sleeper agent, ready to act at the opportune moment.<br /> Cost: +1 Psi<br /> Effect: Commands given by Kneel can be delayed in their execution. The Monarch can choose a time or set of circumstances when the command will take effect. One target cannot have more delayed commands than the lower of her Resolve or Composure. The command fades after successes months if the parameters are not met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:09:08-07:00","id":867672,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Cade brings up the right imagery. Or what the right imagery is.<br /> <br /> The idea is a bit of... irony since up til now we've all focused on the irony of nobility refining the Savage, alien monster nature of the Monarchs. Whatever it is, I want it to be a reminder of despite the appearances of the beacons or hallmarks of control and order, they're still monsters in of themselves. This should be a more.... natural ideal, a root or base urgings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:15:42-07:00","id":867677,"title":"","content":"Genus? Subspecies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:18:59-07:00","id":867681,"title":"","content":"Base, maybe? As in base nature, something low and primal, and also the basic foundations of who you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:23:22-07:00","id":867684,"title":"","content":"Source for the term: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clade\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clade</a><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A </span></span></span><b>clade</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (from </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greek\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Greek</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u03ba\u03bb\u03ac\u03b4\u03bf\u03c2</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><i>klados</i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, &quot;branch&quot;) is a group of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organism\" target=\"_blank\">organisms</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> that consists of a </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_descent\" target=\"_blank\">common ancestor</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and all its </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lineal_descendant\" target=\"_blank\">lineal descendants</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, and represents a single &quot;branch&quot; on the &quot;</span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_of_life_(science)\" target=\"_blank\">tree of life</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;.</span></span></span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T12:14:55-07:00","id":867721,"title":"","content":"Bad news I'm afraid. I've just had a look over my assignments for tomorrow and I'm not sure I'll be able to do the whole of the Principality tonight. I'll write up the powers , their flavour text and some basic stuff and come back to them tomorrow if you don't mind.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Crucibles</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>A crucible is a tool of transformation and of refinement. A ruler should be as a crucible to the unworked ore of his lands and fiefdoms, ever refining them into more perfect forms.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> <br /> <u>(1) Internal Alchemy</u><br /> <br /> The first step in both chemistry and alchemy is understanding, and this Mandate transforms the Monarch's body into a laboratory capable of analysing any substance without harm.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (Free in Noble Form)<br /> Duration: 1 scene (permanent in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: The Monarch becomes capable of digesting any substance and will suffer no ill effects. This means that he can eat rocks, wood, rotten meat or even metal and suffer no ill effects. He may even thrive on such fare, although it becomes no more appetising. Furthermore, the Monarch may reflexively roll Intelligence + Science (with no penalty for lacking dots in the latter) in order to identify the properties and chemical make-up of an ingested substance. A single success is enough to successfully analyse the material, although supernatural compounds may take more (this includes most substances created through the Principality of Chalices).<br /> <br /> <u>(2) Transmutation of Structure</u><br /> <br /> The laboratory of the Monarch's body is now capable of not only analysis but also of transmutation, reconfiguring molecules in order to attain the desired effect. The Monarch can use this Mandate in order to transmute a mass of material weighing no more than the Monarch's Authority in lbs (in earth gravity) to another state of that same material (water to ice, iron to molten iron etc) or into another substance which is made of the same elements (water to hydrogen and oxygen, coal to graphite). The Monarch must be touching the material he intends to transmute. Extremely rare or unique materials such as diamond or radioactive metals may only be transmuted at the Storyteller's discretion. This Mandate cannot be used to alter the physical shape of an object, that is the domain of the Principality of Hammers. <br /> In Noble Form, the Monarch may elect to ingest the substance to be transmuting it, passing it through a specialised series of organs before regurgitating it or expelling it via a specialised orifice. Doing so eliminates the Psi cost.<br /> (Note: this need not be an option if your group is not all that OK with biosquick).<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Psi or free in Noble Form<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Science +Crucibles<br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended, 3 turns per roll<br /> <b>Effect:</b><br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The transmutation backfires, transmuting a portion of the Monarch's body randomly and inflicting (Crucibles) in Lethal damage. The Monarch loses all successes accumulated so far.<br /> <u>Failure:</u> No successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation.<br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation. The Storyteller sets the target number of successes. Usually, making simple, natural transmutations such as water to ice take 3 successes, more complex ones such as water to oxygen and hydrogen take 5 successes and complex molecular realignments such as changing plastics to oil or petrol take 8.<br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The Monarch so masterfully manipulates the molecular structure of the matter that any Psi spent is recovered.<br /> <br /> <u>(3) Workshop</u><br /> <br /> The monarch can exert his psychic abilities to create an area in which he can easily call upon the strange physics of the Void in order to utilise Mandates of the Principality of Crucibles outside his own body, as well as easing his transmutations. This area endures for a reasonable time and is usually about the size of a small apartment.<br /> Cost: 3 Psi<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Science + Crucibles<br /> Action: Extended, 10 minutes per roll<br /> Effect: The Monarch attunes an area of approximately the size of a small apartment to the physics of the Void, allowing him to more easily call upon them in the delicate manners necessary for the application of the Principality of Crucibles. A Monarch may only have one Workshop at a time.<br /> The number of successes needed to in order to successfully create the Workshop depends upon the location in which it is being created.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Location</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Number of Required Successes</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within a Province of the Monarch in the Beneath</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the Beneath but outside of the Monarch's Province</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">10</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the Monarch's Province in the phenomenal world.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">15</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Outside the Monarch's Province in the phenomenal world.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">20</td> </tr> </table></div> While within this area, the Monarch gains a bonus to all rolls involving Science, including Mandates of the Principality of Crucibles, equal to the Monarch's rating in Crucibles, as well as being able to waive Psi costs for using Mandates of this Principality.<br /> If the Monarch at any time rolls an Exceptional Success, he may add the 9-again rule to any Science rolls within the Workshop. if he rolls a second Exceptional Success, he may add 8-again. If he rolls a third, he may add the Rote quality to any Science rolls. Only only one bonus from Exceptional Success may be applied to a given roll.<br /> If the Monarch rolls a Dramatic Failure, he loses all successes accrued so far and the location instead becomes anathema to the powers of the Void, causing a penalty to any attempt to use Principalities suffer a penalty equal to the Monarch's Authority. This effect endures for the same amount of time as a successful Workshop would.<br /> The Workshop will endure for a number of days equal to (Authority*3).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>(4) Transmutation of Substance</u><br /> <br /> . The Monarch can now not only manipulate molecular structure but also the positions of subatomic particles, allowing the Monarch to transmute a substance into a completely different one, so long as the input and output have the same mass. The mass of the material transmuted can be no greater than the Monarch's Authority in lbs. The Monarch must be touching the material he intends to transmute. Extremely rare or unique materials such as diamond or radioactive metals may only be transmuted at the Storyteller's discretion. This Mandate cannot be used to alter the physical shape of an object, that is the domain of the Principality of Hammers. The Storyteller sets the target number of successes.<br /> In Noble Form, the Monarch may elect to ingest the substance to be transmuting it, passing it through a specialised series of organs before regurgitating it or expelling it via a specialised orifice. Doing so reduces the Psi cost to 1<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Psi or 1 Psi in Noble Form<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Science + Crucibles<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended, 3 turns per roll<br /> <b>Effect: </b><br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The transmutation backfires, transmuting a portion of the Monarch's body randomly and inflicting (Crucibles) in Lethal damage. The Monarch loses all successes accumulated so far.<br /> <u>Failure:</u> No successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation.<br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation. The Storyteller sets the target number of successes. Making transmutations within the same 'category' of material, such one ferrous or noble metal to another usually require 3 successes, making transmutations across categories take 5 and drastic changes such as granite to plutonium require at least 8, if not more.<br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The Monarch so masterfully manipulates the molecular structure of the matter that any Psi spent is recovered.<br /> <br /> <u>(5) Mass Transmutation</u><br /> <br /> By exerting more of his psionic strength, the Monarch becomes able to transmute materials of far greater mass, as well as more swiftly, although this is quite draining.<br /> Cost: +3 Psi<br /> Effect: By paying the extra Psi when using either Transmutation of Structure or Transmutation of Substance, the Monarch becomes able to transmute materials of a mass equal to (Authority*10). He must still be able to touch the material. He may no longer opt to ingest it. This can be used to attack a structure, ignoring Durability and inflicting Damage to Structure equal to the highest individual roll (e.g., if a Monarch rolls three times and achieves 3, 1 and 2 successes respectively before completing the transmutation, it deals 3 damage to Structure).<br /> If the Monarch chooses to, they can also make the Action to use the aforementioned Mandates an Instant one, although this means that the Monarch only has 1 roll with which to gather the required Successes.<br /> The fact that the transmutation is now Instant means that it can be used as an attack. Before rolling to see if the Mandate succeeds, the Monarch chooses whether to inflict (successes*2) Bashing, (successes) Lethal or (successes/2) Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Colony Benefits</b><br /> <br /> Synthesizer<br /> Bonus to gathering Wealth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-19-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:12:53-07:00","id":867766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867721#post867721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad news I'm afraid. I've just had a look over my assignments for tomorrow and I'm not sure I'll be able to do the whole of the Principality tonight. I'll write up the powers , their flavour text and some basic stuff and come back to them tomorrow if you don't mind.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Crucibles</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>A crucible is a tool of transformation and of refinement. A ruler should be as a crucible to the unworked ore of his lands and fiefdoms, ever refining them into more perfect forms.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> <br /> <u>(1) Internal Alchemy</u><br /> <br /> The first step in both chemistry and alchemy is understanding, and this Mandate transforms the Monarch's body into a laboratory capable of analysing any substance without harm.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (Free in Noble Form)<br /> Duration: 1 scene (permanent in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: The Monarch becomes capable of digesting any substance and will suffer no ill effects. Furthermore, the Monarch may reflexively roll Intelligence + Science (with no penalty for lacking dots in the latter) in order to identify the properties and chemical make-up of an ingested substance.<br /> <br /> <u>(2) Transmutation of Structure</u><br /> <br /> The laboratory of the Monarch's body is now capable of not only analysis but also of transmutation, reconfiguring molecules in order to attain the desired effect.<br /> <br /> [the monarch can change small amounts of any ingested substance into any other that either has roughly similar properties or is composed of the same chemical elements.]<br /> <br /> <u>(3) Workshop</u><br /> <br /> The monarch can exert his psychic abilities to create an area in which he can easily call upon the strange physics of the Void in order to utilise Mandates of the Principality of Crucibles outside his own body, as well as easing his transmutations. This area endures for a reasonable time and is usually about the size of a small apartment. Setting up a Workshop takes time (an Extended action).<br /> <br /> <u>(4) Transmutation of Substance</u><br /> <br /> The Monarch becomes able to use his psionic abilities with the utmost delicacy, even manipulation protons, electrons and neutrons in order to create the desired substance (the more valuable or 'weird' (e.g. radioactive) the substance, the more difficult it is to transmute.<br /> <br /> <u>(5) External Alchemy</u><br /> <br /> By exerting more of his psionic strength, the Monarch becomes able to transmute with merely a touch, although this is quite draining. This can be used as an attack by transmuting a victim's blood to oil or similar unpleasant processes.</div> </div> </div> </div>For personal Shape Changing, do a Union with Cloaks, then?<br /> Union with Blades/Arrows: Material dependent composition (Silver claws, Cold Iron spines, etc.)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:24:07-07:00","id":867774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867681#post867681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Base, maybe? As in base nature, something low and primal, and also the basic foundations of who you are.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867684#post867684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source for the term: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clade\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clade</a><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A </span></span></span><b>clade</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (from </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greek\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Greek</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u03ba\u03bb\u03ac\u03b4\u03bf\u03c2</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><i>klados</i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, &quot;branch&quot;) is a group of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organism\" target=\"_blank\">organisms</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> that consists of a </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_descent\" target=\"_blank\">common ancestor</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and all its </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lineal_descendant\" target=\"_blank\">lineal descendants</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, and represents a single &quot;branch&quot; on the &quot;</span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_of_life_(science)\" target=\"_blank\">tree of life</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;.</span></span></span>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, Clade might be it then...<br /> <br /> <br /> Hm... so.<br /> <br /> My first thought is...<br /> <br /> Predator, a sort of well, predatory urgings for one of the splats. Socially or physically, not just blood and gore.<br /> <br /> Controller of some sort, domination...<br /> <br /> <br /> What else....<br /> <br /> <br /> And what kind of bonus they all give...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:55:53-07:00","id":867803,"title":"","content":"Does Crucibles seem OK so far? I'm not sure if it's overpowered, underpowered or somewhere in the middle. By the way, using External Alchemy as an attack will probably allow you to either cause the victim to suffer Aggravated damage equal to successes or inflict a poison on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:09:47-07:00","id":867807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867803#post867803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Crucibles seem OK so far? I'm not sure if it's overpowered, underpowered or somewhere in the middle. By the way, using External Alchemy as an attack will probably allow you to either cause the victim to suffer Aggravated damage equal to successes or inflict a poison on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the balance of all of them, but I am a little perplexed by 2. Because you have to eat a thing, then you can make it into another thing...but you've still eaten it. It's not very useful when it's inside you, and options for getting it out again veer into the unnessesarily gross. I'd change 2 to be by touch, still limiting it to simple changes (can turn water into ice, or hydrogen and oxygen, but not into mercury or swamp water). Maybe then 1 would also need to be by touch, but I kinda like the immunity + know what a thing is by eating/tasting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:16:42-07:00","id":867812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=867807#post867807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the balance of all of them, but I am a little perplexed by 2. Because you have to eat a thing, then you can make it into another thing...but you've still eaten it. It's not very useful when it's inside you, and options for getting it out again veer into the unnessesarily gross. I'd change 2 to be by touch, still limiting it to simple changes (can turn water into ice, or hydrogen and oxygen, but not into mercury or swamp water). Maybe then 1 would also need to be by touch, but I kinda like the immunity + know what a thing is by eating/tasting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of want to keep the bio-factor for 2, but I agree that in human form it's kind of unnecessary. Perhaps it's done with touch and spending 1 psi in both human and Noble form but in Noble form you can forego the cost by eating it and passing it through a specialized series of organs?<br /> <br /> By the way, both of the 'normal' transmutations are Extended actions taking 3 turns per roll. It's not an instant thing unless you pair it with External Alchemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T07:35:09-07:00","id":868414,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alright so got a modified version of the older Vassal rules for Servants.<br /> <br /> Can anyone look in the tag below and tell me what else should I put in before I go writing up specific servants.<br /> <br /> I'm looking at .... 1 for all of the races for an infested version. And then a few other specific sheets for Elites.<br /> <br /> Also going to write stuff about an Elite Foreman (normal Foreman is dumb and just acts as a helper for Drone herds)</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Servants are more advanced creatures created by the Monarch to act as her lieutenants. Each is more free willed and intelligent than a basic drone and is able to act as a driver, manager, coordinator, or often, commander in the Monarch\u2019s stead.Servants are created a number of ways. The most basic vassals, the Elite Foreman, is available to all Monarchs at all times. Other Servants require the Monarch possesses or has access to specific genetic templates found in specific Gene Foundries and Provinces. Other times, a Servant requires a specific independent creature be infested. It all depends on the servant you are attempting to create.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regardless of the means, Servant creation requires the Monarch order her Colony to perform a Create Servant action and pay the cost in Wealth and takes a number of days equal to Wealth spent. Many servants require specific types of resources in their creation, others do not care about it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pre-existing and soon to be hatched Servants may be modified from the norm. Most templates possesses a number of \u201cMutations\u201d representing packages of genetic modifications. Each, for the cost for further resources, provides new abilities, augments existing ones, or changes the Vassal\u2019s equipment from the norm.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to apply a Mutation, the Monarch simply pays for the cost of the Mutation as well as possess the Principalities to handle it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the description of each Mutation, it lists which Vassals it may be applied to. In the case of some Mutations, such as weaponry or armor morphs, they may remove existing features or come with statistics penalties, also specified in the Mutation\u2019s description. Each specific Mutations may only be applied once to a Vassal once and obviously, if a Mutation replaces an existing feature from the template, such as a weapon, other Mutations that replace that feature may not be applied.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mutations take 1 hour to apply, during which the Vassal is disabled and inside a Cocoon mutation. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Removing or changing mutations from an existing Vassal or outright disposing of a Vassal does not refund the costs made to produce either.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As Vassals are part of the Monarch\u2019s Colony, any metanormal effects that involve Authority use the Monarch\u2019s Authority when determining the Vassal\u2019s.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-19-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T08:44:20-07:00","id":868462,"title":"","content":"The Mandates of Crucibles are up. Some feedback would be great. I'm fresh out of ideas for colony benefits though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:15:10-07:00","id":868477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868462#post868462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mandates of Crucibles are up. Some feedback would be great. I'm fresh out of ideas for colony benefits though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Crucibles transforms stuff, right? I'd say that's worth some Wealth production (or even generation, though obvious not an alternative to real harvesting), or maybe allowing you to ignore the specific &quot;type&quot; of wealth when necessary. Would this, or Hammers, let your Colony give you &quot;free&quot; Equipment? Nothing like bio-horror Sweat Shops churning out masses of guns or shoes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:20:22-07:00","id":868480,"title":"","content":"All the Crucibles stuff lacks Dramatic Failures and Exceptional Successes.<br /> <br /> (1) Internal Alchemy: what kind of successes are required for analyzing a thing? Simple pass/fail? More info for more successes? I personally wouldn't have untrained Science be free of penalties, but I'm mean like that.<br /> <br /> (2) Transmutation of Structure: description doesn't say the Monarch has to poke what they're transmuting. <br /> <br /> (3) Workshop: how long is &quot;a reasonable time&quot;? Scene? Day? Story? How many Workshops can a Monarch have? Do they have to own/be able to change the space? I'd rule the bonus to be based on successes, rather than Authority, with Exceptional granting Rote Science or something.<br /> <br /> (4) Transmutation of Substance: as with #2<br /> <br /> (5) Mass Transmutation: I might add mechanics for when this is used as an attack (successes*2 bashing, successes lethal, or successes/2 agg).<br /> <br /> Colony Aspects: maybe they can also use Internal Alchemy? Or a bonus to wealth, or ability to change some ambient attributes of an area (by changing what's in it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:21:14-07:00","id":868538,"title":"","content":"So... this reminds me of things I need to set straight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Firstly. Aspects are a swarm specific modification. You enable them to give your Swarms more capabilities at the cost of reduced numbers or resources.<br /> <br /> Colony.... upgrades shouldn't be called Aspects and should be called something else to avoid confusion in the future. They should either enable new capabilities or modify existing ones and are always enabled with it having to do the equipment management thing. I guess upgrades work for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly. I think maybe it's time to start settling on the Principality dice pool. More specifically, I think the dice pool should be Attribute, Skill, and Principality dots added together, instead of Authority with other elements<br /> I suppose I might still have some biases against it, but after I started fleshing out Colonies and now Servants, I realize that having Authority feed into Principality dice pools makes them too pervasive since it means it's used also in Colony and servant actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> And honestly I think it makes more sense to have Authority for Colony and servant actions since the point of Authority is to delegate, represent the power the Monarch has through others or through communication . Principalities meanwhile reflect your own leanings and personal power, which in turn affects your Servants and Colony through your decisions and emulation of you..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:38:09-07:00","id":868557,"title":"","content":"So Aspects are chosen, Upgrades are automatic. Why is there a difference? How can you tell what should be an Aspect and what should be an Upgrade? <br /> <br /> I'm still against Attribute + Skill + Principality. As I stated before, I don't like how it scales, and I don't like how it forces you to specialize rather than generalize. I'm fine with Authority being pervasive, as it is the power stat, that's how power stats work, they are valuable and tie into everything. I'm more in favor of Attribute + Authority, Attribute + Skill + Authority, or Attribute + Skill. (Obviously only one should be picked and stuck with, rather than having two or three different ways of doing things.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:43:50-07:00","id":868566,"title":"","content":"OK, I've had a go at revising Crucibles, as well as adding mechanics for using Mass Transmutation to attack objects and people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:46:53-07:00","id":868568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868557#post868557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Aspects are chosen, Upgrades are automatic. Why is there a difference? How can you tell what should be an Aspect and what should be an Upgrade? <br /> <br /> I'm still against Attribute + Skill + Principality. As I stated before, I don't like how it scales, and I don't like how it forces you to specialize rather than generalize. I'm fine with Authority being pervasive, as it is the power stat, that's how power stats work, they are valuable and tie into everything. I'm more in favor of Attribute + Authority, Attribute + Skill + Authority, or Attribute + Skill. (Obviously only one should be picked and stuck with, rather than having two or three different ways of doing things.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's actually the exception, rather than the norm for Power stats to be used in Power dicepools, atleast for Splats that have a Principality like equivalent. Still, I think specialization should be encouraged, because then it gives more reason for Alliances to form, covering for each other's capabilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also the reason why Swarms have to choose and enable aspects and why Colonies get free upgrades is a simple one. You have to go out of your way to make a Swarm, a true Swarm and you build it to complete specific tasks, usually fighting but sometimes building things. Your Colony always and still exists with upgrades representing infastructure or wide range gene modifications that are frankly.... everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T11:20:23-07:00","id":868598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868568#post868568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's actually the exception, rather than the norm for Power stats to be used in Power dicepools, atleast for Splats that have a Principality like equivalent. Still, I think specialization should be encouraged, because then it gives more reason for Alliances to form, covering for each other's capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splats that use Power Stat in dicepools: Changeling, Promethean (some), Demon (some)<br /> Splats that use Power in dicepools: Vampire, Geist<br /> Splats that use both: Mage<br /> Splats that use neither: Werewolf (Attribute + Skill + Renown), Mummy (doesn't use pools AFAIK), Beast (Attribute + Satiety), Promethean (some), Demon (some)<br /> <br /> It's the exception for Power Stat to be used, but it's also the exception for Power to be used, if by &quot;exception&quot; you mean &quot;less than 50% of major splats.&quot; More splats use Power Stat than Power in pools, and more still do neither, but none of them are the majority. <br /> <br /> Choosing specialization is fine, and having cooler powers as a reward for that is a valid thing. But building the powers such that you can only be effective if you specialize limits choice in an unfun way, hence why I don't want to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868566#post868566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I've had a go at revising Crucibles, as well as adding mechanics for using Mass Transmutation to attack objects and people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still lacking Dramatic fails and most Exceptional successes, but looking good to me. (Maybe Structure damage should work like lethal damage? IDK.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T11:39:34-07:00","id":868617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868538#post868538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Colony.... upgrades shouldn't be called Aspects and should be called something else to avoid confusion in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Investments? (As in, the investment of power and/or authority)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868538#post868538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should either enable new capabilities or modify existing ones and are always enabled with it having to do the equipment management thing. I guess upgrades work for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, considering Servants/Vassals are more individualized, it should be the opposite, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868538#post868538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly. I think maybe it's time to start settling on the Principality dice pool. More specifically, I think the dice pool should be Attribute, Skill, and Principality dots added together, instead of Authority with other elements<br /> I suppose I might still have some biases against it, but after I started fleshing out Colonies and now Servants, I realize that having Authority feed into Principality dice pools makes them too pervasive since it means it's used also in Colony and servant actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you wanted to mix things up, you could always do something like Attribute + Authority + Principality, arguing on the basis that these are more inherent powers than applications of skill. I wouldn't recommend that, just throwing the idea out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868538#post868538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And honestly I think it makes more sense to have Authority for Colony and servant actions since the point of Authority is to delegate, represent the power the Monarch has through others or through communication . Principalities meanwhile reflect your own leanings and personal power, which in turn affects your Servants and Colony through your decisions and emulation of you..</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds reasonable.<br /> <hr /><br /> Addendum: At this point, I'm getting a little confused regarding the distinction between Swarms and Servants. Both occupy the &quot;minion of the Hive/Colony&quot; niche. Where they differ is scale, right? Swarms are masses of creatures, while Servants are custom made lieutenants, right? Principalities primarily add to the Monarch's power, while offering some benefit to the Colony and Servants?<br /> <br /> What role do each occupy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-19-2016, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T12:37:45-07:00","id":868672,"title":"","content":"Crucibles has been re-re-revised, with added dramatic Failures and Exceptional Successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T12:42:25-07:00","id":868676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868598#post868598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Splats that use Power Stat in dicepools: Changeling, Promethean (some), Demon (some)<br /> Splats that use Power in dicepools: Vampire, Geist<br /> Splats that use both: Mage<br /> Splats that use neither: Werewolf (Attribute + Skill + Renown), Mummy (doesn't use pools AFAIK), Beast (Attribute + Satiety), Promethean (some), Demon (some)<br /> <br /> It's the exception for Power Stat to be used, but it's also the exception for Power to be used, if by &quot;exception&quot; you mean &quot;less than 50% of major splats.&quot; More splats use Power Stat than Power in pools, and more still do neither, but none of them are the majority.<br /> <br /> Choosing specialization is fine, and having cooler powers as a reward for that is a valid thing. But building the powers such that you can only be effective if you specialize limits choice in an unfun way, hence why I don't want to do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Still lacking Dramatic fails and most Exceptional successes, but looking good to me. (Maybe Structure damage should work like lethal damage? IDK.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Promethean isn't standardized and actually seemed to run the whole gamut plus more. Mummy is also the same way having lots of different dicepools. It actually seems to be the thing about 1e WoD lines, that they sometimes lack consistency. Werewolf has similar problems in the old Edition, not anymore though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Still, I do understand where you are coming from. Personally, I'm mostly invested for following the Attribute + Skill + Principality dots thing is largely because Principalities are closest to Disciplines in structure and thus I feel it is adequate to emulate their dice pool mechanics. I mean, we've got a Devotion equivalent at this point...<br /> <br /> That plus... as I said before, I don't want to make Authority the primary dice modifer because of Authority is used in all Colony action as it is and as I thought on it more, the more I felt that the main seperation point between Authority and Principality is in regards to what is being acted upon.<br /> <br /> Authority is used when we're talking about the Colony as a whole or when you use things pertaining to it or your servitors.<br /> Principality is a bit more personal, referencing your own skill and ability as a Monarch on an individual level.<br /> <br /> It also makes more sense, to me at least... that something called Authority only applies in the context of the group you rule over... rather than your own dealings of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> However, I think both of us can agree to Attribute + Skill as the basis... with the 3rd component perhaps might remain in contest. Perhaps it should be a context dependant thing? You use Principality dots when you are alone, but when with your Swarm or in your Colony, you use Authority dots when it's an improvement to do so?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868617#post868617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Investments? (As in, the investment of power and/or authority)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If anything, considering Servants/Vassals are more individualized, it should be the opposite, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, if you wanted to mix things up, you could always do something like Attribute + Authority + Principality, arguing on the basis that these are more inherent powers than applications of skill. I wouldn't recommend that, just throwing the idea out there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sounds reasonable. <hr /><br /> Addendum: At this point, I'm getting a little confused regarding the distinction between Swarms and Servants. Both occupy the &quot;minion of the Hive/Colony&quot; niche. Where they differ is scale, right? Swarms are masses of creatures, while Servants are custom made lieutenants, right? Principalities primarily add to the Monarch's power, while offering some benefit to the Colony and Servants?<br /> <br /> What role do each occupy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Investments work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The reason why Aspects exist was because I copied and edited the rules from Claire's zombie swarm creation guide, where Aspects was a mechanic I thought might make sense in the context of Swarms. I kept it because I liked the idea that you could spend &quot;size&quot; of the Swarm to represent investing in a more &quot;tactical&quot; loadout as opposed to a mass of numbers as well as provide something to trade for when you had a Swarm above 10.<br /> <br /> We could remove them and rejig the Swarm mechanics to do without them, but I'd need to figure out a trade off mechanic of some description.... Maybe successes to attribute dots could work... I'd need to allow for more dice to be involved in that case....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Colony represents... everything. Every organism and every &quot;building&quot;, the totality of your nation. It's the biggest group and also represents your total capacity to accomplish tasks.<br /> <br /> Swarm are represents specific task forces made from the Colony's industries to either fight or complete complex tasks, such as build a bridge or feats of architecture. It's seperate from the Colony in order to represent that even if the Swarm dies... or multiple Swarms die, you can still always replace them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Servants are elite one-off unique creatures that act as lieutenants. Think of a lesser Monarch or ghoul retainer. They can act as leaders to Swarms in your stead or well, act as Retainers. Granted... I think Servants are the most disposable of the 3 to remove if I ever wanted to because they aren't as important as say a Colony or Swarm is....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-19-2016, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T13:25:20-07:00","id":868704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868617#post868617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you wanted to mix things up, you could always do something like Attribute + Authority + Principality, arguing on the basis that these are more inherent powers than applications of skill. I wouldn't recommend that, just throwing the idea out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be the one thing Almarck and I could agree on not doing :P But congrats on finding the perfect compromise! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868676#post868676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean isn't standardized and actually seemed to run the whole gamut plus more. Mummy is also the same way having lots of different dicepools. It actually seems to be the thing about 1e WoD lines, that they sometimes lack consistency. Werewolf has similar problems in the old Edition, not anymore though.<br /> <br /> Still, I do understand where you are coming from. Personally, I'm mostly invested for following the Attribute + Skill + Principality dots thing is largely because Principalities are closest to Disciplines in structure and thus I feel it is adequate to emulate their dice pool mechanics. I mean, we've got a Devotion equivalent at this point...<br /> <br /> That plus... as I said before, I don't want to make Authority the primary dice modifer because of Authority is used in all Colony action as it is and as I thought on it more, the more I felt that the main seperation point between Authority and Principality is in regards to what is being acted upon.<br /> <br /> Authority is used when we're talking about the Colony as a whole or when you use things pertaining to it or your servitors.<br /> Principality is a bit more personal, referencing your own skill and ability as a Monarch on an individual level.<br /> <br /> It also makes more sense, to me at least... that something called Authority only applies in the context of the group you rule over... rather than your own dealings of.<br /> <br /> However, I think both of us can agree to Attribute + Skill as the basis... with the 3rd component perhaps might remain in contest. Perhaps it should be a context dependant thing? You use Principality dots when you are alone, but when with your Swarm or in your Colony, you use Authority dots when it's an improvement to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're throwing out 1e, then there's only one splat that uses Power as part of the pool of activation: Vampire. Mage might (probably will, probably will also use Gnosis) but it hasn't dropped, and Werewolf, Changeling, Demon, and Beast don't do that thing. Basically, saying &quot;most splats do it this way&quot; is false, and not a good argument to make. <br /> <br /> Personally, I don't like how Vampire does pools, and I'd rather move away from it. I like how Changeling, Werewolf, and Demon do pools. Changeling's a great example, actually: it was previously Wyrd + Attribute, Wyrd + Skill, or Wyrd + Skill + Mantle, very inconsistent. In the 2e revision, it's Attribute + Skill + Wyrd, same as Demon (when Demon uses pools, anyway). While we are mimicking Devotions, that doesn't mean we have to copy all of it. <br /> <br /> My understanding was that Authority = Power. You impose your Authority on others, you impose your Authority on the world, you impose your Authority on yourself. Principalities start with knowledge, but making a change in the world with that knowledge requires will, effort, and sheer bloody-mindedness. That's Authority. It's the right to rule, and also the will to do so. <br /> <br /> In terms of compromise, I'm in favor of simplicity above anything else, even above my dislike of using Principalities in the pool. Of the choices that have been floated, in order of most to least favored, is:<br /> Attribute (or Skill) + Authority<br /> Attribute + Skill + Authority<br /> Attribute + Skill<br /> Attribute + Skill + Principality<br /> Attribute + Authority + Principality<br /> Attribute + Skill + (context dependent)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=868676#post868676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Investments work.<br /> <br /> The reason why Aspects exist was because I copied and edited the rules from Claire's zombie swarm creation guide, where Aspects was a mechanic I thought might make sense in the context of Swarms. I kept it because I liked the idea that you could spend &quot;size&quot; of the Swarm to represent investing in a more &quot;tactical&quot; loadout as opposed to a mass of numbers as well as provide something to trade for when you had a Swarm above 10.<br /> <br /> We could remove them and rejig the Swarm mechanics to do without them, but I'd need to figure out a trade off mechanic of some description.... Maybe successes to attribute dots could work... I'd need to allow for more dice to be involved in that case....<br /> <br /> Colony represents... everything. Every organism and every &quot;building&quot;, the totality of your nation. It's the biggest group and also represents your total capacity to accomplish tasks.<br /> <br /> Swarm are represents specific task forces made from the Colony's industries to either fight or complete complex tasks, such as build a bridge or feats of architecture. It's seperate from the Colony in order to represent that even if the Swarm dies... or multiple Swarms die, you can still always replace them.<br /> <br /> Servants are elite one-off unique creatures that act as lieutenants. Think of a lesser Monarch or ghoul retainer. They can act as leaders to Swarms in your stead or well, act as Retainers. Granted... I think Servants are the most disposable of the 3 to remove if I ever wanted to because they aren't as important as say a Colony or Swarm is....</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to simplify: <br /> <br /> <b>Colonies </b>are a passive thing that every Monarch gets. They are a bunch of small creatures that do simple tasks, like getting resources and information.<br /> <b>Swarms</b> are active creations/organizations of Colonies. They are a bunch of small creatures that do more complicated tasks, like fighting and spying.<br /> <b>Servants </b>are active creations of Colonies. They are a single, powerful creature that does more complicated tasks, like fighting and spying.<br /> <br /> Might I suggest that Servants are made into a Merit? Possibly also Swarms. Both seem to be active choices that a Monarch can choose to have or not, while Colonies are ubiquitous. Principalities can have three tracks: <i>Mandates </i>(powers for you), <i>Benefits </i>(auto-powers/benefits for your colony), and <i>Aspects </i>(powers you can apply to Swarms and Servants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:47:20-07:00","id":868840,"title":"","content":"My list is partially opposite which makes this harder than yiud think. Well subtracting context dependant and both stats....<br /> <br /> I think we might have to go with attribute + skill. Simplest compromise then. That neither of us are diametrically opposed to.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think Principalities will have to use both Authority and Principality anyways for the Clash of Wills anyways... I know werewolf and vampire both use power stat + trait for clash of wills...<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage last i checked was using arcana + gnosis with rotes adding skill or an Attribute or perhaps rerolling....<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways. I think maybe Servants could be made into a merit, not sure about swarms though. The idea for then was always building a disposable army made up of rapidly conscripted and freshly grown units on the fly rather than a permanent armed force that you kept around.<br /> <br /> Sure you have a security force and your drones basically were that too, but mustering a real army is different","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-19-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T04:16:18-07:00","id":869214,"title":"","content":"So:<br /> <b>Colony</b>: Inherent stuff Monarchs get. Extends into numerous sub-systems.<br /> <b>Swarms</b>: Temporary forces the Colony can generate. Distinct from &quot;Colony actions&quot; in that Swarms are for shorter timescale things (attacks, active spying, fast movement of resources).<br /> <b>Servants</b>: Singular creatures custom built to a task. Enduring.<br /> <br /> Suggestions:<br /> <b>Colony</b>: Make this handle the general, slower, unrolled actions. Principalities unlock more things that they can do, or let them do things faster. Doesn't have &quot;rolled&quot; actions (on the basis of - if the Colony is doing it, they can take long enough to get it done right).<br /> <b>Swarms</b>: Make these the temporary, abstract collection of forces. Used for actual Dice pool actions. Keep the previous system where Principalities allow for Size to be traded for ability. They cost to create and have a shelf life, so they aren't always in existence.<br /> <b>Servants</b>: Model these off Retainer, but expand a bit with Servant-only Merits that can improve them. Make Principality X at Y dots pre-requisites for said improvement Merits (yes you have to spend XP on them). Mitigate the XP costs by: Certain Clades or Castes get &quot;discounts&quot; or &quot;rebates&quot; (Beat or XP refunds). Make them cheaper in general. Fitting the &quot;minion&quot; theme still, let Monarchs recycle them to rebuild new Servants per Chapter/Story. <hr /><br /> Addendum: After thinking about this after posting, I'm now enthusiastic about this approach and will explain more when I have time later. Also, commentary on Principality passive bonuses (if they are still a thing). <hr /><br /> So, some more thought/text:<br /> <br /> I think removing Rolled actions from Colonies themselves might help, both to streamline, and to add clear distinction on purpose. Colony actions would be mostly maintenance or simple tasks that aren't really risky, but they are time consuming. Not sure if you'd place Principality unlocks under the section for Colonies, or on the Principality - it depends on how many there are. Play would basically be: determine what your Colony is doing this Chapter/etc. Unless something comes up, it gets done. Basically, this is the automatic stuff that Cults can do.<br /> <br /> Swarms, then, would be for when you need something you either need done now-ish, or something that Colonies can't just <i>do</i>. Breed/Conscript armies to fight, generate swarms of spy creatures, spawn special harvesters to collect some resources/Wealth before a rival gets back, etc. These have dice pools, and are involved in chancy things like combat. Because they are special purpose, they exist only as long as their task requires, being recycled back into the Colony (as much as possible) after the action. The &quot;trade swarm size for [benefit]&quot; can be seen as the time/resource cost involved in spawning/designing the extra capabilities. This is similar to the rolled action Cults can do, and summoning up cult fighters.<br /> <br /> Servants are the pet projects and favored minions of the Monarch. They are individualized (even if based on a basic template), specially tinkered with and modified to suit the Monarch's goals, but lasting longer than the single purpose Swarms. They functionally serve the same roles as Retainers, subject to the Principality and Province based augmenting Merits that the Monarch crafts them with. Recycling is basically in-universe Sanctity of Merits to rebuild your agents and minions. Once nice thing about Servant Investments being Merit-based is that it lets them be offloaded to the Merits section (rather than bloating the Principalities write up), and allows more flexibility. A Monarch can sink a lot of XP into designing a multitude of new and terrifying creations, similar to (but different) than Mummies sinking XP and effort into their Cults.<br /> <br /> As to Principality granted inherent bonuses, after thinking about it in the vein of XP costs and redundancy, I'm actually against them. If Bows gives free Attributes or Skills, for instance, it either needs to add that cost into the Principality, or why would anyone bother spending XP on &quot;mere&quot; Attributes and Skills when they can get them in a bulk package as part of Principalities (which also have Active powers, Colony upgrades, Swarm Aspects, etc.). Those inherent abilities and traits a master of Blades &quot;should&quot; have? Let them pick them up separately. And maybe use as many of the existing Merits as possible (such as Iron Skin for inherent armor, upgrading to Advanced and Epic versions as needed). For things that are missing: new Monarch (and Servant) only Merits (such as Size increases, etc.). Maybe some fancy new Style Merits, for logically chained improvements?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-20-2016, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T07:34:07-07:00","id":869304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869214#post869214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So:<br /> <b>Colony</b>: Inherent stuff Monarchs get. Extends into numerous sub-systems.<br /> <b>Swarms</b>: Temporary forces the Colony can generate. Distinct from &quot;Colony actions&quot; in that Swarms are for shorter timescale things (attacks, active spying, fast movement of resources).<br /> <b>Servants</b>: Singular creatures custom built to a task. Enduring.<br /> <br /> Suggestions:<br /> <b>Colony</b>: Make this handle the general, slower, unrolled actions. Principalities unlock more things that they can do, or let them do things faster. Doesn't have &quot;rolled&quot; actions (on the basis of - if the Colony is doing it, they can take long enough to get it done right).<br /> <b>Swarms</b>: Make these the temporary, abstract collection of forces. Used for actual Dice pool actions. Keep the previous system where Principalities allow for Size to be traded for ability. They cost to create and have a shelf life, so they aren't always in existence.<br /> <b>Servants</b>: Model these off Retainer, but expand a bit with Servant-only Merits that can improve them. Make Principality X at Y dots pre-requisites for said improvement Merits (yes you have to spend XP on them). Mitigate the XP costs by: Certain Clades or Castes get &quot;discounts&quot; or &quot;rebates&quot; (Beat or XP refunds). Make them cheaper in general. Fitting the &quot;minion&quot; theme still, let Monarchs recycle them to rebuild new Servants per Chapter/Story. <hr /><br /> Addendum: After thinking about this after posting, I'm now enthusiastic about this approach and will explain more when I have time later. Also, commentary on Principality passive bonuses (if they are still a thing).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would like to think I am open to revising things, yet I don't know about it.<br /> <br /> Your suggestion would require me to redo pretty much everything in Colonies or Swarms. Not neccesarily a bad idea.<br /> <br /> As of the moment, the Colony when instructed to do something just rolls a relevant Attribute + Authority such as military for Mustering forces. This handles the logistics of determining how many to send. There's also supposed to be a list of &quot;unrolled&quot; actions but that never got fleshed out yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Swarms, currently, are mostly a military thing. Their mechanics for creation as well as the Swarm rank thing has always been linked to that. I am somewhat for broadening their utility though, but the fluff for them is pretty much a large mass of &quot;dumb&quot; Endless headed by smarter &quot;Foremen&quot;. In the other Colony actions, I.E. Sending Emmisaries, using Scientists, archetects, these Foremen do all of the thinking and don't often &quot;need&quot; the big numbers of the Swarms to do things... by and large, a Swarm doesn't work for all &quot;rolled&quot; actions since the large mass of the Swarm is often a detriment...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll discount Servants for now since they were always an optional thing. Maybe go for Retainers....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I got some work in last night for Cades.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Things I need:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=1 more Cade if I want to have 5 of them</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=Benefits for Cades.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ideas:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=What if Caste defined Monarch forms cleanly and switching Caste made you adopt that Caste\u2019s Traits? I.E Marshall to Scribe means trading brawn for brain. Strength for Intelligence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other projects I started on:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=High Priority: Autonomy. Need suggestions for how to handle sliding scale. At the moment, I think a Harmony styled balancing act is ideal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the heart of everyone Monarch is an impulse, a specific desire brought upon and imprinted at the core of their very sequences. While all Monarchs are rulers, they are all also beasts, monsters, savages, no matter how hard they attempt to forget it for that is written within their blood and is immutable.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is not merely a curse however, but also a source of power. While a Monarch is granted these instincts to struggle against, the benefits they provide are potent.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dominator: The need for control. With this Cade, a Monarch seeks to control everything and have it subjected to her will.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Predator: The need for the hunt. With this Cade, the Monarch is a huntress, stalking and devouring her prey for the enjoyment of it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evolutionist: The need for change. With this Cade, the Monarch seeks to grow and evolve to become stronger, not for any real reason, safe evolution itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breeder: The need to procreate. With this Cade, the Monarch\u2019s attention is turned towards creation and birthing, where she seeks to incubate the next generation, one better than the current one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:32:01-07:00","id":869336,"title":"","content":"Aspects using Attribute + Skill is something I could get behind, as is using Authority + Principality for Clash of Wills. I'm interested if anyone else has strong opinions about it.<br /> <br /> I think Vent0's suggestions for how to delineate Colonies/Swarms/Servants makes them easier to understand and deal with from a gameplay side. Colonies could still have a task of &quot;build Swarm&quot;, which would then give you a Swarm to use before it died/disbanded/went back to being a Colony. It also helps move Swarms away from just being fighty-military, since they're now doing all tasks where there's a chance for failure, including spying, active gathering, etc. <br /> <br /> I also agree with dropping passive bonuses for Principalities.<br /> <br /> Interested to see Autonomy; it does seem like it should be sliding scale a la Harmony.<br /> <br /> For Cades, I like the ideas, though I want to rename the last two (&quot;Evolutionist&quot; doesn't fit the pattern; &quot;Breeder&quot; is a loaded term). Something like &quot;Mutator&quot; and &quot;Creator&quot;? Also, maybe playing up the alien mindset more? Having them be based on base impulses make sense, but so much of the fiction that's been shared is emphasizing how weird and alien they are. Maybe their base impulses are different than ours (&quot;Predator&quot; seems like the most human/Earthy one). Control, adapt, multiply, and...seek? Destroy? Obey? I'm trying to think of what aliens <i>do</i>, what their purpose is. They find new lands; they take over the lands; they kill those who don't submit; they change to fit their environment; they make more of themselves; they do it all again. Maybe the fifth could be some kind of seeker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:58:30-07:00","id":869361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869336#post869336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspects using Attribute + Skill is something I could get behind, as is using Authority + Principality for Clash of Wills. I'm interested if anyone else has strong opinions about it.<br /> <br /> I think Vent0's suggestions for how to delineate Colonies/Swarms/Servants makes them easier to understand and deal with from a gameplay side. Colonies could still have a task of &quot;build Swarm&quot;, which would then give you a Swarm to use before it died/disbanded/went back to being a Colony. It also helps move Swarms away from just being fighty-military, since they're now doing all tasks where there's a chance for failure, including spying, active gathering, etc.<br /> <br /> I also agree with dropping passive bonuses for Principalities.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My main issue with changing Swarms is.... I'd need to completely redo the entire Swarm mechanics functionalities since the model I went with was based off a zombie horde and got more powerful based on size.<br /> <br /> I suppose what I could do then is have a break down similar to this:<br /> <br /> <br /> Colony still has the attributes.<br /> <br /> Swarms represent specific task groups of the Colony that use Colony's Attributes for all things and has any number of them.... as long as they could be paid for.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... Military is used for all Combat traits wit The &quot;Swarm size&quot; is based on resources spent building the Swarm....<br /> <br /> <br /> I would want to have Swarms have more varried combat stats though.... and having them all be based off of Military is... boring if practical.<br /> <br /> <br /> The main issue then is... for many tasks, you don't need the extra size or resources for anything. I guess they can still be used for trading...or for extra dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Resource Gathering should be automatic then for one's Core Province. Still need to &quot;manually&quot; deploy a task force to do harvesting.<br /> <br /> You can send Swarms to go do other area<br /> <br /> Maybe Swarm size can be limits for things, such as in gathering, how much they can carry before going back on. But what about Diplomacy or Espionage, those.. don't need excess size.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... on the topic of Dice. It's still probably reasonable to give every ability a dice roll of Authority+Attribute.... except for... Military. Which I don't think makes sense to give it that for attacking...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I guess we intergrate Aspects and Investments into the same listing then....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Passive bonuses to Principalities was something I kinda wanted to be a thing largely to represent the &quot;evolving&quot; theme, as you got versed in topics, you were stronger. I know that for the physical principalities, they'll likely keep their passive bonuses that's what they're about, but I was hoping mental and social attributes would be raised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-20-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:20:12-07:00","id":869376,"title":"","content":"Why would you have to redo swarm mechanics? They could still be size-based. Pools could improve as size got larger; there'd just be more kinds of pools. Varied stats could be gotten via Principalities; if you want a Swarm that's better at ranged stuff, pick up Bows; if you want one that's better at getting optimal materials, use Crucibles. Just because combat has Military as a base doesn't mean that variations can't build upon that base. Espionage could totally use a larger swarm: you have more bugs you can put in more places, you're better able to track targets, if some get caught and fried it's not the end of the mission. Diplomacy, having a bigger force means folks are more likely to respect you. Send one bug, it gets laughed out of court; send ten, they get to sit at the table; send fifty, they sit at the head. <br /> <br /> Why is it not reasonable to give swarm attack rolls Authority + Military? Have a base swarm use that as an attack roll, counts as a 0L weapon, no range. Spend Aspects to get greater damage (Blades), range (Bows), targets (Spheres), mobility (Cloaks), etc, etc. Maybe at each level of a Principality, you can pick an Aspect to unlock, related to one of the five areas. And then you can choose to apply it to future Swarms as a trade-off to Size.<br /> <br /> You already get stronger as you unlock stuff with Principalities. That's what the new powers represent. There's already a mechanic for &quot;getting stronger/evolving&quot;, it's &quot;spending XP on Attributes and Authority&quot;. Adding it on makes Principalities mechanically unbalanced, particularly if only some of them get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:24:08-07:00","id":869380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869304#post869304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of the moment, the Colony when instructed to do something just rolls a relevant Attribute + Authority such as military for Mustering forces. This handles the logistics of determining how many to send. There's also supposed to be a list of &quot;unrolled&quot; actions but that never got fleshed out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my idea was instead of rolling, just make it a flat effect, reserved for unrolled actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869304#post869304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarms, currently, are mostly a military thing. Their mechanics for creation as well as the Swarm rank thing has always been linked to that. I am somewhat for broadening their utility though, but the fluff for them is pretty much a large mass of &quot;dumb&quot; Endless headed by smarter &quot;Foremen&quot;. In the other Colony actions, I.E. Sending Emmisaries, using Scientists, archetects, these Foremen do all of the thinking and don't often &quot;need&quot; the big numbers of the Swarms to do things... by and large, a Swarm doesn't work for all &quot;rolled&quot; actions since the large mass of the Swarm is often a detriment...</div> </div> </div> </div>With the suggestion, Swarms would then be used for Military (obvious), but also for any other task that involves some risk/roll, again limited by the fact they are a mere mob of bioforms. Build a structure quick? Generate a Swarm suited to building, or just let the Colony do it (but take a lot longer). Harvest non-Automatic resources? Generate a Harvester Swarm and let it roll to do it.<br /> <br /> [Potentially] In this model, Swarms would cost something (Wealth? Biomass?) to generate (so you couldn't just spawn an infinite amount). They do their thing. If successful (or at least, not Dramatic Failure), you get some of the resource back as they are recycled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869304#post869304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll discount Servants for now since they were always an optional thing. Maybe go for Retainers....</div> </div> </div> </div>Discount as in &quot;less XP&quot;, or discount as in &quot;ignore for now&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869304#post869304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, I got some work in last night for <b>Cades</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't it be C<b>l</b>ades? Or are you changing the term?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869304#post869304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Things I need:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=1 more Cade if I want to have 5 of them</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=Benefits for Cades.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ideas:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=What if Caste defined Monarch forms cleanly and switching Caste made you adopt that Caste\u2019s Traits? I.E Marshall to Scribe means trading brawn for brain. Strength for Intelligence.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Inherent traits, or Principality discounts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869304#post869304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other projects I started on:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">=High Priority: Autonomy. Need suggestions for how to handle sliding scale. At the moment, I think a Harmony styled balancing act is ideal.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give examples?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869304#post869304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the heart of everyone Monarch is an impulse, a specific desire brought upon and imprinted at the core of their very sequences. While all Monarchs are rulers, they are all also beasts, monsters, savages, no matter how hard they attempt to forget it for that is written within their blood and is immutable.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is not merely a curse however, but also a source of power. While a Monarch is granted these instincts to struggle against, the benefits they provide are potent.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dominator: The need for control. With this Cade, a Monarch seeks to control everything and have it subjected to her will.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Predator: The need for the hunt. With this Cade, the Monarch is a huntress, stalking and devouring her prey for the enjoyment of it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evolutionist: The need for change. With this Cade, the Monarch seeks to grow and evolve to become stronger, not for any real reason, safe evolution itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breeder: The need to procreate. With this Cade, the Monarch\u2019s attention is turned towards creation and birthing, where she seeks to incubate the next generation, one better than the current one.</span></span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Hoarder? Amassing resources for security or the mere sake of it?<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <b>Dominator</b>: Needs to control things? Socially, environmentally? Might favor strong Colonies, and Provincial control.<br /> <b>Predator</b>: Needs to test self against challenges? Might favor strong personal power, with some Swarm use (as &quot;hunting dogs&quot; to find, box in, and flush out prey).<br /> <b>Evolutionist</b>: Needs to try new things? Anti-tranditionalist? Might favor diverse Principalities, and changing Servants' abilities around.<br /> <b>Breeder</b>: Needs to make new things, or at least, <i>more</i>? Might favor populous Colonies, and many Servants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:35:08-07:00","id":869383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869361#post869361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main issue with changing Swarms is.... I'd need to completely redo the entire Swarm mechanics functionalities since the model I went with was based off a zombie horde and got more powerful based on size.<br /> <br /> I suppose what I could do then is have a break down similar to this:<br /> <br /> <br /> Colony still has the attributes.<br /> <br /> Swarms represent specific task groups of the Colony that use Colony's Attributes for all things and has any number of them.... as long as they could be paid for.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... Military is used for all Combat traits wit The &quot;Swarm size&quot; is based on resources spent building the Swarm....<br /> <br /> <br /> I would want to have Swarms have more varried combat stats though.... and having them all be based off of Military is... boring if practical.<br /> <br /> <br /> The main issue then is... for many tasks, you don't need the extra size or resources for anything. I guess they can still be used for trading...or for extra dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Size is the numbers in the Swarm, yes? You can usually do more, with more numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869361#post869361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resource Gathering should be automatic then for one's Core Province. Still need to &quot;manually&quot; deploy a task force to do harvesting.<br /> <br /> You can send Swarms to go do other area</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869361#post869361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Swarm size can be limits for things, such as in gathering, how much they can carry before going back on. But what about Diplomacy or Espionage, those.. don't need excess size.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diplomacy itself is just inter-personal Persuasion, right? Swarms might help by aiding you diplomatic target. Gifts often bring good will, after all.<br /> <br /> Espionage is made easier by the number of eyes, ears, and potential tails. Swarm size is the quantity of assets, not just them clumped as one big mass. In Espionage actions, they'd spread out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869361#post869361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... on the topic of Dice. It's still probably reasonable to give every ability a dice roll of Authority+Attribute.... except for... Military. Which I don't think makes sense to give it that for attacking...</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't the Swarms going to get Power/Finesse/Resistance?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869361#post869361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passive bonuses to Principalities was something I kinda wanted to be a thing largely to represent the &quot;evolving&quot; theme, as you got versed in topics, you were stronger. I know that for the physical principalities, they'll likely keep their passive bonuses that's what they're about, but I was hoping mental and social attributes would be raised.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, but they can do that by spending the XP to improve those specific traits. Merits are fairly cheap, and you can prevent easy access to them via Principality prerequisites. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869376#post869376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you have to redo swarm mechanics? They could still be size-based. Pools could improve as size got larger; there'd just be more kinds of pools. Varied stats could be gotten via Principalities; if you want a Swarm that's better at ranged stuff, pick up Bows; if you want one that's better at getting optimal materials, use Crucibles. Just because combat has Military as a base doesn't mean that variations can't build upon that base. Espionage could totally use a larger swarm: you have more bugs you can put in more places, you're better able to track targets, if some get caught and fried it's not the end of the mission. Diplomacy, having a bigger force means folks are more likely to respect you. Send one bug, it gets laughed out of court; send ten, they get to sit at the table; send fifty, they sit at the head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869376#post869376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it not reasonable to give swarm attack rolls Authority + Military? Have a base swarm use that as an attack roll, counts as a 0L weapon, no range. Spend Aspects to get greater damage (Blades), range (Bows), targets (Spheres), mobility (Cloaks), etc, etc. Maybe at each level of a Principality, you can pick an Aspect to unlock, related to one of the five areas. And then you can choose to apply it to future Swarms as a trade-off to Size.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Principality 1 unlocks one ability, that further dots improve upon? IE, Swarms can make ranged attacks at Bows 1, and additional dots improve the damage? Basic, but scale-able. Hmm, but also kinda boring...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869376#post869376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You already get stronger as you unlock stuff with Principalities. That's what the new powers represent. There's already a mechanic for &quot;getting stronger/evolving&quot;, it's &quot;spending XP on Attributes and Authority&quot;. Adding it on makes Principalities mechanically unbalanced, particularly if only some of them get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. If a Monarch wants to improve themselves, let them improve themselves. If they want freaky powers (and options those freaky powers make possible), let them get Principalities. If they want to improve their general power, let them increase Authority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-20-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:51:59-07:00","id":869392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869376#post869376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you have to redo swarm mechanics? They could still be size-based. Pools could improve as size got larger; there'd just be more kinds of pools. Varied stats could be gotten via Principalities; if you want a Swarm that's better at ranged stuff, pick up Bows; if you want one that's better at getting optimal materials, use Crucibles. Just because combat has Military as a base doesn't mean that variations can't build upon that base. Espionage could totally use a larger swarm: you have more bugs you can put in more places, you're better able to track targets, if some get caught and fried it's not the end of the mission. Diplomacy, having a bigger force means folks are more likely to respect you. Send one bug, it gets laughed out of court; send ten, they get to sit at the table; send fifty, they sit at the head.<br /> <br /> Why is it not reasonable to give swarm attack rolls Authority + Military? Have a base swarm use that as an attack roll, counts as a 0L weapon, no range. Spend Aspects to get greater damage (Blades), range (Bows), targets (Spheres), mobility (Cloaks), etc, etc. Maybe at each level of a Principality, you can pick an Aspect to unlock, related to one of the five areas. And then you can choose to apply it to future Swarms as a trade-off to Size.<br /> <br /> You already get stronger as you unlock stuff with Principalities. That's what the new powers represent. There's already a mechanic for &quot;getting stronger/evolving&quot;, it's &quot;spending XP on Attributes and Authority&quot;. Adding it on makes Principalities mechanically unbalanced, particularly if only some of them get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's more that I have to redo the nature of determining size. Either way, I think I got something..... I also changed my mind on Military and decided... why not go overkill and let them go as high as 20 offensive dice.<br /> <br /> I will note that in Espionage, I meant that flooding the sky with burning alien fliers was going to be a bit hard to not notice. I think once you got too big stealth becomes alot harder.... at least without seperating a small task force from the main body....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways... I know that attribute gains might have been a bit imbalanced. But well, it was something I wanted to do because it seemed like a great way to emphasize that you were even more &quot;evolved&quot; in your posthuman state. Still, I think Blades Bows and Shields, probably still should be giving attribute dots since they're meant to be very physical and don't have much advantages to them other than their boosts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869380#post869380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, my idea was instead of rolling, just make it a flat effect, reserved for unrolled actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With the suggestion, Swarms would then be used for Military (obvious), but also for any other task that involves some risk/roll, again limited by the fact they are a mere mob of bioforms. Build a structure quick? Generate a Swarm suited to building, or just let the Colony do it (but take a lot longer). Harvest non-Automatic resources? Generate a Harvester Swarm and let it roll to do it.<br /> <br /> [Potentially] In this model, Swarms would cost something (Wealth? Biomass?) to generate (so you couldn't just spawn an infinite amount). They do their thing. If successful (or at least, not Dramatic Failure), you get some of the resource back as they are recycled.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Discount as in &quot;less XP&quot;, or discount as in &quot;ignore for now&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Shouldn't it be C<b>l</b>ades? Or are you changing the term?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Inherent traits, or Principality discounts?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can you give examples?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hoarder? Amassing resources for security or the mere sake of it?<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <b>Dominator</b>: Needs to control things? Socially, environmentally? Might favor strong Colonies, and Provincial control.<br /> <b>Predator</b>: Needs to test self against challenges? Might favor strong personal power, with some Swarm use (as &quot;hunting dogs&quot; to find, box in, and flush out prey).<br /> <b>Evolutionist</b>: Needs to try new things? Anti-tranditionalist? Might favor diverse Principalities, and changing Servants' abilities around.<br /> <b>Breeder</b>: Needs to make new things, or at least, <i>more</i>? Might favor populous Colonies, and many Servants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I got some of that. Also, yes, Servants are on the back burner.<br /> <br /> Clades... I think. I might have made a typo. Still, no idea what things they should give. I don't think Principalities should be what they offer, so much as they have inherent things about them, that maybe scale as you get more powerful.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Autonomy think, it's a measure of obediance and control. You get more Autonomy from being rebellious, and it lowers based on your obedience. But this has both positive... and negative effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also.. Greed/Hoarding could work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I have no idea what kinds of Unrolled actions should there be other than spending Wealth on junk.... If you're going to push it, you might as well be the one to define and structure it, Vent0<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> Draft 1. Colony + Swarm revisions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies are represented by five attributes, each representing an estimation of the Colony\u2019s abilities at given tasks. These are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Military</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Knowledge</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Industry</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Espionage</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Diplomacy</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All are rated from 1 to 10, with a single dot in each at the start, plus an extra dot in the Monarch\u2019s primary area of focus. Raising Colony Attributes is a single merit dot.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aside from attributes, Colonies possess a resource pool called Wealth, representing natural or geographic Resources harvested from Provinces. Wealth has no real cap, but it does require harvesting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Swarm</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At any time, a Monarch or Servant may order the Colony to dispatch a unit of Drones or even weaker organisms, called a Swarm, to fulfill an assigned task. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The size and number of Drone forces a Monarch can deploy is limited solely by her budget, how many Resources she spend on them. For every point of Wealth she has, she may create a Swarm or increase a Swarm\u2019s maximum size by 1, up to a maximum of 20, ranging from a small pack of dog like animals to a kilometer long strike force.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Swarm then is sent out and attempts to perform said task, using the Colony\u2019s Attributes as its own attributes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the event of combat, the Swarm attempts to protect itself, using the following attributes in combat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Health: </b>A swarm\u2019s Health is equal to its Military + Size.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiative: </b> Initiative is always considered 0, with all Swarms going at the same time simultaneously.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Defense: </b> Defense is always considered 0. It is impossible for a Swarm to evade in a meaningful way with their congestion and mass working against them. Not to mention a complete lack of fear when in numbers\u2026.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Speed: </b>Speed is equal to Military + Authority + 5.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attack:</b> Military + Authority. Represents the Swarm attacking all opponents in close range with it, with successes translating into damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Swarm is also hard to damage from most weapons. Most single target weapons deal only 1 damage. Bashing damage effects are too weak to have an impact most of the time when it\u2019s against a single target.. The Swarm benefits from the racial Endless natural healing, representing natural regeneration and cannibalization of resources taking effect.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swarms may also be upgraded with Aspects, representing advanced modifications to make them better suited for specific tasks.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, this process is costly, and gets more inefficient the more Aspects placed onto a Swarm.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a general rule: each Aspect cost 1 resource plus an extra resource for every Aspect the Swarm already has.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So 1 Aspect costs 1, 2 cost 3, 3 costs 6, and 4 costs 10 and so on.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Swarm Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unless otherwise stated, a Monarch does not need to be involved any of her Swarm\u2019s actions. Willpower is not allowed to be spent on these actions either, but Wealth may be spent, representing over budgeting and waste, providing a single</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spy </i> Order your Swarm to Spy on a target location or creature via dispatching smaller Endless. Roll Espionage + Authority to determine their effectiveness at stealth and camouflage. You receive only basic details such as \u201ctarget is flying away\u201d \u201ctarget notices us\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Harvest </i> Order your Swarm to harvest the Resources in a Province. Roll Industry + Authority, with each roll taking an hour or more depending on distance traveled.. Successes translates to a number of Resource being removed from the Province and moved to the Colony, up to the limit the Province has remaining.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harvested Resources perish or are consumed at the start of a new Story, unless Stockpiled, another action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resources cannot be spent on this action unless the Province requires other resources.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Research</i> Order your your Swarm to perform research and experimentation on your behalf using Knowledge + Authority as a dice pool. Each roll is one hour.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence</i> Influence another party by dispatching a diplomat of your own to speak to them. Roll Diplomacy + Authority as a social to improve relations or coerce someone. In certain situations, Military might be substituted for Diplomacy, representing aggressive negotiations.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:56:58-07:00","id":869396,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869376#post869376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you have to redo swarm mechanics? They could still be size-based. Pools could improve as size got larger; there'd just be more kinds of pools. Varied stats could be gotten via Principalities; if you want a Swarm that's better at ranged stuff, pick up Bows; if you want one that's better at getting optimal materials, use Crucibles. Just because combat has Military as a base doesn't mean that variations can't build upon that base. Espionage could totally use a larger swarm: you have more bugs you can put in more places, you're better able to track targets, if some get caught and fried it's not the end of the mission. Diplomacy, having a bigger force means folks are more likely to respect you. Send one bug, it gets laughed out of court; send ten, they get to sit at the table; send fifty, they sit at the head.<br /> <br /> Seconding what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What about Principality 1 unlocks one ability, that further dots improve upon? IE, Swarms can make ranged attacks at Bows 1, and additional dots improve the damage? Basic, but scale-able. Hmm, but also kinda boring...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Agreed. If a Monarch wants to improve themselves, let them improve themselves. If they want freaky powers (and options those freaky powers make possible), let them get Principalities. If they want to improve their general power, let them increase Authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'd need to scrap a bunch of junk, particularly the Aspects methodology, redo the Size determining mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways. Yes. That's kinda what Aspects are supposed to be. Granted, Bow's case, it improves just the range, with damage going to blades as otherwise, you wouldn't care about Blades. It is boring, yeah but that's practical for a war.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, Swarms are now generalized &quot;Task forces&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, I thought it would be a cool thing to have attribute gains everwhere. Granted, this was a hold over from when the Principalities system had more in common with Civ Beyond Earth's Tech Web so you had no obvious route of maximization.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-20-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:39:30-07:00","id":869421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that in Espionage, I meant that flooding the sky with burning alien fliers was going to be a bit hard to not notice. I think once you got too big stealth becomes alot harder.... at least without seperating a small task force from the main body....</div> </div> </div> </div>I always saw an Espionage action as many small eye-bugs and such coordinating in a kind of surveillance web.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways... I know that attribute gains might have been a bit imbalanced. But well, it was something I wanted to do because it seemed like a great way to emphasize that you were even more &quot;evolved&quot; in your posthuman state. Still, I think Blades Bows and Shields, probably still should be giving attribute dots since they're meant to be very physical and don't have much advantages to them other than their boosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. It mirrors Vigor, Celerity, and Resilience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got some of that. Also, yes, Servants are on the back burner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pity, but there is time for that later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clades... I think. I might have made a typo. Still, no idea what things they should give. I don't think Principalities should be what they offer, so much as they have inherent things about them, that maybe scale as you get more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. More &quot;extra&quot; abilities, like Werewolf's Auspices, maybe? What about my ideas on them above?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Autonomy think, it's a measure of obediance and control. You get more Autonomy from being rebellious, and it lowers based on your obedience. But this has both positive... and negative effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, be less of a doormat to the Endless, and you can do more yourself... but your Colony doesn't interface as well with a human-minded Monarch? Kiss the Kingmakers' thoraxes, and you find the Colony responds to your desires almost subconsciously?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, I have no idea what kinds of Unrolled actions should there be other than spending Wealth on junk.... If you're going to push it, you might as well be the one to define and structure it, Vent0</div> </div> </div> </div>:-) Okay. Might be delays, though. And I might need to get a better grasp of what is possible before defining &quot;yeah, a Colony could just do that&quot; actions.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head: (noting that all these take time)<br /> <u>Harvest Wealth</u>: As you've stated.<br /> <u>Build Structure/Project</u>: With Hammers? Speed determined by Industry?<br /> <u>Construct Causeway</u>: Fancy name for making two Provinces connect in the Beneath. Needs Spheres? Or was it Staves? The Space warping one. Speed determined by Industry? Or Knowledge?<br /> <u>Reinforce Defenses</u>: Adds a Defensive Condition or something, representing traps and preparation that gives you bonuses in combat in/near your Colony. Needs Shields? Speed determined by Military or Industry? Or make the Bonus tied to that?<br /> <u>Transmute Wealth</u>: Turns Wealth into something (specific kind? Resources as the Merit? Equipment for use?). Needs Crucibles? Uses Industry for speed or quantity?<br /> <u>Augury</u>: Run predictive analysis using the Colony's Hive-Minded Brain-organisms. Makes Plans Equipment or Investigation actions? Needs the scrying Principality - Orbs? Spheres? Uses Knowledge<br /> <u>Camouflage</u>: Obscures Colony access points, and signs of your presence. Dependent upon some mechanic/trait for acting too overtly and drawing attention. Needs Cloaks or Veils? The hide-y one. Uses Espionage.<br /> <u>Revivification</u>: The Colony reconstructs your body and mind after you died. Some memory and identity loss may occur (they mean well, but Drones aren't the best surgeons). Might not be allowed, depending on if you want Cerebrate immortality or not. Uses ??? Diplomacy (so it gets some love), via negotiating with the Kingmakers for your brain backup?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swarms may also be upgraded with Aspects, representing advanced modifications to make them better suited for specific tasks.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, this process is costly, and gets more inefficient the more Aspects placed onto a Swarm.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a general rule: each Aspect cost 1 resource plus an extra resource for every Aspect the Swarm already has.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So 1 Aspect costs 1, 2 cost 3, 3 costs 6, and 4 costs 10 and so on.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Diminishing returns means you can't just make some giant ultra-swarm monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Swarm Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unless otherwise stated, a Monarch does not need to be involved any of her Swarm\u2019s actions. Willpower is not allowed to be spent on these actions either, but Wealth may be spent, representing over budgeting and waste, providing a single</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This got cut off?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Harvest </i> Order your Swarm to harvest the Resources in a Province. Roll Industry + Authority, with each roll taking an hour or more depending on distance traveled.. Successes translates to a number of Resource being removed from the Province and moved to the Colony, up to the limit the Province has remaining.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harvested Resources perish or are consumed at the start of a new Story, unless Stockpiled, another action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resources cannot be spent on this action unless the Province requires other resources.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Why not spend Resources on it? I mean, at a certain point it is stupid, but why not let that become clear? Or Maybe there is a role in over-harvesting, merely to deprive a rival of the Wealth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Research</i> Order your your Swarm to perform research and experimentation on your behalf using Knowledge + Authority as a dice pool. Each roll is one hour.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly are they doing here? Researching what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869392#post869392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence</i> Influence another party by dispatching a diplomat of your own to speak to them. Roll Diplomacy + Authority as a social to improve relations or coerce someone. In certain situations, Military might be substituted for Diplomacy, representing aggressive negotiations.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-20-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T12:28:37-07:00","id":869533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869421#post869421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always saw an Espionage action as many small eye-bugs and such coordinating in a kind of surveillance web.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is... but the general purpose drone Swarm is made up of zergling equivalents...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm. More &quot;extra&quot; abilities, like Werewolf's Auspices, maybe? What about my ideas on them above?<br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, be less of a doormat to the Endless, and you can do more yourself... but your Colony doesn't interface as well with a human-minded Monarch? Kiss the Kingmakers' thoraxes, and you find the Colony responds to your desires almost subconsciously?<br /> </div> </div> </div>No, it's to your King and the laws. The Kingmakers just make more Monarchs and don't get involved in the politics unless things get really bad. And no one even knows what they want.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also exerting your will too much bringing down autonomy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Basically at the polar ends, the Colony is meant to either be actively rebelling and acting on its own accord to sate needs without concern for safety so much as conveince..... OR... be acting to fullfill YOUR needs... regardless of dangers to doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> :-) Okay. Might be delays, though. And I might need to get a better grasp of what is possible before defining &quot;yeah, a Colony could just do that&quot; actions.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head: (noting that all these take time)<br /> <u>Harvest Wealth</u>: As you've stated.<br /> <u>Build Structure/Project</u>: With Hammers? Speed determined by Industry?<br /> <u>Construct Causeway</u>: Fancy name for making two Provinces connect in the Beneath. Needs Spheres? Or was it Staves? The Space warping one. Speed determined by Industry? Or Knowledge?<br /> <u>Reinforce Defenses</u>: Adds a Defensive Condition or something, representing traps and preparation that gives you bonuses in combat in/near your Colony. Needs Shields? Speed determined by Military or Industry? Or make the Bonus tied to that?<br /> <u>Transmute Wealth</u>: Turns Wealth into something (specific kind? Resources as the Merit? Equipment for use?). Needs Crucibles? Uses Industry for speed or quantity?<br /> <u>Augury</u>: Run predictive analysis using the Colony's Hive-Minded Brain-organisms. Makes Plans Equipment or Investigation actions? Needs the scrying Principality - Orbs? Spheres? Uses Knowledge<br /> <u>Camouflage</u>: Obscures Colony access points, and signs of your presence. Dependent upon some mechanic/trait for acting too overtly and drawing attention. Needs Cloaks or Veils? The hide-y one. Uses Espionage.<br /> <u>Revivification</u>: The Colony reconstructs your body and mind after you died. Some memory and identity loss may occur (they mean well, but Drones aren't the best surgeons). Might not be allowed, depending on if you want Cerebrate immortality or not. Uses ??? Diplomacy (so it gets some love), via negotiating with the Kingmakers for your brain backup? </div> </div> </div>The main issue is... what about non-Principality things? Other than birth more Endless via Create Swarm or Create Servant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not spend Resources on it? I mean, at a certain point it is stupid, but why not let that become clear? Or Maybe there is a role in over-harvesting, merely to deprive a rival of the Wealth. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how to handle overharvesting. Maybe as a special action where you can permanently reduce the dots of a Province to get another yield immediately...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What exactly are they doing here? Researching what? </div> </div> </div>A topic. Any topic via searching or experimentation. You have scientists, give them a sample to work with and they can crank out details for you.<br /> <br /> An interesting thing I note is that Monarch might work best with fewer players. There's a bunch of support systems and everyone can do most of the same things. <br /> <br /> Then again... maybe everyone shares the same Colony....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T12:54:58-07:00","id":869569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869533#post869533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is... but the general purpose drone Swarm is made up of zergling equivalents...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you are spawning creatures for surveillance or infiltration, I'd go with smaller, more agile things. Standardization is for humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869533#post869533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's to your King and the laws. The Kingmakers just make more Monarchs and don't get involved in the politics unless things get really bad. And no one even knows what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Kings then. But how does that really work? Obey and loose Integrity equivalent?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869533#post869533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also exerting your will too much bringing down autonomy.<br /> <br /> Basically at the polar ends, the Colony is meant to either be actively rebelling and acting on its own accord to sate needs without concern for safety so much as conveince..... OR... be acting to fullfill YOUR needs... regardless of dangers to doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>High Autonomy, Colony acts on its own, Low Autonomy, they act on their own, but for you? All based on whether you obey the local King?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869533#post869533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main issue is... what about non-Principality things? Other than birth more Endless via Create Swarm or Create Servant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. I need to think about possible actions a Monarch that avoid Principalities might want to get up to, then whether it is something the Colony can just <i>do</i> given enough time. Colony actions don't sync perfectly with Cult action due to, you know, freaking normal humans out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869533#post869533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how to handle overharvesting. Maybe as a special action where you can permanently reduce the dots of a Province to get another yield immediately...</div> </div> </div> </div>Harvesting removes Resources from the Province. I could see a Monarch spending/wasting their own Wealth, just to deprive an enemy from being able to harvest those Resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869533#post869533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A topic. Any topic via searching or experimentation. You have scientists, give them a sample to work with and they can crank out details for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>But aren't you Colony <i>your</i> mind? All major inspiration would come from you, yes? I mean, they can process, and read, and do tests, yeah. I guess you might be able to consider them scientists (or at least lab techs). You'd come up with the Observation and Hypothesis, while you delegate Testing to them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869533#post869533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting thing I note is that Monarch might work best with fewer players. There's a bunch of support systems and everyone can do most of the same things.<br /> <br /> Then again... maybe everyone shares the same Colony....</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely one game style. It seems like the group would need to agree on how the Colony's efforts are being spent, but otherwise it would reduce the need for Swarms and Servants. I'd have all Colony action drawing from the same pool of Wealth, though.<br /> <br /> Though, I'd note, Monarchs would ally with others because while their Colonies can plug up some holes, other sentients are often more effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-20-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T13:00:11-07:00","id":869580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869569#post869569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if you are spawning creatures for surveillance or infiltration, I'd go with smaller, more agile things. Standardization is for humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, Kings then. But how does that really work? Obey and loose Integrity equivalent?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> High Autonomy, Colony acts on its own, Low Autonomy, they act on their own, but for you? All based on whether you obey the local King?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, which is what the old Spy was about. The general purpose Swarm is not as innately suited to spying, atleast not all of it. I imagine that the influff justification is a lurker controlling smaller spawn.<br /> <br /> &quot;Standardization&quot; is in the sense we're all talking a mass of units that fill a mix of different roles and has advantages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, Autonomy is a question of Free Will versus Conformity. Neither are good in the extreme...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T13:14:24-07:00","id":869592,"title":"","content":"Random thought on Clades: what if they determine your starting Caste, and make it easier to &quot;fall back&quot; into that Caste? Kinda similar to how in Promethean, most Lineages have Stannum as their fallback/easy-to-join Refinement, but Zeka have Centimanus. So then, it takes time and effort to join a non-default Caste (and internally adjust yourself accordingly), but easy to shift back to what you were born as. <br /> <br /> Also, I see an Autonomy 10 Monarch as being a loner, someone cut off from the Beneath, lacking a Colony and ability to create one, but personally powerful. An Autonomy 0 Monarch becomes part of their Colony, body, mind, and soul-equivalent, and eventually join with another Colony (possibly the King's, possibly not). Obeying a King's/superior's commands despite not wanting to breaks down; disobeying despite it being an order breaks up. Creating a Swarm might break down if you're 8+; making a significant decision without asking your leader might break up if you're 2-.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T14:08:35-07:00","id":869640,"title":"","content":"I don't know. It seems kinda floppy and subjective to me. I'm not sure how a social construct in this form has metaphysical impact. What if you declare yourself King/Queen of a smaller area? Are you then exempt from the former system's influence regarding orders? Is there a hard Authority-derived mechanism, where Monarchs of lesser Authority must obey orders from higher Authority ones? That seems to screw with games where players aren't all the same Authority.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer if the breaking points were more abstract or inherent. Like, merging your mind with the Colony (via whatever action or power) breaks toward 0, while avoiding your Endless responsibilities and embracing humanity breaks toward 10. Who cares what some other Monarch is saying - how much of your own person are you?<br /> <br /> <b>Towards 0</b>:<br /> <u>Get killed and revived</u> - Having your mind only exist in the Hive-Mind is hard on one's self. Only applicable if this is possible, of course.<br /> <u>Micromanage Colony/Swarm</u> - Merging with your minions lets you use your skills and Willpower, and enables finer control, but subsumes your mind amongst the many.<br /> <u>Commit an utterly inhuman act</u> - Legacy &quot;acting like a monster&quot; sin.<br /> <u>Neglecting Human Contact</u> - Hard enough maintaining a semi-human worldview with a million voices chattering in your head, but when you loose benchmarks for how &quot;normal&quot; people are supposed to behave, it becomes easier to slip.<br /> <u>Embrace your instincts</u> - The Clade derived ones. It's you being more a Predator/whatever and less, John Doe, former human and current Monarch of the Emerald Hive.<br /> <br /> <b>Towards 10</b>:<br /> <u>Neglect Managing You Colony</u> - When you tell the voices in your head to shut up and leave you alone. They just might do so (but then, they'll likely &quot;raid the fridge&quot; themselves if pressed).<br /> <u>Act counter to your instincts</u> - The Clade ones again. This is rejecting your new monstrous drives to (hopefully) embrace human ones.<br /> <u>Place Human concerns above Endless ones</u> - This is you picking a side.<br /> <u>Personally acting, when using minions would have made more sense</u> - This is you deciding to handle things for yourself, even though you are supposed to be merely the director of a multitude.<br /> <br /> Note: I'd put the above examples at certain values, beyond which they'd have no effect (like the old Hierarchy of Sins).<br /> <hr /><br /> Maybe Penalties for High Autonomy might be things like:<br /> Colony commits independent actions (such as abduct animals and/or people for feed Biomass when resources are low).<br /> Colony &quot;respects your privacy&quot; in that they don't give you status updates automatically (Job's done, Resources are low, We are under attack, etc.).<br /> Telepathic orders are &quot;harder&quot; (they can get misinterpreted, or take longer).<br /> <br /> Maybe Penalties for Low Autonomy are:<br /> Social Penalties (standard, yes, I know, but this represents you listening more to the alien voices in your head than who you are talking to).<br /> Willpower spent on personal endeavors (Willpower spent on forwarding the Monarch's personal goals, maybe upgrading to Willpower spent on the Monarch themselves - making using the Colony only more attractive).<br /> Colony acting subconsciously, fulfilling your Aspirations without your direct oversight (increasing the chance they screw up and draw attention if you are, you know, paying attention).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-20-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:40:47-07:00","id":870193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869592#post869592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thought on Clades: what if they determine your starting Caste, and make it easier to &quot;fall back&quot; into that Caste? Kinda similar to how in Promethean, most Lineages have Stannum as their fallback/easy-to-join Refinement, but Zeka have Centimanus. So then, it takes time and effort to join a non-default Caste (and internally adjust yourself accordingly), but easy to shift back to what you were born as.<br /> <br /> Also, I see an Autonomy 10 Monarch as being a loner, someone cut off from the Beneath, lacking a Colony and ability to create one, but personally powerful. An Autonomy 0 Monarch becomes part of their Colony, body, mind, and soul-equivalent, and eventually join with another Colony (possibly the King's, possibly not). Obeying a King's/superior's commands despite not wanting to breaks down; disobeying despite it being an order breaks up. Creating a Swarm might break down if you're 8+; making a significant decision without asking your leader might break up if you're 2-.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The main issue with me wanting to have fallback Castes based on Clades is that... we'd need to tie the Clades very strongly with Caste or derrive a Caste from a Clade. Can we do that adequately right now?<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah those are potential fates of going too far in one direction....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=869640#post869640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. It seems kinda floppy and subjective to me. I'm not sure how a social construct in this form has metaphysical impact. What if you declare yourself King/Queen of a smaller area? Are you then exempt from the former system's influence regarding orders? Is there a hard Authority-derived mechanism, where Monarchs of lesser Authority must obey orders from higher Authority ones? That seems to screw with games where players aren't all the same Authority.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer if the breaking points were more abstract or inherent. Like, merging your mind with the Colony (via whatever action or power) breaks toward 0, while avoiding your Endless responsibilities and embracing humanity breaks toward 10. Who cares what some other Monarch is saying - how much of your own person are you?<br /> <br /> <b>Towards 0</b>:<br /> <u>Get killed and revived</u> - Having your mind only exist in the Hive-Mind is hard on one's self. Only applicable if this is possible, of course.<br /> <u>Micromanage Colony/Swarm</u> - Merging with your minions lets you use your skills and Willpower, and enables finer control, but subsumes your mind amongst the many.<br /> <u>Commit an utterly inhuman act</u> - Legacy &quot;acting like a monster&quot; sin.<br /> <u>Neglecting Human Contact</u> - Hard enough maintaining a semi-human worldview with a million voices chattering in your head, but when you loose benchmarks for how &quot;normal&quot; people are supposed to behave, it becomes easier to slip.<br /> <u>Embrace your instincts</u> - The Clade derived ones. It's you being more a Predator/whatever and less, John Doe, former human and current Monarch of the Emerald Hive.<br /> <br /> <b>Towards 10</b>:<br /> <u>Neglect Managing You Colony</u> - When you tell the voices in your head to shut up and leave you alone. They just might do so (but then, they'll likely &quot;raid the fridge&quot; themselves if pressed).<br /> <u>Act counter to your instincts</u> - The Clade ones again. This is rejecting your new monstrous drives to (hopefully) embrace human ones.<br /> <u>Place Human concerns above Endless ones</u> - This is you picking a side.<br /> <u>Personally acting, when using minions would have made more sense</u> - This is you deciding to handle things for yourself, even though you are supposed to be merely the director of a multitude.<br /> <br /> Note: I'd put the above examples at certain values, beyond which they'd have no effect (like the old Hierarchy of Sins).<br /> <hr /><br /> Maybe Penalties for High Autonomy might be things like:<br /> Colony commits independent actions (such as abduct animals and/or people for feed Biomass when resources are low).<br /> Colony &quot;respects your privacy&quot; in that they don't give you status updates automatically (Job's done, Resources are low, We are under attack, etc.).<br /> Telepathic orders are &quot;harder&quot; (they can get misinterpreted, or take longer).<br /> <br /> Maybe Penalties for Low Autonomy are:<br /> Social Penalties (standard, yes, I know, but this represents you listening more to the alien voices in your head than who you are talking to).<br /> Willpower spent on personal endeavors (Willpower spent on forwarding the Monarch's personal goals, maybe upgrading to Willpower spent on the Monarch themselves - making using the Colony only more attractive).<br /> Colony acting subconsciously, fulfilling your Aspirations without your direct oversight (increasing the chance they screw up and draw attention if you are, you know, paying attention).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the social construct is wired heavily into genetics and telepathy. It's the human element that destabilizes it, because by going against the strictures naturally inherent to a Monarch, you make yourself seperated from the Colony or the Colony follows in the footsteps of its leader or parent... and that's not neccesarily stable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, Authority isn't the &quot;Be all&quot; stat of determining superiority. Titles are more important, specifically, whether or not you are the Vassal under that Monarch. This is the why of the Court system...<br /> <br /> <br /> The way I see it, yes, Autonomy should have Sins that go one direction to the other. Lower Autonomy is more collectivist, more binding yourself to your Swarm/ becoming more &quot;natural&quot;. Higher autonomy is more trending towards humanity and individualism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:16:55-07:00","id":870264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=870193#post870193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the social construct is wired heavily into genetics and telepathy. It's the human element that destabilizes it, because by going against the strictures naturally inherent to a Monarch, you make yourself seperated from the Colony or the Colony follows in the footsteps of its leader or parent... and that's not neccesarily stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>But <i>are</i> the Endless naturally hierarchical? Do they have Kings &gt; Drones etc., or are all equal (but with differing roles) in the swarm? Is the very concept of a Feudal Monarchy simply a human addition to help Monarchs understand their situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:28:27-07:00","id":870274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=870264#post870264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But <i>are</i> the Endless naturally hierarchical? Do they have Kings &gt; Drones etc., or are all equal (but with differing roles) in the swarm? Is the very concept of a Feudal Monarchy simply a human addition to help Monarchs understand their situation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes.They are naturally a Heirarchal society with more intelligent and powerful Endless acting as coordinators and rulers.<br /> <br /> Feudalism is actually a catch all term for a variety of very similar heirarchal structures based on some research I did, so I think it's not too unreasonable to have that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:03:30-07:00","id":871170,"title":"","content":"Can we get a Google Drive folder set up with the material thus far? It would make things easier to comment on directly and review what is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:06:11-07:00","id":871171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=871170#post871170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get a Google Drive folder set up with the material thus far? It would make things easier to comment on directly and review what is done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes this please. Much easier than hopping through the entire thread or hoping the first post is updated and accurate. Stuff that's not in a state to share could be left out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:42:58-07:00","id":871619,"title":"","content":"Well, I set things up. Are there any plans right now?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From the moment of their rebirth every Monarch feels the call of the innumerable animalistic Intelligences that seek out for her instructions and guidance. From then on, she has a struggle, that of defining herself against her Colony\u2026. To be Endless or to be Human. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If she leans too closely to her human heritage, the Colony risks going Rogue, no longer recognizing her as a rightful ruler until ammend could be made.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But if she invests too much of her focus onto the Colony, abandons life outside of it, she might find it hard to seperate herself from the other voices, until she is more horror than a person.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Neither of these fates are considered desireable by the Kingmakers, considering them to be signs of failure to be adequate rulers. Still\u2026. It is possible to salvage are situation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The measure of a Monarchs individuality versus her collectivism, which not only applies to herself, but her Colony, is called Autonomy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Gameplay </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of Integrity, Monarchs have autonomy. New and in play Monarchs start at 7, representing their still human leaning individuality with a modicum of control over the collective will of her Colony.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 is the ideal and the Monarch may not spend experience points to change it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">During play, Monarchs raise and lower their autonomy based on a variety of factors, most especially based on whether or not she refuses or accepts the authority or rules placed on those above\u2026 and below her. Depending on the situations and how she responds to them, she can recieve Breaking Points that cause her Autonomy to fluctuate, either to Individualism (10) or to Collectivism (0).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Breaking point roll is Resolve + Composure + modifiers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a character hits a breaking point towards Collectism, she subtracts one die from the roll for each point of Autonomy below 5. If the roll fails, he loses a point of Autonomy. Whens he</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">hits a breaking point towards Individualism, he gets a penalty for each point of Harmony above 5. If the roll is a failure, the character gains a point of Autonomy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Towards Individualism</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>:</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Get killed and revived</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - Having your mind only exist in the Hive-Mind is hard on one's self. Only applicable if this is possible, of course.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Micromanage Colony/Swarm</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - Merging with your minions lets you use your skills and Willpower, and enables finer control, but subsumes your mind amongst the many.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Commit an utterly inhuman act</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - Legacy &quot;acting like a monster&quot; sin.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Neglecting Human Contact</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - Hard enough maintaining a semi-human worldview with a million voices chattering in your head, but when you loose benchmarks for how &quot;normal&quot; people are supposed to behave, it becomes easier to slip.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Embrace your instincts</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - The Clade derived ones. It's you being more a Predator/whatever and less, John Doe, former human and current Monarch of the Emerald Hive.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Towards Collectivism</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>:</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Neglect Managing You Colony</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - When you tell the voices in your head to shut up and leave you alone. They just might do so (but then, they'll likely &quot;raid the fridge&quot; themselves if pressed).</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Act counter to your instincts</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - The Clade ones again. This is rejecting your new monstrous drives to (hopefully) embrace human ones.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Place Human concerns above Endless ones</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - This is you picking a side.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Personally acting, when using minions would have made more sense</u></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> - This is you deciding to handle things for yourself, even though you are supposed to be merely the director of a multitude.</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Consequences of Autonomy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">9</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">8</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">0</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TBA</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:12:30-07:00","id":873813,"title":"","content":"Any comments? I haven't had much time working on Monarch as I've been working on other projects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, I thought of something to do with Geodics. I think that maybe a &quot;tech tree&quot; style of approach would be interesting for how they get more tech or Fragmments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T12:16:05-07:00","id":873933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=873813#post873813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any comments? I haven't had much time working on Monarch as I've been working on other projects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, I thought of something to do with Geodics. I think that maybe a &quot;tech tree&quot; style of approach would be interesting for how they get more tech or Fragmments.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:19:40-07:00","id":874018,"title":"","content":"One of the things I wanted to do with Monarch early on was that I wanted to have a &quot;Tech tree&quot; style of advancement... think of like how Technologies worked in Civilization games and you understand what I mean.<br /> <br /> Obviously, we no longer do that, <br /> <br /> But I'm thinking of salvaging the idea for a number of things, not all of them are Monarch related.<br /> <br /> <br /> The most relevant to this thread purpose is... you know how like Starcraft has a &quot;techtree&quot; of where basically buildings unlock new units or allow you to purchase upgrades for new units. The Geodics have that in a sense for how Coreminds work. Because each and every Fragment is the fragments of the same Geodic and they're hard to &quot;defeat&quot; on a strategic level, it can make sense for a Coremind to evolve and unlock more functions as the Campaign goes on.<br /> <br /> <br /> Simple explanation<br /> Their first &quot;building&quot; unlocks Rank 1-2 Fragments<br /> <br /> They can then choose to get Battlesuits, very weak models, or perhaps to Unlock more powerful Rank 3 or Rank 4 Fragments, or some support technology which upgrades Rank 1-2's such as by mass producing swarms or giving more default Numina<br /> <br /> <br /> Later on, they can choose to upgrade existing unlocks.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:48:34-07:00","id":874044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=874018#post874018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I wanted to do with Monarch early on was that I wanted to have a &quot;Tech tree&quot; style of advancement... think of like how Technologies worked in Civilization games and you understand what I mean.<br /> <br /> Obviously, we no longer do that,<br /> <br /> But I'm thinking of salvaging the idea for a number of things, not all of them are Monarch related.<br /> <br /> <br /> The most relevant to this thread purpose is... you know how like Starcraft has a &quot;techtree&quot; of where basically buildings unlock new units or allow you to purchase upgrades for new units. The Geodics have that in a sense for how Coreminds work. Because each and every Fragment is the fragments of the same Geodic and they're hard to &quot;defeat&quot; on a strategic level, it can make sense for a Coremind to evolve and unlock more functions as the Campaign goes on.<br /> <br /> <br /> Simple explanation<br /> Their first &quot;building&quot; unlocks Rank 1-2 Fragments<br /> <br /> They can then choose to get Battlesuits, very weak models, or perhaps to Unlock more powerful Rank 3 or Rank 4 Fragments, or some support technology which upgrades Rank 1-2's such as by mass producing swarms or giving more default Numina<br /> <br /> <br /> Later on, they can choose to upgrade existing unlocks.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. A concrete sense and representation of escalating threat. Leave Geodics alone long enough and they grow into a terrible threat. Strike at their support infrastructure, and you can knock them down a few pegs. So like the Pillars they use to reinforce the physics of an area enough for more powerful Fragments to operate, they might create other specialized structures that grant them new abilities.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Perhaps they can have a remote &quot;possession&quot; transmitter? Have it work like Open -&gt; Possessed -&gt; Controlled -&gt; Claimed (but its less about a Fragment merging with the target, and more about the target being conditioned as a Geodic channel).<br /> <br /> Heh, maybe give them a &quot;Basilisk Effect&quot; power for Cryso-forming things (such as, say, a flash of light that installs some psychic malware that forces targets to transform themselves into salt crystals)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:52:52-07:00","id":874675,"title":"","content":"So what Principalities are left? Shields, Hammers, Staves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 20