om/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:55:13-07:00","id":874755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=874720#post874720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Try not to make it get too powerful compared to vigor.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I see it currently has a scattered buffet of passive abilities. Perhaps, if more active powers are effective and interesting enough, those could be down-scaled. Resilience (2E) is a flat bonus to Stamina (only) and Aggravated Damage soak (with activation boosting it further). To prevent Shield from being a straight copy cat, what about it granting Armor and/or Defense? As for activated abilities, I could see a &quot;turtle&quot; power where they bolster defenses at some maneuverability cost. Hmm. A lot of others, but they'd be Unions (retributive armor with Blades, insta-fortresses with Hammers, healing carapace/cocoons with Crucibles maybe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:27:49-07:00","id":874781,"title":"","content":"I can't find the Principalities dump. Also, it won't allow me to edit them. If i re-post Crucibles here and then you put it into a GDoc <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a>?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Crucibles</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>A crucible is a tool of transformation and of refinement. A ruler should be as a crucible to the unworked ore of his lands and fiefdoms, ever refining them into more perfect forms.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> <br /> <u>(1) Internal Alchemy</u><br /> <br /> The first step in both chemistry and alchemy is understanding, and this Mandate transforms the Monarch's body into a laboratory capable of analysing any substance without harm.<br /> Cost: 1 Psi (Free in Noble Form)<br /> Duration: 1 scene (permanent in Noble Form)<br /> Effect: The Monarch becomes capable of digesting any substance and will suffer no ill effects. This means that he can eat rocks, wood, rotten meat or even metal and suffer no ill effects. He may even thrive on such fare, although it becomes no more appetising. Furthermore, the Monarch may reflexively roll Intelligence + Science (with no penalty for lacking dots in the latter) in order to identify the properties and chemical make-up of an ingested substance. A single success is enough to successfully analyse the material, although supernatural compounds may take more (this includes most substances created through the Principality of Chalices).<br /> <br /> <u>(2) Transmutation of Structure</u><br /> <br /> The laboratory of the Monarch's body is now capable of not only analysis but also of transmutation, reconfiguring molecules in order to attain the desired effect. The Monarch can use this Mandate in order to transmute a mass of material weighing no more than the Monarch's Authority in lbs (in earth gravity) to another state of that same material (water to ice, iron to molten iron etc) or into another substance which is made of the same elements (water to hydrogen and oxygen, coal to graphite). The Monarch must be touching the material he intends to transmute. Extremely rare or unique materials such as diamond or radioactive metals may only be transmuted at the Storyteller's discretion. This Mandate cannot be used to alter the physical shape of an object, that is the domain of the Principality of Hammers. <br /> In Noble Form, the Monarch may elect to ingest the substance to be transmuting it, passing it through a specialised series of organs before regurgitating it or expelling it via a specialised orifice. Doing so eliminates the Psi cost.<br /> (Note: this need not be an option if your group is not all that OK with biosquick).<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Psi or free in Noble Form<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Science +Crucibles<br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended, 3 turns per roll<br /> <b>Effect:</b><br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The transmutation backfires, transmuting a portion of the Monarch's body randomly and inflicting (Crucibles) in Lethal damage. The Monarch loses all successes accumulated so far.<br /> <u>Failure:</u> No successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation.<br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation. The Storyteller sets the target number of successes. Usually, making simple, natural transmutations such as water to ice take 3 successes, more complex ones such as water to oxygen and hydrogen take 5 successes and complex molecular realignments such as changing plastics to oil or petrol take 8.<br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The Monarch so masterfully manipulates the molecular structure of the matter that any Psi spent is recovered.<br /> <br /> <u>(3) Workshop</u><br /> <br /> The monarch can exert his psychic abilities to create an area in which he can easily call upon the strange physics of the Void in order to utilise Mandates of the Principality of Crucibles outside his own body, as well as easing his transmutations. This area endures for a reasonable time and is usually about the size of a small apartment.<br /> Cost: 3 Psi<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Science + Crucibles<br /> Action: Extended, 10 minutes per roll<br /> Effect: The Monarch attunes an area of approximately the size of a small apartment to the physics of the Void, allowing him to more easily call upon them in the delicate manners necessary for the application of the Principality of Crucibles. A Monarch may only have one Workshop at a time.<br /> The number of successes needed to in order to successfully create the Workshop depends upon the location in which it is being created.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Location</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Number of Required Successes</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Within a Province of the Monarch in the Beneath</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Within the Beneath but outside of the Monarch's Province</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">10</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Within the Monarch's Province in the phenomenal world.</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">15</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Outside the Monarch's Province in the phenomenal world.</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">20</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> While within this area, the Monarch gains a bonus to all rolls involving Science, including Mandates of the Principality of Crucibles, equal to the Monarch's rating in Crucibles, as well as being able to waive Psi costs for using Mandates of this Principality.<br /> If the Monarch at any time rolls an Exceptional Success, he may add the 9-again rule to any Science rolls within the Workshop. if he rolls a second Exceptional Success, he may add 8-again. If he rolls a third, he may add the Rote quality to any Science rolls. Only only one bonus from Exceptional Success may be applied to a given roll.<br /> If the Monarch rolls a Dramatic Failure, he loses all successes accrued so far and the location instead becomes anathema to the powers of the Void, causing a penalty to any attempt to use Principalities suffer a penalty equal to the Monarch's Authority. This effect endures for the same amount of time as a successful Workshop would.<br /> The Workshop will endure for a number of days equal to (Authority*3).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>(4) Transmutation of Substance</u><br /> <br /> . The Monarch can now not only manipulate molecular structure but also the positions of subatomic particles, allowing the Monarch to transmute a substance into a completely different one, so long as the input and output have the same mass. The mass of the material transmuted can be no greater than the Monarch's Authority in lbs. The Monarch must be touching the material he intends to transmute. Extremely rare or unique materials such as diamond or radioactive metals may only be transmuted at the Storyteller's discretion. This Mandate cannot be used to alter the physical shape of an object, that is the domain of the Principality of Hammers. The Storyteller sets the target number of successes.<br /> In Noble Form, the Monarch may elect to ingest the substance to be transmuting it, passing it through a specialised series of organs before regurgitating it or expelling it via a specialised orifice. Doing so reduces the Psi cost to 1<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Psi or 1 Psi in Noble Form<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Science + Crucibles<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended, 3 turns per roll<br /> <b>Effect: </b><br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The transmutation backfires, transmuting a portion of the Monarch's body randomly and inflicting (Crucibles) in Lethal damage. The Monarch loses all successes accumulated so far.<br /> <u>Failure:</u> No successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation.<br /> <u>Success:</u> Successes are accrued towards completing the transmutation. The Storyteller sets the target number of successes. Making transmutations within the same 'category' of material, such one ferrous or noble metal to another usually require 3 successes, making transmutations across categories take 5 and drastic changes such as granite to plutonium require at least 8, if not more.<br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The Monarch so masterfully manipulates the molecular structure of the matter that any Psi spent is recovered.<br /> <br /> <u>(5) Mass Transmutation</u><br /> <br /> By exerting more of his psionic strength, the Monarch becomes able to transmute materials of far greater mass, as well as more swiftly, although this is quite draining.<br /> Cost: +3 Psi<br /> Effect: By paying the extra Psi when using either Transmutation of Structure or Transmutation of Substance, the Monarch becomes able to transmute materials of a mass equal to (Authority*10). He must still be able to touch the material. He may no longer opt to ingest it. This can be used to attack a structure, ignoring Durability and inflicting Damage to Structure equal to the highest individual roll (e.g., if a Monarch rolls three times and achieves 3, 1 and 2 successes respectively before completing the transmutation, it deals 3 damage to Structure).<br /> If the Monarch chooses to, they can also make the Action to use the aforementioned Mandates an Instant one, although this means that the Monarch only has 1 roll with which to gather the required Successes.<br /> The fact that the transmutation is now Instant means that it can be used as an attack. Before rolling to see if the Mandate succeeds, the Monarch chooses whether to inflict (successes*2) Bashing, (successes) Lethal or (successes/2) Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Colony Benefits</b><br /> <br /> Synthesizer<br /> Bonus to gathering Wealth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:41:44-07:00","id":874842,"title