e/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:50:53-07:00","id":880233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=880177#post880177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's more that the style of it should be seperate from the Beneath. Otherwise it's useless within the Beneath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I thought of it as working both ways. Need to flank an opponent's position in the Beneath? Go &quot;there&quot; Topside, open a hole, invade from there. Need to get out of the Beneath <i>now</i>? Open a hole Topside and escape.<br /> <br /> But temporary. I think only the Kingmakers and other major powers can create new, stable Access Points, yeah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:11:49-07:00","id":880255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=880233#post880233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I thought of it as working both ways. Need to flank an opponent's position in the Beneath? Go &quot;there&quot; Topside, open a hole, invade from there. Need to get out of the Beneath <i>now</i>? Open a hole Topside and escape.<br /> <br /> But temporary. I think only the Kingmakers and other major powers can create new, stable Access Points, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes. Only godlike beings can really do permanent rifts like that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T15:33:38-07:00","id":880531,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So... we've got alot of monsters in the depths. Do we need something more in the skies above? Or the waters? Maybe Dwellers races that are in and out of the Beneath at times?<br /> <br /> <br /> A very simplistic draft of Geodic progression. Can be fleshed out into something more coherent. Going to work on Devic mechs next I think.<br /> .</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Geodics are a race that has lost the majority of its technology since Planetfall, being reduced to mere splinters of their true power. However, that power is mighty, and the ancient ones are able to rebuild, using the tools they have to build better and stronger tools.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If given enough time, they could overrun the world. In order to slow them down, Monarchs would need to destroy their infastructure to prevent them from becoming a threat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In game turns, as the Chroncicle advances, the Geodics unlock more of their buildings which in turn unlock new capabilities.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mainframe Nexus </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Geodics were Kings, these Ziggauruts would be their temples and thrones, the place where their bodies and minds lay. From here, they may splinter themselves, albefit this isn\u2019t easy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of Rank 1 Geodics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: None (free)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Cybercore, Mass Fabricator, Neutronium Reactor</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mainframe Nexus </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Geodics were Kings, these Ziggauruts would be their temples and thrones, the place where their bodies and minds lay. From here, they may splinter and become legions unto themselves.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of Rank 1 Geodics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: None (free)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Cybercore, Metal Extractor, Neutronium Reactor</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cybercore </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Cybercore is the mainline computer and technical control building for the Nexus. Through it, Geodics may assemble more advanced technologies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Predictive Computing, Analytics Scanning, and Cyber Breaching </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Mainframe Nexus II</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Metal Extractor </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order for the Nexus to produce robotics, it needs to acquire materials, common metals and earth to be converted into usable resources.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of Drones</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: War Factory, Mainframe Nexus II</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Neutronium Reactor </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Though Geodics power the most basic parts of the Nexus with their own power, that power has limits. In order to advance, the machines must become self sufficient, by draining the power of neutron dense matter. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of Rank 1 Geodics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks:, Xenoformer Ring, Mainframe Nexus II</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mainframe Nexus II </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Nexus must grow more advanced, more complex if it must become the center stage of the Geodic warmachine. More systems are required for this great temple of destruction.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of up to Rank 3 Geodics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Cybercore, Metal Extractor, Neutronium Reactor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Mainframe Nexus III, Figment Hall</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Xenoformer Ring</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Geodics are trapped in the Beneath, but are destined to be its masters. They intend to make it and the surface world in their image.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Crysiformation</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Neutronium Reactor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Mainframe Nexus III</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>War Factory </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Geodic\u2019s use advanced cybernetics is but a hallow shell of what it was. Still, it is enough to build an army to stand against the tide.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of DT-Battlesuits</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Metal Extractor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Mainframe Nexus III</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Figment Hall </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Though the Coreminds are trapped in the Beneath, Fragments may rise to the surface. There, they must be able to blend in, disguised in human form, for the opportunities are myriad. Many Monarchs fell thinking their enemy lay underground when in truth the surface was no safe.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Gives Fragments the \u201cstealth\u201d options</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus II</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Mainframe Nexus III</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mass Fabricator </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The substances of the Earth are inefficient for the Geodic\u2019s needs. They are too different in chemistry to make use of it to the fullest extent. However, synthetic materials can be bent and shapped more easily in the right</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of SV-Battlesuits</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Cybercore, Metal Extractor, Neutronium Reactor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mainframe Nexus III </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this plateau of power, the Nexus has reached a point of its development where any further growth might take eons to accomplish. Still, many technologies are unlocked.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows production of up to Rank 5 Geodics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus II, ANY 2 (Figment Hall, War Factory, Xenoformer Ring, Mass Fabricator)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks: Robotics Support Bay, Battle Lab, Crystal Plague Launch Bay</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Robotics Support BayI </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Geodics begin to approach the same level their ancestors once did, their machines grow ever more powerful.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Upgrades all Battlesuits and Robots with +1 Strength, +1 Durability, and +1 Structure</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus III</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Battle Lab </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">War is a science that must be disected to evolve to. The Geodics will rise once more through conquest.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Geodic Fragments get\u2026.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus III</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Crystal Plague Launch Bay</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By far the most deadly weapon in the Geodic arsenal, a superweapon that converts whatever striken by its radiation into lifeless crystal and renders the area warped closer to the Geodic\u2019s ideal world.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits: Allows creation of a Superweapon</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Mainframe Nexus III</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlocks:</span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-02-2016, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:12:42-07:00","id":881109,"title":"","content":"So... my immediate thoughts on Staves are straight forward, save what should be in 3/4<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Defensive ward, activated defense that imposes Staves rating against attacks, and double that against spatial attacks or hostile attempts to reach your current space coordinates. Or maybe forces a Clash of Wills. Foils teleporting too.<br /> <br /> 2. Blink. Short range mobility power.<br /> <br /> 3. Erect walls of solidified space?Shrink or Grow?<br /> <br /> 4. Not sure here<br /> <br /> 5. Dimensional tunneling. Establish a scene long wormhole from one end to another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:03:34-07:00","id":881194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=881109#post881109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... my immediate thoughts on Staves are straight forward, save what should be in 3/4<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Defensive ward, activated defense that imposes Staves rating against attacks, and double that against spatial attacks or hostile attempts to reach your current space coordinates. Or maybe forces a Clash of Wills. Foils teleporting too.<br /> <br /> 2. Blink. Short range mobility power.<br /> <br /> 3. Erect walls of solidified space?Shrink or Grow?<br /> <br /> 4. Not sure here<br /> <br /> 5. Dimensional tunneling. Establish a scene long wormhole from one end to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see Blinking as easier than Warding, personally. Maybe 4 could be pocket spaces? Like storing a small army of minions in your purse or backpack or something.<br /> <br /> Regarding spatial manipulation, I was playing around with a number of effects for a Demonic Exploit. Maybe the first power could be &quot;simple&quot; expansion and contraction of space? Contraction - poor man's Blinking, by making the distance between A and B shorter (also allows for distant &quot;melee&quot; attacks). Expansion - keep targets at a distance, by making there be more distance between A and B (also rendering most melee attacks ineffective, since even if the Monarch <i>seems</i> 1 meter away, suddenly they are effectively <i>10</i> meters away).<br /> <br /> True teleportation (Blinking, &quot;Mirroring&quot;, and redirection) would then be dot 2 or 3. Complete folding would be 3 or 4. Leaving massively distant (or inter-dimensional) wormholes for 5. On that note, maybe some rules covering &quot;offensive&quot; use? (such as opening a point leading to the vacuum of space or a particularly dangerous point in the Beneath)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-03-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:18:25-07:00","id":881209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=881194#post881194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see Blinking as easier than Warding, personally. Maybe 4 could be pocket spaces? Like storing a small army of minions in your purse or backpack or something.<br /> <br /> Regarding spatial manipulation, I was playing around with a number of effects for a Demonic Exploit. Maybe the first power could be &quot;simple&quot; expansion and contraction of space? Contraction - poor man's Blinking, by making the distance between A and B shorter (also allows for distant &quot;melee&quot; attacks). Expansion - keep targets at a distance, by making there be more distance between A and B (also rendering most melee attacks ineffective, since even if the Monarch <i>seems</i> 1 meter away, suddenly they are effectively <i>10</i> meters away).<br /> <br /> True teleportation (Blinking, &quot;Mirroring&quot;, and redirection) would then be dot 2 or 3. Complete folding would be 3 or 4. Leaving massively distant (or inter-dimensional) wormholes for 5. On that note, maybe some rules covering &quot;offensive&quot; use? (such as opening a point leading to the vacuum of space or a particularly dangerous point in the Beneath)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking of the spatial defense was going to be simplest... because it's the least overt use of space.<br /> <br /> Still, Blinking as 2/3 would be okay. Yeah. Pocket space should be in the gaps.... Hm.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... 3/4 is Warp Space... makes space seem bigger or smaller as needed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:50:40-07:00","id":881241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=881209#post881209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was thinking of the spatial defense was going to be simplest... because it's the least overt use of space.<br /> <br /> Still, Blinking as 2/3 would be okay. Yeah. Pocket space should be in the gaps.... Hm.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... 3/4 is Warp Space... makes space seem bigger or smaller as needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess?<br /> <br /> I don't know. I see basic distance manipulation as &quot;early game&quot; utility, but it is conceptually the same as Pocket spaces which would be higher, I'd think. Blink, usability-wise, is merely a nice movement power, but conceptually represents uncoupling and recoupling two distinct points in space.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;area wards&quot; how are these wards working? If it's just &quot;protection in X area&quot;, it seems like it would be a Shields Mandate, or a Union of Shields and Staves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T10:53:45-07:00","id":884742,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Okay so AceOfAlmonds is almost back so. I've got 3 important things to discuss.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Staves:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A Monarch must be lord over even the very space that she claims for herself. She twists and turns it into a potent tool, where her edicts are received.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1. Dimensional tunneling. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 minute casting</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Psi</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch can anchor two points of space so that they lead into one another, essentially burrowing into the very fabric of reality itself. The maximum amount of distance between the two points is equal to her staves rating times 10</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2.Blink</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Psi</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch moves to any location within five times of her Staves rating, so long as the space is able to support her. She does not need direct line of sight to even do this.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3. Sabotage Spaces</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent Upgrade</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of using Dimensional Tunneling to anchor two points together, you may sabotage the connection and cause them to link up to unexpected locations.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This increase the Psi cost by 1.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4. Far Casting</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Upgrade</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch\u2019s skill with spatial warping has grown to the point that she is able to extend her range tremendously.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She may spend 2 extra Psi (4 for Tunneling) and extend the casting time of Blink to one minute and Dimensional tunneling to 10 and choose to treat her range as in Kilometers. </span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Set up some racial traits in the style of mirrors. I realize these are all probably gamebreakingly powerful for a player character but eh\u2026 stuff happens. And none of them can pass as human without some serious disguise checks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Gitserai</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Advanced Physiology : Due to powerful physiological advantages, Gitserai treat their Strength, Dexterity, and Presence as having attribute caps 2 higher than normal and have 2 damage claws and talons as natural weapons.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Glide : Due to naturally occuring wing membranes, Gitserai may gently glide dowards or perform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Telepathy : Gitserai do not speak any language, but have telepathy able to send complex thoughts bypassing language barriers. This telepathy is also usable as a weapon, using a contested roll of Empathy + Manipulation subtracting the lower of the target\u2019s Composure or Resolve and dealing bashing damage equal to Successes plus the Gitserai\u2019s Presence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Darkvision : Gitserai ignore all penalties from darkness. However, this comes with the downside of being very sensitive to very bright lights, leaving them stunned. Gitserai must take a Stamina check every turn in bright lights. Failure leaves them stunned as per the tilt or condition for one round.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Glowing : Gitserai let out a faint luminescent glow from their wings. This provides them with illumination at all times whilst simultaneously penalizing attempts to hide. -3 penalty to stealth checks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Modkan</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Augmented Physiology : Due to cybernetic implants replacing brain and muscle tissue, Modkan treat their mental and physical maximums as being 6. This comes at the cost of having inferior social skills due to their lack as a priority. Maximum social attribute and skills maximum is 3. They must be taken as tertiary.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blindness Assisted Senses : Modkan do not see the world around them via light due to eons of life underground. They only are able to perceive the world as a result of short range built in radar that extends for 100 meters in all directions. However, anything past 20 meters is blurry and indistinct unless it is another Modkan, resulting in a -4 to Perception for most objects past this range.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cybernetic Organs : Modkan have replaces their digestive and immune systems with efficient machinery. They treat toxins, poisons, and disease as having half the severity minus an additional 2 </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kessen</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Machine Biology : Immunity to poisons and disease.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Protean Existence : As nanomachine sludge that can reform itself. Can freely redistribute attribute dots at will at the start of a turn. May also allocate \u201cdots\u201d into the attributes of \u201cArmor\u201d and \u201cWeaponry\u201d, granting general armor and a melee weapon with the appropriate ratings. Both can go up to 5.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">@Vent0</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Nukukari </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">are yours. If you would like to give them proper racial traits, you may.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alright, so the last thing on my list is\u2026. Something about the Endgame.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I \u2018ve kept you in the dark about this, but I think it\u2019s time to tell you. If you want to read, the below is for you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Vent0 brought up the possibility of ressurection of a Monarch, I have decided that such a thing is restricted, reserved for a special few. Why it is, is very important.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For you see, it ties to the reason why Monarchs exist in the first place. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Endless are not called simply such because of their numbers, but because they truly could never die, existing in a constant circle of death and rebirth, but not just in a individual level, but a societal one as well. It is a constant cycle of Empires forming, rising, and then falling all together in cataclysmic war and disaster.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs exist in the Rebirth cycle, with the Kingmakers being part of the Death cycle. In truth they are like the Monarchs they create, but at a more advanced stage, more evolved, yet having maintained their grasp on themselves. They continue to exist to lay the foundation to the next phase and select the new rulers who should usher in a new age. The Terran Endless are the means to the end, a promise to evolve, one of many\u2026 The homeworlds of primitive species are preserved so as to maintain a proving grounds and there are many of them all through out the cosmos.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All for the goal of creating an Emperor, the final stage of life for a Monarch, becoming truly Endless and immortal. Lesser stages of development have shades of this, possessing regenerative or ressurective immortality, but an Emporer\u2019s immortality should be above even that with his nation becoming a lasting memory even in the great and unknowable universe.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-07-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:31:36-07:00","id":884990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=884742#post884742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">@Vent0</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Nukukari </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">are yours. If you would like to give them proper racial traits, you may.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I'm thinking about how to mechanically representing extreme proficiency with deconstruction and copying, but creative sterility otherwise. Basically, if they see someone else do it, they can probably copy it, but they can't do practically <i>anything</i> unless they see someone else do it first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=884742#post884742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alright, so the last thing on my list is\u2026. Something about the Endgame.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I \u2018ve kept you in the dark about this, but I think it\u2019s time to tell you. If you want to read, the below is for you.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>More details? How do you see this playing out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:38:48-07:00","id":885001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=884990#post884990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More details? How do you see this playing out?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the end goal of the chronicle... the Ascendancy aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> The goal is either to achieve or subvert it, as well as deal with the fact that even if you don't persue it... someone else will.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:45:11-07:00","id":886170,"title":"","content":"I'm back, but no wiki yet.<br /> <br /> Staves: The distances don't have a unit (Staves times five of feet? Meters? Miles? Inches?) I think I could mechanize this, along with some of the earlier ideas (first dot as granting defense against ranged makes sense; mid dots giving short personal teleports and small pocket dimensions; high dots creating temporary tunnels). I don't think it's too powerful; high dots in Changeling and Mage do similar levels of shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Aliens: If they're restricted from having a template, they don't seem more powerful than Monarchs. I'd say those seem playable enough assuming they don't start with any Principalities (but can buy them later). Gitserai seem like huge targets: they live underground and they glow, making them very easy for anyone (except the Modkan) to spot and shoot. <br /> <br /> Endgame: Interesting. Would this be supported mechanically for an Authority 10 Monarch? Would other qualifications need to apply (probably based on ST discretion, but suggested ideas)? Where will the &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">regenerative or ressurective immortality&quot; come into play? Higher Authority levels? In-setting, is this assumed to have happened already (Archmages, Prometheans becoming human) or only rumored/theoretical (Golconda, Changelings becoming Fae)?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:53:02-07:00","id":886181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886170#post886170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Staves: The distances don't have a unit (Staves times five of feet? Meters? Miles? Inches?) I think I could mechanize this, along with some of the earlier ideas (first dot as granting defense against ranged makes sense; mid dots giving short personal teleports and small pocket dimensions; high dots creating temporary tunnels). I don't think it's too powerful; high dots in Changeling and Mage do similar levels of shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding Temporary Tunnels... are poor-man's-black-holes (A Portal to the vacuum of space) still a 5 dot possibility?<br /> <br /> Ooo, or for Vampire/Strix blasting, opening a (extremely short-lived) Portal near the Sun, for making everything near it tan and extra-crispy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-09-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:42:53-07:00","id":886237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886181#post886181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding Temporary Tunnels... are poor-man's-black-holes (A Portal to the vacuum of space) still a 5 dot possibility?<br /> <br /> Ooo, or for Vampire/Strix blasting, opening a (extremely short-lived) Portal near the Sun, for making everything near it tan and extra-crispy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would argue those are too powerful, and a heck of a headache for an ST to arbitrate. (Particularly as more and more science gets involved, particularly with a sun-portal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:00:44-07:00","id":886261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886237#post886237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally would argue those are too powerful, and a heck of a headache for an ST to arbitrate. (Particularly as more and more science gets involved, particularly with a sun-portal.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww. No vortex fun or fiery blasts?<br /> <br /> I just like thinking with Portals. And using abilities in inventive ways in general. Like taking logical conclusions to turn transit powers into weapons of mass destruction.<br /> <br /> For the Vortex, its effectiveness is capped at how long you can keep it open.<br /> <br /> For the Sub-Blast, I'd make sure it is very momentary, and just apply a couple Tilts to the are for 1 Turn. Inferno, Blinding Light, Hurricane, etc. Damage wouldn't be that much, due to the heat not having long to work on things. I'd rule the greater the distance, the longer the Principality takes to activate, too (planetary distances are same turn, orbit might be 1 full turn, the Sun might be 3+ Turns). Can a Monarch Walk to Alpha Centauri? Sure! If they feel like channeling Staves 5 for a year or more.<br /> <hr /><br /> More fun about thinking with spatial manipulation.<br /> <br /> Stretching the space around the above Vortex (or a Grenade) beyond the &quot;area-of-effect&quot;, effectively neutralizes it, since the blast radius is contained inside the &quot;virtual space&quot; you are adding.<br /> <br /> Compressing space already lets you &quot;move&quot; quicker from A to B, and also lets you &quot;shorten&quot; range bands - long can become medium or short, because there is less distance to traverse along the modified trajectory, making Bows more effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-09-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:03:54-07:00","id":886266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886170#post886170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm back, but no wiki yet.<br /> <br /> Staves: The distances don't have a unit (Staves times five of feet? Meters? Miles? Inches?) I think I could mechanize this, along with some of the earlier ideas (first dot as granting defense against ranged makes sense; mid dots giving short personal teleports and small pocket dimensions; high dots creating temporary tunnels). I don't think it's too powerful; high dots in Changeling and Mage do similar levels of shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Aliens: If they're restricted from having a template, they don't seem more powerful than Monarchs. I'd say those seem playable enough assuming they don't start with any Principalities (but can buy them later). Gitserai seem like huge targets: they live underground and they glow, making them very easy for anyone (except the Modkan) to spot and shoot. <br /> <br /> Endgame: Interesting. Would this be supported mechanically for an Authority 10 Monarch? Would other qualifications need to apply (probably based on ST discretion, but suggested ideas)? Where will the &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">regenerative or ressurective immortality&quot; come into play? Higher Authority levels? In-setting, is this assumed to have happened already (Archmages, Prometheans becoming human) or only rumored/theoretical (Golconda, Changelings becoming Fae)?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it can be given good rules for ascension level gameplay. I don't have an idea in how to model it<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886237#post886237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally would argue those are too powerful, and a heck of a headache for an ST to arbitrate. (Particularly as more and more science gets involved, particularly with a sun-portal.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I put hard limits in my second draft of Staves based on Principality rating. It's a basic model. I thought I put then into meters and miles though... Maybe dozens of miles of you really want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:12:10-07:00","id":886275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886261#post886261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awww. No vortex fun or fiery blasts?<br /> <br /> I just like thinking with Portals. And using abilities in inventive ways in general. Like taking logical conclusions to turn transit powers into weapons of mass destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the creativity is great, it's the mass destruction that I'm averse to. Because either you have players steamrolling through problems using the power of the sun, or you have NPCs using these tricks and becoming impossible to stop. I don't find either of those fun for more than a scene, so I'd rather not have a power that encourages that kind of thing. (You can still have shenanigans with portals at the bottoms of lakes and the like; the scale is just smaller and less &quot;no physics says you're all dead now&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:15:20-07:00","id":886278,"title":"","content":"If anyone attempted to use a portal that way, they'd also kill themselves and like a chunk of the planets biosphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> They have to anchor one end of the portal to their current locations as they literally burrow through space to create it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-09-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:49:11-07:00","id":886306,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> What about my suggested limits (edited in above)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:51:48-07:00","id":886309,"title":"","content":"Where is the draft?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:53:59-07:00","id":886312,"title":"","content":"Also, I think that an interesting Union of Staves and Shields would be to have a kind of chaotic space-warping field around the Monarch, so that projectiles or attacks coming towards him simply miss, being 'bent' onto trajectories which will not hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:35:59-07:00","id":886344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886312#post886312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think that an interesting Union of Staves and Shields would be to have a kind of chaotic space-warping field around the Monarch, so that projectiles or attacks coming towards him simply miss, being 'bent' onto trajectories which will not hit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe. Some overlap behind the suggested Union of Shields and Veils or Censers, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:54:16-07:00","id":886443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886266#post886266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure it can be given good rules for ascension level gameplay. I don't have an idea in how to model it<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I put hard limits in my second draft of Staves based on Principality rating. It's a basic model. I thought I put then into meters and miles though... Maybe dozens of miles of you really want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more &quot;are there going to be rules in place for reaching the goal of Emperor&quot; rather than &quot;are there going to be rules in place for playing as an Emperor&quot;. And right now, the only thing in your version of Staves that has distances is the last dot, which talks about kilometers. (Personally, I think that the distances should stick to either metric or imperial, for sanity reasons.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886261#post886261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awww. No vortex fun or fiery blasts?<br /> <br /> I just like thinking with Portals. And using abilities in inventive ways in general. Like taking logical conclusions to turn transit powers into weapons of mass destruction.<br /> <br /> For the Vortex, its effectiveness is capped at how long you can keep it open.<br /> <br /> For the Sub-Blast, I'd make sure it is very momentary, and just apply a couple Tilts to the are for 1 Turn. Inferno, Blinding Light, Hurricane, etc. Damage wouldn't be that much, due to the heat not having long to work on things. I'd rule the greater the distance, the longer the Principality takes to activate, too (planetary distances are same turn, orbit might be 1 full turn, the Sun might be 3+ Turns). Can a Monarch Walk to Alpha Centauri? Sure! If they feel like channeling Staves 5 for a year or more.<br /> <hr /><br /> More fun about thinking with spatial manipulation.<br /> <br /> Stretching the space around the above Vortex (or a Grenade) beyond the &quot;area-of-effect&quot;, effectively neutralizes it, since the blast radius is contained inside the &quot;virtual space&quot; you are adding.<br /> <br /> Compressing space already lets you &quot;move&quot; quicker from A to B, and also lets you &quot;shorten&quot; range bands - long can become medium or short, because there is less distance to traverse along the modified trajectory, making Bows more effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm still against this, working on explaining why. When I create a power, it needs to fit five criteria: cool, thematic, realistic, balanced, simple. Vortexes and sun-blasts are cool, certainly. They fit the theme of bending space, and tie into general Monarch themes of outerspace and science. Where they don't fly is the other three.<br /> <br /> Realism is hard to fit, because this is a science fiction power, we don't know what happens when you open a portal to outer space/the sun. However, based on what I know of physics and what other media has done, I can make a guess, and get a feeling on how it should work. Space portals suck you into them. If you're close enough to create it, you're gonna get sucked in because vacuum. It's going to mess with the pressure of the area, probably causing the earth to lose atmosphere and any not-immune-to-vacuum-beings to get the bends, at best. Sun portals are worse, because you've got a massive outpouring of heat and light (even if open briefly) as well as a massive pull of gravity sucking you in. So even Monarchs with their healing powers are getting blinded and fried while yet again getting sucked in.<br /> <br /> Balance is still rough. One use of the power creates a massive number of damaging Tilts, but no other version does. Simplicity is worse, since if sun-blasts and vortexes are included, what about opening portals at the bottom of the ocean? What about at the earth's core? What about into other splat's realms (Shadow, Hedge, Primordial Dream, etc)? How can you tell what sort of portals can be open for long periods, and what sort are only short-term? That's more stuff to create/remember than I as a creator/ST want to deal with. <br /> <br /> So while the suggestions are better, I side on the scale of miles, not planets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:02:20-07:00","id":886529,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> ... I don't think the range of the Principality would be that extreme, or any Principality.<br /> <br /> Second, we're talking about opening a portal to the sun. First off, we'd have a massive explosive decompression as since you openned a portal from a dense atmosphere with air pressure to an area that DOESN'T have that. The result is everyone and everything being dumped into outerspace with potentially disasterous consequences.<br /> Baring that, depending on how far away the portal is, you can have things such as solar eruptions and solar wind leaking into the planet not to mention sheer heat that could reduce an entire city block to ash....<br /> <br /> It's probably way too overkill to do something like that... in much the same way as forcibly teleporting someone into a wall in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Grenade thing is maybe doable depending on how to do it, but is probably unreliable and depending on the matter, takes too long. to be useful in a combat<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5695_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5695\" data-vbnamecard=\"5695\">AceOfAlmonds</a> AceofAlmonds The road would definately require rules. For the most part, it'd be one extended quest... With some very notable phases. Perhaps in stark contrast to the rest of the game, the ascension process is more biological in terms of theming than it is noble.<br /> <br /> WoD uses meters and miles for some reason. Probably because they used to use yards.. So assume I meant distance for short range stuff in meters, while miles is for big ranges?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:13:46-07:00","id":886769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886529#post886529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> ... I don't think the range of the Principality would be that extreme, or any Principality.<br /> <br /> Second, we're talking about opening a portal to the sun. First off, we'd have a massive explosive decompression as since you openned a portal from a dense atmosphere with air pressure to an area that DOESN'T have that. The result is everyone and everything being dumped into outerspace with potentially disasterous consequences.<br /> Baring that, depending on how far away the portal is, you can have things such as solar eruptions and solar wind leaking into the planet not to mention sheer heat that could reduce an entire city block to ash....<br /> <br /> It's probably way too overkill to do something like that... in much the same way as forcibly teleporting someone into a wall in D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sad there won't be any &quot;Nuclear Launch Detected&quot; equivalents, but I'm just spinning ideas. I understand the potential it has to make things lopsided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886529#post886529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Grenade thing is maybe doable depending on how to do it, but is probably unreliable and depending on the matter, takes too long. to be useful in a combat</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the expand/contract space Mandate is Reflexive, then it could be done as needed. Someone throws a grenade or casts a fireball? Expand space around that point 20 feet (or whatever) and the blast is contained. Won't stop a point-blank hit, but can negate or minimize area damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-09-2016, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:28:15-07:00","id":886781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886769#post886769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sad there won't be any &quot;Nuclear Launch Detected&quot; equivalents, but I'm just spinning ideas. I understand the potential it has to make things lopsided.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, if the expand/stretch space Mandate is Reflexive, then it could be done as needed. Someone throws a grenade or casts a fireball? Stretch space around that point 20 feet (or whatever) and the blast is contained. Won't stop a point-blank hit, but can negate or minimize area damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You do have nuclear options.... they're just not part of the whole Principals system. The majority of your threat should come from your Colony. After all, you have an army and a nation backing you up. Literally. No other splat has that sheer level or scale of indirect power, before factoring your potential alliances. Most splats have to wage guerrilla warfare to stand a chance against that... And there's probably options to build personal kaiju or call in an orbital strike or subterrain strike from somewhere... but well....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The reflexive space negation thing might be... too specific against blast weaponry to be worth bringing in as a primary mandate. You put it as an addon of an existing mandate and well... wouldn't such spatial warping need more time to enact than on the fly?<br /> There's also just making it a generic &quot;space trap&quot; where the space you are in mutilated and twisted to make it hard to escape or access... even by supernatural means. This creates a tilt I guess?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:21:55-07:00","id":886820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=886781#post886781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You do have nuclear options.... they're just not part of the whole Principals system. The majority of your threat should come from your Colony. After all, you have an army and a nation backing you up. Literally. No other splat has that sheer level or scale of indirect power, before factoring your potential alliances. Most splats have to wage guerrilla warfare to stand a chance against that... And there's probably options to build personal kaiju or call in an orbital strike or subterrain strike from somewhere... but well....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The reflexive space negation thing might be... too specific against blast weaponry to be worth bringing in as a primary mandate. You put it as an addon of an existing mandate and well... wouldn't such spatial warping need more time to enact than on the fly?<br /> There's also just making it a generic &quot;space trap&quot; where the space you are in mutilated and twisted to make it hard to escape or access... even by supernatural means. This creates a tilt I guess?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blast negation is actually an unintended use you can employ space expansion for. Primary uses I see are anti-melee: hard to melee or grapple someone when they are 10 meters away (even when you think they are only right next to you). Space Contraction would be used for &quot;ranged&quot; melee (a reverse of the previous trick), and faster movement. Unorthodox uses would be &quot;extending&quot; range bands/intervals by making targets technically closer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:25:54-07:00","id":887667,"title":"","content":"Additional thoughts, before I forget them. Apologies if I missed something or retread ground. I'll edit later. <hr /><b>Psi economy</b><br /> How easy or hard is Psi to get? I know Mandates typically have low or no Psi costs, so it isn't something that has massive turnover (like Vitae or Pyros).<br /> <br /> Suggested recovery methods:<br /> [Colony Action] <u>Generate Psi</u>: The colony works tapping into the vast energies of the Void, intense psychic meditation, and/or biological alchemy to release vital energies. Gain 1 Psi this [Colony Turn. Day? Chapter?].<br /> [Event (Tilts for Provinces)] <u>Void Storm</u>: Roll a die, all beings in the Province gain that much Psi as wild Void energies bombard the area. [Add random damage or Conditions/Tilts?] <hr /><br /> <b>Kessen</b><br /> Ah, the semi-independent grey goo. I can see them as very hard to actually damage, due to redundant nanobots. A more-there-are-the-smarter-they-become trait might be nice, but hard to model.<br /> <br /> [Racial trait] <u>Amorphous form</u>: Lethal damage from non-supernatural sources is downgraded to bashing (justification - they don't need individual organs/parts any more than vampires do).<br /> <br /> This specific variant was directly inspired by thought about Province-level &quot;random events&quot;. I'd think Psi might be hard to come by, perhaps making its availability to the Endless (and Geodics?) one of the key things separating them from the rest of the Dwellers. Also inspired by the common (if unrealistic) &quot;grey goo&quot; fear - self propagating, exponential growth. The sample/creature below is limited in that it runs out of Psi, but it is capable for alarming growth proportional to the amount it starts with.<br /> <u>Polygeneratoi</u> - Kessen mass activated with Psi energy. Will approach other creatures (Swarms?) and use some variation of Crucibles to transform the target... into a copy of the Polygeneratoi (minus the 1 Psi to activate the ability). It and its copies will continue to replicate until they run out of Psi and go dormant once more. Note: Each new Polygeneratoi is an <i>exact copy</i> of its &quot;parent&quot; at the time it is created - attributes, powers, Health, current Psi. A near-dead P will create more near-dead Ps. <hr /><br /> <b>Geodics</b><br /> I'm fairly interested in looking more into the Geodic &quot;tech tree&quot; or build structure. How are Geodic &quot;structures&quot; going to be handled? Simple ST notes? Province Traits? Province Conditions? &quot;Buildings&quot; as in large Objects that have their listed effects?<br /> <br /> Their dependency structure look similar to the Condition Dependency ephemerals use (Resonant -&gt; Open -&gt; Controlled), but I get the impression they are more physically <i>there</i> than some vague Condition field.<br /> <br /> Another thought that I had was playing around with using Geodics-as-old-biblical sources. The Crysoform Device plays with the whole Sodom and Gomorrah story/myth. I mean, turning people into salt - a <i>crystal</i>? And the Geodics being beings of Order. A goldmine for ideas. Is there overlap (nay, crowding) with the &quot;who is really God&quot; slot (what with the Theban Sorcery's backer, Benediction's backer, the Principle, the God-Machine, etc.)? Sure, but that more fun.<br /> <br /> <u>Crysoform Device</u> - WMD that turns all thinking beings that see its pulse into crystal. <i>EDIT: Overlap with the </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Crystal Plague Launch Bay.</b></span></span><br /> <u>Possession Antenna</u> - Uses ephemeral entity rules without making an actual ephemeral entity. Sets up Transmission(basically Infrastructure) Condition, progresses it to Open, Possesses a target (using its pseudo-ephemeral) to turn them into a sleeper/active agent, then finally Claims the target (making them a organic-crystal hybrid). Destroy the Antenna removes the supporting Conditions and ends the Urging/Possession/Claim. An alternative to Stealth'd Shards.<br /> <u>Void Reactor</u> - Generates Psi energy for Geodics and minions to use. Provided the Geodics use Psi (I'm assuming they are, for simplicity's sake). Attacking Monarchs might face the choice of: Destroy it and deny the Geodics the resource, or leave it standing and siphon some of the power for themselves. <hr /><b>Colony Structures</b><br /> See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/858523-cults-for-everyone\">Cults</a>, but with merits/improvement representing specialized Colony &quot;structures&quot; that can grant bonuses. Model it like expansions to the various Safe Place alternatives (Like Tomb, from M:tC, or Bolthole from D:tD).<br /> <br /> Potential Structures:<ul><li><u>Psi Battery</u> - If Increased Authority <i>doesn't</i> increase Psi capacity, maybe this can? Considering how low Psi costs are so far, extra storage is of circumstantial use.</li> <li><u>Wormhole Gate</u> - A stable portal, used for connecting points of high value/interest to the Monarch to their Colony.</li> <li><u>Proving Ground</u> - Bloodsport arena or testing lab? You decide! Augments a Colonies ability to Spawn Military Swarms (bonus damage? health?)</li> <li><u>Envoy Nest</u> - Skilled inter-Dweller diplomat breeds and/or mind-control worms. Augments Diplomatic Swarms (opens doors quicker?)</li> <li><u>Whispers Synapse Cluster</u> - Biological intelligence center, perfect(ed) for coordinating your Espionage Swarms, listening to stray thoughts, and cataloging all that data.</li> <li>High-End Colony Structures<ul><li><u>Trans-spatial Relay</u> - Requires Staves 5, Authority 8+, [Colony Stat X?]. Allow interstellar Portals now?</li> <li><u>Dissolution Pool</u> - Requires Crucibles 5, Authority 7+. Allows truly massive scales of transmutation. Need to turn a whole hill/city into raw material? Here's your friend.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Staves Unions</b><br /> +Shields: Spatial Warding. So no one teleports you away, or sends you up the bomb.<br /> +Spheres: Panoptic Vision. See <i>all</i> of an area at once.<br /> +Quills: Broadcast. When you need to issue your decrees to all the tenants and peasants.<br /> +Veils: Occlude Location. For hiding entire areas, like your Colony entrances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-11-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:18:21-07:00","id":890069,"title":"","content":"Should we do general discussion here, or move it to the shared folder?<br /> <br /> Something I wanted to bring up. Inherent Splat is Clade, Social splat is Caste. To proof these out, and help determine what they should do, how do the combinations work?<br /> <br /> <b>Dominator</b><br /> +<b>Diplomat</b> - Seeks control via social imposition and forming alliances.<br /> +<b>Marshal</b> - The definition of a Warlord, marshaling armies to conquer.<br /> +<b>Scribe</b> - Seeks control through controlling knowledge?<br /> +<b>Shade</b> - ?<br /> +<b>Steward</b> - Seeks to fully control Logistics?<br /> <br /> <b>Predator</b><br /> +<b>Diplomat</b> - Seeks to undermine the weakest social link?<br /> +<b>Marshal</b> - A Personal Warrior, enhancing their form and dealing with conflict themselves.<br /> +<b>Scribe</b> - ?<br /> +<b>Shade</b> - The silent killer, the stalker and assassin.<br /> +<b>Steward</b> - ?<br /> <br /> <b>Evolver</b><br /> +<b>Diplomat</b> - ?<br /> +<b>Marshal</b> - Seeks/test new forms of minions to increase their efficiency.<br /> +<b>Scribe</b> - ?<br /> +<b>Shade</b> - ?<br /> +<b>Steward</b> - ?<br /> <br /> <b>Breeder</b><br /> +<b>Diplomat</b> - Create alliance for a stronger whole?<br /> +<b>Marshal</b> - Quantity is quality?<br /> +<b>Scribe</b> - ?<br /> +<b>Shade</b> - ?<br /> +<b>Steward</b> - They like big hives, they cannot lie?<br /> <br /> I'm not able to picture synergy with a number of the combinations here. That suggests they may need to be rethought, a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:23:47-07:00","id":890072,"title":"","content":"Nah, this is fine here. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm actually semi busy reading the Pack today since I just got it.<br /> <br /> <br /> We may need to rethink the ideals of the Clades, atleast, some of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:08:28-07:00","id":890117,"title":"","content":"I still dislike Breeder as a name. Call it Creator or something. <br /> <br /> There were two other suggested Clades, Seeker and Hoarder. <br /> <br /> Quick ideas for filling out the stereotype list (having a lot of trouble with Shades):<br /> <br /> <b>Dominator</b><br /> +Diplomat - Seeks control via social imposition and forming alliances, <br /> +Marshal - The definition of a Warlord, marshaling armies to conquer.<br /> +Scribe - Seeks control through knowledge (knowledge is power)<br /> +Shade - Controls others through the shadows, generally a puppetmaster<br /> +Steward - Controls through beaurocracy and little, easily ignored things; master of &quot;for want of a nail&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Predator</b><br /> +Diplomat - Destroys others socially, turns enemies against their own allies with the power of words<br /> +Marshal - A Personal Warrior, enhancing their form and dealing with conflict themselves.<br /> +Scribe - Memetic attacks, knowledge as a weapon, weilder of things man (and Monarch) was not meant to know<br /> +Shade - The silent killer, the stalker and assassin.<br /> +Steward - Monster who's lair strikes down foes, mobile attack castle<br /> <br /> <b>Evolver</b><br /> +Diplomat - Constantly trying new social manouvers, not afraid to burn one ally to find out what doesn't work to convince them<br /> +Marshal - Seeks/test new forms of minions to increase their efficiency.<br /> +Scribe - Scientist, researcher, trying to find new information<br /> +Shade - ?<br /> +Steward - ?<br /> <br /> <b>Creator</b><br /> +Diplomat - Make lots of friends, literally<br /> +Marshal - Massive armies to crush the foe, Zerg rush all the way<br /> +Scribe - ?<br /> +Shade - ?<br /> +Steward - [M/P]atriarch of the castle, or maybe the castle is a living creation<br /> <br /> <b>Seeker</b><br /> +Diplomat - Seeks out new peoples to deal with, missionary<br /> +Marshal - Knight errant, conquistador, finds new lands and fights their monsters<br /> +Scribe - Wizard in the tower, finding knowledge in books and in the field<br /> +Shade - Scout, sneaks into new places without being seen<br /> +Steward - Master of the home base; knows every secret passage and trick bookcase in their own and other's lairs<br /> <br /> <b>Hoarder</b><br /> +Diplomat - Constantly creating more allies, walking any tightrope needed to keep them all on the same side<br /> +Marshal - Armories to die for<br /> +Scribe - Collector of knowledge, ammasses giant libraries<br /> +Shade - ?<br /> +Steward - Could withstand a seige into the next century","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:24:06-07:00","id":890133,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Some thoughts on Clade abiltities:<br /> <br /> Dominator: Can employ Monarch Telepathy aggressively (Lashing Out, applying mental Conditions)?<br /> Predator: Mastery of the self enables easier transition between Noble and Human form?<br /> Evolver: Can do some XP refunding/manipulation tricks <i>way</i> quicker than normal (like swapping out a Merit dot, once per scene, or overnight)?<br /> Creator: Boosts to Swarms and/or Servants, such as &quot;free&quot; Aspects or Merits?<br /> Seeker: Enhanced senses? Better Union use?<br /> Hoarder: Bonus Wealth acquisition or to Province resources?<br /> <br /> Since Clades are supposed to be more inborn and instinctual, I was aiming for bonuses that are modifications to the core Monarch existence. As opposed to generic Skill or Attribute boosts. The Castes determine &quot;approach&quot; (Social, Physical, Mental), while the Clades boost &quot;systems&quot; (Transformation, Psychic, Adaptation, Colony, Provinces).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T15:37:20-07:00","id":890199,"title":"","content":"Currently looking at the Pack and seeing what ideas I can pull from it. A part of me is interested in canibalizing the Pack Mechanics to create a Federation or Alliance system with important NPCs... Or even... hm.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if all Characters share a single Colony? The government form is less of an absolute monarch then and more of... a task group of councilmen and governors....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-13-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:09:54-07:00","id":890740,"title":"","content":"Not sure about for standard play, though as a potential game type, sure. If Colony is shared how is its use determined?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:11:57-07:00","id":890741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=890740#post890740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about for standard play, though as a potential game type, sure. If Colony is shared how is its use determined?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By popular vote?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:45:41-07:00","id":890764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=890741#post890741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> By popular vote?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As well as whatever Charter or political rules you have.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any event, it might be best to try to intergrate Federations or Alliances as an assumption simply to streamline things for groups of multiple Monarchs so as to reduce book keeping.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Admittedly, this means I have to also ebb away a little at the progression of authority via titles, but I suppose I can justify by having &quot;shared&quot; titles or that the others being technically Vassals of a primary title holder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:03:17-07:00","id":891903,"title":"","content":"Should the local group be modeled after the Feudal/Monarchic structure, or a more Collectivist structure? Might &quot;Titles&quot; be situational? Such as the Hive/Colony of San Fransisco is under attack, Monarchs X, Y, and Z get nominated/designated/deputized as Defenders while it is under attack. After hostilities have ceased, Z looses the Title and gets assigned/awarded the Title of Peacemaker in recognition of their superior social acumen? Monarchs obviously have talents that they are skilled at, and sometimes the Hive/Colony needs the most talented to perform certain roles from time to time.<br /> <br /> I don't know. It's definitely different/distinct. But it seems like it might impinge on Castes. Unless this <i>is</i> what Castes are, and Castes become as fluid as Promethean Refinements (as opposed to the more &quot;static&quot; social splats of Vampires or Mummies). If so, perhaps defying &quot;assignment&quot; counts as a Breaking Point towards Independence (Autonomy 10)?<br /> <hr /><br /> So, we have Provinces as an in-game object/thing, yes? They have a name, some Resources Traits, and some special Traits. Can they have Tilts and Conditions, representing transitory (and more lasting) effects that are influencing them? Might Colonial control be represented via (stacking) Conditions? Like Establishing (for when you are branching out into new territory), Occupied (for when you are established and harvesting resources), Entrenched (for when you've taken the effort to dig in and fortify defenses), Exploited (for when the Resources of an area have been overtaxed)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:34:39-07:00","id":892019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=891903#post891903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should the local group be modeled after the Feudal/Monarchic structure, or a more Collectivist structure? Might &quot;Titles&quot; be situational? Such as the Hive/Colony of San Fransisco is under attack, Monarchs X, Y, and Z get nominated/designated/deputized as Defenders while it is under attack. After hostilities have ceased, Z looses the Title and gets assigned/awarded the Title of Peacemaker in recognition of their superior social acumen? Monarchs obviously have talents that they are skilled at, and sometimes the Hive/Colony needs the most talented to perform certain roles from time to time.<br /> <br /> I don't know. It's definitely different/distinct. But it seems like it might impinge on Castes. Unless this <i>is</i> what Castes are, and Castes become as fluid as Promethean Refinements (as opposed to the more &quot;static&quot; social splats of Vampires or Mummies). If so, perhaps defying &quot;assignment&quot; counts as a Breaking Point towards Independence (Autonomy 10)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a traditional monarchy structure is more theme appropriate, themewise, it's easier and more iconic to build. However. it doesn't seem as &quot;fair&quot; from a gamewise perspectve since such social codes can cause political friction...<br /> <br /> Then again, we could build those into the game where one person is a Title holder and the others are part of a Council and then well... you get the point. Perhaps a justification that there's more resources pooling together all resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's different type of titles now that you bring it up.<br /> Honorary Titles refer to accomplishments or specific roles such as &quot;Royal Huntsmaster&quot; or &quot;Peace Maker&quot; or &quot;MVP of X&quot;.<br /> Land Titles are titles about ownership; they're the simplest to understand but subtitles immediately under a Land Title can be distributed to Vassals. Such &quot;Duchy or Orleans&quot; also possessing the &quot;County of Len&quot; as a subtitle, which can be handed out to some subordinate if you really want it<br /> Succession Titles indicate your standing as well as where you are falling in line for the Kingship. Closely tied with Land titles.<br /> <br /> Caste is a subgroup of Honorary Title I suppose in this framework, specifically, a chosen role.... Maybe this should be tied to Z splat progression? Perhaps Caste defines not just biological progression but determines what Honorary Titles you can take.<br /> <br /> Being a &quot;Defender&quot; isn't worth a normal title. You're just called into war and acting in one. But being a &quot;Savior of Paris&quot; is worth it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> So, we have Provinces as an in-game object/thing, yes? They have a name, some Resources Traits, and some special Traits. Can they have Tilts and Conditions, representing transitory (and more lasting) effects that are influencing them? Might Colonial control be represented via (stacking) Conditions? Like Establishing (for when you are branching out into new territory), Occupied (for when you are established and harvesting resources), Entrenched (for when you've taken the effort to dig in and fortify defenses), Exploited (for when the Resources of an area have been overtaxed)? </div> </div> </div>I already have a framework for them posted. Temporary Conditions will have to come later when the thing is finalized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-16-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:36:06-07:00","id":893485,"title":"","content":"So, here's an interesting question. While we got an idea of Space warping... what does time warping do via records?<br /> <br /> Going on what Mage has done with it, it's a GMing nightmare at times...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:43:34-07:00","id":893493,"title":"","content":"I think that Records should be less time warping (although some time dilation would not go amiss) and more prophecy and postcognition, fitting with the theme of remembering both past and future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T12:02:01-07:00","id":893505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=893493#post893493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Records should be less time warping (although some time dilation would not go amiss) and more prophecy and postcognition, fitting with the theme of remembering both past and future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It'd also have some... interesting themes in regards to other time travel methods, in that perhaps even histories of altered time might be known to it. After all, if theme for the Endless in regards to time is seemingly inescapable cycles that repeat....<br /> <br /> Bu that's probably best saved for 5....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:03:23-07:00","id":893534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=893505#post893505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It'd also have some... interesting themes in regards to other time travel methods, in that perhaps even histories of altered time might be known to it. After all, if theme for the Endless in regards to time is seemingly inescapable cycles that repeat....<br /> <br /> Bu that's probably best saved for 5....</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to prevent headaches is to treat &quot;current&quot; times as the stable, cross point in any divergence. So, if you see/travel to the past, it can cause a branch (or you traveled to an &quot;alternate past&quot;), but doesn't effect the disembarking time that the Monarch returns too.<br /> <br /> Not sure what precise effects that might have, but I'll think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T08:53:43-07:00","id":895509,"title":"","content":"An idea for Hammers: one of the Mandates should be something along the lines of being able to temporarily change a solid into a thick liquid (like wet sand, maybe) and back again, allowing the Monarch to quickly and easily construct simple structures by 'melting' stone, for example, and then shaping it into the desired form. I was thinking either the 1st or 2nd Mandate for that. Sound OK?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T09:25:38-07:00","id":895521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=895509#post895509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea for Hammers: one of the Mandates should be something along the lines of being able to temporarily change a solid into a thick liquid (like wet sand, maybe) and back again, allowing the Monarch to quickly and easily construct simple structures by 'melting' stone, for example, and then shaping it into the desired form. I was thinking either the 1st or 2nd Mandate for that. Sound OK?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That could be an interesting application. Not sure of how to balance it game mechanics wise though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T09:29:14-07:00","id":895522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=895521#post895521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That could be an interesting application. Not sure of how to balance it game mechanics wise though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One thing I would reccommed would be making the basic version of the Mandate an Extended action, perhaps with something like 3 turns per roll, as well as making it only operate on simple inorganic materials. That would make it impractical to use in combat and also make it so that you don't have Monarchs going around and just liquifying their enemies. Perhaps you could make it so that the target number for completing the transformation is equal to the object's Durability + Structure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T09:44:58-07:00","id":895526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=895522#post895522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One thing I would reccommed would be making the basic version of the Mandate an Extended action, perhaps with something like 3 turns per roll, as well as making it only operate on simple inorganic materials. That would make it impractical to use in combat and also make it so that you don't have Monarchs going around and just liquifying their enemies. Perhaps you could make it so that the target number for completing the transformation is equal to the object's Durability + Structure?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Maybe. Using it on an enemy would perhaps be cost inefficient to just stabbing them since it takes so long to actually... do anything.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Size should be a factor too. So maybe it takes Size multiplied by Stamina or Durability? This discourages using it in many circumstances. <br /> <br /> I think that in order to &quot;Start&quot; using it, it just takes a single fee rather than constantly paying for the dismantle effect....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T11:04:22-07:00","id":895574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=895526#post895526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah. Maybe. Using it on an enemy would perhaps be cost inefficient to just stabbing them since it takes so long to actually... do anything.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Size should be a factor too. So maybe it takes Size multiplied by Stamina or Durability? This discourages using it in many circumstances.<br /> <br /> I think that in order to &quot;Start&quot; using it, it just takes a single fee rather than constantly paying for the dismantle effect....</div> </div> </div> </div>In order:<br /> <br /> 1. Yep, that's about what iw as thinking.<br /> <br /> 2. That would certainly make sense.<br /> <br /> 3. Perhaps it could be a 'you pay to activate it and can then use it free for X minutes' thing, where X = Authority or Hammers or something. That would make it so that you could actually feasibly sue it to build something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T08:06:41-07:00","id":896088,"title":"","content":"I mean, the first thing I thought of when turning stone to wet sand was &quot;hey, quicksand that dries into cement!&quot; Because if I can make quicksand in three rounds, I can definitely use that as a combat trap, and depending on how fast it hardens...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T08:14:58-07:00","id":896093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=896088#post896088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the first thing I thought of when turning stone to wet sand was &quot;hey, quicksand that dries into cement!&quot; Because if I can make quicksand in three rounds, I can definitely use that as a combat trap, and depending on how fast it hardens...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that's certainly a thing you could do. Something I'd like for Monarch in general is powers which can be exploited really well if you think a little about their use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T08:21:54-07:00","id":896096,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, it might be better to have the Monarch just create a kind of resin-ey stuff instead of moulding pre-existing materials. Like the aliens from Alien or like bees with their wax or like giant spiders or something. I mean, spiderweb is supposed to be stronger than steel, pound for pound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:36:57-07:00","id":900218,"title":"","content":"hm, ell, it'd definately be a first or second dot thing.<br /> <br /> For the latter levels... what'd be more appropriate? I think geomancy is a reasonable topic for hammers to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:05:42-07:00","id":900236,"title":"","content":"Would <i>control</i> of structures also be in theme for Hammers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:11:05-07:00","id":900240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=900236#post900236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would <i>control</i> of structures also be in theme for Hammers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I don't say so. So perhaps physical terrain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:08:13-07:00","id":900284,"title":"","content":"Spit-balling progression:<br /> 1. Create Material. Makes malleable Resin/Stuff, than can be shaped into crud implements with the Crafts Skill<br /> 2. Shape/Fabricate? Molds existing material (bonus for using on Resin?), and can make object auto-magically fast.<br /> 3.<br /> 4. Raise Structures? Like 1 &amp; 2, but industrial construction scale. Need a tower? Poof.<br /> 5. Control Structure/Area? Fisher King/Lord of the Hive feel. Changing layout, inflicting appropriate Tilts, etc. (bonus for using it on Monarch-created structures/terrain?)<br /> <br /> ?. Maybe make one of the Mandates a kind of Permanency - other stuff has a duration, but this make it last indefinitely?<br /> <br /> Hammers is more &quot;make stuff&quot;, especially on an industrial scale, right? Enhancing existing stuff would be more Crucibles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-26-2016, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:43:44-07:00","id":902805,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's about right. Spider silk and other biomatwrials would be a thing I suppose.<br /> <br /> Creating should then be the basis but manipulating should be the topm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T22:53:16-07:00","id":903973,"title":"","content":"So... I think I'll be finally getting back to work on this real soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> We apparently are missing Veils, Chalices.<br /> <br /> And need to work more on staves, records, and hammers. After that, we go through and clean up and standardize.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am however currently looking onto creating an assumption that Monarchs are able to join into a federation or alliance as a single political entity, just to simplify the logistics of handling a big colony for everyone.<br /> I jus need a justification under some legal system to do that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:21:36-07:00","id":904132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=903973#post903973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I think I'll be finally getting back to work on this real soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> We apparently are missing Veils, Chalices.<br /> <br /> And need to work more on staves, records, and hammers. After that, we go through and clean up and standardize.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am however currently looking onto creating an assumption that Monarchs are able to join into a federation or alliance as a single political entity, just to simplify the logistics of handling a big colony for everyone.<br /> I jus need a justification under some legal system to do that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Interlocking contracts, organized by specialty, enforced with Quills. Base it off the various shared Safe Place merits (in that multiple members can contribute to make it bigger, but if a contributor leaves, they take their dots with them)?<br /> <br /> I mean, in a way, the Colony is just one giant super-Safe Place, right? All its other functions are derived from that, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T11:59:04-07:00","id":905088,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Draft 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch sees and recalls events that have yet to have happened. Time is but a single moment for them to witness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1. Perception of Time. Detect uses and alterations of time and events.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2. RememberenceCognition. Pre and Post condition. Requires an object or person to focus on.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Draft 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch\u2019s limbs will grasp destinity if he has the desire, he will shape the world with his own talons and lordly will.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1. Create Material. Makes malleable Resin/Stuff</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2. Shape/Fabricate? Molds existing material (bonus for using on Resin?), and can make object auto-magically fast. Such as webs.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3. Geomancy, control the earth to create structures and formations in a slow manner, or fast to \u201cburrow\u201d. Actually 2 Mandates. All shaping is temporary.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4. Permanency, invest more Psi to have constructions last indefinately.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5. Massively expanded range. We\u2019re talking large complex building.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No idea what to fill in Records.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:01:15-07:00","id":905121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905088#post905088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Draft 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Monarch sees and recalls events that have yet to have happened. Time is but a single moment for them to witness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1. Perception of Time. Detect uses and alterations of time and events.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2. RememberenceCognition. Pre and Post condition. Requires an object or person to focus on.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5.</span></span><br /> No idea what to fill in Records.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. This seems like it needs a little meat. Maybe Scene perspective Eidetic Memory (as in, you can perfectly recall all that happened in the current Scene... even if you weren't technically there to witness it, or it <i>changed</i> due to other temporal manipulation). Basically, the current encounter is like a transcript you can check at any time, even before your entry to it, and after your exit from it. Throw in an Initiative bonus?<br /> 2. Seems golden. Needs some limitation as to the &quot;distance&quot; though. This empowers the 4 and 5 Mandates in my suggestions below - the Monarch needs to &quot;see&quot; the change they want to make.<br /> 3. ??? General haste/slow time effect? Maybe a temporal stutter - IE, editing them out of the current &quot;present&quot;? Delay effect to occur into the future, either defensively (explosive doesn't go off), or offensively (create a delayed blast trap)?<br /> 4. <u>Recursive Change</u> - The Monarch parts the veils of time and reaches out into alternate pasts. They can choose to &quot;edit&quot; their timeline, splicing it with another where some detail or circumstance happened differently within [X] [Interval] into the past. [If Johnny got shot, you can make it so that never happened, or do the same with your social faux pas at the last gathering.]<br /> 5. <u>Temporal Dictum</u> - The Monarch binds a desirable future timeline to their present, writting what <i>will</i> be. They can choose some future condition/result within [X] [Interval] into the future. Circumstances happen to ensure such a result comes to fruition in the current timeline, though other factors not directly related are unaffected and may lead to unforeseen complications. [Want X to happen? Make It So! Just be aware you are handing the ST a big blank check for introducing complications necessary to make X so.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-01-2016, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:18:53-07:00","id":905135,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the 3-dot one could be based off of the Hesitation Cacophony Embed if we're doing a 'pause time for him' thing? Maybe make it more powerful or something. Perhaps you can cause a person to basically 'skip' a round?<br /> <br /> By the way, does a Shields + Records Union that lets you freeze bullets in time sound good to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:49:49-07:00","id":905152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905135#post905135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the 3-dot one could be based off of the Hesitation Cacophony Embed if we're doing a 'pause time for him' thing? Maybe make it more powerful or something. Perhaps you can cause a person to basically 'skip' a round?</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal Stutter suggestion? Narrative justification, you are editing/transplanting their &quot;now&quot; to &quot;later&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905135#post905135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, does a Shields + Records Union that lets you freeze bullets in time sound good to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why stop with just bullets? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;How did you catch my <i>fireball</i>?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:52:53-07:00","id":905154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905152#post905152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Why stop with just bullets? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &amp;quot;How did you catch my <i>fireball</i>?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Projectiles, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T19:10:43-07:00","id":905327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905154#post905154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Projectiles, then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wonder how it'll work with a melee attack. I guess a Stasis or Displacement... How do you even write that.... Hm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T19:49:31-07:00","id":905341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905327#post905327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wonder how it'll work with a melee attack. I guess a Stasis or Displacement... How do you even write that.... Hm...</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Union: Stasis Block</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Records 3, Shields 2<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Psi<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Wits + [?]<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You create a field of up to Authority in Size. Objects or creatures entering (or already in) the field become stuck in time, ceasing movement, action, and effect (for things like explosions or fire), and being immune to being affected in turn, for 1 Turn. If multiple projectiles are part of an attack passing through the field (such as an Autofire burst), count their combined size (for most bullet volleys, this will still be Size 1, or at most 2).<br /> <br /> How does something like that look? Starting Monarchs can handle most projectile attacks easily, but they need to be fairly powerful before neutralizing people. Good luck trying to block a car that gets thrown at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-01-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T20:05:38-07:00","id":905352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905341#post905341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>Union: Stasis Block</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Records 3, Shields 2<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Psi<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Wits + [?]<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You create a field of up to Authority in Size. Objects or creatures entering (or already in) the field become stuck in time, ceasing movement, action, and effect (for things like explosions or fire), and being immune to being affected in turn, for 1 Turn. If multiple projectiles are part of an attack passing through the field (such as an Autofire burst), count their combined size (for most bullet volleys, this will still be Size 1, or at most 2).<br /> <br /> How does something like that look? Starting Monarchs can handle most projectile attacks easily, but they need to be fairly powerful before neutralizing people. Good luck trying to block a car that gets thrown at you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Neutralizing things perhaps displaces them out of space time for a moment. And People can resist.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd argue though that it's better as a Staves and Records thing. the subject is suspended from reality, does not interact with anything, does not move, and for all intents and purposes is a ghost. It's too... aggressive for Shields.<br /> <br /> . And if anything is inside of it when it phases back, it should be unharmed, relatively speaking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T20:13:25-07:00","id":905356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=905352#post905352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Neutralizing things perhaps displaces them out of space time for a moment. And People can resist.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd argue though that it's better as a Staves and Records thing. the subject is suspended from reality, does not interact with anything, does not move, and for all intents and purposes is a ghost. It's too... aggressive for Shields.<br /> <br /> . And if anything is inside of it when it phases back, it should be unharmed, relatively speaking...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah it probably works better for Staves. A Shields Union should probably protect <i>against</i> temporal shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on the other suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-01-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:12:27-07:00","id":905694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbco