ple who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:50:14-07:00","id":917429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=917427#post917427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tool use and utilities mostly. I don't think we should give dice bonuses strictly to every Principality.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe burrowing can be put there</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was under the 3rd Mandate? I can change it if you want. Anyway, I'll add the fluff to the mandates, or at least start, and I'll see where it goes from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:52:54-07:00","id":917435,"title":"","content":"On the first Mandate, should it be an Extended or Instant action to create the resin? I'm thinking an Extended one, in the fashion of what I did with Crucibles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:55:03-07:00","id":917436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=917435#post917435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the first Mandate, should it be an Extended or Instant action to create the resin? I'm thinking an Extended one, in the fashion of what I did with Crucibles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extended. Sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:10:42-07:00","id":917448,"title":"","content":"Here's the first Mandate:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>(1) Spinner</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For he who would build, the first step is to acquire materials. Human builders must satisfy themselves with quarried stone, concrete, steel beams and other tricks of artifice, but a Monarch has no such restrictions. His own body can provide the resources he requires, growing organs reminiscent of a spider\u2019s spinnerets able to secrete a substance not unlike spiderweb, except on a vastly larger scale. Even in human form a Monarch can use his psychic prowess to convert psionic energy into this material.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Psi per 5 Size of resin created or none, in Noble Form</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dexterity + Crafts + Hammers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extended, with 3 turns per roll</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch secretes a kind of fast-solidifying resin from either his hand and fingers, in human form, or from some other organ in noble form. The resin is black and shiny, almost like a kind of plastic and has a smooth surface. However, it behaves almost like anti-slip material, being very difficult to slip against, making it an easy surface to walk on. For the first few seconds it has a consistency like treacle, adhering to anything but the Monarch\u2019s body before swiftly hardening to a Durability of (Authority + Hammers) with Structure equal to Size. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch can mould the resin into any shape he desires, creating webs, restraints or more elaborate constructions, limited only by his imagination and the time at his disposal..</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each success creates 1 Size worth of this material. An Exceptional Success doubles the amount of resin created with that roll while a Dramatic failure means that the Monarch has unwittingly made a fatal mistake, creating a flaw within the structure of the resin, effectively reducing its Durability to 1.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the resin is impervious to water, wind and other natural sources of damage, it is flammable, although not extraordinarily so, and degrades over time, losing 1 Durability for every (Authority) days. When it reaches 0 Durability, the resin collapses into a black sludgy substance before evaporating within a few hours.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:18:06-07:00","id":917456,"title":"","content":"Do you think it's any good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:35:28-07:00","id":917498,"title":"","content":"What's the Target Number on the Extended roll? Size?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how Extended rolls and counting Successes is supposed to interact.<br /> <br /> I think Durability as Authority + Hammers is a bit high. What about Durability is Hammers, while Structure (Health) is Authority? You can always layer the material to increase effective Durability.<br /> <br /> Also, can we have a name for this substance, so other powers can affect it directly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:48:14-07:00","id":917505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=917498#post917498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the Target Number on the Extended roll? Size?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how Extended rolls and counting Successes is supposed to interact.<br /> <br /> I think Durability as Authority + Hammers is a bit high. What about Durability is Hammers, while Structure (Health) is Authority? You can always layer the material to increase effective Durability.<br /> <br /> Also, can we have a name for this substance, so other powers can affect it directly?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order:<br /> <br /> There isn't a target number. You roll until you either get the amount of resin you want, are forced to stop or exhaust your supply. That's a thought I had after I posted it.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I agree with you and will change it.<br /> <br /> Sure. I shall consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:18:06-07:00","id":917524,"title":"","content":"Better?<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>(1) Spinner</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For he who would build, the first step is to acquire materials. Human builders must satisfy themselves with quarried stone, concrete, steel beams and other tricks of artifice, but a Monarch has no such restrictions. His own body can provide the resources he requires, growing organs reminiscent of a spider\u2019s spinnerets able to secrete a substance not unlike spiderweb, except on a vastly larger scale. Even in human form a Monarch can use his psychic prowess to convert psionic energy into this material.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Psi per 5 Size of resin created or none, in Noble Form</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dexterity + Crafts + Hammers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extended, with 3 turns per roll</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch secretes a kind of fast-solidifying resin from either his hands and fingers, in human form, or from some other organ in noble form. The resin is black and shiny, almost like a kind of plastic and has a smooth surface. However, it behaves almost like anti-slip material, being very difficult to slip against, making it an easy surface to walk on. For the first few seconds it has a consistency like treacle, adhering to anything but the Monarch\u2019s body before swiftly hardening to a Durability of (Hammers) with Structure equal to Authority. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch can mould the resin into any shape he desires, creating webs, restraints or more elaborate constructions, limited only by his imagination and the time at his disposal..</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each success creates 1 Size worth of this material. An Exceptional Success doubles the amount of resin created with that roll while a Dramatic failure means that the Monarch has unwittingly made a fatal mistake, creating a flaw within the structure of the resin, effectively reducing its Durability to 1. A Monarch can only roll a number of times equal to his (Authority + Hammers + Stamina) in each scene, after which he has exhausted his reserves, which return at a rate of (Hammers) rolls per scene.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the resin is impervious to water, wind and other natural sources of damage, it is flammable, although not extraordinarily so, and degrades over time, losing 1 Durability for every (Authority) days. When it reaches 0 Durability, the resin collapses into a black sludgy substance before evaporating within a few hours.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:19:36-07:00","id":917525,"title":"","content":"I've no clue what to call the material. My brain is dead at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T14:50:57-07:00","id":917566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=917525#post917525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've no clue what to call the material. My brain is dead at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Resin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T09:04:52-07:00","id":922040,"title":"","content":"Thought regarding HCP: What about, to lighten their dependency upon Geodics alone, mostly what they need to maintain their tech is Psi? Sure, the core components are Geodic, but they can maintain themselves if given Psi... which Monarchs/Endless <i>also</i> possess, and are likely easier targets than Geodics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:45:47-07:00","id":922229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=922040#post922040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought regarding HCP: What about, to lighten their dependency upon Geodics alone, mostly what they need to maintain their tech is Psi? Sure, the core components are Geodic, but they can maintain themselves if given Psi... which Monarchs/Endless <i>also</i> possess, and are likely easier targets than Geodics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A likely alternative. Maybe using clone vats to provide organic parts... basically like how Eva units are made","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:21:20-07:00","id":929933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=922229#post922229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A likely alternative. Maybe using clone vats to provide organic parts... basically like how Eva units are made</div> </div> </div> </div>From Evangelion, yes?<br /> <br /> IN other news, i now have free time and have made use of some of it to have a stab at the second Mandate of Hammers. I'll make a start of the 4th and 5th tomorrow, but some clarification on what you mean with the 3rd would be welcome. Feel free to tell me if the second isn't what you were after.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>(2) Shape</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once materials have been acquired, the next step in construction is to shape them into the proper form. Mortals must make use of tools such as chisels and hammers to accomplish this, but a Monarch can use his considerable psionic powers to bring his will to bear against the the world around him and thereby cause it to take on a form more pleasing to his eye.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Psi per 5 Size of material shaped, none if used on resin created by Spinner</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dexterity + Crafts + Hammers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extended, 1 minute per roll</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch uses his psionic prowess to mould solid matter, effectively softening it to roughly the consistency of a thick treacle before telekinetically shaping it to conform to his desires. In order to do so, the Monarch first states what he is shaping and what form he desires it to have. He then spends the requisite Psi and rolls with the base dice pool. The successes required are determined by adding the target numbers of the hardness of the starting material and the complexity of the desired form, as shown in the tables below.</span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Material</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Target Number</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Loose dirt, clay, resin or sand</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Compacted/hardened dirt, sandstone, soft metals (lead, gold etc)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+3</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cement, shale, slate, plastics, tough metals (bronze, copper etc)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+5</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Granite, basalt, marble, hard metals (iron, steel etc)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+7</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Diamond, titanium</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+10</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Complexity</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Target Number</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple (a rough column, a crude blade, four rough walls)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Moderate (a couple of rooms sunk into a cliffside, a simple statue, a well-made sword)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+3</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Complex (a lifelike rendering of a person, a simple firearm, a simple house)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+5</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Masterful (a perfect classical statue, a well-made gun, an ornate building)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+7</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch can roll a number of times equal to his Authority + Hammers + Stamina before having to spend the Psi again or abandon the attempt. On a Dramatic Failure, the Monarch loses all control and the material to be shaped twists into some strange, alien and - more importantly - useless shape. A Monarch may only attempt to shape Size of material equal to (5*Authority) in one go. LArger constructs require multiple separate uses of the Mandate. Constructions made using this Mandate have Durability and Structure as informed by their material.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Constructs created with Shape last a number of days equal to Authority before collapsing into gravel or whatever state they would most likely crumble to (a gin to scrap metal, sandstone to sand etc).</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T04:52:37-07:00","id":930283,"title":"","content":"I've done a little more on Staves, fleshing out the first and second Mandates, although I'm a little confused about what you mean by the third one. Do you mean that the Mandate effectively messes up space in an area, making pathways lead back on themselves, stairs upward lead down, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T06:53:21-07:00","id":930306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-ca