e floor to trip opponents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T13:35:43-07:00","id":930499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930489#post930489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, make the prior abilities Reflexive, in that you could raise a wall to stop a bullet/attack, or open up a pit in the floor to trip opponents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that. I'm not sure whether it should be Instant or Reflexive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T14:04:13-07:00","id":930514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930499#post930499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something like that. I'm not sure whether it should be Instant or Reflexive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reflexive, but always costs Psi? The Psi cost prevents it from getting too broken, but you can still use it when needed to counter an attack or charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T14:16:34-07:00","id":930523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930514#post930514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reflexive, but always costs Psi? The Psi cost prevents it from getting too broken, but you can still use it when needed to counter an attack or charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T03:54:20-07:00","id":930762,"title":"","content":"For Staves' 5th Mandate, could it maybe allow the Monarch to trap an enemy in a pocket dimension, or maybe expand or contract space in a specific area? Perhaps that should be the 4th and Far Casting should be the 5th? Any other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":".  That's addressed to anyone who wants to answer. 07-13-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T04:19:52-07:00","id":930767,"title":"","content":"Here's the 3rd Staves Mandate.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>3. Euclidean Desecration</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A sufficiently advanced master of Staves can allow the multidimensional nature of psionic energy to run rampant within a limited area, twisting space into an Escher-esque tangle of hallways that lead miles, paths that end up where they began and stair which, should they be climbed, end up lower than where you began. As well as serving as an excellent way to trap an enemy, this also serves to block any use of Dimensional Tunnelling or Blink into or out of the affected area and any attempts to teleport within it suffer a penalty equal to (Staves). Other sources of space-warping or teleportation, such as a demon\u2019s Exploits or a Mage\u2019s spells may or may not be affected at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Psi</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Presence + Science + Staves</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch\u2019s Psi runs rampant, but about the Monarch himself. The Monarch takes 3 Lethal damage and vanishes from the world, trapped within an empty pocket dimension for (Staves) hours. As Monarchs can survive a vacuum, as well as a lack of gravity, he will survive it, although it is not likely to be a pleasant experience. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nothing happens. The Monarch may try again at a cumulative -1 penalty for every failure.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch erects a field of warped space over an area roughly equivalent to a large apartment building or a sports field. Within this area, all attempts to navigate to a specific position, including finding a way out, suffer a penalty equal to the Monarch\u2019s Staves rating. On a dramatic failure, the unfortunate is trapped within a spatial loop, unable to leave it until the effect fades, at which point they find themselves at a random point within the area of the Mandate. No being may enter or exit the field, unless they roll an Exceptional Success on a Wits + Dexterity roll to attempt to escape. If they fail, they find that their paths have looped back on them or otherwise barred their way. They may try again at a cumulative -1 penalty.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortals within the field suffer a Breaking Point at +1 upon the creation of the field, as their minds are stressed by the warped space.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monarch, his Servants and his Colony is immune to all effects of the field, save the fact that even he is unable to Blink or Dimensionally Tunnel in or out.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On an Exceptional Success, the Monarch may choose to exempt a number of individuals equal to his Authority from the effects of the field.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T07:36:45-07:00","id":930838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930762#post930762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Staves' 5th Mandate, could it maybe allow the Monarch to trap an enemy in a pocket dimension, or maybe expand or contract space in a specific area? Perhaps that should be the 4th and Far Casting should be the 5th? Any other ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. What about Staves has 4 effects: Dimensional Tunneling (portals), Blink (short teleport), Spatial Warping, and an Expand/Contract Mandate, and the 5 Mandate allow for dramatic increases to the other ranges, sizes, areas? <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Euclidean Desecration might only affect a single Scene/area for a Tilt, and the Size Boost expands that into a Colony or region-wide maze. Dimensional Tunneling might be for only short accesses, but the Size Boost let's you link vast distances together. Blink becomes a full Teleport. Expansion and Contraction can be extended to create pocket spaces (which could be further enhanced with the other Mandates).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hmm. That doesn't leave room for affecting things at a distance, impersonally. Though Blink and Dimensional Tunneling do have overlap. Maybe merge those two?</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T10:14:57-07:00","id":930918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930838#post930838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. What about Staves has 4 effects: Dimensional Tunneling (portals), Blink (short teleport), Spatial Warping, and an Expand/Contract Mandate, and the 5 Mandate allow for dramatic increases to the other ranges, sizes, areas? <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Euclidean Desecration might only affect a single Scene/area for a Tilt, and the Size Boost expands that into a Colony or region-wide maze. Dimensional Tunneling might be for only short accesses, but the Size Boost let's you link vast distances together. Blink becomes a full Teleport. Expansion and Contraction can be extended to create pocket spaces (which could be further enhanced with the other Mandates).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hmm. That doesn't leave room for affecting things at a distance, impersonally. Though Blink and Dimensional Tunneling do have overlap. Maybe merge those two?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>OK, here's my thoughts:<br /> <br /> Blink is stripped and becomes a Noble Form upgrade, with the Monarch spending 1 Psi for 3 Blink 'charges'.<br /> Blink is replaced with a kind of 'spatial sense' not unlike sonar and radar, scaling in range with Staves. This is the 1st Mandate.<br /> Dimensional Tunnelling becomes the 2nd Mandate<br /> Euclidean Desecration remains the same<br /> The 4th Mandate allows the Monarch to contract/expand space <br /> The 5th Mandate amplifies the previous ones (Increases range on Dimensional Tunnelling, area of effect on spatial sense and Euclidean Desecration and 4th Mandate allows creation of pocket dimensions).<br /> Noble form gets Speed and Defense upgrades (for passive space-bending).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T11:22:35-07:00","id":930946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930918#post930918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, here's my thoughts:<br /> <br /> Blink is stripped and becomes a Noble Form upgrade, with the Monarch spending 1 Psi for 3 Blink 'charges'.<br /> Blink is replaced with a kind of 'spatial sense' not unlike sonar and radar, scaling in range with Staves. This is the 1st Mandate.<br /> Dimensional Tunnelling becomes the 2nd Mandate<br /> Euclidean Desecration remains the same<br /> The 4th Mandate allows the Monarch to contract/expand space<br /> The 5th Mandate amplifies the previous ones (Increases range on Dimensional Tunnelling, area of effect on spatial sense and Euclidean Desecration and 4th Mandate allows creation of pocket dimensions).<br /> Noble form gets Speed and Defense upgrades (for passive space-bending).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Only thing I'd see different would be Expand/Contract occuring earlier, since it seem more conceptually fundamental to play with details, before outright breaking them (such as with teleports).<br /> <hr /><br /> Hmm. Likely far larger than called for, but what about each Mandate (Staves or all in general) has a passive and active effect? Staves 1 Passive might be the spatial sense (which would require an active ability...), 2 would be the Blink ability (technically active, just like Tunneling), 3 would be the passive Defense boost (from warping space and such), 4... maybe allows distant &quot;touch&quot;? (Brawl/Weaponry attacks, moving things, etc.). Can't think of anything for the 5th - maybe they don't need them? Just some thoughts which are probably just recomplicating things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:05:53-07:00","id":930970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930946#post930946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good. Only thing I'd see different would be Expand/Contract occuring earlier, since it seem more conceptually fundamental to play with details, before outright breaking them (such as with teleports).<br /> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that could be the 1st Mandate, make Spatial sense a passive Noble Form upgrade at first level with Blink at level two. So it would look like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> [1] Expand/Contract<br /> [2] Dimensional Tunnel<br /> [3] Euclidean Desecration<br /> [4] Pocket Dimension (upgrades [1])<br /> [5] Amplification (upgrades [2] and [3])<br /> <br /> <b>Noble Form Upgrades</b><br /> [1] Spatial Sense, speed bonus<br /> [2] Blink, increased sese range<br /> [3] Defense boost, increased sense and Blink range, speed bonus<br /> [4] Increased sense and Blink range, bonus to escaping Grapple<br /> [5] speed bonus, defense bonus, ranged 'touch' (Increase reach by 5?)<br /> <br /> How does that seem?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T13:22:43-07:00","id":931007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=930970#post930970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps that could be the 1st Mandate, make Spatial sense a passive Noble Form upgrade at first level with Blink at level two. So it would look like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Mandates</b><br /> [1] Expand/Contract<br /> [2] Dimensional Tunnel<br /> [3] Euclidean Desecration<br /> [4] Pocket Dimension (upgrades [1])<br /> [5] Amplification (upgrades [2] and [3])<br /> <br /> <b>Noble Form Upgrades</b><br /> [1] Spatial Sense, speed bonus<br /> [2] Blink, increased sese range<br /> [3] Defense boost, increased sense and Blink range, speed bonus<br /> [4] Increased sense and Blink range, bonus to escaping Grapple<br /> [5] speed bonus, defense bonus, ranged 'touch' (Increase reach by 5?)<br /> <br /> How does that seem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe make the ranged touch based off Authority? I've got the mental image of a high powered Monarch creeping someone out by stroking their cheek from across the room (using it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:23:22-07:00","id":945133,"title":"","content":"Okay. So, I'm finally back.<br /> <br /> Boy, so much to take care of.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those upgrades all seem rather nice.<br /> <br /> I forgot what we need to take care of though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:58:04-07:00","id":981225,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Group Play: Conclaves</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the imagery of a single reigning ruler lording over a single colony is appealing, the World of Darkness is designed for multiple players. This however doesn\u2019t mean you need multiple Colonies each and real world nature and fictional material is rife with examples of large mega-colonies with multiple Queens birthing young. So as Art imitates Life, Colonies with more than one Monarch aren\u2019t unheard of.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Said Colonies are lead by what is known as a Conclave, a group of elites designated as a ruler.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Colony begins play as a normal Colony and each Monarch that joins into it adds their resources together to make the initial starting Colony more efficient than it would have been otherwise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Monarch has a vote which it may use to dictate matters involving the Colony, with a simple majority dictating terms most of the time, with the catch that Monarchs of an appropriate Caste for a given issue effectively have their votes working as 2 votes. (i.e. Marshalls for Security and War issues) Additionally, a Voice of the Conclave is elected to settle Ties, should they occur.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conclaves begin play with 1 dot in all Attributes. And each Monarch\u2019s Caste adds 1 dot to a respective attribute. </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:35:41-07:00","id":981316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981225#post981225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Group Play: Conclaves</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the imagery of a single reigning ruler lording over a single colony is appealing, the World of Darkness is designed for multiple players. This however doesn\u2019t mean you need multiple Colonies each and real world nature and fictional material is rife with examples of large mega-colonies with multiple Queens birthing young. So as Art imitates Life, Colonies with more than one Monarch aren\u2019t unheard of.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Said Colonies are lead by what is known as a Conclave, a group of elites designated as a ruler.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Colony begins play as a normal Colony and each Monarch that joins into it adds their resources together to make the initial starting Colony more efficient than it would have been otherwise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Monarch has a vote which it may use to dictate matters involving the Colony, with a simple majority dictating terms most of the time, with the catch that Monarchs of an appropriate Caste for a given issue effectively have their votes working as 2 votes. (i.e. Marshalls for Security and War issues) Additionally, a Voice of the Conclave is elected to settle Ties, should they occur.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conclaves begin play with 1 dot in all Attributes. And each Monarch\u2019s Caste adds 1 dot to a respective attribute. </span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part it looks like a good system. The only thing that I might say is that it might not be a good idea to make the 'political' structure of the colony so rigid and standardised. Perhaps a few options could be presented, like there being the option to have a democratic setup or a single leader or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:09:39-07:00","id":981421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981316#post981316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the most part it looks like a good system. The only thing that I might say is that it might not be a good idea to make the 'political' structure of the colony so rigid and standardised. Perhaps a few options could be presented, like there being the option to have a democratic setup or a single leader or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I could see rotating control, enforced consensus, topical autocracy (instead of merely doubling votes), etc.<br /> <br /> And what is wrong with each Monarch having their own Colony? Some games of Vampire are modeled similarly through fiefdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:45:30-07:00","id":981440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981421#post981421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I could see rotating control, enforced consensus, topical autocracy (instead of merely doubling votes), etc.<br /> <br /> And what is wrong with each Monarch having their own Colony? Some games of Vampire are modeled similarly through fiefdom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's mostly to reduce the logistical weight when you have multiple players and wish to have that sort of gameplay. Conclaves are different from Alliances, which is the individualized Colony setup.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think Vampire's system is as defined as the one I have right now which includes defining territory and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:29:27-07:00","id":981459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981440#post981440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's mostly to reduce the logistical weight when you have multiple players and wish to have that sort of gameplay. Conclaves are different from Alliances, which is the individualized Colony setup.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think Vampire's system is as defined as the one I have right now which includes defining territory and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough, I can see the logic in that.<br /> <br /> I guess that as Colonies are such a central part of Monarch that they would be more mechanically developed than Fiefdoms. That said, though, i think that it would be unwise to define them entirely through mechanics without leaving narrative wiggle room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:31:08-07:00","id":981460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981459#post981459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fair enough, I can see the logic in that.<br /> <br /> I guess that as Colonies are such a central part of Monarch that they would be more mechanically developed than Fiefdoms. That said, though, i think that it would be unwise to define them entirely through mechanics without leaving narrative wiggle room.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, which is why after I get through with sample automatic abiltities that are &quot;autopass&quot; like in Cults, I'm not going to define them much beyond that. Any more and we'd be playing EUIV.<br /> The war system is in place, Swarms are setup, and so on.<br /> <br /> I need to fix the last Principalities...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:55:34-07:00","id":981468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981440#post981440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's mostly to reduce the logistical weight when you have multiple players and wish to have that sort of gameplay. Conclaves are different from Alliances, which is the individualized Colony setup.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think Vampire's system is as defined as the one I have right now which includes defining territory and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, though Damnation City does go into a fair amount of detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:58:33-07:00","id":981470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981460#post981460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, which is why after I get through with sample automatic abiltities that are &quot;autopass&quot; like in Cults, I'm not going to define them much beyond that. Any more and we'd be playing EUIV.<br /> The war system is in place, Swarms are setup, and so on.<br /> <br /> I need to fix the last Principalities...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Lieutenant/Servant creatures built using Retainer with some Merits and/or Dread Powers for the mutations/adaptations? Even bare-bones'd like with Best/Worst/Average dice pools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:12:17-07:00","id":981478,"title":"","content":"Wow. Sorry I have been gone, life hit me in the face and I do not have a computer. I like what you've done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:52:38-07:00","id":982098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=981470#post981470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Lieutenant/Servant creatures built using Retainer with some Merits and/or Dread Powers for the mutations/adaptations? Even bare-bones'd like with Best/Worst/Average dice pools?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That might work to simplify things. Though admittedly, I wanted to add more customization, but oh well. <br /> <br /> I think I can probably set up two different types of templates, generic leaders, and elite leaders, like full stated characters and all.... For the real epics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:20:10-07:00","id":982109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=982098#post982098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That might work to simplify things. Though admittedly, I wanted to add more customization, but oh well.<br /> <br /> I think I can probably set up two different types of templates, generic leaders, and elite leaders, like full stated characters and all.... For the real epics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Custom-built creatures are a big part of the concept, but not well supported by Swarms. But it also doesn't seem right just giving them Principalities. So a light-weight Mutation/Dread Power list might work best. And they are basically Retainers, albeit non-human ones.<br /> <br /> The idea for the Brief Nightmares model was to downsize it even more for those who don't really want them taking too much time. Specialized bio-morphs would be, well, specialized, anyways.<br /> <br /> Big issue is a build system. I mean, you <i>could</i> just throw XP at it, but that doesn't seem well integrated into the mechanics or themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T06:50:58-07:00","id":989852,"title":"","content":"So... I had an idea: What if you treated Provinces the same way you treated like MTG cards?<br /> Instead of managing resources, you spent your Colony's &quot;traits&quot; as if they were mana and used them to activate your Province effects with a &quot;mana&quot; cost associated with them.<br /> <br /> Your Colony and Conclave has a few actions where they can spend X mana to solve things. Where the prefered mana type is worth 1, but each Mana type other than that is worth half, so you need 1 for 1 point. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:36:36-07:00","id":989894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=989852#post989852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I had an idea: What if you treated Provinces the same way you treated like MTG cards?<br /> Instead of managing resources, you spent your Colony's &quot;traits&quot; as if they were mana and used them to activate your Province effects with a &quot;mana&quot; cost associated with them.<br /> <br /> Your Colony and Conclave has a few actions where they can spend X mana to solve things. Where the prefered mana type is worth 1, but each Mana type other than that is worth half, so you need 1 for 1 point.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a fairly nice, streamlined method. It kind of reminds me of Aspects from the FATE system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:29:13-07:00","id":991726,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>New Trait: Colony </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Monarchs are tended to by many lesser creatures, all various strains of the Endless made to serve her. They act as everything from a labor force, a private army, personal servants, and everything in between, all at her beck and call. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traditionally, Colonies are located in Beneath, a place underground that skirts between realworld location and alternate reality, usually accessed through wormholes or through spatially folded physical locations. As a general rule a Monarch may access or pull forces from her Colony from any Wormholes from her own Court or via physically entering the Beneath through the realspace anchors of her Colony. Generally speaking, Wormholes are safer and more expensive, but the anchor point of a Colony is a vulnerability that anyone with the knowledge can find.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But as many servants and warriors a Monarch is able to own, there are limits to how much this force can do, its capabilities, its ability to replenish losses, its own lacks from incomplete Geneweb, and other factors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies are represented by five attributes, each representing an estimation of the Colony\u2019s abilities at given tasks. These are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Military</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Knowledge</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Industry</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Espionage</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Connection</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All are rated from 1 to 10, with 1 dot in each at the start, plus an extra dot in the Monarch\u2019s primary area of focus. Raising Colony Attributes is the cost single merit dot.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colony Attributes represent the various strengths the Colony has in various fields and are rolled in situations when the Colony needs to be rolled. However, the Attributes also respent a reserve of power and resources, available to the Monarch to spend. More on this later, but these are called Resources.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Group Play: Conclaves</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the imagery of a single reigning ruler lording over a single colony is appealing, the World of Darkness is designed for multiple players. This however doesn\u2019t mean you need multiple Colonies each and real world nature and fictional material is rife with examples of large mega-colonies with multiple Queens birthing young. So as Art imitates Life, Colonies with more than one Monarch aren\u2019t unheard of.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Said Colonies are lead by what is known as a Conclave, a group of elites designated as a ruler.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Colony begins play as a normal Colony and each Monarch that joins into it adds their resources together to make the initial starting Colony more efficient than it would have been otherwise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Monarch has a vote which it may use to dictate matters involving the Colony, with a simple majority dictating terms most of the time, with the catch that Monarchs of an appropriate Caste for a given issue effectively have their votes working as 2 votes. (i.e. Marshalls for Security and War issues) Additionally, a Voice of the Conclave is elected to settle Ties, should they occur. It is within the rights for a given member of a Conclave to initiate a vote on any topic when all members of the Conclave are in psychic range of each other, though for courtesy\u2019s sake do not usually \u201crecount\u201d votes unless a situation has drastically changed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conclaves begin play with 1 dot in all Attributes. And each Monarch\u2019s Caste adds 1 dot to a respective attribute. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At any point of time, the ruling Monarch or Monarchs may order their Colony to do a task. Tasks can either be automatic and are simply done, or require something done.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Similar to a Cult, a Colony is able to do a number of tasks automatically, following the list of things a Cult\u2019s Reach and Grasp. For the purposes of this, any of the Colony\u2019s attributes count as Reach and Grasp and determining which Attribute is used for an action or a reaction is based on context and judgment. Using the Reach and Grasp actions of a Cult are not free however. Using any of them reduces the given Attribute\u2019s \u201cpool\u201d, as below.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As stated before, Colony Attributes determine the ammount of resources can be thrown at any given time. What this means is, a Colony can spend \u201cpoints\u201d of an attribute, not reducing the attribute dots, but still expending a small portion of temporary resources and using them to enact certain actions, up to the limit of the Attribute until the Colony is \u201crefreshed\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How long it takes for a Colony to refresh is not standard. This is to allow Storytellers to tailor how often Colonies are able to act as well as to represent the fact that situations may be more active or inactive depending on danger or desperation. In any time the Storyteller wishes to refresh Colonies, he can declare it any time he desires. However, the catch is, this happens to all Colonies, including enemy holdings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For instance, via diplomacy, a Monarch wishes to see 11 separate CEOs. She has the Connection attribute high enough to arrange meetings with powerful people, but she can\u2019t do it for all of them in the same day. Each CEO will reduce her Connection\u2019s pool until they are refreshed but as she is at the limit of 10, she can\u2019t see the last one just yet. The next day, the Storyteller declares all Colonies refresh their resources, allowing her to see the last CEO.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Default Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies have more actions available to them than the standard Reach and Grasp system cults employ. Colonies possess 5 special actions that they may use at any time, simply by spending the resources to activate them. Each action takes 1 Scene to complete.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For these actions, you may convert resources from one category to the next, however doing so requires spending 2 points, in any combination of any of the other categories, making this very inefficient. Use when desperate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is no limit to the amount of times a Colony may use these actions, aside from the lack of resources.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Conscripts:</i> Order a small contingent of warrior Endless to come with you, one for each point of Military spent. These warriors are smart enough to understand almost any order and obedient to you alone. Their stats:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spy</i> Order your Colony to Spy on a target location or creature via dispatching smaller Endless. Roll Espionage twice to determine their effectiveness at stealth and camouflage. You receive only basic details such as \u201ctarget is flying away\u201d \u201ctarget notices us\u201d. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, this action may be used to counter an existing Spy attempt, using Espionage twice as the dice pool. 1 Espionage is spent regardless of success or failure.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Create</i> Your swarm creates for you simple items or devices that are mundane in function, though exotic in nature. This can range to simple weapons, body armor, and electronic devices, however where such things would be made out of metal and plastic where they mundane, they are alien in appearance and nature. Each item costs 1 Industry.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Research</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence</i> </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So I think something with the Investigation and Door systems is ideal here. Trade X resources get X clues, but the more you get, the more you need to spend to get more.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Province Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One other thing Monarchs may employ their Colonies for is use their Provinces. Provinces add actions and rules to them, which can benefit the Colony\u2026 provided the appropriate resources are spent to activate and maintain them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Where as other Supernaturals employ powerful artifacts and relics, for Monarchs, this is taken on by control of the land itself. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See Provinces for details.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:51:36-07:00","id":993848,"title":"","content":"This is a very strange and very alien game. I like it.<br /> <br /> Being a Nintendo fan, an example Monarch I have in mind is the bad end of the original Pikmin where Captain Olimar is dying stranded on the alien planet and the Pikmin use the onion to convert him into a permanent leader-Pik-form. Heck, when you start thinking of the 'plant -&gt; harvest -&gt; defeat critters -&gt; more offspring converted from their corpses' example of strange biology that sounds like typical behavior for a ream of Endless in a monster heavy part of the Beneath.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been doing a lot of home-brew tweaks for the Investigative system particularly for ideas to use for Genius. It sounds like base Research would do the work of scaled Investigation, while Doors and Social Maneuvering is the realm of Diplomacy/Connection?<br /> <br /> As a suggestion for Research, perhaps for the most basic act ordering the Colony to Research automatically creates a Clue. It has no Elements though, meaning no bonus for further actions in the Investigation, but it still counts as a step towards the conclusion. More advanced interactions with such Investigations would be higher tier options.<br /> <br /> As it stands, what necessitates more complex uses of Colony traits? A higher cost tapping of the associated trait? Interaction with another trait? For example, I could see a combo of Espionage and Knowledge to infiltrate and deduce the intel of an opponent 'at the source' rather than getting that intel to the Colony to decrypt.<br /> <br /> I also have a few ideas percolating in my head for Monarch: the Endless chapter fictions, if you are ever scouting about for contributions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:07:45-07:00","id":993854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=993848#post993848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very strange and very alien game. I like it.<br /> <br /> Being a Nintendo fan, an example Monarch I have in mind is the bad end of the original Pikmin where Captain Olimar is dying stranded on the alien planet and the Pikmin use the onion to convert him into a permanent leader-Pik-form. Heck, when you start thinking of the 'plant -&gt; harvest -&gt; defeat critters -&gt; more offspring converted from their corpses' example of strange biology that sounds like typical behavior for a ream of Endless in a monster heavy part of the Beneath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider the Pikmin series to be the best RTS game on console you can find. It's such a shame though there's not much multiplayer or unit variety compared to a normal RTS, but then again, it's not a normal RTS.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been doing a lot of home-brew tweaks for the Investigative system particularly for ideas to use for Genius. It sounds like base Research would do the work of scaled Investigation, while Doors and Social Maneuvering is the realm of Diplomacy/Connection?<br /> <br /> As a suggestion for Research, perhaps for the most basic act ordering the Colony to Research automatically creates a Clue. It has no Elements though, meaning no bonus for further actions in the Investigation, but it still counts as a step towards the conclusion. More advanced interactions with such Investigations would be higher tier options. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's something I was thinking of too, just had no idea how to phrase it since I never used those systems before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it stands, what necessitates more complex uses of Colony traits? A higher cost tapping of the associated trait? Interaction with another trait? For example, I could see a combo of Espionage and Knowledge to infiltrate and deduce the intel of an opponent 'at the source' rather than getting that intel to the Colony to decrypt.<br /> <br /> I also have a few ideas percolating in my head for Monarch: the Endless chapter fictions, if you are ever scouting about for contributions. </div> </div> </div>All of the above. But in order to unlock the options, you need to have a means of doing it, either through unlocking the ability from your skill tree... or owning a province that grants it. The basic functions are essentially the bread and butter simple things anyone can do, more advanced actions requires the Monarch to be more advanced, or the land to do it. <br /> <br /> <br /> For instance, you should be all means be able to create wormholes anywhere on the planet using Colony actions, something beyond your personal abilities. The catch is you need a Wormhole generator to do it or to be a Master of Space.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T21:27:02-07:00","id":993878,"title":"","content":"I'm waiting for the Nintendo NX/Switch console of Pikmin 4 that lets you play with every type in the series, not this handled title coming out. Thus far it doesn't look to be going beyond the main 3 colors. If you add up each game there's quite a variety: Red (fire resistant fighters) Yellow (fling far technicians) Blue (aquatic) White (x-ray poisonous) Purple (beefy strong kinds) Rock (crushing immune crystalline breakers) and Pink (flying drones). I'd even include the zombie Mushroom Pikmin or all immunities ground types of the parasitic Bulbmin. The suggested mutation of pikmin to candy pop buds to onions also provides an idea of Colony buildings.<br /> <br /> <br /> So let me try to comprehend the current spread of character (Monarch) vs Colony abilities. If you use your original post for game guide overview it could do with an update from recent developments.<br /> <br /> The main power trees for Monarchs are the Principalities. They bring changes to the Noble form and specific powers at each dot. Some of them have Unions or linked powers with other Principalities, and certain benefits can influence your Colony, rather its Swarms, as well in the terms of free Swarm characteristics. The XP cost favored Principalities are based on the Caste splat.<br /> <br /> The Colony uses its five traits as 'Attributes' for certain matters, referencing the Caste archetypes to some extent, for what the Colony can do on its own. Boosting its abilities requires some type of building or infrastructure gained from a sufficient Principality rating or the control of a Providence, typically a special kind of resource from the Beneath.<br /> <br /> There's also the Clade, or shared focus/mindset of the Monarch and Colony for ongoing goals. I forget if this Splat has any bonus or provides an XP discount. Maybe a per session Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T22:04:14-07:00","id":993888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=993878#post993878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm waiting for the Nintendo NX/Switch console of Pikmin 4 that lets you play with every type in the series, not this handled title coming out. Thus far it doesn't look to be going beyond the main 3 colors. If you add up each game there's quite a variety: Red (fire resistant fighters) Yellow (fling far technicians) Blue (aquatic) White (x-ray poisonous) Purple (beefy strong kinds) Rock (crushing immune crystalline breakers) and Pink (flying drones). I'd even include the zombie Mushroom Pikmin or all immunities ground types of the parasitic Bulbmin. The suggested mutation of pikmin to candy pop buds to onions also provides an idea of Colony buildings.<br /> <br /> <br /> So let me try to comprehend the current spread of character (Monarch) vs Colony abilities. If you use your original post for game guide overview it could do with an update from recent developments.<br /> <br /> The main power trees for Monarchs are the Principalities. They bring changes to the Noble form and specific powers at each dot. Some of them have Unions or linked powers with other Principalities, and certain benefits can influence your Colony, rather its Swarms, as well in the terms of free Swarm characteristics. The XP cost favored Principalities are based on the Caste splat.<br /> <br /> The Colony uses its five traits as 'Attributes' for certain matters, referencing the Caste archetypes to some extent, for what the Colony can do on its own. Boosting its abilities requires some type of building or infrastructure gained from a sufficient Principality rating or the control of a Providence, typically a special kind of resource from the Beneath.<br /> <br /> There's also the Clade, or shared focus/mindset of the Monarch and Colony for ongoing goals. I forget if this Splat has any bonus or provides an XP discount. Maybe a per session Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No XP discounts for anything. And you get bonuses when you go to your &quot;True form&quot; And yes, you got it.<br /> <br /> However, I'm working to remove Swarms as a straight forward rule, simply because I think it'd be better for the players if they didn't have to learn a completely different subsystem of character management. This is why I posted the Colony details thing another time... it was time for a change and a revision on that matter. Instead, the Conscript action lets you spawn heavy hitters you can call in and use for whatever you want. Usually muscle power.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also wondering if Unions need to be less... standard. and more flexible. Like... Vampire Devotions. Like, I can add more Unions to anything depending on combo and level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T02:06:56-07:00","id":993942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=993888#post993888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> However, I'm working to remove Swarms as a straight forward rule, simply because I think it'd be better for the players if they didn't have to learn a completely different subsystem of character management. This is why I posted the Colony details thing another time... it was time for a change and a revision on that matter. Instead, the Conscript action lets you spawn heavy hitters you can call in and use for whatever you want. Usually muscle power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=993888#post993888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also wondering if Unions need to be less... standard. and more flexible. Like... Vampire Devotions. Like, I can add more Unions to anything depending on combo and level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you could probably have a set of pre-made Unions, and then rules for making your own (with Storyteller permission of course). THat way you can get the best of both worlds, I guess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T22:49:47-07:00","id":994417,"title":"","content":"Swarms, or rather the denizens of your Colony, do still have their own form-based abilities right? While part of the Colony can be described via cosmetics and aesthetics (such as being biomechanical, insectoid, etc) there is a point where form begets function.<br /> <br /> Perhaps instead of straight Swarm creation, although I did like the balance of numbers over specialization, the species of your colony has a genetic template. That sounds like something that was mentioned elsewhere, even if just a choice of words. These qualities are gotten from Principalities (the ones that mimic Noble Forms at any rate), could be researched and bred, or adapted from other creatures the Colony defeats and studies. Surely there's an 'assimilate' ability somewhere, probably higher on the power scale or Colony actions.<br /> <br /> This could help give a semblance to the tiers of 'single servitor' NPCs from the Colony idea that was being tossed about previously. At base, your Colony all shares 2 or at most 3 features. Specialized units could have up to 5, your Lieutenants having the most additions to their genetic template no to exceed the Monarch's Noble Form.<br /> <br /> Some kind of background 'generation' mechanic, depending on the length of the Colony lifecycle, could represent shifts in the genetic template starting from the base units upwards. This would be a multi-session thing, longer than refreshing Colony traits I'd wager. Between major story lines sounds like reasonable criteria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T22:30:26-08:00","id":1025007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=994417#post994417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarms, or rather the denizens of your Colony, do still have their own form-based abilities right? While part of the Colony can be described via cosmetics and aesthetics (such as being biomechanical, insectoid, etc) there is a point where form begets function.<br /> <br /> Perhaps instead of straight Swarm creation, although I did like the balance of numbers over specialization, the species of your colony has a genetic template. That sounds like something that was mentioned elsewhere, even if just a choice of words. These qualities are gotten from Principalities (the ones that mimic Noble Forms at any rate), could be researched and bred, or adapted from other creatures the Colony defeats and studies. Surely there's an 'assimilate' ability somewhere, probably higher on the power scale or Colony actions.<br /> <br /> This could help give a semblance to the tiers of 'single servitor' NPCs from the Colony idea that was being tossed about previously. At base, your Colony all shares 2 or at most 3 features. Specialized units could have up to 5, your Lieutenants having the most additions to their genetic template no to exceed the Monarch's Noble Form.<br /> <br /> Some kind of background 'generation' mechanic, depending on the length of the Colony lifecycle, could represent shifts in the genetic template starting from the base units upwards. This would be a multi-session thing, longer than refreshing Colony traits I'd wager. Between major story lines sounds like reasonable criteria.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Drones. Swarms are collections of Drones. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I want to create a system to generate servitors... but procedural generation is actually quite hard","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T21:35:39-08:00","id":1038262,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>New Trait: Colony </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Monarchs are tended to by many lesser creatures, all various strains of the Endless made to serve her. They act as everything from a labor force, a private army, personal servants, and everything in between, all at her beck and call. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traditionally, Colonies are located in Beneath, a place underground that skirts between realworld location and alternate reality, usually accessed through wormholes or through spatially folded physical locations. As a general rule a Monarch may access or pull forces from her Colony from any Wormholes from her own Court or via physically entering the Beneath through the realspace anchors of her Colony. Generally speaking, Wormholes are safer and more expensive, but the anchor point of a Colony is a vulnerability that anyone with the knowledge can find.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But as many servants and warriors a Monarch is able to own, there are limits to how much this force can do, its capabilities, its ability to replenish losses, its own lacks from incomplete Geneweb, and other factors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies are represented by five attributes, each representing an estimation of the Colony\u2019s abilities at given tasks. These are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Military</b> representing the sheer physical and warmaking capabilities of the Colony</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Knowledge</b> representing the ability of the Colony to research and learn as well as create experiments.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Industry</b> representing sheer economic and financial power</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Espionage</b> repressing the Colony\u2019s discrete information network as well as ability to influence events from the shadows.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Connection</b> represents the Colony\u2019s political capital and influence and ability.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All are rated from 1 to 10, with 1 dot in each at the start, plus an extra dot in the Monarch\u2019s primary area of focus. Raising Colony Attributes is the cost single merit dot.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colony Attributes represent the various strengths the Colony has in various fields and are rolled in situations when the Colony needs to be rolled. However, the Attributes also respent a reserve of power and resources, available to the Monarch to spend. More on this later, but these are called Resources.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Group Play: Conclaves</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the imagery of a single reigning ruler lording over a single colony is appealing, the World of Darkness is designed for multiple players. This however doesn\u2019t mean you need multiple Colonies each and real world nature and fictional material is rife with examples of large mega-colonies with multiple Queens birthing young. So as Art imitates Life, Colonies with more than one Monarch aren\u2019t unheard of.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Said Colonies are lead by what is known as a Conclave, a group of elites designated as a ruler.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Colony begins play as a normal Colony and each Monarch that joins into it adds their resources together to make the initial starting Colony more efficient than it would have been otherwise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Monarch has a vote which it may use to dictate matters involving the Colony, with a simple majority dictating terms most of the time, with the catch that Monarchs of an appropriate Caste for a given issue effectively have their votes working as 2 votes. (i.e. Marshalls for Security and War issues) Additionally, a Voice of the Conclave is elected to settle Ties, should they occur. It is within the rights for a given member of a Conclave to initiate a vote on any topic when all members of the Conclave are in psychic range of each other, though for courtesy\u2019s sake do not usually \u201crecount\u201d votes unless a situation has drastically changed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conclaves begin play with 1 dot in all Attributes. And each Monarch\u2019s Caste adds 1 dot to a respective attribute. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At any point of time, the ruling Monarch or Monarchs may order their Colony to do a task. Tasks can either be automatic and are simply done, or require something done.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Similar to a Cult, a Colony is able to do a number of tasks automatically, following the list of things a Cult\u2019s Reach and Grasp. For the purposes of this, any of the Colony\u2019s attributes count as Reach and Grasp and determining which Attribute is used for an action or a reaction is based on context and judgment. Using the Reach and Grasp actions of a Cult are not free however. Using any of them reduces the given Attribute\u2019s \u201cpool\u201d, as above, by 1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As stated before, Colony Attributes determine the amount of resources can be thrown at any given time. What this means is, a Colony can spend \u201cpoints\u201d of an attribute, not reducing the attribute dots, but still expending a small portion of temporary resources and using them to enact certain actions, up to the limit of the Attribute until the Colony is \u201crefreshed\u201d.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For instance, via Connections, a Monarch wishes to see 11 separate CEOs. She has the Connection attribute high enough to arrange meetings with powerful people, but she can\u2019t do it for all of them in the same day. Each CEO will reduce her Connection\u2019s pool until they are refreshed but as she is at the limit of 10, she can\u2019t see the last one just yet. The next day, the Storyteller declares all Colonies refresh their resources, allowing her to see the last CEO.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How long it takes for a Colony to refresh is not standardized. This is to allow Storytellers to tailor how often Colonies are able to act as well as to represent the fact that situations may be more active or inactive depending on danger or desperation. In any time the Storyteller wishes to refresh Colonies, he can declare it any time he desires. However, the catch is, this happens to all Colonies, including enemy holdings. This is better explained in Strategic and Tactical Turns below.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Simple Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies have more actions available to them than the standard Reach and Grasp system cults employ. Colonies possess 5 special actions that they may use at any time, simply by spending the resources to activate them. Each action takes 1 Scene to complete.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For these actions, you may convert resources from one category to the next, however doing so requires spending 2 points, in any combination of any of the other categories, making this very inefficient. Use when desperate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is no limit to the amount of times a Colony may use these actions, aside from the lack of resources.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Conscripts:</i> Order a small contingent of warrior Endless to come with you, one for each point of Military spent. These warriors are smart enough to understand almost any order and obedient to you alone. Their stats are:</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All physical Attributes 3. All mental Attributes 1. Size 4, health 7.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">0 Defense (never evades attacks). 2/2 Armor. 1 damage claws, AP 2.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 brawl, weaponry.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Never takes untrained penalties. And is immune to all fear effects.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Damage Claws.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spy</i> Order your Colony to Spy on a target location or creature via dispatching smaller Endless. Roll Espionage twice to determine their effectiveness at stealth and camouflage. You receive only basic details such as \u201ctarget is flying away\u201d \u201ctarget notices us\u201d. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, this action may be used to counter an existing Spy attempt, using Espionage twice as the dice pool. 1 Espionage is spent regardless of success or failure.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Create</i> Your Colony creates for you simple items or devices that are mundane in function, though exotic in nature. This can range to simple weapons, body armor, and electronic devices, however where such things would be made out of metal and plastic where they mundane, they are alien in appearance and nature. Each item or group of similar small items costs 1 Industry.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Research</i> Your Colony is tasked with learning all of the secrets of a given scene or item and rapidly produces worthwhile intel. This ability produces Clues. The cost of this ability varies based on the number of clues already gathered from any source including this ability. 1 Knowledge will reveal the first Clue, but additional Clues beyond the first cost 1 additional Knowledge for each Clue already obtained.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Research may be used multiple times on the same instance, but each use obviously increases the requirements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence</i> Your Colony is tasked with diplomatically influencing a subject, using all manner of persuasion and bribery it has. This ability opens Doors in social interaction provided there is a means to influence the person. The cost of this ability varies based on the number of Doors already gathered from any source including this ability. 1 Connection will open the first Door, but additional Door beyond the first cost 1 additional Connection for each Door already obtained.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Influence may be used multiple times on the same instance, but each use obviously increases the requirements.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Province Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One other thing Monarchs may employ their Colonies for is use their Provinces. Provinces add actions and rules to them, which can benefit the Colony\u2026 provided the appropriate resources are spent to activate and maintain them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Where as other Supernaturals employ powerful artifacts and relics, for Monarchs, this is taken on by control of the land itself. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Provinces</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> for details.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Strategic and Tactical Turns</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While in a normal game of World/Chronicles of Darkness, turns happen based on the person who has the best initiative roll. In the vast scale of commanding an Empire, such a system breaks down in this sort of scale.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enter Strategic and Tactical turn orders, which are more abstract and follow their own rules to make managing a government easier. How long these turns last is varied based on the Storyteller\u2019s whims, effectively being ticked over at when would be the most appropriate time. As a general rule, for every 1-3 Tactical turns, there should be one 1 Strategic turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Strategic and Tactical turns, all players and Colonies move simultaneously and resolve their actions simultaneously. It is the main way to keep track and organize Empire and Warfare actions and is organized into phases, explained in depth below, in chronological sequence of events.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The start of Strategic turns are also when all Colonies and Empires regain their Attributes supply. For those of you who played Magic the Gathering, this system was heavily influenced by that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tactical Turns are the GM\u2019s way of keeping track of War progress and are used to determine how things are going.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Start Strategic Turn</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Refresh Attributes</i> All Colonies and Empires restore up their attribute total.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Spend on Upkeep</i> Colonies spend any Upkeep they are required to spend. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Trigger Abilities</i> If the Monarch wishes to use a Colony or Province ability, she may use it. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Begin Tactical Turn</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Activate Abilities</i> If the Monarch wishes to use an ability tied to Minions, she may use it now.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Attack Phase</i> All players choose what Minions, they wish to send on an attack and which opponent they wish to attack. All attacks resolve immediately. Count the damage dealt this way by summing up the Power of each Minion appropriately and where it went.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Defense Phase </i> All players then may choose to negate the damage they received. To do this, they may choose a Minion (including one that has been used in an attack) and have it block the damage, reducing the value of damage received by a number equal to the Minion\u2019s Toughness. If the Minion\u2019s toughness is reduced to 0, the Minion is destroyed any remaining damage is still bled through and still damage the targeted player. A player may use more than one minion, each one at a time. And may use his minions to block the damage taken by another player, important for any Alliance. All units.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>War Score Phase</i> After all of the damage is done. Each player rolls a number of dice equal to the damage they successfully dealt to their opponents. Each success grants them 1 War Score pertaining to a specific opponent they attacked. This is used in the Spoils Phase. If two characters have War Score over each other, the player with the lower War Score removes his War Score and reduces the larger player\u2019s War Score by an appropriate amount.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>End Tactical Turn</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>After All Tactical Turns </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spoils Phase</i> Here, War Score may be spent to specific ends, usually the reason for war in the first place. As described in the War, Simplied table.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>End Strategic Turn</i> </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>War, Simplified</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A full, and proper military campaign is far from the abilities of a tabletop game to express. However, War Score allows you to keep track of how much is needed to achieve certain goals or maybe make the war easier on yourself.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Just as a note, War Score costs vary based on the Authority of the person you have War Score over, representing the sheer control and willingness to keep fighting of a higher and stronger Monarch. As a rule. Multiply the costs below by 2 for characters with 4+ Authority, 3 times for +8 Authority. Excluding all Vassalize or Exterminate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Free/Demand Captive (2) - Your opponent releases a captive or releases a person under her care/custody to yours.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deny Province (2) - You deny your opponent the ability to use a specific Province as long as you are hostile to him. This lasts until the War is over.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Annex Province (5 per ability) - You force your opponent to cede a land title or possess enough political power to forcefully take a Province from your enemy and keep it. It is now yours</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Acquire Artifact (1 per dot rating) - Your opponent releases an item into your custody.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vassalize Defeated (10 per Authority) - You force your opponent to be your servant. This may only be done to enemies with less Titles than you.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exterminate Defeated (20 per Authority) - You completely eradicate your opponent and take the rest of his belongings and thralls as your own. This may only be done if your opponent is reduced to a single holding.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:30:23-08:00","id":1038378,"title":"","content":"Is this reposted with edits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:47:22-08:00","id":1038389,"title":"","content":"yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> I added a list for how combat is done for instance<br /> ... basically all of the second half is new","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:29:49-07:00","id":1124708,"title":"","content":"Nice to see there is some movement on this in the docs. I forget: did we consider merely using the Brief Nightmares model for Swarms, or no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:42:30-07:00","id":1124978,"title":"","content":"They weren't out at the time or I didn't read them.<br /> <br /> I do want to Consider handing this project off to someone who has more the though. I am in a load of other writing jobs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:32:30-07:00","id":1150319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=1038262#post1038262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>New Trait: Colony </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Monarchs are tended to by many lesser creatures, all various strains of the Endless made to serve her. They act as everything from a labor force, a private army, personal servants, and everything in between, all at her beck and call. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traditionally, Colonies are located in Beneath, a place underground that skirts between realworld location and alternate reality, usually accessed through wormholes or through spatially folded physical locations. As a general rule a Monarch may access or pull forces from her Colony from any Wormholes from her own Court or via physically entering the Beneath through the realspace anchors of her Colony. Generally speaking, Wormholes are safer and more expensive, but the anchor point of a Colony is a vulnerability that anyone with the knowledge can find.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But as many servants and warriors a Monarch is able to own, there are limits to how much this force can do, its capabilities, its ability to replenish losses, its own lacks from incomplete Geneweb, and other factors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies are represented by five attributes, each representing an estimation of the Colony\u2019s abilities at given tasks. These are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Military</b> representing the sheer physical and warmaking capabilities of the Colony</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Knowledge</b> representing the ability of the Colony to research and learn as well as create experiments.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Industry</b> representing sheer economic and financial power</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Espionage</b> repressing the Colony\u2019s discrete information network as well as ability to influence events from the shadows.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Connection</b> represents the Colony\u2019s political capital and influence and ability.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All are rated from 1 to 10, with 1 dot in each at the start, plus an extra dot in the Monarch\u2019s primary area of focus. Raising Colony Attributes is the cost single merit dot.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colony Attributes represent the various strengths the Colony has in various fields and are rolled in situations when the Colony needs to be rolled. However, the Attributes also respent a reserve of power and resources, available to the Monarch to spend. More on this later, but these are called Resources.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Group Play: Conclaves</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the imagery of a single reigning ruler lording over a single colony is appealing, the World of Darkness is designed for multiple players. This however doesn\u2019t mean you need multiple Colonies each and real world nature and fictional material is rife with examples of large mega-colonies with multiple Queens birthing young. So as Art imitates Life, Colonies with more than one Monarch aren\u2019t unheard of.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Said Colonies are lead by what is known as a Conclave, a group of elites designated as a ruler.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Colony begins play as a normal Colony and each Monarch that joins into it adds their resources together to make the initial starting Colony more efficient than it would have been otherwise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Monarch has a vote which it may use to dictate matters involving the Colony, with a simple majority dictating terms most of the time, with the catch that Monarchs of an appropriate Caste for a given issue effectively have their votes working as 2 votes. (i.e. Marshalls for Security and War issues) Additionally, a Voice of the Conclave is elected to settle Ties, should they occur. It is within the rights for a given member of a Conclave to initiate a vote on any topic when all members of the Conclave are in psychic range of each other, though for courtesy\u2019s sake do not usually \u201crecount\u201d votes unless a situation has drastically changed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conclaves begin play with 1 dot in all Attributes. And each Monarch\u2019s Caste adds 1 dot to a respective attribute. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At any point of time, the ruling Monarch or Monarchs may order their Colony to do a task. Tasks can either be automatic and are simply done, or require something done.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Similar to a Cult, a Colony is able to do a number of tasks automatically, following the list of things a Cult\u2019s Reach and Grasp. For the purposes of this, any of the Colony\u2019s attributes count as Reach and Grasp and determining which Attribute is used for an action or a reaction is based on context and judgment. Using the Reach and Grasp actions of a Cult are not free however. Using any of them reduces the given Attribute\u2019s \u201cpool\u201d, as above, by 1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As stated before, Colony Attributes determine the amount of resources can be thrown at any given time. What this means is, a Colony can spend \u201cpoints\u201d of an attribute, not reducing the attribute dots, but still expending a small portion of temporary resources and using them to enact certain actions, up to the limit of the Attribute until the Colony is \u201crefreshed\u201d.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For instance, via Connections, a Monarch wishes to see 11 separate CEOs. She has the Connection attribute high enough to arrange meetings with powerful people, but she can\u2019t do it for all of them in the same day. Each CEO will reduce her Connection\u2019s pool until they are refreshed but as she is at the limit of 10, she can\u2019t see the last one just yet. The next day, the Storyteller declares all Colonies refresh their resources, allowing her to see the last CEO.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How long it takes for a Colony to refresh is not standardized. This is to allow Storytellers to tailor how often Colonies are able to act as well as to represent the fact that situations may be more active or inactive depending on danger or desperation. In any time the Storyteller wishes to refresh Colonies, he can declare it any time he desires. However, the catch is, this happens to all Colonies, including enemy holdings. This is better explained in Strategic and Tactical Turns below.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Simple Colony Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colonies have more actions available to them than the standard Reach and Grasp system cults employ. Colonies possess 5 special actions that they may use at any time, simply by spending the resources to activate them. Each action takes 1 Scene to complete.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For these actions, you may convert resources from one category to the next, however doing so requires spending 2 points, in any combination of any of the other categories, making this very inefficient. Use when desperate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is no limit to the amount of times a Colony may use these actions, aside from the lack of resources.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Conscripts:</i> Order a small contingent of warrior Endless to come with you, one for each point of Military spent. These warriors are smart enough to understand almost any order and obedient to you alone. Their stats are:</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All physical Attributes 3. All mental Attributes 1. Size 4, health 7.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">0 Defense (never evades attacks). 2/2 Armor. 1 damage claws, AP 2.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 brawl, weaponry.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Never takes untrained penalties. And is immune to all fear effects.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Damage Claws.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spy</i> Order your Colony to Spy on a target location or creature via dispatching smaller Endless. Roll Espionage twice to determine their effectiveness at stealth and camouflage. You receive only basic details such as \u201ctarget is flying away\u201d \u201ctarget notices us\u201d. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, this action may be used to counter an existing Spy attempt, using Espionage twice as the dice pool. 1 Espionage is spent regardless of success or failure.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Create</i> Your Colony creates for you simple items or devices that are mundane in function, though exotic in nature. This can range to simple weapons, body armor, and electronic devices, however where such things would be made out of metal and plastic where they mundane, they are alien in appearance and nature. Each item or group of similar small items costs 1 Industry.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Research</i> Your Colony is tasked with learning all of the secrets of a given scene or item and rapidly produces worthwhile intel. This ability produces Clues. The cost of this ability varies based on the number of clues already gathered from any source including this ability. 1 Knowledge will reveal the first Clue, but additional Clues beyond the first cost 1 additional Knowledge for each Clue already obtained.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Research may be used multiple times on the same instance, but each use obviously increases the requirements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence</i> Your Colony is tasked with diplomatically influencing a subject, using all manner of persuasion and bribery it has. This ability opens Doors in social interaction provided there is a means to influence the person. The cost of this ability varies based on the number of Doors already gathered from any source including this ability. 1 Connection will open the first Door, but additional Door beyond the first cost 1 additional Connection for each Door already obtained.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Influence may be used multiple times on the same instance, but each use obviously increases the requirements.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Province Actions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One other thing Monarchs may employ their Colonies for is use their Provinces. Provinces add actions and rules to them, which can benefit the Colony\u2026 provided the appropriate resources are spent to activate and maintain them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Where as other Supernaturals employ powerful artifacts and relics, for Monarchs, this is taken on by control of the land itself. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">See </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Provinces</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> for details.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Strategic and Tactical Turns</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While in a normal game of World/Chronicles of Darkness, turns happen based on the person who has the best initiative roll. In the vast scale of commanding an Empire, such a system breaks down in this sort of scale.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enter Strategic and Tactical turn orders, which are more abstract and follow their own rules to make managing a government easier. How long these turns last is varied based on the Storyteller\u2019s whims, effectively being ticked over at when would be the most appropriate time. As a general rule, for every 1-3 Tactical turns, there should be one 1 Strategic turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Strategic and Tactical turns, all players and Colonies move simultaneously and resolve their actions simultaneously. It is the main way to keep track and organize Empire and Warfare actions and is organized into phases, explained in depth below, in chronological sequence of events.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The start of Strategic turns are also when all Colonies and Empires regain their Attributes supply. For those of you who played Magic the Gathering, this system was heavily influenced by that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tactical Turns are the GM\u2019s way of keeping track of War progress and are used to determine how things are going.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Start Strategic Turn</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Refresh Attributes</i> All Colonies and Empires restore up their attribute total.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Spend on Upkeep</i> Colonies spend any Upkeep they are required to spend. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Trigger Abilities</i> If the Monarch wishes to use a Colony or Province ability, she may use it. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Begin Tactical Turn</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Activate Abilities</i> If the Monarch wishes to use an ability tied to Minions, she may use it now.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Attack Phase</i> All players choose what Minions, they wish to send on an attack and which opponent they wish to attack. All attacks resolve immediately. Count the damage dealt this way by summing up the Power of each Minion appropriately and where it went.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>Defense Phase </i> All players then may choose to negate the damage they received. To do this, they may choose a Minion (including one that has been used in an attack) and have it block the damage, reducing the value of damage received by a number equal to the Minion\u2019s Toughness. If the Minion\u2019s toughness is reduced to 0, the Minion is destroyed any remaining damage is still bled through and still damage the targeted player. A player may use more than one minion, each one at a time. And may use his minions to block the damage taken by another player, important for any Alliance. All units.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-<i>War Score Phase</i> After all of the damage is done. Each player rolls a number of dice equal to the damage they successfully dealt to their opponents. Each success grants them 1 War Score pertaining to a specific opponent they attacked. This is used in the Spoils Phase. If two characters have War Score over each other, the player with the lower War Score removes his War Score and reduces the larger player\u2019s War Score by an appropriate amount.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>End Tactical Turn</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>After All Tactical Turns </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spoils Phase</i> Here, War Score may be spent to specific ends, usually the reason for war in the first place. As described in the War, Simplied table.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>End Strategic Turn</i> </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>War, Simplified</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A full, and proper military campaign is far from the abilities of a tabletop game to express. However, War Score allows you to keep track of how much is needed to achieve certain goals or maybe make the war easier on yourself.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Just as a note, War Score costs vary based on the Authority of the person you have War Score over, representing the sheer control and willingness to keep fighting of a higher and stronger Monarch. As a rule. Multiply the costs below by 2 for characters with 4+ Authority, 3 times for +8 Authority. Excluding all Vassalize or Exterminate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Free/Demand Captive (2) - Your opponent releases a captive or releases a person under her care/custody to yours.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deny Province (2) - You deny your opponent the ability to use a specific Province as long as you are hostile to him. This lasts until the War is over.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Annex Province (5 per ability) - You force your opponent to cede a land title or possess enough political power to forcefully take a Province from your enemy and keep it. It is now yours</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Acquire Artifact (1 per dot rating) - Your opponent releases an item into your custody.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vassalize Defeated (10 per Authority) - You force your opponent to be your servant. This may only be done to enemies with less Titles than you.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exterminate Defeated (20 per Authority) - You completely eradicate your opponent and take the rest of his belongings and thralls as your own. This may only be done if your opponent is reduced to a single holding.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Question: Wouldn't Chase mechanics, with a modification that it substitutes Authority for speed and turns some of those aspects you listed into &quot;war&quot; merits in a way that Relentless, Greyhound and other Chase related merits do from CofD be a streamlined and conceptually consistent use of existing mechanics? Just an idea.<br /> <br /> Also it seems like some of the consequences of War would seem to be good things to format and use as Conditions, Deny Province is a good example. Give it a Resolution clause and Beat clause and you have a mechanic which is more rich. Indeed the point of the War type Chase could be to inflict War caused Conditions on opponents or self (like Plundered on opponent and Enriched on self) even temporarily empty servant spots caused by casualties based Conditions are totally workable, giving you a chance to neatly define resolving such issues without Xp expenditures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-17-2017, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:52:16-07:00","id":1150330,"title":"","content":"Oh thank the dark gods, I thought that no-one else was interested in this carrying on!<br /> <br /> With reference to the mechanics of war, though, I think that something we need to consider is the fact that war has a price. War drains resources on a massive scale, especially when you have to construct not only your soldiers' armaments but their very bodies. Of course, Endless monsters are essentially expendable, but the fact remains that I doubt that Monarchs would <i>like</i> to go to war with one another all that often, especially when they have enemies like the Geodics at their backs. I feel that there should be a significant part of the 'fluff' section dedicated to Monarchs' etiquette amongst themselves and in relation to outsiders. How one declares war, what is required as a pretext, when peace must be held (in response to Geodic incursions, for example), protocols with regards to contact with independent entities in the Underneath or other supernaturals and so on.<br /> <br /> Given that Monarchs have in-built long-range communication with their telepathy, I think that their society would be both widely spread-out and closely-linked together. Quite apart from anything else, I would be horribly disappointed if Monarchs didn't have a wonderfully convoluted series of laws, conventions and the occasional 'party' which is really an excuse for making and breaking alliances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-17-2017, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:59:25-07:00","id":1150331,"title":"","content":"I could have a go at writing up some of those when I've the time, if you'd be happy with that, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T07:43:20-07:00","id":1150349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=1150319#post1150319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Question: Wouldn't Chase mechanics, with a modification that it substitutes Authority for speed and turns some of those aspects you listed into &quot;war&quot; merits in a way that Relentless, Greyhound and other Chase related merits do from CofD be a streamlined and conceptually consistent use of existing mechanics? Just an idea.<br /> <br /> Also it seems like some of the consequences of War would seem to be good things to format and use as Conditions, Deny Province is a good example. Give it a Resolution clause and Beat clause and you have a mechanic which is more rich. Indeed the point of the War type Chase could be to inflict War caused Conditions on opponents or self (like Plundered on opponent and Enriched on self) even temporarily empty servant spots caused by casualties based Conditions are totally workable, giving you a chance to neatly define resolving such issues without Xp expenditures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't read the chase rules at the time, and the main issue is that... War is meant to be a different level of combat entirely, in much the same way controling a whole nation state is like controlling a special character or a starship. There's also the prototping reasons for why it is. So while something made sense as conditions, you had to say, manage army logistics. <br /> I do wonder if I oculd do a better job though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=1150330#post1150330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh thank the dark gods, I thought that no-one else was interested in this carrying on!<br /> <br /> With reference to the mechanics of war, though, I think that something we need to consider is the fact that war has a price. War drains resources on a massive scale, especially when you have to construct not only your soldiers' armaments but their very bodies. Of course, Endless monsters are essentially expendable, but the fact remains that I doubt that Monarchs would <i>like</i> to go to war with one another all that often, especially when they have enemies like the Geodics at their backs. I feel that there should be a significant part of the 'fluff' section dedicated to Monarchs' etiquette amongst themselves and in relation to outsiders. How one declares war, what is required as a pretext, when peace must be held (in response to Geodic incursions, for example), protocols with regards to contact with independent entities in the Underneath or other supernaturals and so on.<br /> <br /> Given that Monarchs have in-built long-range communication with their telepathy, I think that their society would be both widely spread-out and closely-linked together. Quite apart from anything else, I would be horribly disappointed if Monarchs didn't have a wonderfully convoluted series of laws, conventions and the occasional 'party' which is really an excuse for making and breaking alliances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do wonder if there's some sort of thought realm they could commune over, like some sort of gigantic skype/discord that they can access in and out of innately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=1150331#post1150331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have a go at writing up some of those when I've the time, if you'd be happy with that, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Go ahead. Anyone is free to continue and remake as they wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T09:07:34-07:00","id":1150369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=1150349#post1150349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder if there's some sort of thought realm they could commune over, like some sort of gigantic skype/discord that they can access in and out of innately.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you say that I envision something like an unholy telepathic cross of Skype and Reddit. <i>All the flamewars</i>. Imagine a kind of 'duel' wherein you try to overload the other guy with so much telepathic ALL CAPS SCREAMING that they have to shut off the link because migraine.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I like the idea of a 'realm' per se, but I'd be more than happy with the telepathic equivalent of <i>Geist's</i> Twilight Network. Perhaps it's a job - maybe even a Merit - that can be assigned to a Monarch to act as a 'host' for multi-way telepathic conversations, or maybe they can build structures that allow the same.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T09:40:04-07:00","id":1150381,"title":"","content":"Yeah that would work. A psyxhic data haven would be a thing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T15:08:54-07:00","id":1150479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless?p=1150381#post1150381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that would work. A psyxhic data haven would be a thing</div> </div> </div> </div>What about custom built/designed/bred creatures acting as psychic repeaters, routers, etc.? Established hubs could even be Province bonuses.<br /> <br /> As for plots:<br /> Someone &quot;stole&quot; a network bug that was about to relay your (or your Ally's) declaration of war. Without prior statement, there is the risk of Monarch faux pas (and social alienation).<br /> A rival is seeding your territory with Spam Drones, irritating you and disrupting your Colony's organization. Crush the vermin and find out who did it.<br /> One of your Allies has gone dark - communication has stopped and few of their drones have been seen in their territory. Rumor has it they are just conserving resources. But for what purpose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T19:27:11-07:00","id":1150523,"title":"","content":"Is it too late to share a antagonist idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T19:34:46-07:00","id":1150525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-